window.TOPICS=[{"n":78,"t":"Adán y Eva","en":"Adam and Eve","sum":"Adam and Eve were a Material Son and Daughter of Jerusem who came about thirty-eight thousand years ago as biologic uplifters to Urantia, a world isolated by rebellion. They worked in the Garden of Eden for one hundred and seventeen years, but through Eve's impatience to hasten results and Adam's errors of judgment they turned aside from the divine plan and defaulted. They were reduced to mortal status yet cleared of the charge of rebellion, and through the violet race they made a great contribution to the biologic and cultural progress of mankind.","sections":[{"h":"Sending the Biologic Uplifters","items":[{"x":"Material Sons and Daughters are the offspring of the Creator Son, destined to serve as physical uplifters on the evolutionary worlds.","r":["51:1.1"]},{"x":"After the inspection and recommendation of Tabamantia, Adam and Eve were sent to Urantia, a world retarded and isolated by rebellion.","r":["73:0.3"]},{"x":"They were members of the senior corps of Material Sons on Jerusem, an experienced pair who had led research on the modification of life forms.","r":["74:1.1","74:1.2"]},{"x":"The entire senior corps volunteered, and Adam and Eve, who had stayed loyal during the Lucifer rebellion, were chosen.","r":["74:1.3","74:1.4"]},{"x":"They arrived 37,848 years before A.D. 1934, in the season when the Garden was in full bloom.","r":["74:0.1"]}]},{"h":"The Culture of the Garden of Eden","items":[{"x":"The schools of Eden taught health, the golden rule, individual and group rights, play, and competition, aiming at socialization.","r":["74:7.2","74:7.3"]},{"x":"Adam discouraged set prayers and taught that effective prayer must be the personal longing of the soul.","r":["74:7.21"]},{"x":"Adam sought to awaken sex equality by teaching that woman contributes equally with man to new life.","r":["74:7.22"]},{"x":"Traditions such as the six days of creation and the rib story are later confusions and condensations of events from the Garden days.","r":["74:8.1","74:8.3"]},{"q":"La «edad de oro» es un mito, pero Edén fue un hecho, y la civilización del Jardín fue de hecho derrocada.","r":"74:8.14"}]},{"h":"A Difficult Task and Impatience","items":[{"x":"They faced deep loneliness in a world of spiritual darkness, wholly unprepared to accept brotherhood.","r":["75:1.3","75:1.4"]},{"q":"they were not willing to settle down to the long, long endurance test.","r":"75:1.6"},{"x":"Caligastia often visited the Garden urging easier ways, but at first they firmly rejected every proposal of compromise.","r":["75:2.1"]},{"x":"Serapatatia sincerely wanted to help the world but never knew that he had become Caligastia's tool.","r":["75:3.6"]}]},{"h":"The Default and Its Consequences","items":[{"x":"In her secret meeting with Cano, Eve broke the long-standing warning against mixing good and evil.","r":["75:4.4","75:4.5"]},{"q":"it constituted evil because it represented the wrong way to achieve righteous ends, because it departed from the right way, the divine plan.","r":"75:4.6"},{"x":"Realizing the failure, Adam in despair committed the same folly as Eve, and enraged inhabitants destroyed a Nodite settlement.","r":["75:5.2","75:5.3"]},{"x":"They left the Garden for the second garden, and their children who had reached twenty could choose the way to Jerusem.","r":["75:6.2","75:6.3"]},{"x":"Gabriel adjudged them in default but cleared them of the charge of rebellion against the universe government.","r":["75:7.1","75:7.2"]},{"q":"Lo que habían hecho, en efecto, fue malo, pero nunca se les declaró culpables por desacato a la verdad, tampoco participaron con conocimiento de causa en la rebelión contra el justo régimen del Padre Universal y su Hijo Creador.","r":"75:7.7"}]},{"h":"There Was No Fall of Man","items":[{"q":"No ha habido ninguna «caída del hombre».","r":"75:8.2"},{"x":"The Adamic bestowal greatly improved mankind biologically, and Adam should not be regarded as the cause of a curse on the human race.","r":["75:8.2","75:8.3"]},{"x":"After their demotion to mortal status they sincerely repented, and Thought Adjusters came to indwell them.","r":["76:5.2"]},{"x":"In the second garden Adam left his life plasm, adding 1,570 superior men and women to the world.","r":["76:4.8"]},{"x":"Adam lived 530 years and, after death, awoke in a special resurrection and attained citizenship on Jerusem.","r":["76:5.5","76:6.2","76:6.3"]},{"q":"Never, in all your ascent to Paradise, will you gain anything by impatiently attempting to circumvent the established and divine plan by short cuts, personal inventions, or other devices","r":"75:8.5"}]}],"see":["Hijos e Hijas Materiales","Caligastia","Razas","Urantia","Revelación","Rebelión de Lucifer"]},{"n":53,"t":"Adoración","en":"Worship","sum":"Worship is the act of recognizing and rejoicing in the intimate relationship with the Creator; it is the highest privilege and the first duty of all intelligent beings. Unlike prayer, which contains an element of self-interest, worship asks nothing and adores God for what he is. The worship impulse, beginning in primitive nature worship, was turned by the adjutant spirits toward the God of nature, and on Paradise it becomes the highest delight.","sections":[{"h":"The Nature of Worship","items":[{"q":"La adoración es el privilegio más elevado y el primer deber de todas las inteligencias creadas.","r":"27:7.1"},{"x":"Worship is the conscious and joyous recognition of the intimate and personal relationships of the Creators with their creatures.","r":["27:7.1"]},{"x":"In the highest sense, worship is directed, directly or indirectly, to the Universal Father.","r":["5:3.1"]},{"x":"Worship is personal communion with that which is divinely real, the source of reality, not a vain monologue.","r":["196:3.22"]},{"x":"Worship is the act of the part identifying itself with the Whole, the finite with the Infinite, the son with the Father.","r":["143:7.8"]}]},{"h":"Worship and Prayer","items":[{"q":"Worship is for its own sake; prayer embodies a self- or creature-interest element","r":"5:3.3"},{"x":"True worship requests nothing and expects no reward; it is a natural response to the Father's lovable nature.","r":["5:3.3"]},{"x":"When self-interest enters worship, it turns into prayer.","r":["5:3.4"]},{"q":"El orar es recordar a sí mismo —pensamiento sublime; el adorar es olvidar a sí mismo —superpensamiento.","r":"143:7.7"},{"x":"Prayer is spiritually sustaining, but worship is divinely creative; prayer enriches life, and worship illuminates destiny.","r":["143:7.5","102:4.5"]},{"x":"Modern religions have overemphasized prayer and neglected the more essential communion of worship.","r":["102:4.5"]}]},{"h":"Worship of Soul and Adjuster","items":[{"x":"Sincere worship is the mobilization of all the powers of the personality under the leadership of the evolving soul and the direction of the Adjuster.","r":["5:3.7"]},{"x":"The mortal mind consents to worship, the soul craves it, and the Adjuster conducts that worship to the Father.","r":["5:3.8"]},{"x":"The fragments of the Father are empowered to register the genuine adoration of their subjects before the Universal Father.","r":["5:3.2"]},{"x":"The Father's spirit speaks best when the human mind is in an attitude of true worship.","r":["146:2.17"]},{"q":"La mente mortal consciente en adorar; el alma inmortal anhela e inicia la adoración; la presencia del Ajustador divino dirige tal culto en nombre de la mente mortal y del alma inmortal evolutiva.","r":"5:3.8"}]},{"h":"Origin of the Worship Impulse","items":[{"x":"Primitive man, fearing the incomprehensible forces of nature, worshiped almost everything on earth and in the heavens.","r":["85:0.4"]},{"x":"The spirit of worship, the sixth adjutant spirit, constantly stimulated the worship urge in the primitive mind.","r":["85:7.1"]},{"x":"The spirit of worship is the mark of spiritual-ascension candidacy, separating beings capable of possessing souls from those who are not.","r":["36:5.11"]},{"x":"When the spirit of wisdom guides the worship impulse, man begins to turn from the objects of nature to the God of nature.","r":["85:7.3"]},{"q":"La adoración es la insignia de la candidatura a la ascensión espiritual.","r":"36:5.11"}]},{"h":"The Worshipful Life","items":[{"x":"Worship, or spiritual contemplation, must alternate with service, which keeps contact with material reality.","r":["143:7.3"]},{"q":"La adoración es la técnica de buscar en el Único la inspiración para servir a muchos.","r":"143:7.6"},{"x":"Worship is effortless attention, the true rest of the soul, a form of restful spiritual activity.","r":["143:7.7"]},{"x":"In time, thought leads to wisdom, and wisdom leads to worship.","r":["112:2.13"]},{"x":"On Paradise worship is the highest delight and a refreshing play, and all the arts are employed in worship.","r":["27:7.2","27:7.5"]},{"x":"On the seventh mansion world the ascender begins a new and more spiritual worship of the invisible Father.","r":["47:9.2"]}]}],"see":["Oración","Padre Universal","Ajustador del Pensamiento","Espíritus ayudantes de la mente","Experiencia religiosa","Servicio"]},{"n":71,"t":"Adversidad y pruebas","en":"Adversity and Trials","sum":"The confusion and trials of Urantia signify not God's indifference but part of the divine plan to forge strong and noble characters between the anvils of necessity and the hammers of anguish. Virtues such as courage, altruism, hope, and faith can grow only in a world of hardship and uncertainty. Jesus corrected the superstition that suffering is God's punishment, and while he did not exempt believers from difficulty, he promised to go with them through all their trials.","sections":[{"h":"Why There Is Adversity","items":[{"x":"The uncertainties and vicissitudes of life are in no way contradictory to the universal sovereignty of God.","r":["3:5.5"]},{"q":"¿Es el valor — la fuerza de carácter— deseable? Si es así, el hombre debe criarse en un ambiente que requiera el enfrentamiento con dificultades y la reacción a los desencantos.","r":"3:5.6"},{"x":"Altruism requires inequality, hope requires insecurity, and faith requires a situation in which one must believe more than one knows.","r":["3:5.7","3:5.8","3:5.9"]},{"x":"Even the satisfaction of happiness is truly experienced only in a world open to the possibility of pain and distress.","r":["3:5.14"]},{"x":"The perfect beings of Havona know neither the sweetness of escaping the potential of pain nor saving faith.","r":["3:5.17"]}]},{"h":"The Anvil and Hammer That Forge Character","items":[{"x":"The Creators could make Urantia a paradise, but such an Eden would not produce strong and noble characters.","r":["23:2.12"]},{"q":"Vuestras ansiedades y penas, vuestras pruebas y desilusiones, son tanto parte del plan divino en vuestra esfera como lo son la perfección exquisita y la adaptación infinita de todas las cosas a su propósito supremo en los mundos del universo central y perfecto.","r":"23:2.12"},{"q":"El universo de vuestro origen está siendo forjado entre el yunque de la justicia y el martillo del sufrimiento; pero los que esgrimen el martillo son los hijos de la misericordia, la progenie espiritual del Espíritu Infinito.","r":"9:1.8"},{"q":"No podéis percibir la verdad espiritual hasta tanto no la experimentéis con los sentimientos, y muchas verdades no son realmente sentidas excepto en las adversidades.","r":"48:7.18"},{"x":"God sometimes disciplines us for our good, but he suffers with us in our fiery trials.","r":["2:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Suffering Is Not Punishment","items":[{"x":"Jesus declared superstitious the belief that prosperity is a sign of God's approval and adversity a sign of his displeasure.","r":["166:4.3"]},{"x":"Those killed by the falling tower of Siloam were not greater sinners but innocent victims of the accidents of time.","r":["166:4.4"]},{"x":"As the story of Job shows, material prosperity is no proof of God's favor, and the Father loves the poor just as much.","r":["148:6.2"]},{"x":"People suffer from the accidents of time, from imperfection, from the consequences of sin, and from the harvest of rebellion; suffering is not a visitation of divine judgment.","r":["148:6.11"]},{"x":"Even in suffering Job pierced the clouds by faith and found the God of comfort and salvation.","r":["148:6.11","148:6.10"]}]},{"h":"The Believer's Attitude Toward Trials","items":[{"q":"No os prometo liberaros del mar de adversidades, pero sí os prometo que navegaré a través de todas ellas con vosotros.","r":"159:3.13"},{"x":"Believing the gospel does not exempt one from accidents and calamities, but it keeps one unafraid when trouble comes.","r":["159:3.13"]},{"q":"Sabe cómo soportar valientemente los sufrimientos inevitables; no se queja al enfrentarse con dificultades inescapables.","r":"156:5.20"},{"x":"In times of testing a person's soul is revealed, and the loyal who endure trials are entrusted with the work of the kingdom.","r":["165:6.2"]},{"x":"Even when floods of adversity and hatred sweep over the soul, the one who entrusts his soul to the indwelling spirit has a citadel of the spirit that does not fall.","r":["100:2.7"]},{"x":"True religion produces profound courage and confidence even in natural adversity and physical calamity.","r":["101:3.7","34:6.13"]}]},{"h":"The Way Jesus Showed","items":[{"x":"Jesus met suffering with faith, courage, and the determination to do the Father's will, and thus conquered life and death.","r":["194:3.3"]},{"x":"Even before apparent defeat and the anguish of despair, Jesus stood calm and unafraid in the divine presence.","r":["196:0.5"]},{"x":"Jesus encouraged a fear-ridden young man that suffering would give vigor, disappointment a spur, and obstacles a stimulus.","r":["130:6.4"]},{"x":"Jesus taught the multitude gathered at Bethsaida for more than an hour on \"the mission of adversity and the spiritual value of disappointment.\"","r":["151:0.1"]},{"x":"The two hard years before his marriage were a time of real trial in Jesus' earth life.","r":["126:0.1"]}]}],"see":["Mal","Miedo y preocupación","Fe","Crecimiento","Alegría y felicidad","Carácter de Jesús"]},{"n":33,"t":"Ajustador del Pensamiento","en":"Thought Adjuster","sum":"The Thought Adjuster is a fragment of God that comes directly from the Universal Father and indwells the human mind. It is not a created being but divinity itself; it leads man from within to do the Father's will and seeks to become one with the evolving soul and go forward with it in the eternal career. At the center of the personal religion presented in The Urantia Book stands this indwelling spirit of the Father.","sections":[{"h":"A Divine Fragment from the Father","items":[{"x":"Though he dwells on Paradise, the Father is actually present in the human mind as the Mystery Monitor.","r":["107:0.1"]},{"q":"No son seres creados; son entidades fragmentadas que constituyen la presencia de hecho del Dios infinito.","r":"107:1.2"},{"x":"Adjusters are limited in scope yet absolute in essence, and so they are called the \"qualified absolute fragments\" of the Father.","r":["107:4.2"]},{"x":"The Adjuster is not a personality, yet it is a true reality of the purest order in the universe, a divine presence.","r":["107:7.1"]},{"q":"No Adjuster has ever been disloyal to the Paradise Father","r":"107:4.3"}]},{"h":"When and How It Comes","items":[{"x":"The Adjuster is assigned after the child makes its first moral choice, and on Urantia it arrives, on the average, just before the sixth birthday.","r":["108:2.1"]},{"x":"The preparation of the seven adjutant mind-spirits and the circuitizing of the Holy Spirit must come first before an Adjuster can enter the mind.","r":["108:2.2"]},{"x":"That a perfect Adjuster should volunteer to dwell in a mortal of animal origin is a marvel of divine condescension.","r":["108:6.1"]},{"q":"which came forth from God to find man and sonship him even in the days of the flesh.","r":"107:0.3"}]},{"h":"What the Adjuster Does","items":[{"x":"The basic mission of the Adjuster is to represent the Universal Father to the mortal creature, and indeed to be that Father.","r":["108:0.1"]},{"x":"The Adjuster comes with a plan for the ideal life, but man is free to accept or reject that plan.","r":["110:2.1"]},{"x":"It undertakes the difficult work of an interpreter, receiving counsel from spiritual intelligences and conveying it to the material mind.","r":["108:5.1"]},{"q":"only occasionally do you catch an echo, a faint and distant echo, of the divine voice.","r":"110:3.1"},{"x":"Unless the mind's capacity is wholly destroyed, the Adjuster stays with a person through every calamity and illness.","r":["110:1.5"]}]},{"h":"A Life of Co-operation with the Adjuster","items":[{"q":"The great goal of human existence is to attune to the divinity of the indwelling Adjuster;","r":"110:3.4"},{"x":"Mental poisons such as fear, anger, envy, and suspicion greatly retard the Adjuster's work, as bodily poisons do.","r":["110:1.5"]},{"x":"Confusion, discouragement, or ignorance alone does not prevent survival; only conscious resistance to the Adjuster's leading does.","r":["110:3.5"]},{"x":"When clouds gather, faith should accept the fact of the Adjuster's presence and look to the light beyond.","r":["108:6.8"]}]},{"h":"Fusion and Eternal Destiny","items":[{"x":"The Adjuster is the Father's love incarnate in the human soul, the essence of the finaliter personality foretasted in time.","r":["107:0.2"]},{"x":"Mastering the seven psychic circles is not fusion itself but the preparatory stage leading to fusion.","r":["110:6.1"]},{"q":"but fusion depends on yet other greater and more sublime spiritual achievements, upon the attainment of a final and complete attunement of the mortal will with the will of God as it is resident in the Thought Adjuster.","r":"110:7.1"},{"x":"The eternal union of the Adjuster with a perfected creature brings into being a unique creature that no other universe technique can produce.","r":["108:0.1"]}]}],"see":["Fusión con el Ajustador","Alma","Personalidad","Espíritus ayudantes de la mente","Voluntad de Dios","Supervivencia"]},{"n":70,"t":"Alegría y felicidad","en":"Joy and Happiness","sum":"True happiness comes from the inner life rather than from wealth or environment, and it is achieved when the selfish desires and the unselfish urges of the indwelling spirit are reconciled in one will. The highest happiness is inseparable from spiritual progress, and joy is experienced not alone but in sharing love and service. Jesus was not a man of sorrows but a man of gladness, and his peace is the joy and satisfaction of one who does the will of God.","sections":[{"h":"Where Happiness Comes From","items":[{"q":"La felicidad y el regocijo se originan en la vida interior. No puedes experimentar verdadero regocijo completamente solo. Una vida solitaria es fatal para la felicidad.","r":"111:4.7"},{"x":"Happiness is the sum of techniques for gratifying natural urges in better ways, and it does not depend greatly on environment.","r":["140:4.10"]},{"x":"Human happiness is achieved when the desires of the self and the unselfish urges of the higher self, the divine spirit, are coordinated in one will.","r":["103:5.5"]},{"x":"Health, mental efficiency, and happiness arise from the unification of body, mind, and spirit.","r":["100:4.3"]},{"q":"El esfuerzo no siempre produce el deleite, pero no hay felicidad sin esfuerzo inteligente.","r":"48:7.10"}]},{"h":"Spiritual Growth and Lasting Joy","items":[{"x":"The highest happiness is inseparable from spiritual progress, and spiritual growth yields lasting joy and a peace that passes understanding.","r":["100:4.3"]},{"x":"The Adjuster respects the value of selfish motives but gives weight to the unselfish urges that lead to happiness and the joys of the kingdom of heaven.","r":["103:2.7"]},{"x":"One born of the spirit is released from the bondage of self-denial and translated into the joyous kingdom of the spirit.","r":["143:2.8"]},{"q":"Science yields knowledge; religion yields happiness; philosophy yields unity","r":"101:2.8"},{"x":"There is an inherent joy in freewill existence independent of all external influences, and the angels of the joy of existence strive to demonstrate it.","r":["28:5.16"]}]},{"h":"Happiness as Jesus Taught It","items":[{"x":"The sermon on the beatitudes opened on the keynote of happiness, and its faith and love strengthen character and create happiness.","r":["140:5.6"]},{"x":"A child's happiness is immediate pleasure, but an adult sows seeds of self-denial for greater happiness.","r":["140:5.7"]},{"x":"Those who humbly seek God do not wait for distant rewards but experience the happiness of the kingdom in their hearts now.","r":["140:5.7"]},{"x":"Asked why some are happier than others, Jesus answered that much depends on willingness to be led by the Father's indwelling spirit.","r":["149:5.1","149:5.2"]},{"x":"Much sorrow comes from thwarted ambition and wounded pride, so after doing one's best one should accept one's lot and exercise ingenuity.","r":["149:5.3"]},{"q":"Seek not, then, for false peace and transient joy but rather for the assurance of faith and the sureties of divine sonship","r":"149:5.4"}]},{"h":"The Joy of Love and Service","items":[{"x":"The new commandment was meant not as a burden but as a new joy of sharing affection with one's fellows.","r":["180:1.2"]},{"q":"Si quieres compartir la felicidad del Maestro, debes compartir su amor.","r":"180:1.5"},{"x":"Jesus showed a fear-ridden young man the paths of service and the highways of happiness that lead to the joy of loving activity.","r":["130:6.2"]},{"x":"Loving service rendered with full affection becomes not a sacrifice but supreme joy.","r":["180:1.6"]},{"x":"After Pentecost the believers broke bread together with gladness and singleness of heart, enjoying the spiritual joy of the brotherhood's fellowship.","r":["194:4.3","190:5.4"]}]},{"h":"Jesus, a Man of Gladness","items":[{"q":"Este hombre de Galilea no fue hombre de sufrimientos; fue un alma de alegría.","r":"100:7.13"},{"x":"The peace of Jesus is neither stoic resignation nor vague optimism but the joy and satisfaction of one who has fully learned how to do the will of God.","r":["181:1.7","181:1.8"]},{"x":"The religion of Jesus does not flee from this life but ennobles present living with the joy and peace of a spiritual state of being.","r":["194:3.3"]},{"x":"Morontia life is about half work and half play, and it enjoys the humor of realizing how trivial many past worries were.","r":["48:4.1","48:4.6"]},{"x":"Jesus regarded this world not as a vale of tears but as a vale of soul making, where eternal spirits are born.","r":["149:5.5"]}]}],"see":["Miedo y preocupación","Servicio","Amor","Crecimiento","Reino del cielo","Religión personal"]},{"n":35,"t":"Alma","en":"Soul","sum":"The soul is a morontia reality newly arising from the relationship between the material mind and the indwelling Thought Adjuster, the child born of human effort and the divine spirit together. During the life in the flesh it grows like an embryo; it then survives death and becomes the new vehicle of personality on the mansion worlds. The growth of the soul depends on moral choices and the decision to seek God, and personality identity survives in the survival of the soul.","sections":[{"h":"How the Soul Comes into Being","items":[{"x":"When a mortal chooses to do the Father's will, the indwelling spirit becomes the father of a new reality and the material mind becomes its mother.","r":["0:5.10"]},{"x":"Three factors operate in making the soul: the human mind, the indwelling divine spirit, and the relationship between the two.","r":["111:2.4","111:2.5","111:2.6"]},{"q":"La realidad de esta relación singular no es ni material ni espiritual, sino morontial. Es el alma.","r":"111:2.7"},{"x":"The divine spirit arrives with the first moral activity of the human mind, and at that very moment the soul is born.","r":["133:6.5"]},{"x":"The morontia life of an ascending mortal actually begins at the moment the soul is conceived, when the Adjuster comes to indwell.","r":["48:6.2"]}]},{"h":"The Nature of the Soul","items":[{"x":"The midway creatures called this soul the \"midmind,\" meaning that it lies between the material mind and the cosmic mind.","r":["111:2.8"]},{"x":"The soul is the part that lifts man above the animal level, characterized by moral choice and the urge to know God and be like him.","r":["133:6.5"]},{"x":"Self-consciousness itself is not the soul; moral self-consciousness, as true self-realization, forms the foundation of the soul.","r":["133:6.5"]},{"x":"The soul cannot be proved by material investigation or by purely spiritual tests, yet the morally awakened mortal knows its reality by experience.","r":["133:6.7"]},{"q":"Desde sus comienzos más tempranos el alma es real; tiene cualidades cósmicas de sobrevivencia.","r":"16:9.2"},{"x":"The morontia soul is the child both of the Father's Adjuster action and of the cosmic reaction of the Supreme Being.","r":["117:6.5"]}]},{"h":"The Growth of the Soul","items":[{"x":"Mind is the human soil on which the Adjuster, with the co-operation of the personality, evolves the morontia soul.","r":["111:1.1"]},{"q":"The material mind of mortal man is the cosmic loom that carries the morontia fabrics","r":"111:2.2"},{"x":"The soul can grow regardless of cultural level, but not without the decision to choose survival and to do the Father's will.","r":["65:8.4"]},{"x":"Mistakes and errors may delay the evolution of the soul, but they cannot prevent the soul evolution that began with the consent of the will.","r":["111:3.1"]},{"q":"El alma del hombre no puede existir aparte del pensamiento moral y de la actividad espiritual. Un alma estancada es un alma moribunda.","r":"133:6.5"},{"x":"The more the soul is filled with truth, beauty, and goodness, the more indestructible the resulting being becomes.","r":["111:3.7"]}]},{"h":"The Soul and the Human Will","items":[{"x":"During life the deciding will resides in the material mind, but as the self grows, it becomes increasingly identified with the emerging morontia soul.","r":["111:3.2"]},{"q":"El alma, de este modo, es el embrión del futuro vehículo morontial de la identidad de la personalidad.","r":"111:3.2"},{"x":"By its own choice the mortal personality can transfer the seat of its identity from the transient material-intellect system to the morontia-soul system.","r":["112:5.4","112:2.20"]},{"q":"The faith-activated soul of man cannot stop short of the attainment of this goal of destiny;","r":"132:3.7"},{"x":"Whether a soul is saved or lost depends on whether moral consciousness gains survival value through eternal alliance with its immortal spirit endowment.","r":["133:6.6"]}]},{"h":"The Soul After Death","items":[{"q":"Esta entidad de nueva aparición es el alma, y sobrevive a la muerte tanto del cuerpo físico como de la mente material.","r":"112:5.12"},{"x":"From death until repersonalization the soul is wholly unconscious, in the keeping of the seraphic guardian of destiny.","r":["112:5.13"]},{"x":"In the resurrection halls the seraphim bestow the sleeping soul upon a new morontia form and unite it with the returning Adjuster.","r":["112:5.18","112:5.19"]},{"x":"If a mortal does not survive, the spiritual values of his experience remain in the Adjuster, but his identity does not survive.","r":["16:9.3"]},{"x":"The soul in the body is embryonic; it is born into the morontia life and grows through the mansion worlds.","r":["66:4.9"]},{"x":"The immortal soul is at first morontial but rises to true spirit levels and usually fuses with the spirit of the Father who started it.","r":["111:3.3"]}]},{"h":"Human Ideas About the Soul","items":[{"x":"Primitive man associated the soul with blood, breath, shadows, and reflections in water, or believed it dwelt in various organs of the body.","r":["111:0.3"]},{"x":"Early man took the other self of dreams to be the soul, and this idea led on to belief in nature spirits.","r":["86:5.1"]},{"x":"Hindu teachers, in the concept of the atman, almost discerned the Adjuster, but they failed to distinguish the co-evolving soul.","r":["111:0.4"]}]}],"see":["Ajustador del Pensamiento","Personalidad","Mente","Morontia","Supervivencia","Fusión con el Ajustador"]},{"n":60,"t":"Amor","en":"Love","sum":"\"God is love.\" In The Urantia Book love is the dominant characteristic of all God's personal dealings with his creatures, and it embraces truth, beauty, and goodness. The Father's love individualizes each person as an irreplaceable child and dwells within man through the Adjuster. Love is the desire to do good to others; it cannot be held captive and becomes real only when bestowed upon one's fellows. Jesus gave the new commandment to love one another \"as I have loved you.\"","sections":[{"h":"God Is Love","items":[{"x":"Because God is love, his only personal attitude toward the affairs of the universe is always a reaction of divine affection.","r":["2:5.1"]},{"x":"The love of God is not induced by sacrifice or intercession; the Father himself loves us.","r":["2:5.2"]},{"q":"Dios es amor, pero el amor no es Dios.","r":"2:5.10"},{"x":"The love of God is a farseeing parental affection that functions in unity with wisdom and sometimes includes discipline for our good.","r":["2:5.3","2:5.10"]},{"x":"Love is the dominant characteristic of all God's personal dealings with his creatures.","r":["2:5.12"]}]},{"h":"Manifestations of the Father's Love","items":[{"x":"The Father's love individualizes each personality as a unique child, eternally irreplaceable.","r":["12:7.9"]},{"x":"The greatest manifestation of divine love for mortals is the bestowal of the Adjusters, and its greatest revelation is the bestowal life of Michael.","r":["2:5.10"]},{"x":"The love and devotion an Adjuster gives to its subject is the most truly divine affection in all creation.","r":["110:0.2"]},{"x":"God is love and the Son is mercy; mercy is applied love, love in action.","r":["6:3.5"]},{"x":"We love God because we discern that he truly loves us; the experience of loving is a response to the experience of being loved.","r":["2:5.8"]},{"q":"El amor del Padre está con nosotros ahora y a través del círculo sin fin de las edades eternas.","r":"2:5.9"}]},{"h":"What Love Is","items":[{"q":"El amor es el deseo de hacer el bien a los demás.","r":"56:10.21"},{"x":"In its true sense, love, whether human or divine, connotes the mutual regard of whole personalities.","r":["112:2.7"]},{"q":"it cannot be created, manufactured, or purchased; it must grow.","r":"100:3.7"},{"x":"Love is born only of thoroughgoing understanding of a neighbor's motives and sentiments; one cannot love fellows by mere willpower.","r":["100:4.6"]},{"x":"Love must continually readapt its concept of the highest good of the one loved, under the guidance of the Spirit of Truth.","r":["180:5.10"]}]},{"h":"The Circuit of Love","items":[{"x":"All true love is from God, and man receives the divine affection as he bestows that love upon his neighbors.","r":["117:6.10"]},{"q":"El hombre no puede tomar jamás el amor del Padre y aprisionarlo en su corazón.","r":"117:6.10"},{"x":"The circuit of love proceeds from the Father, through sons to brothers, and thence to the Supreme.","r":["117:6.10"]},{"x":"Love is the soil of religious growth; love is the essence of religion and the wellspring of superior civilization.","r":["100:0.2","102:6.3"]}]},{"h":"Love as Jesus Revealed It","items":[{"x":"Jesus revealed a God of love, and that love embraces truth, beauty, and goodness.","r":["5:4.6"]},{"q":"El amor es la más grande de todas las realidades espirituales.","r":"143:1.4"},{"x":"Beyond the commandment to love one's neighbor as oneself, Jesus gave the new commandment: \"Love one another as I have loved you.\"","r":["180:1.1"]},{"x":"The new commandment is not a new burden but a new joy of sharing affection with one's fellows, and the greatest love is to lay down one's life for one's friends.","r":["180:1.2","180:1.3"]},{"x":"To share the Master's love is to share his service; that love does not make a new world but makes the old world new.","r":["180:1.5"]},{"x":"Advanced mortals on worlds settled in light and life have learned that love is the greatest thing in the universe and know that God is love.","r":["56:10.20"]}]}],"see":["Padre Universal","Misericordia","Servicio","Hermandad de los hombres","Bondad","Ajustador del Pensamiento"]},{"n":21,"t":"Ancianos de los Días","en":"Ancients of Days","sum":"Los Ancianos de los Días son veintiún gobernantes supremos originarios de la Trinidad del Paraíso que, en grupos de tres, gobiernan cada uno de los siete superuniversos. Solo ellos dictan los veredictos ejecutivos finales sobre la vida y la muerte eternas de las criaturas volitivas, y mediante la técnica de la reflectividad ven y oyen a la vez el Paraíso, arriba, y los universos locales, abajo. Son la cumbre del gobierno superuniversal que los mortales encuentran en su viaje de ascensión tras graduarse del universo local.","sections":[{"h":"Gobernantes procedentes de la Trinidad","items":[{"x":"Los Ancianos de los Días son la tercera de las siete órdenes de Personalidades Supremas de la Trinidad; su número es fijo y no se crean más.","r":["18:0.4","18:0.9"]},{"q":"Los Ancianos de los Días son todos básicamente idénticos; revelan el carácter combinado y la naturaleza unificada de la Trinidad.","r":"18:3.2"},{"x":"Los Siete Espíritus Rectores difieren en naturaleza, pero los Ancianos de los Días, aunque poseen individualidad, son descendientes uniformes y superperfectos de la Trinidad.","r":["18:3.2"]},{"x":"Los veintiuno fueron trinidizados al mismo tiempo, y la primera de todas las anotaciones de los registros de personalidad del Paraíso es el relato de su trinidización.","r":["18:3.4"]},{"q":"Representan el comienzo de los archivos de la personalidad del universo de universos, de aquí su nombre: Ancianos de los Días.","r":"18:3.4"},{"x":"Los seres de origen trinitario no corren peligro de fracaso ni de rebelión, y estos gobernantes nunca se han desviado del camino de la conducta perfecta de la personalidad.","r":["18:0.11"]}]},{"h":"El supergobierno regido por tres","items":[{"q":"Cada superuniverso está presidido por tres Ancianos de los Días, los ejecutivos jefes conjuntos del supergobierno.","r":"15:10.3"},{"x":"En la alta administración los tres actúan siempre juntos; aunque nunca abandonan su mundo sede central, la posición de este como foco del sistema de reflectividad hace que su gobierno no se vea obstaculizado.","r":["18:3.5"]},{"x":"Mientras que los Espíritus Rectores determinan la naturaleza de un superuniverso, los Ancianos de los Días determinan su administración, y aportan un gobierno uniforme a superuniversos por lo demás diferentes.","r":["18:3.3"]},{"x":"Les ayudan los Perfeccionadores de la Sabiduría, los Consejeros Divinos y los Censores Universales, así como Hijos Trinidizados procedentes de mortales ascendentes glorificados.","r":["15:10.11","15:10.12"]},{"x":"Las observaciones y recomendaciones reunidas por los gobernantes de los sectores mayores y menores ascienden paso a paso hasta llegar por fin a los tribunales de los Ancianos de los Días.","r":["15:13.6"]},{"q":"La sabiduría de originalidad y la iniciativa de individualidad caracterizan todos los decretos y dictámenes de los Ancianos de los Días.","r":"18:3.9"}]},{"h":"El juicio final de la vida y la muerte eternas","items":[{"x":"Son los más poderosos de los gobernantes directos de las creaciones espaciotemporales, y solo ellos tienen el poder de dictar sentencia final sobre la extinción eterna de las criaturas volitivas.","r":["18:3.7"]},{"q":"Los Hijos de los universos locales pueden decretar la sobrevivencia de un hombre mortal, pero sólo los Ancianos de los Días pueden sentarse en juicio ejecutivo de los asuntos de la vida y muerte eternas.","r":"15:12.2"},{"x":"Cuando el amor restaurador de los Hijos Creadores es rechazado definitivamente, la sentencia de extinción es ejecutada por fuerzas que están bajo su jurisdicción.","r":["2:3.6","2:3.3"]},{"q":"No hay desacuerdos ni opiniones minoritarias en los decretos de estos tribunales supremos y superlativos.","r":"15:12.3"},{"x":"No hay apelación contra los veredictos de un superuniverso, porque son la opinión unánime de los Ancianos de los Días y del Espíritu Rector que preside ese superuniverso.","r":["15:12.4"]},{"q":"Cuando los tres Ancianos de los Días actúan, la Trinidad del Paraíso actúa.","r":"19:3.5"},{"x":"Ellos y sus asociados de origen trinitario dictan los juicios justos de la equidad suprema en los siete superuniversos.","r":["10:6.17"]}]},{"h":"El gobierno reflectivo que todo lo ve y todo lo oye","items":[{"q":"the Ancients of Days from their position midway between the inhabited worlds and Paradise—between man and God—can instantly look both ways, hear both ways, and know both ways.","r":"28:4.1"},{"x":"Los seconafines primarios sirven de espejos vivientes, que reflejan ante ellos las mentes y las voces del Espíritu Infinito, de los Hijos Creadores y de las huestes angélicas.","r":["28:4.4","28:4.6","28:4.11"]},{"x":"Deducen la voluntad del Padre armonizando la voz del espíritu, que viene de arriba, con las voces de los Micaeles, que vienen de abajo, y como esto requiere a los tres juntos, un superuniverso siempre está presidido por tres.","r":["28:4.10"]},{"x":"Los superuniversos están aislados unos de otros, y la comunicación personal directa con los gobernantes de otro superuniverso debe pasar por los Mensajeros Solitarios.","r":["23:2.15","15:10.23"]}]},{"h":"Relación con los universos locales y el futuro","items":[{"x":"Un Hijo Creador se compromete ante la Trinidad a no asumir la plena soberanía hasta que sus siete autootorgamientos como criatura hayan sido certificados por los Ancianos de los Días.","r":["119:0.3"]},{"x":"No certifican a un Hijo Creador como soberano del universo hasta que haya vivido realmente como criatura y adquirido el punto de vista de la criatura.","r":["119:0.6"]},{"x":"A petición de Micael autorizaron la detención de las personalidades implicadas en la rebelión de Lucifer, y la disposición final de los archirrebeldes sigue en sus manos.","r":["53:9.3","53:9.6"]},{"x":"Como sus prerrogativas de gobierno no fueron adquiridas por experiencia, algún día serán reemplazados por el Ser Supremo, el soberano experiencial, y llegarán a ser sus vicegerentes.","r":["18:3.8"]},{"x":"El viaje del mortal para encontrar a Dios comienza con el Hijo Creador y prosigue, a través de los Ancianos de los Días y del Espíritu Rector del superuniverso, hasta el Padre Universal.","r":["0:8.9"]}]}],"see":["Trinidad del Paraíso","Los siete superuniversos","Dios el Séptuple","Ser Supremo","Siete Espíritus Rectores","Hijo Creador Micael"]},{"n":46,"t":"Ascensión mortal","en":"Mortal Ascension","sum":"The mortal ascension is the long road by which a human being of animal origin sets out from an evolutionary planet, passes through the mansion worlds and the morontia worlds of the local universe, the spirit training worlds of the superuniverse, and the central universe of Havona, and at last finds the Universal Father on Paradise and becomes a finaliter. The command \"Be you perfect, even as I am perfect\" is both the starting point and the goal of this journey, and the way must be walked step by step in experience.","sections":[{"h":"The Call to Be Perfect","items":[{"x":"The will creatures of all the universes have embarked on the eternal adventure of reaching God the Father, the long journey to Paradise.","r":["1:0.3"]},{"x":"Striving for the perfection of divinity should be the first duty and highest ambition of every creature.","r":["1:0.4"]},{"x":"Though man cannot be perfect in the infinite sense, he can fully attain the divine goal that God has set for him.","r":["1:0.5"]},{"q":"Esta sublime búsqueda del Dios de los universos es la aventura suprema de los habitantes de todos los mundos del tiempo y el espacio.","r":"1:0.6"}]},{"h":"An Outline of the Seven Stages","items":[{"x":"The ascending career is summed up in seven stages: planetary mortals, sleeping survivors, mansion world students, morontia progressors, superuniverse wards, Havona pilgrims, and Paradise arrivals.","r":["30:4.1","30:4.2","30:4.8"]},{"x":"For sleeping survivors the passing of time does not matter; one who has slept five thousand years awakens no differently from one who has rested five days.","r":["30:4.12"]},{"x":"Ascenders progress individually within a sphere, but between the stages of universe study they always move in classes.","r":["30:4.17"]},{"x":"Just before leaving the local universe they acquire true spirit identity, and from then on the ascender's status is forever settled.","r":["30:4.20","30:4.21"]}]},{"h":"Through the Local Universe and the Superuniverse","items":[{"x":"Passing from the mansion worlds through the spheres of the system, the constellation, and the universe headquarters, the ascender as a morontia progressor develops in intellect, spirit, and form.","r":["30:4.18","30:4.19"]},{"q":"La mente, la personalidad y el carácter son inalterados por dicho avance; tan sólo la forma sufre modificaciones.","r":"30:4.20"},{"x":"On the superuniverse training worlds the young spirits share what they have learned with others and master local universe and superuniverse administration.","r":["30:4.22","30:4.23","30:4.24"]},{"q":"No ha ocurrido nunca que los pupilos del superuniverso se descarrien.","r":"30:4.21"}]},{"h":"Havona and Paradise","items":[{"x":"The journey from superuniverse headquarters to Havona is always made alone, and the instruction of Havona is personal and individual.","r":["30:4.27"]},{"x":"The pilgrim arrives in Havona possessing only one perfection, perfection of purpose, and his faith has already been tested.","r":["26:4.13"]},{"q":"La habilidad para comprender es el pasaporte mortal al Paraíso. El deseo de creer es la llave de Havona.","r":"26:4.15"},{"x":"Attaining the Universal Father on the third circle of Havona, with the help of the Father guides, becomes the passport to eternity.","r":["26:9.1","26:9.2"]},{"x":"Residence on Paradise means that God has been found, and Father-fused mortals are mustered into the mortal Corps of the Finality.","r":["30:4.31"]},{"q":"On earth you were a creature of flesh and blood; through the local universe you were a morontia being; through the superuniverse you were an evolving spirit;","r":"30:4.26"}]},{"h":"The Purpose of the Journey and Beyond","items":[{"x":"Step by step, life by life, world by world, the ascending career is mastered and the goal of Deity is attained, and survival is completed in perfection.","r":["26:9.4"]},{"x":"Finaliters are recorded as spirits of the sixth stage, so a destiny of the unrevealed seventh stage still remains.","r":["31:3.3","31:3.5"]},{"x":"The long and tremendous training of the ascension must surely be designed to fit them for tests of greater trust and more sublime service.","r":["31:3.2","48:8.3"]},{"x":"The destinies of Adjuster-fused, Son-fused, and Spirit-fused mortals differ, but none is greater or lesser, for God loves all his sons alike.","r":["40:10.5","40:10.13"]},{"x":"Every facility and power is provided so that the Paradise goal of divine perfection may at last be attained.","r":["40:10.14"]},{"q":"La supervivencia es completa en perfección, y la perfección es pletórica en la supremacía de la divinidad.","r":"26:9.4"}]}],"see":["Mundos de estancia","Morontia","Cuerpo de la Finalidad","Havona","Paraíso","Búsqueda de la perfección"]},{"n":2,"t":"Atributos de Dios","en":"Attributes of God","sum":"Los atributos de Dios muestran cómo se relaciona el Padre infinito con su creación. Está presente en todas partes, es todopoderoso y lo sabe todo. Se otorga a sí mismo sin reservas y, sin embargo, en nada se ve disminuido, y gobierna por medio de sus Hijos reservándose la soberanía final. Todos estos atributos están unificados y coordinados en el amor y la sabiduría, la justicia y la misericordia.","sections":[{"h":"Creatividad y omnipresencia","items":[{"x":"La creatividad no es tanto un atributo como la totalidad de la naturaleza activa de Dios, que culmina en la verdad de la paternidad de Dios.","r":["3:0.3"]},{"x":"Solo Dios puede estar en innumerables lugares al mismo tiempo; está presente en todas las partes de su creación y en todos los corazones.","r":["3:1.1","3:1.2"]},{"q":"Dios se revela a través del cosmos, pero el cosmos no puede jamás contener o comprender la totalidad de la infinidad de Dios.","r":"3:1.2"},{"x":"Dios está presente de manera plenamente discernible solo en el Paraíso y en el universo central; en las creaciones exteriores limita su presencia directa por respeto a la soberanía de sus creadores coordinados.","r":["3:1.6"]},{"x":"La presencia efectiva del Padre en el hombre depende del grado en que su mente coopera con el Ajustador residente.","r":["3:1.11","3:1.12"]}]},{"h":"Poder infinito","items":[{"x":"La larga evolución de las razas, los planetas y los universos se despliega de manera ordenada según el propósito eterno del Padre, bajo el control de los creadores.","r":["3:2.2"]},{"x":"Considerado en los fenómenos no espirituales, Dios es energía; toda energía física procede de él y se mantiene dentro del control de gravedad del Paraíso bajo.","r":["3:2.3","3:2.4"]},{"q":"A pesar de su apariencia, el poder de Dios no funciona en el universo como una fuerza ciega.","r":"3:2.6"},{"x":"Los actos de Dios parecen a veces despiadados solo por la visión finita; todos ellos tienen por objeto el mayor bien de todos los interesados.","r":["3:2.8","3:2.10"]},{"x":"El poder de Dios solo está limitado por su naturaleza (amor, verdad, belleza y bondad), por su voluntad (misericordia) y por su ley (la justicia de la Trinidad).","r":["3:2.12","3:2.13","3:2.14"]}]},{"h":"Conocimiento universal","items":[{"x":"Dios es consciente de los pensamientos de toda la creación y es la única personalidad que conoce realmente el número de las estrellas y los planetas del espacio.","r":["3:3.1","3:3.2"]},{"x":"Su conocimiento se complementa mediante el circuito de personalidad que abarca a todas las personalidades, mediante los Hijos divinos descendentes y mediante los Ajustadores del Pensamiento residentes.","r":["3:3.3"]},{"x":"Aun cuando Dios conociera de antemano los actos de libre albedrío de sus hijos, esa presciencia no anula en modo alguno su libertad.","r":["3:3.4"]},{"q":"Una cosa es segura: A Dios no le sorprende nada.","r":"3:3.4"},{"x":"La omnipotencia no implica el poder de hacer lo que no es propio de Dios, y la omnisciencia no significa conocer lo incognoscible.","r":["3:3.5"]}]},{"h":"Infinitud sin disminución","items":[{"x":"Tras haberse otorgado sin reservas a sus Hijos y a su creación, el Padre en nada ve disminuido su potencial de poder, sabiduría y amor.","r":["3:4.1","3:4.3"]},{"x":"Aunque la creación continuara sin fin, el poder de control del Paraíso sería suficiente, y el Infinito seguiría colmado de la misma fuerza y energía.","r":["3:4.2"]},{"x":"El hombre no puede concebir plenamente la infinitud del Padre, pero puede experimentar realmente el impacto de su amor; la calidad de esa experiencia es ilimitada, mientras que su cantidad depende de la capacidad espiritual.","r":["3:4.6"]},{"q":"Por consiguiente el más próximo y más querido acceso a Dios es a través del amor, porque Dios es amor.","r":"3:4.7"}]},{"h":"Supremacía y primacía","items":[{"x":"Fuera de Havona, el Padre ejerce su poder por medio de sus Hijos y de las personalidades subordinadas a ellos, y solo actúa directamente cuando un agente delegado falla en su cometido.","r":["3:5.1","3:5.2"]},{"x":"En el corazón de los hombres la voluntad del Padre puede no cumplirse siempre, pero en el curso y el destino de un planeta prevalece el plan divino.","r":["3:5.3"]},{"x":"La adversidad, la desigualdad, la incertidumbre y la posibilidad de error son condiciones de vida necesarias para desarrollar cualidades como el valor, el altruismo, la esperanza y la fe.","r":["3:5.6","3:5.7","3:5.9"]},{"x":"El Padre delega la autoridad libremente, pero se reserva la decisión final y el veto sobre el bienestar y el destino de la creación.","r":["3:6.1"]},{"q":"La soberanía de Dios es ilimitada; es el acto fundamental de toda creación.","r":"3:6.2"}]},{"h":"Perfección, justicia y misericordia","items":[{"x":"Los planes y propósitos de la Primera Fuente y Centro son, como él mismo, eternos, perfectos e inmutables; aunque parezcan cambiar, el propósito subyacente no cambia.","r":["2:2.1","2:2.3"]},{"x":"La justicia del Padre no depende de la conducta de sus criaturas, y aun cuando les permite cosechar los resultados de sus malas acciones, siempre está templada por la misericordia.","r":["2:3.1","2:3.2"]},{"q":"La misericordia es simplemente justicia atemperada por esa sabiduría que proviene de la perfección del conocimiento y del pleno reconocimiento de la debilidad natural y las limitaciones ambientales de las criaturas finitas.","r":"2:4.1"},{"x":"Gracias a su sabiduría infinita, Dios otorga a la vez justicia y misericordia, y nunca se ve dividido por actitudes contradictorias hacia sus hijos.","r":["2:4.3"]}]}],"see":["Padre Universal","Personalidad de Dios","Misericordia","Justicia","Amor","Voluntad de Dios"]},{"n":84,"t":"Autootorgamiento de Jesús","en":"Bestowal of Jesus","sum":"The bestowal of Jesus is the event in which Michael, Creator Son of Nebadon, in his seventh and final bestowal, was born on Urantia as a mortal infant and lived a human life to its end. Through this bestowal Michael completed his universe sovereignty by experience and ended the Lucifer rebellion; above all, he revealed God to man and showed God a man made perfect. The Urantia Book stresses that the supreme purpose of the bestowal was to enhance the revelation of God.","sections":[{"h":"Seven Bestowals and Sovereignty Earned by Experience","items":[{"x":"A Creator Son must live the life of his creatures in their likeness, and this is part of the price paid for universe sovereignty.","r":["120:0.1"]},{"x":"After six bestowals, as a Melchizedek, a Lanonandek, an Adam, a seraphim, a mortal, and a morontia mortal, Michael became a mortal of flesh and blood on Urantia in his seventh.","r":["119:8.4","120:0.2"]},{"q":"Micael nació creador, fue instruido como administrador, capacitado como ejecutivo, pero se le exigió que ganara su soberanía por la experiencia.","r":"119:8.2"},{"x":"In each bestowal Michael subjected himself to a different will of the Paradise Deities, and on Urantia he submitted wholly to the will of the Universal Father.","r":["120:0.4","120:1.2"]},{"x":"The sum of the seven bestowals became Nebadon's new revelation of the Supreme Being and also contributed to expanding the sovereignty of the Supreme.","r":["119:8.3","119:8.5"]},{"x":"The Eternal Son shares creature experience through the incarnations of the Paradise Sons, and so in Michael he actually came to mortal man.","r":["7:5.3","7:5.4"]}]},{"h":"Immanuel's Charge","items":[{"x":"Unlike his earlier bestowals, Michael had to appear on Urantia not as a fully grown being but as a helpless infant.","r":["120:1.1"]},{"x":"Michael was to lay aside all extraplanetary help and live his mortal life relying only on the Paradise Father.","r":["120:1.3"]},{"q":"Throughout your Urantia bestowal you need be concerned with but one thing, the unbroken communion between you and your Paradise Father","r":"120:1.4"},{"x":"Immanuel advised him to be chiefly a teacher, first liberating man's spiritual nature, enlightening his mind, and freeing him from age-old fears.","r":["120:2.5"]},{"x":"He was also counseled not to become involved in economic and political matters, not to form an organized cult, and to leave no writings or portraits.","r":["120:3.4","120:3.6","120:3.7"]},{"x":"Since a bestowal Son leaves no human offspring on a planet, Jesus would not enter the marriage relation.","r":["120:3.8"]}]},{"h":"The Purposes of the Bestowal","items":[{"x":"One goal of the bestowal was, as the Son of Man, to formally terminate the Lucifer rebellion in Satania and be recognized as the Planetary Prince of Urantia.","r":["120:2.2","120:2.3"]},{"x":"His life was intended less as an example for the people of Urantia than as an inspiration for all generations in all of Nebadon.","r":["120:2.7"]},{"x":"He revealed the Father to the creatures of flesh and at the same time showed God a new revelation of man.","r":["120:2.8"]},{"x":"He was charged to pour out the Spirit of Truth at the end of his bestowal, so that all normal mortals would have immediate access to the ministry of the Adjusters.","r":["120:2.6"]},{"q":"No olvidéis jamás el hecho de que el fin espiritual supremo de la encarnación de Micael era el aumentar de la revelación de Dios.","r":"120:4.4"},{"x":"His life of self-forgetful service forever silenced those who had charged the Creators with selfishly holding on to power.","r":["120:4.1"]}]},{"h":"God and Man","items":[{"q":"No fue Dios en asociación con el hombre; más bien fue Dios encarnado en el hombre.","r":"120:4.2"},{"x":"Jesus did not gradually become God, nor did he become man at some moment; he was always God and man, and what grew was his awareness of that fact.","r":["120:4.2","120:4.3"]},{"x":"A bestowal in which a Paradise Son appears in the world by natural processes is the most fascinating of miracles even to local universe citizens.","r":["120:4.5","120:4.6"]}]},{"h":"A Full Human Life","items":[{"x":"Jesus passed through every stage of human life from infancy to death and personally experienced a wide range of emotions, from joy to deep sorrow.","r":["129:4.4","129:4.5"]},{"x":"He did not set a detailed example for all to copy but lived a truly human life so that each person could live his own life in his own time.","r":["129:4.7"]},{"x":"His life fully revealed God to man and offered God a perfected human personality, and it was wholly accepted by the Father.","r":["129:4.6"]},{"q":"Vino a la tierra para que se le manifestase la plenitud de Dios al hombre; ya se ha convertido casi en la perfección del hombre que aguarda la ocasión de manifestarse a Dios.","r":"129:4.8"},{"x":"At his baptism in the Jordan he was a perfected mortal at the height of mind mastery, and his Adjuster stood by him as a Personalized Adjuster instead of fusing.","r":["136:2.2","136:2.3"]}]},{"h":"The Completion of the Bestowal","items":[{"x":"Having completed the Urantia bestowal, Michael was recognized by the Ancients of Days and the Universal Father as the settled ruler of Nebadon.","r":["119:8.1"]},{"x":"Your little world has become known throughout Nebadon as the place where the Creator Son completed the experience required for sovereignty.","r":["119:8.2"]},{"q":"Con Jesús el universo produjo un hombre mortal en quien el espíritu del amor triunfó sobre las desventajas materiales del tiempo y trascendió el hecho del origen físico.","r":"195:10.2"}]}],"see":["Hijo Creador Micael","Carácter de Jesús","Enseñanzas de Jesús","Muerte en la cruz","Resurrección de Jesús","Rebelión de Lucifer"]},{"n":58,"t":"Belleza","en":"Beauty","sum":"Beauty, together with truth and goodness, is one of the three ways in which man comprehends divinity; it is the recognition of the harmonious unification of diverse realities. In the physical universe we see divine beauty, and its climax is the cosmic drama of man seeking God and God seeking man. Art and the appreciation of beauty become part of religion when they are linked with ethics and spiritual motivation, and Jesus valued the power of beauty to lead to worship.","sections":[{"h":"A Face of Divinity","items":[{"x":"Creatures can comprehend divinity as truth, beauty, and goodness.","r":["0:1.17"]},{"x":"In the physical universe one sees divine beauty, in the intellectual world one discerns truth, and goodness is found in religious experience.","r":["2:6.1"]},{"x":"The Father enjoys the response of divine beauty that Havona presents and delights in providing the evolving universes with patterns of harmony.","r":["14:6.8"]},{"x":"Even beauty and truth would be divorced from the hope of survival were they not attributes of a loving Father.","r":["1:7.3"]}]},{"h":"What Beauty Is","items":[{"x":"Beauty, or art, is largely a matter of the unification of contrasts, and diversity is essential to the concept of beauty.","r":["56:10.3"]},{"x":"Beauty is the intellectual recognition of the harmonious synthesis of the diversities of phenomenal reality, derived from eternal oneness.","r":["56:10.11"]},{"q":"The discernment of supreme beauty is the discovery and integration of reality","r":"2:7.8"},{"q":"The discernment of the divine goodness in the eternal truth, that is ultimate beauty.","r":"2:7.8"},{"x":"Universal beauty is the recognition of the reflection of the Isle of Paradise in the material creation.","r":["56:10.17"]},{"q":"La belleza, el ritmo, y la armonía están intelectualmente asociados y espiritualmente emparentados.","r":"44:7.2"}]},{"h":"The Climax of Universe Art","items":[{"x":"The climax of finite art is the drama of uniting the two poles of Creator and creature: man seeking God and God seeking man.","r":["56:10.3"]},{"q":"De aquí que el materialismo, el ateísmo, sea la maximación de la fealdad, la cúspide de la antítesis finita de lo bello.","r":"56:10.4"},{"x":"The existence of beauty implies the presence of an appreciative creature mind.","r":["56:10.11"]},{"x":"Cosmologic thinking is accompanied by curiosity toward harmony, aesthetic appreciation, and ethical sensitivity leading to God-consciousness.","r":["56:10.6","56:10.7","56:10.8"]}]},{"h":"Art and Religion","items":[{"x":"The search for beauty becomes part of religion only when it enriches ethical and moral concepts.","r":["101:9.4"]},{"q":"El arte es religioso tan sólo cuando está infundido de propósito que sea derivado de motivaciones espirituales elevadas.","r":"101:9.4"},{"x":"The high mission of all art is to foreshadow higher reality and to crystallize the emotions of time into the thought of eternity.","r":["48:7.23"]},{"x":"Art arises from the attempt to escape the lack of beauty in the material environment; it is a gesture toward the morontia level.","r":["196:3.30"]},{"x":"If truth, beauty, and goodness are not unified in the experience of the artist or philosopher, the expression lacks a true soul.","r":["44:7.3"]},{"x":"The celestial artists of the morontia worlds portray in art the divine beauty of the Paradise Creators.","r":["44:8.6"]}]},{"h":"Beauty and Jesus","items":[{"x":"Viewing Flavius's art treasures, Jesus said there was no reason to condemn the appreciation of the beauty of things created by the Father and fashioned by man.","r":["142:4.2","142:4.3"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that beauty has great value in leading to the worship impulse, especially in children.","r":["167:6.5"]},{"x":"The spirit that Jesus and the Father send is not only the spirit of truth but also the spirit of idealistic beauty.","r":["155:6.11"]},{"x":"The Hebrews based their religion on goodness and the Greeks on beauty, but the love Jesus revealed embraces truth, beauty, and goodness together.","r":["5:4.6","196:3.19"]},{"x":"The beauty of divine love, once fully admitted to the human heart, forever destroys the charm of sin and the power of evil.","r":["188:5.3"]},{"q":"De esta manera construye en ti y para ti galerías donde tienes en reserva belleza, bondad y grandeza artística.","r":"160:4.12"}]}],"see":["Verdad","Bondad","Amor","Adoración","Filosofía","Luz y vida"]},{"n":59,"t":"Bondad","en":"Goodness","sum":"Goodness, together with truth and beauty, is one of the three ways of comprehending divinity, but it is understood only in relation to personality. God's primal perfection consists in the perfection of the goodness inherent in his nature, and that goodness is fully revealed only in personal religious experience. For man, goodness is always relative and growing, more a quest than a possession until Paradise is attained. The goodness of God leads people to repentance.","sections":[{"h":"The Goodness of God","items":[{"q":"La perfección primordial de Dios no consiste en una rectitud asumida sino más bien en la perfección inherente de la bondad de su naturaleza divina.","r":"2:2.5"},{"q":"La bondad de Dios descansa en el fondo del libre albedrío divino: la tendencia universal al amor, a mostrar misericordia, a manifestar paciencia y a ministrar el perdón.","r":"2:6.9"},{"x":"God is supremely great and good, and greatness and goodness are inseparably one in him.","r":["28:6.21"]},{"x":"The infinite goodness of the Father is beyond the finite mind's comprehension and is discerned only by contrast with relative imperfection.","r":["4:3.6"]},{"x":"God the Supreme is truth, beauty, and goodness, for these concepts are the finite maximum of ideational experience.","r":["117:1.7"]}]},{"h":"Goodness in Personality and Religion","items":[{"x":"Truth and beauty may be conceived without personality, but divine goodness is understood only in relation to personality.","r":["1:7.3"]},{"x":"The goodness of God is found only in the spiritual world of personal religious experience, and religion is essentially faith-trust in that goodness.","r":["2:6.1"]},{"q":"Man might fear a great God, but he trusts and loves only a good God.","r":"2:6.1"},{"x":"Goodness is the mind's recognition of the relative values of the levels of divine perfection, and it implies a moral mind that discriminates between good and evil.","r":["56:10.12"]},{"x":"Goodness embraces ethics, morality, and religion, the craving for experiential perfection.","r":["56:10.10"]}]},{"h":"Goodness Is Relative and Growing","items":[{"x":"Good and evil are words denoting relative levels of human comprehension of the observable universe.","r":["132:2.2"]},{"x":"One should not take social custom or religious tradition as the standard of goodness but choose the good by the spiritual standards set by the indwelling spirit.","r":["132:2.2"]},{"x":"Experience is good when it heightens the appreciation of beauty, strengthens the moral will, and enlarges the capacity to love and serve one's fellows.","r":["132:2.5"]},{"q":"Hasta que alcances los niveles del Paraíso, la bondad será siempre más una búsqueda que una posesión, más una meta que una experiencia de logro.","r":"132:2.8"},{"x":"As one ascends the universe scale, goodness increases and evil diminishes, and on Paradise goodness is no longer contrastive but perfect.","r":["132:2.6","132:2.9"]},{"q":"La bondad es viviente, relativa, siempre progresiva, invariablemente una experiencia personal y sempiternamente correlacionada con el discernimiento de la verdad y de la belleza.","r":"132:2.7"}]},{"h":"Goodness and the Possibility of Evil","items":[{"x":"The possibility of evil is necessary to moral choosing, but actual evil need not exist.","r":["132:2.10"]},{"x":"The presence of good and evil in the world is proof of the reality of personality, with a moral will that chooses between them.","r":["132:2.8"]},{"x":"Spiritual evolution is an experience of increasingly choosing the good, with a corresponding decrease in the potential of evil.","r":["132:3.8"]},{"x":"No good deed is ever wholly lost; it remains forever effective in proportion to the divinity of its motivation.","r":["48:6.7"]}]},{"h":"How Goodness Leads Men","items":[{"q":"La bondad de Dios conduce al arrepentimiento; la beneficencia de Dios conduce al servicio; la misericordia de Dios conduce a la salvación; mientras que el amor de Dios conduce a la adoración inteligente y espontánea.","r":"149:6.4"},{"x":"Goodness without graciousness commands respect but repels affection; only when it is gracious is it universally attractive.","r":["171:7.2"]},{"x":"Righteousness of conduct must be judged by motives, so the highest goodness is unconscious.","r":["170:3.9"]},{"x":"An isolated morality that overemphasizes goodness while excluding truth and neglecting beauty fails to hold many modern minds.","r":["2:7.9"]},{"x":"All true goodness, whether personal morality, social fairness, or divine ministry, is equally true and beautiful.","r":["2:7.11"]}]}],"see":["Verdad","Belleza","Mal","Moralidad","Amor","Padre Universal"]},{"n":100,"t":"Búsqueda de la perfección","en":"Quest for Perfection","sum":"The Father's command, \"Be you perfect, even as I am perfect,\" is an invitation calling every creature of time and space to the long and fascinating ascent toward Paradise. Urantia mortals cannot attain perfection in the infinite sense, but it is entirely possible for them to reach divine perfection on their own level. This journey begins with the hunger for perfection that the Adjuster awakens, passes through Havona to the Father bearing a perfection of purpose forged by faith, and continues beyond into the finaliter career.","sections":[{"h":"The Command to Be Perfect","items":[{"x":"The will creatures of all the universe have embarked on the eternal adventure of attaining God the Father, the long, long journey to Paradise.","r":["1:0.3"]},{"x":"The effort to achieve the perfection of divinity should be the first duty and the highest ambition of every struggling creature.","r":["1:0.4"]},{"x":"Mortals cannot be perfect in the sense of infinity, but it is entirely possible for them, from their starting point, to reach the divine goal God has set.","r":["1:0.5"]},{"q":"Esta sublime búsqueda del Dios de los universos es la aventura suprema de los habitantes de todos los mundos del tiempo y el espacio.","r":"1:0.6"},{"x":"The Eternal Son, together with the Father, broadcast this command to all creation, and it has motivated every survival plan and bestowal plan.","r":["7:5.1"]}]},{"h":"The Hunger for Perfection","items":[{"x":"The indwelling Adjuster unfailingly arouses in man's soul a searching hunger for perfection, which can be satisfied only by communion with God.","r":["102:1.6"]},{"q":"El alma hambrienta del hombre se niega a satisfacerse con algo que sea menos que la realización personal del Dios vivo.","r":"102:1.6"},{"x":"The names of Andon and Fonta, the first parents of mankind, mean the first creatures to show the longing for human perfection.","r":["63:0.3"]},{"x":"Spiritual progress rests on the recognition of spiritual poverty, the hunger for perfection, the desire to be like God, and the purpose to do the Father's will.","r":["100:2.1"]},{"x":"The cosmic tension arising as all creatures and Creators together pursue divine perfection is resolved in the Supreme Being.","r":["116:7.6"]}]},{"h":"The Meaning of an Imperfect World","items":[{"x":"Courage requires an environment of hardship, altruism of inequality, and hope of uncertainty.","r":["3:5.6","3:5.7","3:5.8"]},{"x":"Faith grows where more can always be believed than known, and loyalty amid the possibility of disloyalty.","r":["3:5.9","3:5.12"]},{"x":"Had the Father made all mortals perfect from the start, he would have deprived them of the adventure and training of the long, gradual ascent.","r":["32:3.11"]},{"x":"The perfection that creatures of time finally attain is a true personal possession gained through personal effort.","r":["32:3.9"]}]},{"h":"Perfection of Purpose and Faith","items":[{"x":"On arriving in Havona the pilgrim brings only one perfection, perfection of purpose.","r":["26:4.12","26:4.13"]},{"x":"Faith has won perfection of purpose, and now the pilgrim must develop perfection of understanding.","r":["26:4.14"]},{"q":"La habilidad para comprender es el pasaporte mortal al Paraíso.","r":"26:4.15"},{"x":"Long before reaching Havona, ascenders have learned to feast upon uncertainty and to fatten upon disappointment.","r":["26:5.3"]},{"q":"«Juntamente con Dios, nada —absolutamente nada— es imposible».","r":"26:5.3"}]},{"h":"Havona and Attaining the Father","items":[{"x":"After the brief test on Urantia, the morontia stages of the mansion worlds and the local universe, and spiritual training in the superuniverse, the pilgrim goes to Havona.","r":["14:5.1"]},{"x":"In the circuits of Havona ascenders progress inward, coming to comprehend in turn God the Supreme, the Infinite Spirit, and the Eternal Son.","r":["26:6.2","26:8.1"]},{"x":"Those who fail in Deity attainment are comforted and try again; their disappointment differs only in magnitude from many experiences in rising from chaos to glory.","r":["26:10.2"]},{"x":"Attaining the Universal Father is the passport to eternity, and it forever demonstrates the justice of the command to be perfect.","r":["26:9.2","26:9.3"]},{"q":"La prueba del tiempo está casi concluida; la carrera de la eternidad se ha corrido casi por entero.","r":"26:9.3"}]},{"h":"The Endless Journey","items":[{"q":"Nosotros los de Uversa no sabemos el «destino de la finalidad» de los mortales ascendentes del tiempo.","r":"31:3.2"},{"x":"Finaliters are recorded only as spirits of the sixth stage, suggesting that yet another stage lies before them.","r":["31:3.3"]},{"x":"Even the splendid development of worlds settled in light and life is only the first stage of an endless ascending career.","r":["55:6.7"]},{"x":"Though his body came from the dust, man, if he truly wills it, will become a child of God the Supreme and a divine son of the Paradise Father.","r":["112:7.19"]}]}],"see":["Ascensión mortal","Havona","Cuerpo de la Finalidad","Crecimiento","Fe","Padre Universal"]},{"n":77,"t":"Caligastia","en":"Caligastia","sum":"Caligastia was the Planetary Prince who came to Urantia some five hundred thousand years ago, a Lanonandek Son of rich experience and a brilliant career, who joined the Lucifer rebellion and betrayed the world entrusted to him. His apostasy isolated Urantia from the universe circuits, sixty members of the planetary staff followed him, and the culture of Dalamatia collapsed. He later entrapped Adam and Eve, and after Jesus defeated him on Mount Hermon he lost the power to invade the minds of men.","sections":[{"h":"A Brilliant Planetary Prince","items":[{"x":"Caligastia was a secondary Lanonandek Son with rich experience in the administration of the local universe and of Satania.","r":["66:1.1"]},{"x":"Lucifer promoted him to his personal staff, and he had long sought appointment as a Planetary Prince.","r":["66:1.2","66:1.3"]},{"x":"He had a record of loyalty and devotion, but also a restless temperament and a tendency to oppose the established order.","r":["66:1.4"]},{"q":"Ningún príncipe de los planetas se había embarcado jamás en una carrera de autoridad mundial con experiencias preparatorias más ricas ni con perspectivas mejores que las de Caligastia en aquel memorable día hace medio millón de años.","r":"66:1.5"},{"x":"He arrived about five hundred thousand years ago, when the Sangik races were appearing, and set up his headquarters in the Mesopotamian region.","r":["66:0.2"]}]},{"h":"Dalamatia and the One Hundred","items":[{"x":"His associate assistant, Daligastia, headed the staff, and one hundred volunteers chosen from Jerusem formed the corporeal staff.","r":["66:2.2","66:2.4"]},{"x":"The Life Carriers transplanted the life plasm of one hundred male and female descendants of Andon and Fonta into the material bodies of the staff.","r":["66:2.6","66:2.7"]},{"x":"The Dalamatian revelation, the first teaching of the staff, lasted more than three hundred thousand years until it was interrupted by secession.","r":["92:4.5"]}]},{"h":"Betrayal and Isolation","items":[{"x":"At Satan's visit in the three hundred thousandth year of his rule, Caligastia agreed to betray the planet once the rebellion was proclaimed.","r":["67:1.1","67:1.2"]},{"q":"De todas las formas de la maldad, ninguna destruye más la condición de la personalidad que la traición de un encargo y la deslealtad a los amigos de confianza.","r":"67:1.3"},{"x":"Daligastia proclaimed Caligastia \"God of Urantia,\" and at that moment the system circuits were cut and Urantia was isolated.","r":["67:2.3","67:2.4"]},{"x":"Van declared this tantamount to planetary rebellion and protested, and after a struggle of more than seven years the loyalists were vindicated.","r":["67:2.2","67:2.6"]},{"x":"Forty members of the staff refused to rebel; the sixty who rebelled chose Nod as their leader and were reduced to mortal status.","r":["67:3.2","67:4.2"]}]},{"h":"Consequences of the Rebellion","items":[{"q":"Caligastia, con máxima inteligencia y vastas experiencias en los asuntos del universo, se descarrió —abrazó el pecado.","r":"67:3.9"},{"x":"Amadon, of lesser intellect, remained loyal to the end, showing that loyalty counts more than intelligence in spiritual choice.","r":["67:3.8","67:3.9"]},{"x":"His plan to rebuild society at once on his ideas of personal and group liberty failed, plunging the world into deeper confusion.","r":["67:5.3"]},{"x":"One hundred and sixty-two years after the rebellion, Dalamatia sank beneath the sea.","r":["67:5.4"]},{"x":"Afterward twelve Melchizedek receivers administered the planet, and Van established outposts of civilization throughout the world.","r":["67:6.5","67:6.6"]}]},{"h":"From the Days of Adam to the Days of Jesus","items":[{"x":"Caligastia and Daligastia hindered the preparation of the Garden of Eden and confused its inhabitants with teachings of unbridled liberty.","r":["73:2.5","74:5.6"]},{"q":"Caligastia sí logró atrapar a Adán y Eva, pero no logró su objetivo de dirigirlos en rebelión abierta contra el gobierno del universo.","r":"75:7.7"},{"x":"Serapatatia, though well-meaning, never realized that he was playing into the hands of Caligastia and Daligastia.","r":["75:3.6"]},{"x":"Jesus met Caligastia alone on Mount Hermon and prevailed, after which Caligastia's apostasy was virtually settled.","r":["134:8.6","134:8.9","136:3.1"]},{"x":"Before leaving Urantia, Michael offered mercy to Caligastia and Daligastia, but they rejected his offer.","r":["53:8.6"]},{"q":"he has absolutely no power to enter the minds of men, neither can he draw near to their souls to tempt or corrupt them unless they really desire to be cursed with his wicked presence.","r":"53:8.6"},{"q":"Caligastia ha sido comparativamente impotente a partir de la cruz de Cristo.","r":"53:8.9"}]}],"see":["Rebelión de Lucifer","Urantia","Adán y Eva","Seres intermedios","Maquiventa Melquisedek","Civilización"]},{"n":85,"t":"Carácter de Jesús","en":"Character of Jesus","sum":"In The Urantia Book's portrayal of the character of Jesus, the most distinctive feature is not so much flawlessness as symmetry, the exquisite and balanced unification of all his qualities. He was enthusiastic but never fanatical, courageous but never foolhardy, full of gladness yet humble. At the center stood a childlike trust in God and a deep love for people, and he asked his followers not so much to believe in him as to believe with him.","sections":[{"h":"Balance and Unity","items":[{"q":"La característica singular de la personalidad del Maestro era, no tanto su perfección, como su simetría, su exquisita y equilibrada unificación.","r":"100:7.1"},{"x":"An ordinary mortal cannot attain Jesus' perfection of character, but it is altogether possible to develop a strong and unified personality along the lines of his.","r":["100:7.1"]},{"x":"He was emotional but not flighty, sympathetic but not sentimental, pious but not sanctimonious.","r":["100:7.4"]},{"x":"His plans were marked by consecrated common sense, with nothing queer, erratic, or hysterical about them.","r":["100:7.3"]},{"x":"As a perfectly unified personality, Jesus still today unifies human experience and simplifies life.","r":["100:7.18"]},{"q":"Jesús fue grande porque era bueno; sin embargo, fraternizó con los niñitos.","r":"100:7.17"}]},{"h":"Sincerity and Courage","items":[{"x":"He was free from affectation and hypocrisy and lived as he taught, staying true to the truth even when his sincerity brought him suffering.","r":["100:7.2"]},{"x":"He was frank but always kind; he hated sin but loved the sinner, and in all his honesty he was fair.","r":["100:7.11"]},{"q":"Su valor era magnífico, pero nunca fue temerario. Su palabra clave era: «No temáis».","r":"100:7.15"},{"x":"Even when urged, he did not hurry, saying his hour had not yet come; when indignant at evil, his anger was never directed at the sinner.","r":["100:7.14"]},{"x":"He did not seek popular support and was not swayed by people's opinions; he was brave but never proud.","r":["161:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Gladness and Kindness","items":[{"q":"Este hombre de Galilea no fue hombre de sufrimientos; fue un alma de alegría.","r":"100:7.13"},{"x":"He was not a blind optimist, but out of trust in God and confidence in man he always encouraged others to be of good cheer.","r":["100:7.9"]},{"x":"Jesus was a child of joy and a man of rare humor, and at the same time a man acquainted with sorrow.","r":["129:4.4"]},{"x":"Graciousness is the aroma of friendliness from a love-saturated soul, and Jesus spread that gladness wherever he went.","r":["171:7.1","171:7.2"]},{"x":"He was always generous, repeating that it is more blessed to give than to receive, but he was never wasteful or extravagant.","r":["100:7.10"]}]},{"h":"His Way with People","items":[{"x":"Because Jesus truly understood people, he showed genuine sympathy, yet he never indulged in pity or fostered their self-pity.","r":["171:7.3"]},{"x":"He never hurried and comforted people \"as he passed by\"; they felt they were consulting with him rather than confessing to him.","r":["171:7.5"]},{"x":"He did not try to direct or manage people, and those who received his smile felt their power to solve their own problems increase.","r":["171:7.6"]},{"x":"Great things happened because people not only believed in him but he also believed greatly in them.","r":["171:7.8"]},{"q":"Era literalmente verdad, «caminaba haciendo el bien».","r":"171:7.9"},{"x":"The apostles remembered him as a loyal friend who treated all with equal kindness without flattery, and who loved even sinners and enemies.","r":["161:2.3"]}]},{"h":"Childlike Faith","items":[{"x":"Jesus' faith was not tradition or intellectual belief but wholly personal and spiritual, born of experience with the indwelling Adjuster.","r":["196:0.1","196:0.5"]},{"x":"He did not hold faith as a consolation in hardship but enjoyed it as the serenity and thrill of living in the Father's presence.","r":["196:0.3"]},{"q":"Jesús confiaba en Dios como un niño confía en su padre.","r":"196:0.11"},{"x":"His strong faith never turned into fanaticism and was always in harmony with balanced judgment about family love, social obligation, and economic necessity.","r":["196:0.6","196:0.7"]},{"x":"His sublime self-forgetfulness shows in his reply when called good teacher: \"Why do you call me good?\"","r":["196:0.9"]}]},{"h":"What It Means to Follow Him","items":[{"x":"Jesus did not ask his disciples to believe in him but to believe with him in the love of God.","r":["196:0.13"]},{"x":"To follow Jesus means to share his faith and to take part in his spirit of unselfish service to men.","r":["196:1.3"]},{"x":"A great service of this revelation will be to bring back the living Jesus, the human Jesus buried in theological tradition.","r":["196:1.1","196:1.2"]}]}],"see":["Autootorgamiento de Jesús","Enseñanzas de Jesús","Fe","Amor","Alegría y felicidad","Los doce apóstoles"]},{"n":73,"t":"Ciencia y religión","en":"Science and Religion","sum":"Science explores the world of facts and energy-matter by reason, and religion experiences values and spiritual realities by faith. They are independent domains starting from different postulates; philosophy seeks to coordinate them, and revelation affirms that the First Cause of science and the saving God of religion are one and the same. Science purifies religion by clearing away superstition, and religion gives the impulse of brotherhood by which the civilization of a scientific age can live together.","sections":[{"h":"Two Different Domains","items":[{"q":"La ciencia trata de los hechos; la religión se preocupa tan sólo de los valores.","r":"101:5.2"},{"q":"La razón es el método de la ciencia; la fe es el método de la religión; la lógica es la técnica intentada de la filosofía.","r":"101:2.2"},{"x":"Science assumes without proof the reality of matter, motion, and life; religion assumes mind, spirit, and the Supreme.","r":["103:7.11","103:7.10"]},{"q":"Las certidumbres de la ciencia proceden enteramente del intelecto; las certidumbres de la religión surgen de los cimientos mismos de la entera personalidad.","r":"102:1.4"},{"x":"In science the idea precedes its expression, but in religion the experience of realization precedes the expression of the idea.","r":["102:3.13"]}]},{"h":"Different Eyes for Seeing God","items":[{"x":"God is to science a cause, to philosophy an idea, and to religion a person, the loving heavenly Father.","r":["1:6.2","4:4.7"]},{"x":"The existence of God can never be proved by scientific experiment or pure logic; it is realized only in human experience.","r":["1:2.7","101:10.6"]},{"x":"Reason may reach a First Cause by studying nature, but faith is needed to transform it into a God of salvation.","r":["101:2.3"]},{"x":"Revelation affirms that the First Cause of science and the saving God of religion are the same Deity.","r":["101:2.7"]},{"x":"In science God is a possibility, in philosophy a probability, and in religion a certainty.","r":["102:6.8"]}]},{"h":"A Relationship of Mutual Help","items":[{"q":"Y la ciencia también estabiliza a la filosofía a través de la eliminación del error, mientras que purifica la religión en destruir la superstición.","r":"81:6.10"},{"x":"Evolutionary religion must be continually refined by the censorship of revelation and in the crucible of true science.","r":["92:3.10","99:3.7"]},{"x":"Science enables man to control his physical environment, and religion gives the impulse of brotherhood that lets people live together in the complex civilization of a scientific age.","r":["103:7.9"]},{"x":"Both science and religion need more searching and fearless self-criticism, and teachers in both fields are often too dogmatic.","r":["103:7.7"]},{"x":"Harmonizing the discoveries of science with the insights of religion requires a sincere desire to follow truth wherever it leads.","r":["103:7.5"]}]},{"h":"Coordinating Philosophy and Revelation","items":[{"x":"Science discovers the material world, religion evaluates it, and philosophy seeks to interpret meanings by coordinating both viewpoints.","r":["103:7.15"]},{"x":"Harmonizing science and religion is difficult because of ignorance of the intervening domain of morontia; the morontia viewpoint removes the difference.","r":["103:6.7"]},{"x":"Metaphysics is man's earnest but futile attempt to compensate for the absence of the morontia mota.","r":["103:6.7"]},{"x":"Revelation does not originate science or religion; its function is to coordinate both with the truth of reality.","r":["103:7.8"]},{"x":"True revelation never renders science unnatural, religion unreasonable, or philosophy illogical.","r":["101:2.2","102:3.15"]}]},{"h":"Beyond the Materialistic Age","items":[{"x":"The statements on physical science in revelatory papers will soon need revision, and their cosmology is not inspired.","r":["101:4.2"]},{"q":"Cuanta más sepas de ciencia, menos podrás estar seguro; cuanta más religión tengas, más seguro estarás.","r":"102:1.3"},{"x":"Scientists unintentionally plunged mankind into a materialistic panic, but the religion of Jesus has never become bankrupt.","r":["195:6.1"]},{"x":"What science has destroyed is only childish illusions born of mistaken interpretations; true religion remains untouched.","r":["195:6.4"]},{"q":"Facts never quarrel with real spiritual faith; theories may.","r":"195:7.1"}]}],"see":["Filosofía","Revelación","Verdad","Fe","Experiencia religiosa","Morontia"]},{"n":82,"t":"Civilización","en":"Civilization","sum":"Civilization is a racial acquirement that mankind won through a long and arduous struggle, starting from a state close to the animal. Because it is not passed on automatically by heredity, each generation must hand it on anew through the home and education. The Urantia Book examines one by one the material, intellectual, and social factors that sustain civilization, yet it says that the power that truly lifts culture is spiritual idealism.","sections":[{"h":"Civilization, an Acquired Heritage","items":[{"q":"Civilization is a racial acquirement; it is not biologically inherent","r":"68:0.2"},{"x":"Scientific, philosophic, and religious achievements are not inherited; they are kept only by wisely conserving social inheritance and educating each generation anew.","r":["68:0.2"]},{"x":"Biologic evolution and cultural civilization do not necessarily go together, but culture cannot flourish without a background of adequate racial progress.","r":["81:5.1"]},{"x":"Even though the missions of Caligastia and Adam failed, evolution kept the races moving forward; evolution may be delayed but it cannot be stopped.","r":["81:0.1"]},{"x":"The slogan \"back to nature\" is an ignorant delusion based on belief in a golden age that never existed.","r":["68:1.7"]}]},{"h":"How Society Arose","items":[{"x":"Primitive man was not naturally brotherly; through bitter experience he learned that to survive he must unite, and so he cooperated reluctantly.","r":["68:1.1","68:1.4"]},{"x":"Civilization became man's insurance against violent death, and man pays the premium by submitting to society's mores.","r":["68:1.2","81:5.4"]},{"x":"Hunger, sex love, vanity, and fear of ghosts drew people together and bound them into society.","r":["68:2.4","68:2.6"]},{"q":"Casi todo lo que es de valor duradero en la civilización tiene sus raíces en la familia.","r":"68:2.8"},{"x":"The one hundred of Dalamatia did not try to change the primitive races all at once but trained the best of the tribes and sent them back as emissaries of social uplift.","r":["66:6.3","66:6.4"]},{"x":"The chief purpose of the Material Sons and Daughters is to move evolving man from the hunting and herding stages to the agricultural stage.","r":["52:3.3"]}]},{"h":"Factors Sustaining Civilization","items":[{"x":"Factors such as the natural environment, capital goods, scientific knowledge, human resources, language, machines, and the coordination of experts sustain present civilization.","r":["81:6.2","81:6.3","81:6.29"]},{"q":"La cultura jamás se ha desarrollado bajo condiciones de pob reza; el tiempo libre es esencial para el progreso de la civilización.","r":"81:6.6"},{"x":"Science stabilizes philosophy by eliminating error and purifies religion by destroying superstition.","r":["81:6.10"]},{"x":"A common language promotes peace and insures culture, and international exchange in language, trade, art, science, and religion should be encouraged.","r":["81:6.18","81:6.19"]},{"x":"Science guided by wisdom can liberate mankind, but it becomes a calamity for nations lacking the wisdom to adjust the transitional problems of mechanization.","r":["81:6.22"]}]},{"h":"Ideals, Education, and Leadership","items":[{"x":"The basic institution for passing the torch of culture to the next generation is the home, followed by play, social life, and the school.","r":["81:6.23","81:6.24"]},{"q":"Los ideales de una generación forjan la ruta del destino para la posteridad inmediata.","r":"81:6.26"},{"x":"Intelligence controls the machinery of civilization and wisdom directs it, but the energy that lifts culture from level to level is spiritual idealism.","r":["81:6.27"]},{"q":"At first life was a struggle for existence; now, for a standard of living; next it will be for quality of thinking","r":"81:6.28"},{"x":"High civilization is born when material wealth, intellectual greatness, moral worth, social cleverness, and cosmic insight are wisely coordinated.","r":["81:6.38"]},{"x":"Civilization is jeopardized only when able and wise leadership disappears, and such leadership has never exceeded one per cent of the population.","r":["81:6.37","81:6.42"]}]},{"h":"Duties and Dangers of Civilization","items":[{"x":"Cultural society is not a club of free memberships but a union of workers making a better world for their descendants.","r":["81:5.3"]},{"x":"Every right is linked with social obligation, and liberty that accepts collective regulation is the legitimate goal of social evolution.","r":["81:5.6","81:5.7"]},{"q":"La autoconservación origina la sociedad, en tanto que la autogratificación excesiva destruye la civilización.","r":"68:2.2"},{"x":"Society is not a divine institution but a phenomenon of evolution, so it may be experimented with fearlessly, but great changes should not be attempted suddenly.","r":["81:6.39","81:6.40"]},{"x":"Modern civilization has grown intellectually and scientifically but has stagnated in ethical awareness, spiritual development, and the safeguarding of the home.","r":["81:6.25"]}]},{"h":"Civilization and Religion","items":[{"x":"Religion renders its highest social service when least entangled with secular institutions, and it should not directly engage in building a new order or preserving the old.","r":["99:0.1","99:0.2"]},{"x":"As civilization advances, the attitude of seeking first heavenly realities becomes all the more necessary, even amid efforts to solve material problems.","r":["195:5.1"]},{"x":"Modern culture must become spiritually baptized with a new revelation of Jesus' life.","r":["195:10.1"]}]}],"see":["Gobierno y sociedad","Matrimonio y familia","Razas","Evolución","Ciencia y religión","Adán y Eva"]},{"n":16,"t":"Constelaciones y sistemas locales","en":"Constellations and Local Systems","sum":"Un universo local se divide en cien constelaciones, y cada constelación en cien sistemas locales. La constelación, gobernada por los Altísimos de la orden Vorondadek, es una unidad legislativa que socializa a los mortales ascendentes en sedes centrales como Edentia; el sistema local, gobernado por un Soberano del Sistema de la orden Lanonandek, es una unidad ejecutiva que recibe en Jerusem y en los mundos de estancia a los mortales recién sobrevivientes. Urantia pertenece al sistema de Satania, en la constelación de Norlatiadek, y ha recibido un cuidado especial desde la rebelión de Lucifer.","sections":[{"h":"Las divisiones del universo local","items":[{"x":"Urantia es el mundo habitado número 606 del sistema de Satania, en Norlatiadek, una de las cien constelaciones de Nebadon.","r":["43:0.1"]},{"x":"Un sistema consta de unos mil mundos habitables, y una constelación de cien sistemas.","r":["15:2.3","15:2.4"]},{"x":"Las constelaciones funcionan como unidades legislativas y los sistemas locales como unidades ejecutivas, mientras que el gobierno de Salvington es la autoridad judicial y coordinadora suprema.","r":["43:2.2"]},{"x":"Los gobernantes de las constelaciones vinculan los sistemas locales con la administración universal de Salvington y, mediante la reflectividad, con los Ancianos de los Días en Uversa.","r":["43:0.1"]}]},{"h":"El gobierno de la constelación y los Altísimos","items":[{"x":"Una constelación es gobernada por tres Altísimos de la orden Vorondadek, y el que preside se llama Padre de la Constelación.","r":["43:3.2"]},{"q":"no disaffection of the Vorondadek Sons has ever occurred in Nebadon.","r":"43:3.1"},{"x":"La asamblea legislativa de la constelación consta de tres grupos: una cámara baja de ascendentes, una tercera cámara de serafines y otros seres, y una cámara alta de los Hijos divinos.","r":["43:2.5","43:2.6","43:2.7"]},{"x":"Los Altísimos se ocupan del bienestar de las naciones y de las razas más que de los individuos, y gobiernan en los reinos de los hombres más que en el corazón individual.","r":["43:3.5","43:9.4"]},{"x":"En los mundos aislados por la rebelión hay destacado un observador Vorondadek, y es él quien realmente «gobierna en los reinos de los hombres».","r":["43:5.17"]},{"x":"El Fiel de los Días en Edentia está junto a los Padres de la Constelación como representante de la Trinidad, pero nunca da consejo a menos que se le pida.","r":["43:4.2"]}]},{"h":"Edentia: el jardín de Dios","items":[{"x":"Edentia, la sede central de la constelación, es unas cien veces mayor que Urantia, y a su alrededor giran setenta esferas principales y setecientos satélites.","r":["43:0.2"]},{"x":"La capital de la constelación abunda en ornamentación viviente y se llama «los jardines de Dios»; la mitad de la superficie de Edentia está dedicada a los jardines de los Altísimos.","r":["43:6.1","43:6.2"]},{"q":"there is nothing in all Edentia to make any living being afraid.","r":"43:6.5"},{"x":"Al pasar por los setenta mundos, los mortales ascendentes viven con los univitatias y aprenden la ética de grupo y la verdadera socialización de la personalidad morontial.","r":["43:8.3","43:8.4"]},{"q":"Intelectual, social y espiritualmente dos criaturas morales no aumentan sus potenciales personales de logro universal al doble mediante la técnica asociativa sino que multiplican casi por cuatro sus posibilidades de logro y cumplimiento.","r":"43:8.11"},{"x":"La estancia en la constelación es el punto medio del camino entre el ser semejante al animal y el espíritu ascendente, el período más uniforme y estable de la carrera morontial.","r":["43:9.2","43:9.3"]}]},{"h":"El sistema local y Jerusem","items":[{"x":"El jefe ejecutivo de un sistema local es el Soberano del Sistema, un Hijo Lanonandek primario; el actual soberano de Satania es Lanaforge, sucesor de Lucifer.","r":["45:2.1","45:3.2"]},{"x":"En la historia de Nebadon ha habido tres casos de deslealtad entre los Soberanos de Sistema, y la rebelión de Lucifer en Satania fue el último y el más extenso.","r":["45:2.1"]},{"x":"Jerusem está rodeado de siete mundos de cultura de transición y sus satélites, y los siete mundos de estancia son satélites del primer mundo de transición.","r":["45:0.1","45:0.2"]},{"q":"Las capitales del sistema son singulares en cuanto son los únicos mundos que exhiben casi perfectamente las tres fases de la existencia universal: la material, la morontial y la espiritual.","r":"46:4.8"},{"x":"En Jerusem no hay día y noche separados ni estaciones, y la luz se filtra uniformemente desde todo el cielo y no desde una sola fuente.","r":["46:1.4","46:1.5"]},{"q":"El gobierno representativo es el ideal divino del autogobierno entre los seres no perfectos.","r":"45:7.3"}]},{"h":"La formación para la ascensión en la capital del sistema","items":[{"x":"Los mundos de estancia son el lugar donde los mortales que no se fusionaron con su Ajustador en la vida en la carne reciben la oportunidad de reanudar su logro espiritual interrumpido.","r":["45:7.1"]},{"x":"Los Hijos e Hijas Materiales, ciudadanos permanentes de Jerusem, se convierten en los patrocinadores y maestros inmediatos de los mortales ascendentes.","r":["45:5.5","45:6.2"]},{"x":"Los ascendentes que carecen de experiencia como padres deben adquirir esa experiencia esencial en los hogares de los Hijos Materiales en Jerusem o en las guarderías probatorias.","r":["45:6.4","45:6.6"]},{"x":"En las elecciones de Jerusem el valor de un voto varía según el grado de sabiduría morontial, y solo se puede partir hacia la constelación después de alcanzar la personalidad mota.","r":["45:7.6","45:7.8"]},{"x":"Las asambleas celebradas en el mundo de los finalistas aseguran a los residentes de los mundos de estancia que también ellos pueden completar el largo viaje.","r":["45:1.2"]}]},{"h":"Cuidado especial después de la rebelión","items":[{"x":"Desde la rebelión de Lucifer, los Altísimos de Edentia han asumido ciertas fases de la autoridad planetaria en los mundos rebeldes y todavía las ejercen.","r":["43:3.7"]},{"x":"Lucifer y la mayoría de las personalidades que lo siguieron están confinados en los mundos prisión que rodean el mundo del Padre en Jerusem, una solemne advertencia para todo Nebadon.","r":["45:1.11"]},{"x":"Después del triunfo de Cristo Micael, Satanás fue rechazado por unanimidad por los Soberanos de Sistema en un cónclave en Edentia.","r":["43:4.9"]},{"q":"When there exists no open door for the reception of evil, there exists no opportunity for the entertainment of sin.","r":"43:4.9"},{"x":"Los veinticuatro consejeros de Jerusem son personas originarias de Urantia que representan a Micael en las listas de llamada de Satania y en los planes de ascensión de los mundos aislados.","r":["45:4.1","45:4.2"]}]}],"see":["Universo local de Nebadon","Mundos de estancia","Rebelión de Lucifer","Ascensión mortal","Hijos e Hijas Materiales","Los Melquisedek"]},{"n":72,"t":"Crecimiento","en":"Growth","sum":"Growth is the process in which the actual and the potential combine and values are realized in experience; unlike perfect Havona, it is the hallmark of the evolving grand universe and the Supreme Being. Man's spiritual growth proceeds from an awakening to needs to the discernment of meanings and the discovery of values, and it always takes place unconsciously. Man cannot cause growth, but through devotion to supreme values and living faith he can supply its conditions.","sections":[{"h":"The Nature of Growth","items":[{"q":"La asociación de los actuales y los potenciales equivale al crecimiento, la realización experiencial de los valores.","r":"100:3.6"},{"x":"Growth is not mere progress; progress is meaningful, but without growth it is relatively valueless.","r":["100:3.6"]},{"x":"Values are never static, and change that does not enlarge meanings and elevate values is potential evil.","r":["100:3.5"]},{"x":"The supreme value of human life lies in the growth of values, the progress of meanings, and the realization of their cosmic interrelatedness.","r":["100:3.6"]},{"x":"Growth of a part is not the same as maturity of the whole; to traverse the psychic circles, the whole personality must grow harmoniously.","r":["110:6.3"]}]},{"h":"The Growing Universe and the Supreme Being","items":[{"q":"El crecimiento es la marca de la deidad experiencial: Havona no creció;","r":"116:0.3"},{"x":"Experiential growth implies a creature-Creator partnership, the association of God and man.","r":["116:0.3"]},{"x":"The Supreme Being is first a spirit personality derived from the Trinity and second a God of evolutionary growth.","r":["115:4.2"]},{"x":"The growth of the whole is the sum of the growth of all its parts, and its completion is an act of the Almighty Supreme.","r":["116:6.6"]},{"x":"Creative growth is endless, but along the way moments of satisfying goal attainment become preludes to new adventure.","r":["118:0.10"]}]},{"h":"Stages and Signs of Spiritual Growth","items":[{"q":"El crecimiento espiritual es en primer lugar, el despertar a las necesidades, luego el discernimiento de los significados y finalmente el descubrimiento de los valores.","r":"100:2.2"},{"x":"True spiritual development shows itself in a life motivated by love, activated by unselfish ministry, and dominated by wholehearted worship.","r":["100:2.2"]},{"x":"Spiritual development depends on maintaining a living connection with true spiritual forces and bearing fruit by sharing what one receives with one's fellows.","r":["100:2.1"]},{"x":"Spiritual growth is mutually stimulated by intimate association with other religionists, and love is the soil of that growth.","r":["100:0.2"]},{"x":"Loyal persons are growing persons, and children are lastingly impressed by the loyalties of the adults with whom they live.","r":["100:1.4"]}]},{"h":"Conditions That Favor Growth","items":[{"q":"El hombre no puede desencadenar el crecimiento, pero sí puede proveer las condiciones favorables.","r":"100:3.7"},{"x":"Growth, whether physical, intellectual, or spiritual, is always unconscious; like love, it must grow.","r":["100:3.7","100:1.9"]},{"x":"Habits such as sensitivity to divine values, reflective meditation, worshipful problem solving, and avoidance of selfishness favor growth.","r":["100:1.8"]},{"x":"The innate drive toward growth is most surely fostered by an attitude of wholehearted devotion to supreme values.","r":["100:1.6"]},{"q":"El crecimiento espiritual es más grande cuando todas las presiones externas son mínimas.","r":"103:5.11"}]},{"h":"Hindrances to Growth and the Teaching of Jesus","items":[{"q":"Algunas personas están demasiado ocupadas para crecer y por consiguiente corren el grave peligro de la fijación espiritual.","r":"100:1.2"},{"x":"Jesus taught not the building of character but the growth of character, and he likened the kingdom of heaven to a mustard seed.","r":["140:8.27","151:4.2"]},{"x":"With a carpenter's analogy Jesus taught that the soul is a living growth, and mind and morals are the soil from which its higher expressions spring.","r":["156:5.2"]},{"x":"The true believer should ask whether he is becoming more skillful in showing goodness today than yesterday, this year than last.","r":["156:5.15"]},{"x":"The morontia life forever uproots animal vestiges such as procrastination and evasion, so that growth may continue.","r":["48:5.8"]}]}],"see":["Experiencia","Ser Supremo","Alma","Búsqueda de la perfección","Adversidad y pruebas","Religión personal"]},{"n":32,"t":"Cuerpo de la Finalidad","en":"Corps of the Finality","sum":"The Corps of the Finality is the presently known destination of the ascending mortals of time, who are mustered into it after finding God and attaining Paradise. Centered on glorified mortals, it also includes Havona natives, Gravity Messengers, adopted seraphim, Material Sons, and midway creatures, and its members now serve on worlds settled in light and life. Their ultimate destiny has not been revealed, but it is conjectured to concern the future universes of outer space.","sections":[{"h":"Composition of the Corps","items":[{"x":"The primary Corps of the Finality consists of Havona natives, Gravity Messengers, glorified mortals, adopted seraphim, and glorified Material Sons and midway creatures.","r":["31:0.1","31:0.8"]},{"x":"The corps is organized in companies of one thousand, of which mortals and seraphim make up 990, leaving only ten places for the other beings.","r":["31:1.3","31:3.1"]},{"x":"All are received as equals, yet that equality does not erase individuality or personal identity.","r":["31:0.9"]},{"x":"Gravity Messengers are personalized Adjusters who transcend time and space, and they share a deep affection with mortals who have fused with Adjusters.","r":["31:2.2","31:2.4"]},{"q":"Son en efecto las almas verdaderas y probadas del tiempo y del espacio que se van acumulando —la sal evolucionaria del universo— y están protegidos para siempre tanto contra el mal como contra el pecado.","r":"31:0.13"},{"x":"Evangels of light are attached temporarily without taking the oath, and the one vacancy beyond the 999 permanent members remains a mystery.","r":["31:7.1","31:7.2"]}]},{"h":"Who Enters","items":[{"x":"Of all the creatures of the grand universe, only those fused with the Father are mustered into the mortal Corps of the Finality and take the finaliter oath.","r":["30:4.31"]},{"x":"Spirit-fused mortals usually remain in local universe service and do not share the destiny of the Paradise Corps of the Finality.","r":["40:9.9"]},{"x":"Many guardian seraphim ascend with their mortal wards, take the same finaliter oath, and are mustered into the corps.","r":["31:4.1","40:1.1"]},{"x":"Children who die early, deprived of the experience of mortal life, become Paradise citizens but do not enter the Corps of the Finality.","r":["47:2.8"]},{"q":"And every God-knowing mortal craves to be a finaliter.","r":"14:6.39"}]},{"h":"The Way to Paradise","items":[{"x":"Mortals ascend through the stages of spirit one by one and become spirits of the sixth stage when they take the oath of the Corps of the Finality.","r":["31:3.4"]},{"x":"The seventh jubilee celebrates entrance into the mortal Corps of the Finality and the beginning of eternal service.","r":["27:7.8"]},{"x":"In the finaliter receiving circle, the chief of the Transcendentalers administers the eternity oath of the Trinity.","r":["31:8.4"]},{"q":"Los mortales evolucionarios nacen en los planetas del espacio, pasan a través de los mundos morontiales, ascienden a los universos espirituales, atraviesan las esferas de Havona, hallan a Dios, logran el Paraíso y son integrados en el Cuerpo primario de la Finalidad, para aguardar allí la próxima asignación de servicio en el universo.","r":"31:10.20"}]},{"h":"Present Service and Organization","items":[{"x":"Finaliters are not assigned to their native superuniverse until they have served in the other six, and so they gain a sevenfold concept of the Supreme Being.","r":["31:0.10"]},{"q":"Una o más compañías de finalistas mortales están constantemente al servicio en Urantia.","r":"31:0.11"},{"x":"The finaliters are a self-governing body that chooses its own leaders, and their oath of allegiance is given to the Paradise Trinity alone.","r":["31:0.12"]},{"x":"The first transition world of Satania is the headquarters of more than one hundred thousand finaliter companies, and finaliters remain invisible until true spirit vision is attained.","r":["47:0.2","47:1.3"]},{"x":"The mortal Corps of the Finality serves in various roles on worlds settled in light and life, but it seems to have no settled duties as yet.","r":["30:4.32"]}]},{"h":"A Destiny Not Yet Finished","items":[{"x":"Finaliters have reached the present limits of creature perfection, but not yet the ultimate spirit status or the finality of creature service.","r":["31:3.6"]},{"q":"Why should the Gods be so concerned in so thoroughly training surviving mortals in the technique of universe management?","r":"31:3.8"},{"x":"In the finaliter circle on Jerusem stands a sealed and empty temple inscribed \"Not yet dedicated to the seventh stage of spirit.\"","r":["46:5.32"]},{"x":"Having found the Father, the finaliters may one day have to begin a new search for the superfinite Father.","r":["10:8.7"]}]},{"h":"Prospects Toward Outer Space","items":[{"x":"The seven corps of finality are supervised by the senior Master Architect, and Grandfanda is head of the council of supreme destiny.","r":["31:10.1","31:10.9"]},{"x":"It is conjectured that the finaliters will compensate for the experiential deficiency of the outer universes, which cannot share in the evolution of the Supreme Being.","r":["31:10.11","31:10.13"]},{"q":"Creemos que los mortales fusionados con el Ajustador, juntamente con sus asociados finalistas, están destinados a funcionar de alguna manera en la administración de los universos del primer nivel del espacio exterior.","r":"112:7.17"},{"x":"Even if there were no unrevealed future destiny, the present assignments of the finaliters would fully justify the ascension plan.","r":["30:4.33"]}]}],"see":["Ascensión mortal","Fusión con el Ajustador","Havona","Paraíso","Ser Supremo","Búsqueda de la perfección"]},{"n":7,"t":"Dios el Séptuple","en":"God the Sevenfold","sum":"Dios el Séptuple es la asociación séptuple de Deidad dispuesta por el Padre Universal para que las criaturas finitas puedan acercarse a la Deidad. Se extiende desde el Hijo Creador del universo local, pasando por los Ancianos de los Días, los Siete Espíritus Rectores, el Ser Supremo, el Espíritu Infinito y el Hijo Eterno, hasta el Padre Universal, y los mortales ascendentes descubren la Deidad de manera experiencial en este orden. Sus tres primeros niveles son también la fuente del poder todopoderoso del Ser Supremo.","sections":[{"h":"Siete escalones hacia la Deidad","items":[{"x":"Para compensar las limitaciones de la condición y del concepto finitos, el Padre Universal estableció el acercamiento séptuple de las criaturas evolutivas a la Deidad.","r":["0:8.1"]},{"x":"Los siete niveles son los Hijos Creadores Paradisiacos, los Ancianos de los Días, los Siete Espíritus Rectores, el Ser Supremo, Dios Espíritu, Dios Hijo y Dios Padre.","r":["0:8.2","0:8.8"]},{"q":"Dios el Séptuple significa el reconocimiento por parte de la Deidad del Paraíso de las barreras del tiempo en los universos evolucionarios del espacio.","r":"106:1.3"},{"x":"La carrera experiencial de encontrar a Dios comienza con el reconocimiento de la divinidad del Hijo Creador del universo local y prosigue, a través de los Ancianos de los Días y los Espíritus Rectores, hasta el Padre del Paraíso.","r":["0:8.9"]},{"x":"Dios el Séptuple es la Deidad que funciona realmente para los mortales evolutivos en la carrera de ascensión al Paraíso.","r":["0:8.9"]}]},{"h":"Creadores Supremos y Deidades del Paraíso","items":[{"x":"De los siete niveles, los tres primeros son los Creadores Supremos y los tres últimos las Deidades del Paraíso, y entre ellos se interpone siempre el Ser Supremo.","r":["116:2.4","116:2.12"]},{"x":"La Deidad del Paraíso atenuó y cualificó la personalización de la divinidad fuera del Paraíso para dar existencia a los Creadores Supremos, y ellos llevan la luz de la vida a los mundos evolutivos.","r":["116:2.3"]},{"x":"Los actos combinados de los tres primeros niveles no equivalen a la Deidad del Paraíso; constituyen un nuevo potencial de poder de Deidad experiencial.","r":["116:2.13"]},{"q":"Los Hijos Creadores en la asociación de Deidad de Dios el Séptuplo, proveen el mecanismo por el cual el mortal se vuelve inmortal y el finito alcanza el abarcamiento de lo infinito.","r":"0:8.11"},{"x":"El ministerio de divinidad del Séptuple llega hacia dentro, a través del Hijo Eterno, hasta el Padre del Paraíso, y hacia fuera, a través de los Ancianos de los Días, hasta los Hijos Creadores.","r":["106:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Relación con el Ser Supremo","items":[{"x":"Dios el Supremo deriva de la Trinidad sus atributos de personalidad y de espíritu, pero su poder se actualiza en las acciones de los Hijos Creadores, los Ancianos de los Días y los Espíritus Rectores.","r":["0:8.10","116:2.2"]},{"x":"Dios el Supremo se manifiesta a las criaturas evolutivas como personalidad de poder solo cuando los tres primeros niveles de Dios el Séptuple funcionan de manera coordinada.","r":["116:2.14"]},{"q":"El Ser Supremo es la revelación máxima de la Deidad a los siete superuniversos y a la presente edad del universo.","r":"116:2.12"},{"x":"En la experiencia mortal, el Ser Supremo es el unificador de Dios el Séptuple, el máximo de Deidad que las criaturas finitas pueden comprender realmente.","r":["56:8.1"]},{"x":"Los diversos aspectos de la Deidad séptuple están ahora integrados de distintas maneras, pero todos están destinados a unificarse en la Supremacía.","r":["106:1.4"]}]},{"h":"Los controladores séptuples y la función cósmica","items":[{"x":"Dios el Séptuple incluye no solo a los creadores, sino también a los controladores séptuples del gran universo, como los Controladores Físicos Decanos, los Centros Supremos de Poder y los Directores Supremos del Poder.","r":["116:5.1","116:5.9"]},{"x":"El consejo de los Siete Espíritus Rectores parece coordinar las vastas actividades de Dios el Séptuple, y contribuye también al último nivel, la unión del Hijo Creador y el Espíritu Creativo.","r":["17:8.3","17:8.8"]},{"q":"La función de Dios el Séptuplo data de la organización de los siete superuniversos, y probablemente se ampliará en relación con la evolución futura de las creaciones del espacio exterior.","r":"0:8.12"},{"q":"Los Absolutos son coordinados en el Último, condicionados en el Supremo, y modificados espacio-temporalmente en Dios el Séptuple.","r":"56:9.1"},{"x":"Mediante el ministerio de Dios el Séptuple, lo imperfecto se vincula con lo perfecto en el intervalo del tiempo, y la criatura se convierte en asociada del Creador en su propia evolución.","r":["106:1.2"]},{"x":"El poder que surge de los logros de Dios el Séptuple es poder experiencial, ganado y demostrado, en contraste con el poder existencial de las Deidades del Paraíso.","r":["106:2.3"]}]},{"h":"Revelación en luz y vida","items":[{"x":"La evolución del tiempo y del espacio comienza en planetas presididos por la unión del Hijo Creador y el Espíritu Creativo, la primera manifestación de Dios el Séptuple, y a medida que un universo local se establece, Dios el Séptuple se revela con mayor claridad.","r":["56:7.2"]},{"x":"A medida que las creaciones se establecen, las tres primeras manifestaciones se retiran y aparece una actividad más plena de Dios el Supremo, pero lo que sigue aún no ha sido revelado.","r":["56:7.6"]},{"q":"Sabemos sin embargo que en los universos del tiempo y del espacio, Dios el Séptuple provee un acercamiento progresivo al Padre Universal, y que este enfoque evolucionario está experiencialmente unificado en Dios el Supremo.","r":"56:7.8"},{"x":"Los mundos de luz y vida captan sucesivamente la realidad de Dios el Séptuple, desde la adoración del Hijo Creador hasta la adoración del Padre del Paraíso.","r":["56:10.1"]},{"x":"Sea cual sea el nivel de Deidad alcanzado, el ascendente redescubre cada vez, en un nuevo nivel de experiencia, al Padre del Paraíso de todas las personalidades.","r":["56:9.10"]}]}],"see":["Ser Supremo","Hijo Creador Micael","Ancianos de los Días","Siete Espíritus Rectores","Trinidad del Paraíso","Ascensión mortal"]},{"n":9,"t":"Dios el Último","en":"God the Ultimate","sum":"Dios el Último es la segunda Deidad experiencial, que se eventúa después del Ser Supremo; es una personalidad-poder trascendental que funciona en el nivel absonito, el cual trasciende el tiempo y el espacio del universo maestro. Se eventúa a partir de la unificación de la Trinidad Última, que estará compuesta por los Creadores Supremos, el Ser Supremo y los Arquitectos del Universo Maestro, y su plena aparición significa la terminación de la creación del universo maestro. Él es el objeto de la búsqueda siguiente de los finalistas y de los ciudadanos perfeccionados, una vez que el gran universo esté establecido en luz y vida.","sections":[{"h":"Deidad del nivel absonito","items":[{"q":"Dios el Último: el Dios que eventúa del supertiempo y del espacio trascendido.","r":"0:2.17"},{"x":"Las realidades absonitas son cosas y seres que han sido eventuados más que creados, sin principio ni fin y que trascienden el tiempo y el espacio, y la función de la Deidad en relación con ellas es la Ultimidad.","r":["0:1.12"]},{"q":"El Supremo es la unificación Trinitaria comprendida por los seres finitos; el Último es la unificación de la Trinidad Paradisiaca comprendida por los seres absonitos.","r":"0:9.2"},{"x":"Entre las siete naturalezas de la Deidad, la Supremacía es el yo evolutivo-experiencial y la Ultimidad el yo trascendental-experiencial.","r":["118:0.5","118:0.7"]},{"x":"Dios el Último trasciende el tiempo y el espacio y es capaz de asociarse funcionalmente con los Absolutos, pero es absonito.","r":["106:4.4"]}]},{"h":"Supremacía y Ultimidad","items":[{"q":"Aunque Dios el Séptuple es indispensable para el logro evolucionario del Supremo, el Supremo es también indispensable para la emergencia eventual del Último.","r":"118:0.9"},{"x":"El Supremo y el Último se complementan en el logro del destino, y forman el puente experiencial que enlaza los comienzos y las culminaciones de todo crecimiento creador en el universo maestro.","r":["118:0.9"]},{"x":"La Ultimidad y la Supremacía son comparables, pero no idénticas, y la Ultimidad no es simplemente una ampliación de la Supremacía.","r":["106:8.15"]},{"x":"Así como el Ser Supremo evoluciona a partir de los potenciales del gran universo, Dios el Último se eventúa a partir de los potenciales de divinidad de los dominios del universo maestro que trascienden el tiempo y el espacio.","r":["0:9.1"]},{"x":"Cuando Dios el Supremo llegue a gobernar directamente los universos del tiempo y del espacio, esa administración funcionará bajo el supercontrol de la Ultimidad, y Dios el Último comenzará a aparecer como el Todopoderoso trascendental.","r":["118:2.4"]}]},{"h":"La Trinidad Última","items":[{"x":"La Trinidad Última es la asociación de Deidad de los Creadores Supremos, Dios el Supremo y los Arquitectos del Universo Maestro, y está ahora en evolución.","r":["0:12.6","106:8.10"]},{"q":"Dios el Último, final e inevitablemente adquirirá poder y se personalizará como consecuencia de Deidad de la unificación de esta Trinidad Última experiencial en el escenario expansivo del universo maestro casi ilimitado.","r":"0:12.6"},{"x":"Cuando termine la presente era del universo y emerja el Supremo Todopoderoso, la primera Trinidad experiencial funcionará plenamente e integrará aún más la evolución de la creación maestra.","r":["106:3.2"]},{"x":"Esta Trinidad incluye a los Hijos Creadores Mayores, de modo que la experiencia real de las criaturas queda abarcada en su asociación.","r":["106:3.3"]},{"q":"La eventuación completada del Último implica que se completó la creación maestra e indica el surgimiento pleno de esta Deidad trascendental.","r":"106:4.2"},{"x":"La unificación del universo maestro es el acto eventuador del Último, y se cree que refleja alguna fase del supercontrol absonito de la Trinidad del Paraíso.","r":["10:8.2"]}]},{"h":"La Ultimidad revelada ahora","items":[{"x":"Así como el Supremo está presente espiritual y personalmente en Havona, la Ultimidad existe allí en un sentido absonito y superpersonal.","r":["106:4.3"]},{"x":"Se sabe que ya existen Vicegerentes Cualificados del Último, pero su ubicación y su función actuales no han sido reveladas.","r":["106:4.3","117:7.4"]},{"x":"Dios el Último anuncia su supercontrol trascendental en las etapas posteriores de los universos locales establecidos en luz y vida.","r":["56:7.5"]},{"x":"Los mortales que llegan a la séptima etapa de luz y vida, a la vez que llegan a conocer a Dios el Supremo, disciernen vagamente el ministerio omnipresente de Dios el Último.","r":["56:10.1"]},{"x":"La «eventuación de la capacidad del universo», que convierte el potencial indiferenciado en planes definidos del universo, es la actividad de la Ultimidad y de las agencias trascendentales.","r":["118:4.6"]}]},{"h":"La siguiente meta de los finalistas","items":[{"x":"Los ascendentes encuentran a Dios el Supremo en Havona, y después de llegar a ser finalistas intentan conocerlo como Ultimidad.","r":["118:2.2"]},{"x":"Cuando la verdad, la belleza y la bondad del Ser Supremo los han impregnado plenamente, las cualidades absonitas de la divinidad última, más allá de ese nivel conceptual, se abren ante las criaturas que progresan.","r":["115:3.19"]},{"x":"Dios el Último existe para ofrecer un destino de servicio último a todas las criaturas que alcanzan los niveles absonitos mediante el ministerio de Dios el Séptuple.","r":["0:9.1"]},{"q":"Seguro, certera e inexorablemente el enigma de la Deidad emergente de Dios el Último desafiará a estos ciudadanos perfeccionados de los universos establecidos, así como sus antepasados evolucionarios luchadores fueron desafiados antaño por la búsqueda de Dios el Supremo.","r":"117:7.17"},{"x":"Para los finalistas que han alcanzado la Ultimidad, el camino que queda es la búsqueda del Absoluto, y saben que al final de él encontrarán al mismo Padre del Paraíso.","r":["118:2.2"]},{"x":"Dios el Supremo y Dios el Último son Deidades eternas solo en el futuro y no en el pasado: tienen un comienzo de personalidad, pero no un final.","r":["0:9.5"]}]}],"see":["Ser Supremo","Trinidad del Paraíso","Los tres Absolutos","Cuerpo de la Finalidad","Gran universo y universo maestro","Luz y vida"]},{"n":89,"t":"Los doce apóstoles","en":"Twelve Apostles","sum":"The twelve apostles were ordinary Galileans whom Jesus personally called, trained, and ordained to proclaim the gospel of the kingdom of heaven. They were not ignorant men but men of varied temperaments who had received synagogue schooling, and each, with his own strengths and weaknesses, was transformed by living with Jesus. That only one of them deserted him, even though Jesus repeatedly shattered their worldly expectations, testifies to the charm of his life.","sections":[{"h":"Calling and Training","items":[{"x":"Jesus chose the first six himself, and each of them recommended one more, making twelve.","r":["139:6.1","138:5.1"]},{"x":"The first six apostles went out two by two, preaching the gospel by personal contact, and learned that religion is a purely personal experience.","r":["138:1.1","138:2.1"]},{"x":"The monotonous period of alternating fishing and personal work was a severe test, but they endured it through loyalty to the Master.","r":["138:9.1"]},{"x":"On January 12, A.D. 27, Jesus ordained the twelve as public preachers of the gospel of the kingdom.","r":["140:0.1"]},{"x":"The so-called Sermon on the Mount was not the gospel itself but Jesus' ordination charge to the twelve.","r":["140:4.1"]}]},{"h":"Ordinary and Diverse Men","items":[{"q":"No cometáis el error de pensar que los apóstoles eran totalmente ignorantes e incultos.","r":"139:0.3"},{"x":"\"Unlearned\" means they were laymen untrained in rabbinical lore and methods of scriptural interpretation.","r":["139:0.4"]},{"x":"The apostles learned about the kingdom of heaven from Jesus, and Jesus learned much about human nature from them.","r":["139:0.2"]},{"x":"All the apostles loved Jesus, but each was drawn by some trait of his character that especially appealed to him.","r":["139:1.11"]}]},{"h":"The Four Chief Apostles","items":[{"x":"Andrew, the eldest, became chief of the apostolic corps and held that place to the end; not a great preacher, he was an effective personal worker.","r":["139:1.2","139:1.3","139:1.4"]},{"x":"Peter was impulsive and optimistic, a born leader and eloquent speaker, but his speech often ran ahead of his thinking.","r":["139:2.3","139:2.4"]},{"x":"James Zebedee had a fierce temper, but his ability to see a problem from many sides brought him closest to the real meaning of Jesus' teaching.","r":["139:3.2","139:3.4"]},{"x":"John, the youngest, served as Jesus' personal representative in many matters, but the phrase \"the disciple whom Jesus loved\" is not accurate.","r":["139:4.2","139:4.4"]},{"x":"Peter, James, and John were appointed by Andrew as personal aides to attend to Jesus at his side.","r":["139:4.3"]},{"q":"Andrew was a man of clear insight, logical thought, and firm decision","r":"139:1.10"}]},{"h":"The Other Apostles","items":[{"x":"Philip, with his \"show me,\" lacked imagination but was a faithful steward who did small things in a great way.","r":["139:5.2","139:5.3","139:5.4"]},{"x":"Nathaniel was an honest man \"in whom there is no guile\" and the philosopher of the twelve; his weakness was a pride that verged on prejudice.","r":["139:6.3","139:6.4"]},{"x":"Matthew, the former publican, handled the finances of the group and was most deeply grateful for the Master's forgiving nature.","r":["139:7.2","139:7.4"]},{"x":"Thomas was the real scientist of the group, with an analytic mind and unflinching courage, but he struggled with doubt all his life.","r":["139:8.2","139:8.4"]},{"x":"The Alpheus twins were ordinary men with neither strong nor weak points, yet through them many timid believers entered the kingdom.","r":["139:9.4","139:9.5"]},{"x":"Simon Zelotes led the hesitant into the kingdom by his inspiring loyalty, but he never fully shed his nationalistic thinking.","r":["139:11.3","139:11.4"]},{"q":"Eran «los menos importantes entre todos los apóstoles»; lo sabían y les complacía.","r":"139:9.5"}]},{"h":"Judas Iscariot","items":[{"x":"Judas was the only Judean among the apostles and the best educated; he handled the treasury honestly and efficiently.","r":["139:12.2","139:12.3"]},{"q":"Judas en realidad no se entendía a sí mismo; no era realmente sincero consigo mismo.","r":"139:12.2"},{"x":"He never overcame his prejudice against his Galilean associates and inwardly criticized Jesus as timid.","r":["139:12.4"]},{"q":"Jesús tan sólo tuvo lástima del traidor.","r":"139:12.14"}]},{"h":"Ambassadors of the Kingdom","items":[{"x":"Jesus told the apostles that, as citizens of another, heavenly kingdom, they must now live better lives than before.","r":["140:3.1"]},{"x":"He taught the apostles at length not so much what they should do as what they should be.","r":["140:10.1"]},{"q":"ES UN testimonio elocuente del encanto y rectitud de la vida terrenal de Jesús que, aunque destruyó en repetidas ocasiones las esperanzas de sus apóstoles y redujo a jirones todas sus ambiciones de exaltación personal, sólo uno de ellos lo abandonó.","r":"139:0.1"}]}],"see":["Enseñanzas de Jesús","Carácter de Jesús","Pentecostés","Resurrección de Jesús","Muerte en la cruz","Reino del cielo"]},{"n":17,"t":"Energía y materia","en":"Energy and Matter","sum":"La energía es la base de toda existencia, una realidad eterna pero no infinita que sale del Paraíso y regresa al Paraíso. Desde la potencia del espacio, pasando por la fuerza primordial y la energía emergente, hasta el poder universal y la materia, es transmutada por los organizadores de fuerza y los directores del poder, y la luz, el calor, la electricidad y la materia son una en su origen y su destino. Sin embargo, el universo no es mecánico; se sitúa dentro de un orden en el que la mente domina a la materia y el espíritu gobierna a la mente.","sections":[{"h":"La energía procedente del Paraíso","items":[{"x":"La energía es la base de toda existencia, y la energía pura está controlada por el Padre Universal; el flujo de energía que sale del Paraíso nunca ha cesado.","r":["42:0.1"]},{"q":"La base del universo es material, pero la esencia de la vida es espíritu.","r":"42:1.1"},{"x":"Considerado en los fenómenos no espirituales, Dios es energía, y toda energía física procede de él.","r":["3:2.3"]},{"x":"La creación de la energía y el otorgamiento de la vida son prerrogativas del Padre y de sus personalidades creadoras; por avanzado que esté, un científico nunca podrá crear un átomo ni añadir vida a la materia.","r":["42:1.4","42:1.5"]},{"q":"Energy is eternal but not infinite","r":"42:1.8"},{"x":"La fuerza-energía es imperecedera e indestructible; puede transmutarse sin fin, pero nunca aniquilarse.","r":["42:1.7"]}]},{"h":"Etapas de la transmutación","items":[{"x":"La potencia del espacio (absoluta) es la presencia espacial libre del Absoluto No Cualificado, que solo responde a la acción personal del Padre Universal.","r":["42:2.3","42:2.5"]},{"x":"Los organizadores de fuerza del Paraíso transforman la potencia del espacio en fuerza primordial (segregata) y la transmutan luego en energía potente y energía gravitacional (ultimata).","r":["42:2.7","42:2.10","42:2.13"]},{"x":"Cuando la energía alcanza la etapa de respuesta a la gravedad del Paraíso, los directores del poder toman el relevo y manejan el poder universal (gravita).","r":["42:2.12","42:2.14"]},{"x":"La energía de Havona no es dual, sino trina (triata), y la energía del Paraíso, monota, se distingue del espíritu del Paraíso solo por el nombre.","r":["42:2.16","42:2.19","42:2.20"]},{"x":"La fuerza cósmica, la energía emergente y el poder universal se distinguen por su manera de responder a la gravedad del Paraíso y a la gravedad lineal.","r":["0:6.5","0:6.6","0:6.7"]}]},{"h":"La estructura de la materia","items":[{"q":"La luz, el calor, la electricidad, el magnetismo, la acción química, la energía y la materia son —en su origen, naturaleza y destino— la misma cosa, juntamente con otras realidades materiales que aún no se han descubierto en Urantia.","r":"42:4.1"},{"x":"La unidad primaria de la existencia material es el ultimatón, y exactamente cien ultimatones constituyen un electrón.","r":["42:3.3","42:6.5"]},{"x":"El universo local tiene una estructura decimal, de modo que los átomos existen solo en cien formas, con entre uno y cien electrones orbitales.","r":["42:7.4"]},{"x":"El núcleo atómico se mantiene unido gracias al mesotrón, ciento ochenta veces más pesado que el electrón, que transporta cargas entre protones y neutrones.","r":["42:8.3","42:8.4"]},{"x":"El espacio no está vacío; incluso el espacio más vacío conocido en Nebadon contiene unos cien ultimatones por pulgada cúbica.","r":["42:4.6"]},{"x":"La repetición de las propiedades de los elementos de siete en siete es una marca de nacimiento de su origen espiritual séptuple, impresa en el mundo material.","r":["42:9.2","42:9.3"]}]},{"h":"El circuito y el equilibrio de la energía","items":[{"x":"Aunque sufre las transmutaciones del tiempo, la materia oscila siempre en el circuito de la eternidad, siempre sensible a la fuente de la que salió.","r":["42:4.2"]},{"x":"Los soles ardientes convierten la materia en energía, mientras que el espacio frío y los mundos oscuros frenan de nuevo la energía hasta convertirla en materia.","r":["42:4.9"]},{"x":"La integridad de la materia está asegurada por el hecho de que la energía solo se absorbe o se emite en unidades cuánticas.","r":["42:4.13"]},{"x":"No hay éter; la luz y la energía son corrientes de partículas que viajan en línea recta y solo parecen ondulatorias por la resistencia del espacio.","r":["42:5.14","42:5.16"]},{"q":"La energía física es la única realidad que es fiel y constante en su obediencia a la ley universal.","r":"12:8.3"},{"x":"Los directores del poder y los organizadores de fuerza, que son seres vivientes, dirigen inteligentemente las metamorfosis sin fin de la formación, la disolución y la reformación de los universos.","r":["15:8.10"]}]},{"h":"La mente y el mecanismo del universo","items":[{"x":"El universo no es mecánico ni mágico; es una creación de la mente y un mecanismo de la ley.","r":["42:11.1"]},{"x":"El universo de los universos es planeado, hecho y administrado por la mente, pero su mecanismo es tan perfecto que los métodos de la ciencia no pueden discernir la huella de la mente infinita.","r":["42:11.2"]},{"x":"Las energías no espirituales se reúnen de nuevo en sistemas vivientes de mente como la mente espiritual preayudante, la mente de los espíritus ayudantes, la mente morontial y la mente cósmica.","r":["42:10.2","42:10.6"]},{"q":"La mente es siempre creadora.","r":"42:12.9"},{"q":"El espíritu es el arquitecto, la mente es el constructor, el cuerpo es el edificio material.","r":"42:12.12"},{"x":"La mente domina a la materia y responde al supercontrol del espíritu, y solo la mente que sigue libremente la guía del espíritu puede sobrevivir más allá de la existencia mortal.","r":["42:12.15"]},{"x":"En el Paraíso las energías física, mental y espiritual son coordinadas, en Havona están coordinadas, y en los niveles absolutos el espíritu es claramente dominante.","r":["42:12.13"]}]}],"see":["Gravedad","Paraíso","Mente cósmica","Los tres Absolutos","Tiempo y espacio","Realidad"]},{"n":86,"t":"Enseñanzas de Jesús","en":"Teachings of Jesus","sum":"The teachings of Jesus are rooted in the simple gospel that God is the Father of all men and that men, recognizing by faith that they are his sons, become brothers to one another. The kingdom of heaven is not a political realm but a spiritual experience that begins within each person, and faith opens its door. Jesus gave the new commandment to love not merely as one loves oneself but as he loved, and he called people out of the religion of tradition and authority into the religion of the spirit that knows God directly.","sections":[{"h":"The Heart of the Gospel","items":[{"q":"«Dios es tu Padre, y la religión — mi evangelio — no es ni más ni menos que el reconocimiento creyente de la verdad de que tú eres su hijo.","r":"141:4.2"},{"x":"Jesus taught a new concept of God, not as a judge keeping a ledger of sins but as a Father who loves each person.","r":["141:4.1"]},{"x":"The kingdom of heaven is built on the truths of the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man, and this teaching frees man from age-old animal fears.","r":["170:2.1","170:2.2"]},{"x":"Jesus said that people of other ages would better understand the gospel if it were presented in terms of family relationships rather than of a kingdom.","r":["142:7.4"]},{"x":"His gospel delivered man from the superstition that he is a child of the devil and lifted him to the dignity of a faith son of God.","r":["194:2.1"]}]},{"h":"The Kingdom of Heaven","items":[{"x":"Jesus said the kingdom of heaven had nothing to do with earthly kingdoms or temporal governments, but the idea of a temporal king rooted deep in the Jewish mind was not easily removed.","r":["170:0.1"]},{"q":"En relación con el reino, sus últimas palabras siempre fueron: «el reino está dentro de vosotros».","r":"170:1.13"},{"x":"Simple, childlike faith is the key that opens the door of the kingdom; once inside, one must grow through the steps of righteousness.","r":["170:3.2"]},{"x":"God's forgiveness is actually experienced in the measure that a person forgives his fellows.","r":["170:3.3","170:3.4"]},{"x":"The kingdom is an evolutionary experience that begins on earth and advances through successive stages of life to Paradise.","r":["142:7.3"]}]},{"h":"Love and the New Commandment","items":[{"x":"Brotherly love is loving one's neighbor as oneself, but fatherly love is loving people as Jesus loved them.","r":["140:5.1"]},{"x":"Disciples should strive to see people as God sees them and so begin to show fatherly affection.","r":["140:5.3"]},{"q":"Que os améis los unos a los otros así como yo os he amado.","r":"180:1.1"},{"x":"The new commandment is not a new burden but meant to bring the new joy of sharing affection with one's fellows.","r":["180:1.2"]},{"x":"\"Resist not evil\" did not mean condoning sin but forgiving rather than retaliating against personal insults.","r":["141:3.8"]}]},{"h":"The Religion of the Spirit","items":[{"x":"Jesus said not to patch new teaching onto the old but to be born again like little children and make a fresh start.","r":["140:6.2"]},{"x":"The righteousness he required is not buying favor through alms, prayer, and fasting, but the desire to do the Father's will in love, mercy, and truth.","r":["140:6.3"]},{"x":"The greatest discovery a human soul can make is to find God within and to make that a fact of personal experience.","r":["155:6.3"]},{"q":"The religion of the mind ties you hopelessly to the past; the religion of the spirit consists in progressive revelation","r":"155:6.4"},{"x":"Jesus did not teach that all should think alike; believers are united in their diversity by the motive and goal of doing the Father's will.","r":["141:5.1","141:5.3"]},{"q":"He venido al mundo para proclamar la libertad espiritual, para que los mortales tengan la fuerza de vivir su vida individual con originalidad y libertad ante Dios.","r":"141:5.1"}]},{"h":"Ways of Spreading the Teaching","items":[{"x":"Always respect human personality, and never sweep people into the kingdom by overpowering them with logic, eloquence, fear, or sentiment.","r":["159:3.2"]},{"x":"The gospel restores self-respect to those who have lost it and restrains those who have too much.","r":["159:3.3"]},{"x":"The teaching to trust God is not passive fatalism; what Jesus opposed was not forethought but worry and anxiety.","r":["140:8.2","140:8.3"]},{"x":"His teaching was not the talk of a meek mystic but dynamic; he not only meant well but actually did good.","r":["141:3.6"]}]},{"h":"The Religion of Jesus","items":[{"q":"Podéis predicar una religión sobre Jesús, pero, por fuerza, debéis vivir la religión de Jesús.","r":"196:2.1"},{"x":"The gospel of the kingdom rests on Jesus' own religious experience, while Christianity rests mainly on Paul's.","r":["196:2.1"]},{"x":"As the Messiah of the kingdom became the Redeemer of the church, Jesus' teachings were transplanted from Jewish to gentile soil.","r":["170:5.3"]},{"x":"The Spirit of Truth restates Jesus' message anew for each generation, helping it remember and understand his teachings.","r":["194:2.1","194:2.5"]}]}],"see":["Reino del cielo","Filiación con Dios","Hermandad de los hombres","Parábolas","Carácter de Jesús","Fe"]},{"n":39,"t":"Espíritu de la Verdad","en":"Spirit of Truth","sum":"The Spirit of Truth is the Creator Son's own spirit, the Comforter, which he pours out upon all flesh after completing his bestowal career. On Urantia it was poured out at Pentecost as the spirit of Michael, preparing every normal mind to receive an Adjuster. This spirit teaches truth not as law or creed but as living conviction; it creates consciousness not of itself but of Michael, and it shows forth anew the life of Jesus in the lives of believers.","sections":[{"h":"The Bestowal Spirit of the Creator Son","items":[{"x":"Of the three spirit circuits of Nebadon, the first is the bestowal spirit of the Creator Son, the Spirit of Truth, the Comforter.","r":["34:4.2","15:9.12"]},{"q":"Este don del Confortador es la fuerza espiritual que siempre dirige a los buscadores de la verdad hacia Aquel que es la personificación de la verdad en el universo local.","r":"34:4.5"},{"x":"This spirit proceeds from the personality of the Son but is functionally focalized in the Divine Minister, so it works without hindrance wherever the Son may be.","r":["34:4.6","34:4.7"]},{"x":"In a sense the Spirit of Truth is the spirit of both the Universal Father and the Creator Son, and it is commonly regarded as the spirit of the Universe Son.","r":["194:2.3","194:2.16"]},{"x":"On Avonal bestowal worlds it comes as the joint spirit of the bestowal Avonal and the Creator Son, but after Michael's final bestowal it becomes more literally the spirit of Michael.","r":["52:5.6","20:6.8","20:6.9"]}]},{"h":"The Promise and Pentecost","items":[{"x":"Before departing, Jesus promised that, if the Father permitted, he would pour out the Spirit of Truth upon all flesh and send it as another teacher.","r":["180:4.1","180:4.2"]},{"q":"Dentro de muy poco tiempo os enviaré mi espíritu, tal como yo, excepto por este cuerpo material.","r":"180:4.5"},{"x":"Not only the one hundred and twenty in the upper chamber but every honest person in the world received this teacher according to his love of truth and his capacity for spiritual understanding.","r":["194:3.6"]},{"x":"The bestowal of the spirit was independent of forms, ceremonies, and sacred places; prayer did not bring the spirit, but it determined the capacity of the vessel that received it.","r":["194:3.10","194:3.20"]},{"x":"At that time the \"baptism of the spirit\" meant only the conscious reception and recognition of the gift of the Spirit of Truth.","r":["194:2.10"]},{"q":"since Pentecost, man is still searching for God, but there shines out over the world the spectacle of God also seeking for man and sending his spirit to dwell within him when he has found him.","r":"194:3.13"}]},{"h":"The Work of the Spirit of Truth","items":[{"q":"La primera misión de este espíritu es, por supuesto, fomentar y personalizar la verdad, puesto que la comprensión de la verdad es lo que constituye la forma más elevada de libertad humana.","r":"194:2.2"},{"x":"It also destroys the believer's feeling of orphanhood and helps him remember and understand the Master's words and reinterpret his life on earth.","r":["194:2.2","194:2.5"]},{"x":"Living within men, the Spirit of Truth restates the message of Jesus for each new generation in terms suited to its time.","r":["194:2.1"]},{"x":"This spirit teaches the truths of the Father's love and the Son's mercy, revealing the Father's spirit nature and the Son's moral character.","r":["194:3.1"]},{"q":"El Hijo Creador, en la carne, reveló Dios a los hombres; el Espíritu de la Verdad, en el corazón, revela el Hijo Creador a los hombres.","r":"194:3.1"},{"x":"This spirit creates no consciousness of itself, only consciousness of Michael, so its evidence is found in deepening communion with Michael.","r":["194:2.4"]}]},{"h":"Living Truth","items":[{"x":"The Spirit of Truth is not the letter or the law of truth but the conviction of its true meaning on spirit levels, a spirit that grows and unfolds of itself.","r":["180:5.1"]},{"q":"La verdad estática es verdad muerta, y sólo la verdad muerta puede ser contenida en una teoría.","r":"180:5.2"},{"x":"Without the insight of the Spirit of Truth the golden rule is only a rule of ethics; its true meaning appears when the spirit of the Son interprets the law of conduct to the spirit of the Father.","r":["180:5.5","180:5.8"]},{"x":"Love must pass through ever-new interpretations, readjusting itself under the guidance of the Spirit of Truth toward the highest good of the one loved.","r":["180:5.10"]},{"x":"The bestowed Spirit of Truth responds unerringly to truth, the living relationship in which all beings are attuned toward God.","r":["56:10.13","2:7.6"]}]},{"h":"Preparation and Guidance for the Adjuster","items":[{"x":"Until a bestowal Son releases the Spirit of Truth, not every normal mind is automatically prepared to receive an Adjuster.","r":["34:5.4","20:5.3","194:2.3"]},{"x":"The Spirit of Truth is poured out upon all flesh, but its function and power depend almost entirely on the degree to which a person personally receives it.","r":["34:5.5"]},{"x":"Spiritual philosophy, the wisdom of spirit realities, is the endowment of the Spirit of Truth given by the bestowal Sons.","r":["101:3.2"]},{"x":"Even when the ascender leaves his local universe, he is not wholly beyond the ministry of the Spirit of Truth, which points the way in every crisis of the ascent.","r":["117:5.9"]},{"q":"for in every dark hour, at every crossroad in the forward struggle, the Spirit of Truth will always speak, saying, \"This is the way.\"","r":"34:7.8"}]}],"see":["Hijo Creador Micael","Pentecostés","Espíritu Santo","Verdad","Autootorgamiento de Jesús","Ajustador del Pensamiento"]},{"n":5,"t":"Espíritu Infinito","en":"Infinite Spirit","sum":"El Espíritu Infinito es la tercera persona de la Deidad, el Actor Conjunto y Creador Conjunto, que vino a la existencia en el momento en que el Padre y el Hijo concibieron una acción unida. Como ejecutivo de la asociación entre el Padre y el Hijo, es la fuente de la mente, el manipulador de la energía y el espíritu omnipresente que otorga a todas las criaturas el amor del Padre y la misericordia del Hijo. Sus numerosos hijos espirituales forman la escalera viviente por la que los mortales suben al Paraíso.","sections":[{"h":"El Dios de Acción","items":[{"x":"En el mismo momento en que el Padre y el Hijo concibieron juntos una acción infinita, la ejecución de un plan-pensamiento absoluto, el Espíritu Infinito surgió a la existencia completa.","r":["8:0.3"]},{"x":"Este orden de origen es solo una explicación para ayudar a la comprensión humana; los tres han existido desde la eternidad, sin principio ni fin.","r":["8:0.4"]},{"x":"El Espíritu Infinito prometió lealtad eterna al Padre y reconoció su dependencia eterna del Hijo, y así vino a la existencia la Trinidad del Paraíso.","r":["8:1.2","8:1.3"]},{"x":"El Espíritu Infinito quedó eternizado con el nacimiento del universo central de Havona, y por este acto creador conjunto llegó a ser el Creador Conjunto eterno.","r":["8:1.7"]},{"q":"Brevemente, el Espíritu Infinito atestigua que, puesto que él es eterno, así también el universo central es eterno.","r":"8:1.9"}]},{"h":"Naturaleza y posición","items":[{"x":"Se le conoce por muchos nombres, entre ellos el Espíritu Universal, el Creador Conjunto, la Mente Infinita, el Espíritu de los Espíritus y el Actor Conjunto, y en Urantia a veces se le confunde con la mente cósmica.","r":["8:2.2"]},{"x":"El Espíritu Infinito comparte la perfección, la rectitud y el amor del Padre, pero se inclina hacia la misericordia del Hijo Eterno y llega a ser el ministro de la misericordia de las Deidades del Paraíso.","r":["8:2.6"]},{"x":"Tras la personalización de la Tercera Fuente, el Padre ya no participa personalmente en la creación del universo; confía al Hijo todo lo que puede, y el Hijo a su vez al Creador Conjunto.","r":["8:3.2"]},{"q":"El Hijo Eterno es la única vía de acceso al Padre Universal, y el Espíritu Infinito es el único medio de alcanzar al Hijo Eterno.","r":"8:3.7"},{"x":"El Espíritu Infinito es la primera Deidad del Paraíso a la que llegan los peregrinos ascendentes en el centro de todas las cosas.","r":["8:3.8"]}]},{"h":"El Espíritu ministrante","items":[{"q":"God is love, the Son is mercy, the Spirit is ministry","r":"8:4.2"},{"x":"En el universo local, por medio del Espíritu Materno, su Hija Creativa, se une al Hijo Creador para fomentar la ascensión espiritual de las criaturas materiales.","r":["8:4.4"]},{"x":"El Espíritu no desciende en la carne, pero se somete gustoso a una serie de atenuaciones de la divinidad hasta que por fin está a nuestro lado, como los ángeles, para guiarnos en nuestro camino terrenal.","r":["8:4.5"]},{"x":"Nuestro universo se forja entre el yunque de la justicia y el martillo del sufrimiento, pero quienes manejan el martillo son los seres de la misericordia, los hijos del Espíritu Infinito.","r":["9:1.8"]},{"x":"Las personalidades espirituales del Espíritu Infinito forman la escalera viviente por la que el hombre mortal sube del caos a la gloria.","r":["9:8.25"]}]},{"h":"El Espíritu omnipresente de Dios","items":[{"x":"El atributo sobresaliente del Espíritu Infinito es la omnipresencia; comparte la omnisciencia del Padre, pero es omnipotente solo en el dominio de la mente.","r":["8:5.1","9:1.5"]},{"x":"El Espíritu Santo es el circuito espiritual distintivo que la Hija Creativa del Espíritu Infinito extiende sobre cada universo local, mientras que el Espíritu Infinito mismo está presente en todas partes.","r":["8:5.3"]},{"q":"Existen muchas influencias espirituales, y todas son como una.","r":"8:5.4"},{"x":"Aunque de origen distinto, el Ajustador, el espíritu del Hijo Eterno y la presencia del Espíritu Infinito cooperan perfectamente en la mente y el alma del hombre, y actúan como un solo espíritu.","r":["8:5.4","9:2.5"]}]},{"h":"Manipulador de la energía y mente absoluta","items":[{"x":"El Creador Conjunto no es la energía misma, sino el manipulador de la energía, y posee el poder de la antigravedad, que no se observa ni en el Padre ni en el Hijo.","r":["9:3.2","9:3.5"]},{"q":"El Paraíso es el modelo original de infinidad; el Dios de Acción es el activador de ese modelo.","r":"9:3.8"},{"x":"La mente de las criaturas se origina únicamente en la Tercera Fuente, y ni siquiera un fragmento del Padre puede morar en el hombre hasta que el Espíritu Infinito ha preparado el camino de la mente.","r":["9:5.2"]},{"x":"Que la fuente de la mente sea divina no hace divino todo fenómeno mental; el intelecto humano tiene sus raíces en orígenes animales.","r":["9:5.5"]},{"x":"Así como el Padre atrae a toda personalidad y el Hijo a todo espíritu, el Actor Conjunto atrae a toda mente mediante el circuito de gravedad de la mente.","r":["9:6.2"]}]},{"h":"Una verdadera personalidad","items":[{"x":"El Espíritu Infinito es una presencia universal, un poder y la mente universal, y más aún; pero es al mismo tiempo una personalidad verdadera y divina.","r":["8:6.1"]},{"x":"El Espíritu Infinito tiene voluntad además de mente; su amor y sus pesares son reales, y reacciona ante el universo como una persona.","r":["8:6.3","8:6.4"]},{"q":"therefore \"Grieve not the Spirit of God.\"","r":"8:6.4"},{"x":"En el Espíritu Infinito el Padre y el Hijo están mutuamente presentes, siempre en perfección no cualificada.","r":["8:6.7"]}]}],"see":["Padre Universal","Hijo Eterno","Espíritu Materno del Universo Local","Mente cósmica","Siete Espíritus Rectores","Espíritu Santo"]},{"n":23,"t":"Espíritu Materno del Universo Local","en":"Local Universe Mother Spirit","sum":"El Espíritu Materno del universo local es la Hija Creativa individualizada por el Espíritu Infinito para cada universo local, la compañera coordinada que construye el universo, hace surgir la vida y gobierna junto con el Hijo Creador. En Nebadon se la llama la Ministra Divina, y por medio del aliento de vida, de los siete espíritus ayudantes de la mente y del Espíritu Santo otorga mente y espíritu a todas las criaturas. Así como Micael actúa como padre, ella desempeña el papel de madre: nunca coacciona, sino que guía suavemente a los hombres por el camino de la filiación.","sections":[{"h":"La Hija del Espíritu Infinito en el universo local","items":[{"x":"Cuando un Hijo Creador es personalizado, el Espíritu Infinito individualiza una representación nueva y única de sí mismo para que salga al espacio con él como su compañera.","r":["34:0.1","17:6.3"]},{"x":"Los Espíritus Maternos del Universo reciben una formación prepersonal en los mundos de Havona, donde aprenden a cooperar con los Hijos del Paraíso bajo la voluntad del Padre.","r":["14:6.32"]},{"q":"She volunteered to accompany Michael on the occasion of his liberation from Paradise obligations","r":"33:3.2"},{"x":"El Espíritu Materno de Nebadon es el número 611.121 del sexto grupo de Espíritus Supremos, y ha creado y gobernado este universo junto con Micael.","r":["33:3.2"]},{"x":"Cuando un Hijo Creador parte hacia el espacio, la proclamación del Padre Universal de la unión eterna de ambos es uno de los acontecimientos más conmovedores del Paraíso.","r":["17:6.5"]}]},{"h":"La personalización y las etapas de su carrera","items":[{"x":"Cuando Micael proclama la creación de la vida, se produce en el Paraíso una «erupción primaria», y en ese momento el Espíritu Creativo se convierte en un ser personal, la Ministra Divina.","r":["34:1.1","17:6.7"]},{"x":"El Espíritu Materno personalizado adquiere una naturaleza personal teñida de la naturaleza del Espíritu Rector que preside ese superuniverso.","r":["34:1.3"]},{"x":"En la etapa de la creación física, el Hijo del Universo proporciona el modelo y el Espíritu del Universo materializa estas creaciones energéticas en sustancia física.","r":["34:0.3"]},{"x":"Cuando Micael regresó de su séptimo autootorgamiento, el Espíritu Materno le prometió su subordinación, y Micael la estableció como cogobernante.","r":["33:3.5","33:3.6","17:6.8"]},{"q":"the Son published to the worlds the fact of the Spirit's equality with him in all endowments of personality and attributes of divine character.","r":"33:3.6"},{"x":"Esta «Proclamación de Igualdad» es el modelo trascendente para la organización de la familia y del gobierno, y el alto ideal del hogar humano y del matrimonio voluntario.","r":["33:3.6"]}]},{"h":"Madre de la vida y de las personalidades espirituales","items":[{"x":"Cuando los Portadores de Vida han preparado los cuerpos físicos, el Espíritu del Universo aporta «el aliento de vida», que activa los modelos sin vida y les imparte el poder de reproducirse.","r":["34:2.5","36:6.3"]},{"x":"Micael y el Espíritu Materno son literalmente el padre-hijo y la madre-espíritu de todas las criaturas nativas de Nebadon.","r":["37:0.1"]},{"q":"Such a Divine Minister is in reality the mother of spirits and spirit personalities, the ever-present and all-wise adviser of the Creator Son","r":"33:3.3"},{"x":"Los serafines fueron creados como la primera reproducción espiritual solitaria del Espíritu Materno, y su actividad creadora nunca cesa a medida que Nebadon crece.","r":["38:1.1","38:1.3"]},{"x":"Cuando surge una rebelión, solo el Hijo puede actuar como salvador, pero el Espíritu siempre lo sostiene en todo lo que padece.","r":["33:3.4"]}]},{"h":"El ministerio de la mente y del espíritu","items":[{"q":"Está igualmente y difusamente presente a través de su entero universo local y está, en consecuencia, tan literal y personalmente presente en un mundo como en cualquiera otro.","r":"34:3.3"},{"x":"Los siete espíritus ayudantes de la mente son creados por la Ministra Divina y se llaman espíritus de la sabiduría, la adoración, el consejo, el conocimiento, el valor, la comprensión y la intuición.","r":["34:4.10"]},{"x":"En cuanto una mente llega al nivel en que recibe a los ayudantes de la adoración y de la sabiduría, queda incluida en el circuito espiritual de la Ministra Divina, el ministerio del Espíritu Santo.","r":["34:5.3","36:5.15"]},{"x":"El Espíritu Materno nunca sale de Salvington, y como está fijo allí, el Espíritu de la Verdad funciona independientemente de dónde se encuentre Micael.","r":["34:4.7"]},{"q":"El Espíritu Materno del Universo actúa como centro y foco universal del Espíritu de la Verdad, así como también del de su propia influencia personal: el Espíritu Santo.","r":"34:4.7"},{"x":"La presencia conjunta del Espíritu Santo, del Espíritu de la Verdad y del Ajustador en un mismo mortal es una simetría de dotación espiritual que aporta la conciencia de la filiación con Dios.","r":["34:5.7"]}]},{"h":"El Espíritu en acción en el hombre","items":[{"q":"From the heights of eternal glory the divine Spirit descends, by a long series of steps, to meet you as you are and where you are","r":"34:6.3"},{"x":"El ministerio del Espíritu Santo es en parte independiente de la actitud del hombre, pero cuanto más plenamente sigue el hombre la guía divina, más eficaz se vuelve para santificar la vida interior.","r":["34:5.5"]},{"q":"El Espíritu nunca impulsa, sólo guía.","r":"34:6.11"},{"x":"Entre la naturaleza animal y los impulsos espirituales, los espíritus combinados ayudan al hombre durante toda la vida a someter cada vez más la carne a la guía del espíritu.","r":["34:6.9"]}]}],"see":["Hijo Creador Micael","Espíritu Infinito","Espíritus ayudantes de la mente","Espíritu Santo","Espíritu de la Verdad","Serafines"]},{"n":40,"t":"Espíritu Santo","en":"Holy Spirit","sum":"The Holy Spirit is the spirit circuit, and the personal influence, that the local universe Mother Spirit, the Divine Minister, extends throughout her universe. Proceeding from the Creative Daughter of the Paradise Infinite Spirit, it is indigenous to that local universe and bound to her personal presence on Salvington. A mind in which the adjutants of worship and wisdom function is soon encircuited in it; this is the first supermind endowment man receives and the foundation for receiving the Adjuster.","sections":[{"h":"The Spirit Circuit of the Mother Spirit","items":[{"q":"El Espíritu Santo es el circuito espiritual de esta Hija Creadora del Espíritu Infinito del Paraíso.","r":"8:5.3"},{"x":"The Holy Spirit is a circuit indigenous to each local universe and confined to the spiritual realm of that creation, whereas the Infinite Spirit is everywhere present.","r":["8:5.3"]},{"x":"In the sacred writings the term \"Spirit of God\" seems to refer interchangeably to the Infinite Spirit on Paradise and the Creative Spirit of the local universe.","r":["8:5.3"]},{"x":"Of the three spirit circuits of Nebadon, the second is the spirit circuit of the Divine Minister, the Holy Spirit.","r":["34:4.3","15:9.13"]},{"x":"As the spirit of the Infinite Spirit and of the Universe Mother Spirit, the Holy Spirit is often regarded as the spirit of the Universe Spirit, the \"spirit of spirit\" in the threefold spirit endowment.","r":["194:2.17","194:2.11"]},{"x":"Mortals too can know the presence of the Infinite Spirit, for they actually experience his grace working through the Holy Spirit bestowed by the local universe.","r":["9:2.5"]}]},{"h":"A Presence Bound to Salvington","items":[{"q":"El Espíritu Santo de la Ministra Divina dejaría de funcionar si su presencia personal saliera de Salvington.","r":"34:4.7"},{"x":"The Mother Spirit never leaves the universe headquarters world, and she acts as the universe focus not only of her Holy Spirit but also of the Spirit of Truth.","r":["34:4.7"]},{"x":"The Holy Spirit and the Spirit of Truth go out from the local universe headquarters and, with the ministry of the adjutant mind-spirits, reach the lower levels of material mind.","r":["56:3.3"]},{"x":"Because the Holy Spirit \"searches all things,\" the Mother Spirit on Salvington knows mortals fully.","r":["28:5.22"]}]},{"h":"The First Supermind Endowment","items":[{"q":"Man's first supermind endowment is that of personality encircuitment in the Holy Spirit of the Universe Creative Spirit;","r":"103:0.1"},{"x":"This influence functions long before the bestowals of the divine Sons or the universal bestowal of the Adjusters, enlarging man's view of ethics, religion, and spirituality.","r":["103:0.1"]},{"q":"El Espíritu Santo — éste es el don inicial de la supermente, e infaliblemente aparece en toda verdadera personalidad humana.","r":"92:0.4"},{"x":"This ministry to a mind that craves worship and desires wisdom creates the capacity to realize human survival both as a concept and as actual experience.","r":["92:0.4"]},{"x":"A mind in which the adjutants of worship and wisdom function is at once included in the spiritual circuit of the Divine Minister.","r":["34:5.3","36:5.15"]},{"x":"A mind ministered by the Holy Spirit has the capacity to choose the Adjuster, and the Adjuster enters only after the preparation of the adjutants and encircuitment in the Holy Spirit.","r":["34:5.4","108:2.2","110:6.13"]}]},{"h":"Inner Ministry and the Fruits of the Spirit","items":[{"x":"Spiritual reason, the intelligence of the soul, is the endowment of the Holy Spirit, the gift of the Creative Spirit to man.","r":["101:3.2"]},{"x":"The Holy Spirit works partly independently of human attitude and partly according to the co-operation of the will, sanctifying the inner life of one who fully follows its leading.","r":["34:5.5"]},{"q":"La semilla de la verdad teórica está muerta, los más altos conceptos morales no tienen vigencia, a menos que, y hasta que, el Espíritu divino infunda inspiración sobre las formas de la verdad y estimule las fórmulas de la rectitud.","r":"34:6.6"},{"q":"El Espíritu nunca impulsa, sólo guía.","r":"34:6.11"},{"x":"In a life led by the spirit, the fruits of the spirit such as love, joy, and peace appear, and the kingdom of God is righteousness, peace, and joy in the Holy Spirit.","r":["34:6.13","137:8.9"]},{"x":"On worlds settled in light and life, the ministry of the Holy Spirit and the angels becomes ever more effective as the ages pass.","r":["55:6.4"]}]},{"h":"Oneness with Other Spirit Ministries","items":[{"x":"Man possesses no separate part of the Creator Son or the Mother Spirit; these ministries do not indwell the mind as the Adjuster does.","r":["34:5.6"]},{"x":"The presence in mortals of the Holy Spirit, the Spirit of Truth, and the Adjuster is a symmetry of spiritual endowment that qualifies them to realize sonship with God.","r":["34:5.7"]},{"q":"Sea cual fuese su pluralidad de origen, todas las experiencias espirituales son una en su función.","r":"34:6.2"},{"x":"The three supermortal endowments, the Adjuster, the Spirit of Truth, and the Holy Spirit, are unified in human experience as the ministry of the Supreme.","r":["101:2.12","113:4.6"]},{"x":"The ascender uses spirit circuits such as the Holy Spirit but does not possess them, and these circuits convey to the Supreme the values emerging in the personality.","r":["117:5.8"]}]}],"see":["Espíritu Materno del Universo Local","Espíritu Infinito","Espíritus ayudantes de la mente","Espíritu de la Verdad","Ajustador del Pensamiento","Reino del cielo"]},{"n":38,"t":"Espíritus ayudantes de la mente","en":"Adjutant Mind-Spirits","sum":"The seven adjutant mind-spirits are circuits of mind ministry created by the local universe Mother Spirit and named the spirits of intuition, understanding, courage, knowledge, counsel, worship, and wisdom. More like circuits than independent personalities, they act on animal and human minds that can learn by experience, conditioning evolution so that it proceeds purposefully rather than by accident. When the adjutants of worship and wisdom begin to function, mind crosses the threshold of spiritual ministry and is prepared to receive the circuit of the Holy Spirit and the Thought Adjuster.","sections":[{"h":"The Mind Circuits of the Mother Spirit","items":[{"x":"The seven adjutant mind-spirits were created by the Divine Minister of the local universe; alike in character but diverse in power, they can hardly be regarded as personalities apart from their mother.","r":["34:4.10"]},{"x":"Of the three spirit circuits of Nebadon, the third is the intelligence-ministry circuit of the seven adjutant mind-spirits.","r":["34:4.4"]},{"q":"Los siete espíritus ayudantes de la mente siempre acompañan a los Portadores de Vida a un nuevo planeta, pero no deben ser considerados como entidades; son más bien como circuitos.","r":"36:5.4"},{"x":"They are in fact a level of consciousness of the Divine Minister and are always subordinate to the action and presence of their creative mother.","r":["36:5.4"]},{"x":"The adjutants grow in function through experience, yet they never become personal beings.","r":["36:5.13"]},{"x":"This ministry emanates from the local universe headquarters, but the actual direction of the lower levels of mind function is centered at the system capitals.","r":["65:7.1"]},{"x":"In the early stages of evolution the mortal races climb the grades of intelligence as they progressively make contact with the seven adjutant mind-spirits of the Mother Spirit.","r":["194:2.12","194:2.18"]}]},{"h":"The Names and Functions of the Seven Adjutants","items":[{"x":"The spirit of intuition gives quick perception, reflex instincts, and the sense of direction, and it is the only adjutant that makes extensive contact with the mechanical levels of mind.","r":["36:5.6","34:4.12"]},{"x":"The spirit of understanding is the gift of spontaneously associating and co-ordinating ideas, shown in quick reasoning and prompt decision.","r":["36:5.7"]},{"q":"El espíritu de valor — la dotación de fidelidad— en los seres personales, la base de la adquisición del carácter y la raíz intelectual de la fibra moral e intrepidez espiritual.","r":"36:5.8"},{"x":"The spirit of knowledge is the mother of the curiosity that leads to adventure and discovery, and the spirit of counsel is the urge to social co-operation that brings harmony with one's fellows.","r":["36:5.9","36:5.10"]},{"q":"La adoración es la insignia de la candidatura a la ascensión espiritual.","r":"36:5.11"},{"q":"Éste es el más elevado de los ayudantes, el espíritu coordinador y articulador de la tarea de todos los demás.","r":"36:5.12"},{"x":"When knowledge is elevated to new levels of meaning and activated by the presence of the adjutant of wisdom, it becomes wisdom.","r":["180:5.3"]}]},{"h":"A Ministry That Guides Evolution","items":[{"x":"Because the presence of the adjutant mind-spirits conditions organic evolution, evolution is purposeful rather than accidental.","r":["36:5.1"]},{"x":"The adjutants do not contact purely mechanical responses; they begin to minister the moment the capacity to learn by experience appears.","r":["65:7.5","65:7.6"]},{"x":"They are not concerned with physical evolution, yet they mesh with it so perfectly that man sees in mind phenomena only the workings of nature.","r":["65:7.2"]},{"x":"Because of Urantia's unique life pattern, the lower adjutants had greater difficulty in making contact here than almost anywhere else in Nebadon.","r":["65:7.3","65:7.4"]},{"x":"Since the functioning of the first five adjutants in the animal stage is essential to human intellect, animals are indispensable to the intellectual evolution of man as well.","r":["36:5.13"]},{"x":"The central focus at Life Carrier headquarters registers the function of the first five adjutants, but the quantitative activity of worship and wisdom is registered in the presence of the Mother Spirit on Salvington.","r":["36:5.3"]},{"x":"The work of the Mother Spirit is done chiefly through the seven adjutants, the spirits of promise, always leading mankind toward higher thoughts and ideals.","r":["34:5.2"]}]},{"h":"The Threshold of Spiritual Ministry","items":[{"q":"Los ayudantes funcionan exclusivamente en la evolución de la mente experiencial, hasta el nivel de la sexta fase, el espíritu de adoración.","r":"65:7.7"},{"x":"When mind becomes able to receive the adjutants of worship and wisdom, the mortal first experiences the ministry of spirit joined with mind.","r":["34:5.3"]},{"x":"Creature mind before it recognizes and worships divinity is the exclusive domain of the adjutants, but as soon as spiritual response appears, it becomes supermind.","r":["36:5.15"]},{"x":"The adjutants are not directly concerned with the highly spiritual functions of the Holy Spirit, but in evolutionary man they prepare the way ahead of the appearance of that spirit.","r":["36:5.16"]},{"q":"Y se requiere la función coordinada de los siete ayudantes para cualificar así a la mente humana para la recepción de un Ajustador.","r":"108:2.2"},{"x":"All genuinely religious reactions of man are sponsored by the adjutant of worship and censored by the adjutant of wisdom.","r":["103:0.1"]}]}],"see":["Espíritu Materno del Universo Local","Mente","Espíritu Santo","Portadores de Vida","Evolución","Ajustador del Pensamiento"]},{"n":94,"t":"Evolución","en":"Evolution","sum":"In The Urantia Book evolution is not a chance process but the divine technique by which the universes of time and space progressively grow. Life implanted by the Life Carriers advanced, under the ministry of the physical controllers and the adjutant mind-spirits, from the protoplasm of the seas to human beings with will, and society, religion, and government have followed the same evolutionary path. All this growth is bound up with the evolution of the Supreme Being and moves at last toward the age of light and life.","sections":[{"h":"The Evolving Universe","items":[{"q":"Estos universos del tiempo y del espacio son todos evolucionarios.","r":"32:0.2"},{"x":"Unlike Havona, which was created perfect, growth is the characteristic of the grand universe and the mark of experiential Deity.","r":["116:0.3"]},{"x":"The confusion and inequality of Urantia show that this world is the work of subabsolute Creators who are not yet perfect.","r":["116:0.2"]},{"x":"Continuing evolution corrects nature, increasing the share of Paradise perfection and decreasing that of evil, error, and disharmony.","r":["4:2.4"]},{"x":"We evolve in God the Supreme, and he also evolves in us.","r":["31:10.12"]}]},{"h":"Plan, Not Chance","items":[{"q":"Puede que la evolución cósmica no sea siempre comprensible (pronosticable), pero es estrictamente planeada, no accidental.","r":"49:1.1"},{"x":"Urantia was a life-experiment world, but the establishment of life was not an experiment in the sense of the haphazard or accidental.","r":["65:4.1","65:4.2"]},{"x":"Features of human existence such as cells that heal their own wounds show that life was intelligently planned.","r":["65:4.3"]},{"q":"La física y la química solas no pueden explicar cómo el ser humano evolucionó a partir del protoplasma primitivo de los primeros mares.","r":"65:6.8"},{"x":"In every living thing dwells an innate, unsatisfied longing for greater perfection.","r":["65:6.2"]}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Life","items":[{"x":"Material life arises from the cooperation of a threefold creativity: the physical controllers, the Seven Master Spirits, and the Life Carriers.","r":["65:0.1"]},{"x":"The development of life passes through three stages: physical energy, the mind ministry of the adjutant spirits, and spiritual endowment completed by the Adjuster bestowal.","r":["65:0.2","65:0.5"]},{"x":"The primitive ancestors of mankind were the mud of the warm bays and lagoons of ancient inland seas, and the transition from plant to animal occurred 450,000,000 years ago.","r":["65:2.1","58:6.1"]},{"x":"New species appear suddenly as fully developed new orders, not by the accumulation of small variations.","r":["58:6.3"]},{"x":"About a million years ago the immediate ancestors of mankind came from a lemur type of mammal through three successive sudden mutations.","r":["62:0.1"]},{"x":"The Life Carriers complete their work when beings with will appear, and thereafter they cannot interfere with will.","r":["36:3.8"]}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Mind and Spirit","items":[{"x":"As life rises higher, the adjutant mind-spirits act one by one, and mind becomes ever more coordinating, creative, and integrating.","r":["65:6.7","62:6.3"]},{"x":"Biologic evolution finally reached the dignity of human will, and Urantia was recognized as a planet of human habitation 993,408 years ago.","r":["62:7.7"]},{"q":"En los laboratorios evolucionarios cósmicos, la mente siempre domina la materia, y el espíritu siempre está correlacionado con la mente.","r":"65:8.5"},{"x":"Spiritual progress depends on mental expansion and is slowed by intellectual retardation, yet the soul can evolve regardless of the cultural level of the mind.","r":["65:8.4"]},{"x":"Evolution seems long because creatures make their own lifespan the measure of time.","r":["65:8.2","65:8.3"]}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Society and Religion","items":[{"x":"Like marriage, industry, and religion, civil government is a product of gradual evolution.","r":["70:5.1"]},{"x":"Early evolution is marked by the survival of the fittest, but later civilization advances better through intelligent cooperation and spiritual brotherhood.","r":["71:5.3"]},{"x":"Until the Planetary Prince arrives, religion is wholly an evolutionary process; thereafter evolution and revelation advance religion together.","r":["52:2.3"]},{"x":"Attempts to overturn the mores by revolution are fatal to civilization, for the mores are the thread of continuity that has held civilization together.","r":["68:4.6"]},{"q":"La evolución puede ser retrasada pero no puede ser detenida.","r":"81:0.1"}]},{"h":"The Purpose of Evolution","items":[{"x":"The march of the universes has a great and glorious purpose, and none of the struggles of mortals is in vain.","r":["32:5.1"]},{"q":"Los acontecimientos del tiempo y las luchas de la existencia material no son otra cosa que el andamio transitorio que tiende un puente hacia el otro lado, hacia la tierra prometida de la realidad espiritual y la existencia celestial.","r":"32:5.2"},{"x":"The final attainment of an evolutionary world is the age of light and life, and the achievements of settled worlds alone justify the creation of man.","r":["55:0.1","55:6.9"]}]}],"see":["Portadores de Vida","Espíritus ayudantes de la mente","Ser Supremo","Luz y vida","Urantia","Civilización"]},{"n":99,"t":"Experiencia","en":"Experience","sum":"In The Urantia Book experience is the way the evolutionary universe lives and the source of its growth. Paradise and Havona are existentially perfect, but the creatures of time and space and the Supreme Being become perfect through experience. Even a Creator Son earned his sovereignty by experience, and the Adjuster too accumulates experience together with man. Above all, the personal religious experience of knowing God remains true and valid even when theology and philosophy waver, and it transforms people and leads them to service.","sections":[{"h":"What Is Experience?","items":[{"q":"Es simplemente cualquier interacción entre un yo activo e interrogante y cualquier otra realidad activa y externa.","r":"102:4.2"},{"x":"The mass of experience is determined by depth of concept and totality of recognition of external reality, and its fact is found in other things, minds, and spirits.","r":["102:4.2"]},{"x":"Man experiences matter in his mind and spiritual reality in his soul, but it is the mind that is conscious of this experience.","r":["103:6.6"]},{"q":"Without experience, no evolutionary creature could even exist","r":"106:9.2"}]},{"h":"Existential and Experiential Perfection","items":[{"x":"Paradise Deity is existential, but the emerging Supreme and Ultimate are experiential.","r":["0:4.9"]},{"x":"The Father has achieved existential expression in the Son and the Spirit and is now achieving experiential expression as God the Supreme, Ultimate, and Absolute.","r":["0:7.6"]},{"x":"The perfection of the creatures of time, though mixed with grace, is a true personal possession gained through personal effort and actual living.","r":["32:3.9"]},{"x":"The experiential nature of evolutionary personalities is the natural complement of the ever-perfect nature of the Paradise-Havona creatures.","r":["32:3.12"]},{"x":"The experience of every evolving creature personality is a phase of the experience of the Almighty Supreme.","r":["116:1.1"]}]},{"h":"The Good Fortune of Starting at the Bottom","items":[{"x":"Animal evolutionary origin is no stigma on any personality; there is greater honor for those who have climbed the ladder of life from the very bottom.","r":["32:3.10"]},{"x":"It would have been easy for the Father to make all mortals perfect from the start, but that would deprive them of the adventure and training of the long, gradual ascent.","r":["32:3.11"]},{"q":"an experience to be had only by those who are so fortunate as to begin at the very bottom of living existence.","r":"32:3.11"},{"x":"The mortal career, the evolution of the soul, is not so much a probation as an education.","r":["111:3.5"]}]},{"h":"The Experience of Divine Beings","items":[{"x":"Michael was born a creator, yet his sovereignty had to be earned through the experience of seven bestowals.","r":["119:8.2"]},{"x":"All the human experiences Jesus passed through became the eternal possession of the Universe Sovereign, making him an experienced sovereign.","r":["127:6.13"]},{"x":"Virgin Adjusters too must gain experience while the mortal creature grows, rehearsing in advance the techniques of the next stage of life.","r":["109:0.1"]},{"x":"A Personalized Adjuster possesses as an eternal endowment all the experience gained while indwelling various mortal minds.","r":["109:6.2"]}]},{"h":"Religious Experience","items":[{"q":"La experiencia religiosa es la realización de la conciencia de haber encontrado a Dios.","r":"102:3.4"},{"q":"Son vuestros pensamientos los que os conducen hacia Dios.","r":"101:1.3"},{"x":"Religion may be accompanied by feeling but is not itself the experience of feeling, and the conditions that induce mystic experience rather show its dangers.","r":["101:5.9","100:5.10"]},{"x":"Though theology and philosophy may be distorted, the spiritual experience of personal religion remains true and valid.","r":["103:9.1"]},{"x":"The experience of God-consciousness is the same in every generation, but philosophic concepts and theologic definitions of God must change with knowledge.","r":["5:5.12"]},{"x":"Religious experience results in a certain consciousness of God and an unquestioned assurance of the survival of personality.","r":["101:1.6"]}]},{"h":"The Fruits of Experience","items":[{"q":"LA EXPERIENCIA de una vida religiosa dinámica transforma al individuo mediocre en una personalidad de poder idealista.","r":"100:0.1"},{"x":"One who has found God is impelled by overflowing goodness to serve his fellows; true religion leads to increased social service.","r":["102:3.4"]},{"x":"The senses reveal the existence of things and the mind their meaning, but spiritual experience reveals the true values of life.","r":["100:4.4"]},{"x":"Faith always triumphs over doubt, for experience is superior to theory, and spiritual reality to isolated facts.","r":["102:6.7"]},{"x":"The Adjuster restores only the memories and experiences needed for the universe career; many memories without spiritual meaning perish with the brain.","r":["112:5.22"]}]}],"see":["Experiencia religiosa","Ser Supremo","Crecimiento","Realidad","Fe","Búsqueda de la perfección"]},{"n":54,"t":"Experiencia religiosa","en":"Religious Experience","sum":"Religious experience is the personal experience of living knowledge of God and supreme values under the guidance of the indwelling spirit. It is neither a reasoned system of belief nor a mystic ecstasy; it sprouts from moral consciousness and grows through faith and insight. However erroneous one's theology, the experience itself can be genuine, and its certainty cannot be refuted. Religious experience culminates in a certain consciousness of God and assurance of survival.","sections":[{"h":"The Nature of Religious Experience","items":[{"x":"True religion is neither a philosophic system proved by reason nor a mystic ecstasy enjoyed by a favored few.","r":["101:1.1"]},{"q":"Son vuestros pensamientos los que os conducen hacia Dios.","r":"101:1.3"},{"x":"Religion is not the search for new facts but the discovery of new spiritual meanings in facts already known.","r":["101:1.4"]},{"x":"The religious tendency is innate and universal; it is fostered by the spirit of worship and censored by the spirit of wisdom.","r":["103:0.1","103:0.2"]},{"x":"The experience of realizing spiritual values is superideational and hard to express in human language; it is called God-consciousness.","r":["103:1.6"]}]},{"h":"Where Experience Begins","items":[{"x":"Every person early experiences conflict between selfish and altruistic urges, and in its resolution may first experience God-consciousness.","r":["103:2.4"]},{"x":"When a moral being makes an unselfish choice against the urge to be selfish, that is primitive religious experience.","r":["103:2.8"]},{"x":"It is right to identify altruistic desire with an influence outside oneself, with God, for it comes from the indwelling Adjuster.","r":["103:2.10"]},{"x":"Religious \"birth\" is usually gradual, though there is a day of spirit rebirth; those who grow without crisis and those who pass through crisis should not disparage one another.","r":["103:2.1","103:2.2"]},{"q":"Cuando un ser moral elige ser altruista, cuando se enfrenta al impulso a ser egoísta, se trata de una experiencia religiosa primitiva.","r":"103:2.8"}]},{"h":"Conversion and Mysticism","items":[{"x":"Religious growth moves from stagnation to adjustment, from insecurity to faith, and from the bondage of fear to the liberty of sonship.","r":["100:5.2"]},{"x":"God-consciousness may grow gradually or arrive in a dramatic moment, as with Paul on the Damascus road.","r":["100:5.3"]},{"q":"But emotion alone is a false conversion; one must have faith as well as feeling.","r":"100:5.5"},{"x":"Rather than seeking conversion, living faith, sincere worship, and unselfish prayer are a better way of approach to the Adjuster.","r":["100:5.7"]},{"x":"Trances and visions should not be sought as religious experience, and Jesus never resorted to such methods.","r":["100:5.8","100:5.11"]}]},{"h":"Experience and Theology","items":[{"x":"Religion begins with the quest for values, and systems of interpretive belief come later, so people agree more readily on values than on creeds.","r":["103:1.4"]},{"q":"Aunque la propia teología sea ilusoria y errónea, la propia religión puede ser totalmente genuina y eternamente verdadera.","r":"103:9.2"},{"q":"Cuando la teología domina la religión, la religión muere; se torna una doctrina en vez de una vida.","r":"103:9.6"},{"x":"Knowing the varied religious experiences of others keeps one's own religion from becoming selfish and narrow.","r":["103:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Fruits and Certainty of Experience","items":[{"x":"True religion is a living love and a life of service; it takes nothing away from a person and adds new meaning to all of life.","r":["100:6.5"]},{"x":"A remarkable trait of the religious life is a peace that passes all understanding, unshaken by any disappointment.","r":["100:6.6"]},{"x":"Religion rests on the Adjuster-derived postulate that God is knowable and attainable.","r":["103:9.8"]},{"x":"The reality of religious experience is proportional to its spiritual content; its certainties are unassailable and its devotion beyond question.","r":["103:9.12"]},{"x":"Religious experience culminates in a sure consciousness of God and an unquestioned assurance of the survival of the believer.","r":["101:1.6"]},{"q":"Pero la verdadera religión es amor vivo, una vida de servicio.","r":"100:6.5"}]}],"see":["Religión personal","Fe","Adoración","Ajustador del Pensamiento","Espíritus ayudantes de la mente","Filosofía"]},{"n":51,"t":"Fe","en":"Faith","sum":"Faith is a living trust in God and in spiritual values, distinct from belief, which merely accepts a doctrine as true. Belief becomes faith only when it actually guides and shapes life, and faith transforms the philosophic God of probability into the God of experiential certainty. Faith is the price of entrance into the family of God and the key to Havona, and Jesus lived out its highest example.","sections":[{"h":"Belief and Faith","items":[{"x":"Accepting a teaching as true is only belief; belief becomes faith when it actually dominates the mode of living.","r":["101:8.1"]},{"q":"La creencia fija, la fe libera.","r":"101:8.2"},{"x":"Beliefs may become group possessions, but faith must always be personal.","r":["101:8.2"]},{"x":"Faith is a God-knowing and man-serving life, a living experience concerned with spiritual meanings and supreme values.","r":["101:8.2"]},{"q":"Belief may not be able to resist doubt and withstand fear, but faith is always triumphant over doubting","r":"102:6.7"},{"q":"The acceptance of a teaching as true is not faith; that is mere belief.","r":"101:8.1"}]},{"h":"Faith and Certainty","items":[{"x":"Faith transforms the philosophic God of probability into the saving God of certainty in personal religious experience.","r":["102:6.4"]},{"q":"Las convicciones sobre Dios pueden ser alcanzadas por sabio razonamiento, pero el individuo se torna consciente de Dios solamente por la fe, a través de la experiencia personal.","r":"102:6.5"},{"x":"In science God is a possibility and in philosophy a probability, but in religion he is a certainty.","r":["102:6.8"]},{"x":"God is not revealed by miracles or material proofs; he is known by trusting him.","r":["102:1.5"]},{"x":"The more one knows of science, the less sure one becomes; the more religion one has, the more certain one is.","r":["102:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Marks of True Faith","items":[{"x":"True faith trusts in the goodness of God even amid bitter disappointment and defeat, and it generates profound courage in the face of calamity.","r":["101:3.6","101:3.7"]},{"x":"Faith maintains an inexplicable poise and serenity in the midst of illness and suffering, abuse and injustice.","r":["101:3.8","101:3.9"]},{"x":"True faith worships God in every circumstance and declares, \"Though he slay me, yet will I serve him.\"","r":["101:3.16"]},{"x":"Faith does not violate intellectual honesty, foster intolerance and persecution, or turn away from scientific discoveries.","r":["101:8.3","101:8.4"]},{"x":"Faith vitalizes religion and moves the religionist to live the golden rule heroically.","r":["101:8.4"]},{"q":"La fe vitaliza la religión y obliga al religionista a vivir heroicamente de acuerdo con la regla de oro.","r":"101:8.4"}]},{"h":"Faith and Salvation","items":[{"x":"Faith links moral consciousness with the spiritual concept of enduring reality, making religion a technique of salvation.","r":["101:9.9"]},{"x":"Faith is the price of entrance into the family of God, and forgiveness is the act of God in accepting that faith.","r":["170:3.3"]},{"x":"Faith releases the divine spark that lives within man, the potential of eternal survival.","r":["132:3.6"]},{"x":"The Adjuster's success in achieving survival depends less on theories of belief than on decisions, determinations, and steadfast faith.","r":["110:3.2"]},{"q":"El deseo de creer es la llave de Havona.","r":"26:4.15"}]},{"h":"The Faith of Jesus","items":[{"x":"Jesus did not use faith as a consolation in suffering or a comfort in despair; he enjoyed serenity in an unquestioning trust in God.","r":["196:0.3"]},{"x":"Jesus' great contribution was less a new idea of God than the human demonstration of a new and higher type of living faith.","r":["196:0.3"]},{"x":"Jesus asks people not so much to believe in him as to believe with him, to believe as he believed.","r":["196:0.13"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that simple, childlike faith is the key that opens the door of the kingdom.","r":["170:3.2"]}]}],"see":["Experiencia religiosa","Religión personal","Verdad","Reino del cielo","Supervivencia","Carácter de Jesús"]},{"n":47,"t":"Filiación con Dios","en":"Sonship with God","sum":"Sonship with God is the family relationship between the heavenly Father and the individual that becomes real when a person accepts God as Father by faith. At the center of the gospel of the kingdom that Jesus proclaimed stand the fatherhood of God and the sonship of man that follows from it. This sonship is not earned by deeds but received as a gift, and the indwelling Adjuster, the Spirit of Truth, and the Holy Spirit bear witness to this fact with the human spirit.","sections":[{"h":"Sonship Received by Faith","items":[{"x":"By accepting the status of sonship and believing in its reality, a person makes sonship with God an eternal reality.","r":["40:6.4"]},{"q":"Mediante la fe en la paternidad de Dios, podéis entrar en el reino del cielo y así ser hijos de Dios.","r":"142:1.3"},{"q":"Si recibís a Dios como vuestro Padre, de verdad y de veras seréis hijos de Dios.","r":"142:5.2"},{"x":"Salvation is the gift of the Father, and those who receive it by faith partake of the divine nature and become sons or daughters of God.","r":["150:5.3"]},{"x":"The first condition for entering the kingdom is the faith and sincerity of coming as a little child and receiving the bestowal of sonship as a gift.","r":["170:2.21"]}]},{"h":"Why Mortals Are Sons","items":[{"x":"It is a solemn and sublime fact that lowly and material man is a faith child of the Most High.","r":["40:6.2"]},{"x":"Because the Creator Son became man and our elder brother, we who are his brothers are sons of the same Father.","r":["40:6.5"]},{"x":"We are sons because the spirit of the Son has been poured out upon all races, because we have received personality from the Father, and because a fragment of the Father indwells us.","r":["40:6.6","40:6.7","40:6.8"]},{"x":"Because the Holy Spirit, the Spirit of Truth, and the Adjuster are present together, mortals are qualified for the conscious realization of sonship with God.","r":["34:5.7"]},{"x":"The spirit bears witness not \"to\" our spirits but \"with\" our spirits that we are children of God.","r":["34:6.12"]},{"q":"he is your elder brother in fact","r":"40:6.5"}]},{"h":"From Servant to Free Son","items":[{"x":"The subjects of a kingdom hear the laws of a ruler, but one who discovers sonship by faith sees himself as the privileged son of a loving Father.","r":["141:2.2"]},{"x":"When the Father's will is your law, you are a noble slave; when the Father's will becomes your will, you are a free child of God.","r":["141:2.2"]},{"x":"As a good earthly father does not keep his children in anxiety, so the heavenly Father does not leave his faith children in doubt.","r":["142:5.2"]},{"q":"whosoever has been born of the spirit has in himself the power to overcome all doubt, and this is the victory that overcomes all uncertainty, even your faith.","r":"142:5.3"}]},{"h":"The Fruits of Sonship","items":[{"x":"Righteousness is not the condition of salvation but the natural fruit of the spirit-born life of sonship.","r":["150:5.5"]},{"q":"La comprensión de la filiación es incompatible con el deseo de pecar.","r":"150:5.5"},{"x":"The evidence to the world of being born of the spirit is that believers sincerely love one another.","r":["142:5.4"]},{"x":"When we accept by living faith that our ideals come from a superhuman source, belief in sonship becomes effective and brotherhood becomes real.","r":["103:5.9"]},{"x":"Religion is the experience that leads from the bondage of primitive fear to the liberty of faith that realizes sonship with God.","r":["101:0.1"]},{"q":"and the evidence to all the world that you have been born of the spirit is that you sincerely love one another.\"","r":"142:5.4"}]},{"h":"The Center of the Gospel Jesus Proclaimed","items":[{"x":"By proclaiming that every mortal creature is a child of a loving Father, a son of God, Jesus raised the concept of the Father to a sublime experience.","r":["196:0.2"]},{"x":"Jesus told his disciples first to make known that God is Father and man his son, and only then to discuss doctrine.","r":["141:6.4"]},{"x":"Jesus said that people of other ages would better understand the gospel in family terms: the fatherhood of God, the brotherhood of man, and sonship with God.","r":["142:7.4"]},{"x":"The gospel of the kingdom is the fact of the fatherhood of God joined with the truth of the sonship-brotherhood of men.","r":["194:0.4"]},{"x":"The Spirit of Truth came to lead believers into a growing consciousness of eternal and ascending sonship with God.","r":["194:2.7"]}]}],"see":["Padre Universal","Hermandad de los hombres","Reino del cielo","Fe","Espíritu de la Verdad","Ajustador del Pensamiento"]},{"n":74,"t":"Filosofía","en":"Philosophy","sum":"Philosophy is the effort of the human mind to weave the facts revealed by science and the values experienced by religion into one coherent view of the universe; it is the domain of wisdom. Its body is founded on material facts, while its soul and energy come from spiritual insight. The highest attainable philosophy rests on the reason of science, the faith of religion, and the truth insight of revelation, and the philosophic quest does not end even on Paradise.","sections":[{"h":"Wisdom Seeking Unity","items":[{"q":"La unidad se encuentra de la mejor manera en la experiencia humana a través de la filosofía.","r":"102:2.6"},{"x":"The body of philosophic thought must be founded on material facts, but its soul and energy is mortal spiritual insight.","r":["102:2.6"]},{"x":"Philosophy arose from the effort to organize the separate findings of science and religion into a reasoned and unified attitude toward the universe.","r":["103:6.9"]},{"x":"Science is the domain of knowledge, religion the sphere of the faith experience, and philosophy the realm of wisdom.","r":["101:5.2"]},{"x":"Science is satisfied with a First Cause, religion with a supreme personality, and philosophy with unity.","r":["102:3.15"]},{"q":"La filosofía es el esfuerzo del hombre por unificar la experiencia humana.","r":"196:3.30"}]},{"h":"The Place and Limits of Philosophy","items":[{"x":"In science the self observes the material world, philosophy observes this observation, and religion experiences the reality that observes it all.","r":["112:2.12"]},{"q":"La filosofía es, inevitablemente, supercientífica. El hombre es un hecho material de la naturaleza, pero su vida es un fenómeno que trasciende los niveles materiales de la naturaleza, porque exhibe los atributos de control de la mente y las cualidades creadoras del espíritu.","r":"195:7.9"},{"x":"Philosophy inclined to matter becomes naturalism, overweighted toward spirit becomes mysticism, and leaning on metaphysics ends in skepticism and confusion.","r":["103:6.14"]},{"x":"Philosophy should not project reality only by straight-line logic but should allow for the elliptic symmetry of reality and the curvature of relation concepts.","r":["103:6.14"]},{"x":"A philosophy useful to both science and religion avoids the extremes of materialism and pantheism and recognizes the reality of personality, the changeless in the midst of change.","r":["103:8.6"]}]},{"h":"The Highest Philosophy","items":[{"q":"La filosofía más elevada obtenible por el hombre mortal debe estar basada lógicamente en la razón de la ciencia, la fe de la religión, y el discernimiento de la verdad ofrecido por la revelación.","r":"103:6.15"},{"x":"Philosophy clarified by revelation can function adequately even in the absence of the morontia mota and despite the failure of metaphysics.","r":["103:6.9","103:8.6"]},{"x":"True philosophy grows out of the wisdom that seeks to correlate the quantitative observations of science with the qualitative observations of religion.","r":["133:5.4"]},{"x":"The lower planes of the morontia mota join directly with the highest levels of human philosophy.","r":["48:7.1"]},{"x":"The ideal human state is one in which wisdom, faith, and experience work together, meaningfully fusing philosophy, religion, and science into one.","r":["98:2.12"]}]},{"h":"The Formation of a Philosophy of Religion","items":[{"x":"An individual's philosophy of religion is formed from many factors, including inner experience, environment, temperament, education, and social conditions.","r":["101:7.1"]},{"q":"Moral cowards never achieve high planes of philosophic thinking","r":"101:7.2"},{"x":"The philosophy of religion evolves through four levels, from conformity to tradition to fearless and sincere thinking and living.","r":["101:7.4"]},{"x":"A sound philosophy of religion distinguishes material and spiritual realities while recognizing their unity in intellectual striving and social service.","r":["101:7.5"]},{"x":"An effective philosophy of living weaves together cosmic insight and emotional reactions to the environment.","r":["140:4.8"]}]},{"h":"Philosophy in History and the Eternal Quest","items":[{"q":"En Grecia, el creer estaba subordinado al pensar; en Palestina, el pensar estaba subordinado al creer.","r":"98:2.8"},{"x":"The Greek philosophers achieved lofty ethical systems, but their concept of God dissolved in a pantheistic haze and failed to satisfy the masses' longing for salvation.","r":["98:2.9","98:2.10"]},{"x":"Religion has long endured without philosophy, but philosophy wholly unconnected with religion has seldom endured long.","r":["98:2.12"]},{"x":"Even on Paradise endless mysteries remain for philosophy to solve, and the exhilaration of philosophy is a satisfaction second only to worship.","r":["27:6.1"]},{"x":"The masters of philosophy on Paradise delight in leading ascenders in the thrilling quest of solving universe problems.","r":["27:6.2","27:6.5"]}]}],"see":["Sabiduría","Ciencia y religión","Revelación","Verdad","Realidad","Morontia"]},{"n":34,"t":"Fusión con el Ajustador","en":"Adjuster Fusion","sum":"Adjuster fusion is the event in which the evolving immortal soul becomes eternally one with the indwelling Thought Adjuster. It usually takes place on the mansion worlds after death, but rarely it is achieved by translation during the life in the flesh. Fusion announces to the universe the mortal's final choice to do the Father's will; by it the ascender's eternal career is assured, and the way opens to the Paradise Corps of the Finality.","sections":[{"h":"What Fusion Is","items":[{"q":"Esta fusión constituye el misterio de hacer uno solo de Dios y el hombre, el misterio de la evolución de la criatura finita, pero es eternamente verdadero.","r":"112:7.2"},{"x":"Since the Adjuster is an immortal spirit, union with it confers eternal life on the soul of the fused mortal.","r":["40:7.1"]},{"x":"In fusion the Adjuster and the soul share all of each other's experiences and values and actually become one being.","r":["110:7.4","110:7.5"]},{"x":"The fused being is one personality, and no universe intelligence can distinguish the human and the Adjuster separately.","r":["112:7.8"]},{"x":"The fused Adjuster keeps its existential divine nature yet is transformed to the level of finite experience and inseparably linked with the ascending personality.","r":["107:2.7"]}]},{"h":"When It Occurs","items":[{"x":"Fusion usually occurs during the sojourn in the local system, and sometimes it is delayed until the ascender reaches the constellation or the local universe capital.","r":["112:7.3"]},{"x":"Fusion that is actually effective is often not achieved until the sojourn on the fifth or sixth mansion world.","r":["47:8.3"]},{"x":"When the seven cosmic circles are attained and the final choice of the will is added, fusion may occur during the life in the flesh, and the body is instantly consumed.","r":["110:7.2"]},{"x":"In the case of most Urantians, the Adjuster must wait patiently for the deliverance of death.","r":["110:7.6"]},{"q":"La muerte física natural no es una inevitabilidad mortal.","r":"55:2.1"},{"x":"On worlds settled in light and life, fusion translations steadily increase, and by the fourth stage more than half of all mortals are translated from among the living.","r":["55:2.2","55:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Conditions of Fusion","items":[{"q":"La fusión con el Ajustador no ocurre jamás hasta tanto no se pronuncien los mandatos del superuniverso relativos a que la naturaleza humana ha hecho su elección final e irrevocable a favor de la carrera eterna.","r":"112:7.5"},{"x":"Until fusion an ascender may at any time forsake the Father's will, but fusion announces that he has chosen the Father's will without reservation.","r":["111:3.1"]},{"x":"The Adjuster of one who has made the supreme decision foresees the time of fusion and regards the union as an already existing fact.","r":["109:2.4"]},{"x":"When Adjuster fusion proclaims the final choice to the universe, the eternal destiny of the human being is assured.","r":["5:1.11"]}]},{"h":"The Scene of Fusion","items":[{"q":"and then, in the presence of such a survivor's morontia associates, these messengers of confirmation speak: \"This is a beloved son in whom I am well pleased.\"","r":"47:8.4"},{"x":"The new being is presented under a new name, spends forty days in spiritual retirement, and chooses a route to Havona.","r":["47:8.5"]},{"x":"On settled worlds the candidate for fusion departs in a flash of life before family and friends gathered in the temple.","r":["55:2.3","55:2.4"]},{"q":"the human beings who might witness such a spectacle would only observe the translating mortal disappear \"in chariots of fire.\"","r":"110:7.2"},{"x":"Those fused during the life in the flesh do not pass through death but go to the higher morontia spheres by direct Adjuster transit.","r":["49:6.18","49:6.19"]}]},{"h":"When Fusion Does Not Take Place","items":[{"x":"Mortals are divided into three groups according to their relation to the Adjuster: temporary indwelling, nonfusion, and fusion-potential types.","r":["40:5.4","40:5.5","40:5.7"]},{"x":"Mortals of primitive ages may survive through the ministry of Adjusters, yet they do not become eternally united with them.","r":["40:5.9","40:5.10"]},{"x":"Mortals of the nonfusion type are also indwelt by Adjusters throughout life, but if they survive, their souls fuse with spirit.","r":["40:5.13","40:5.14"]},{"x":"The few whose survival is recognized but who never become one with their Adjusters go, after the verdict of the courts of inquiry, on the path of fusion with the Son.","r":["40:8.1","40:8.3"]},{"q":"In the fusion experience there is no overlapping","r":"40:9.1"}]},{"h":"Results of Fusion","items":[{"q":"Cuando se ha efectuado la fusión con el Ajustador, ya no puede existir ningún peligro futuro que amenace la carrera eternal de dicha personalidad.","r":"112:7.4"},{"x":"Fusion confers on the personality actualities that were only potential: fixation of divinity qualities, past-eternity experience and memory, and immortality.","r":["112:7.1"]},{"x":"In matters of personality the human leads in the fused ascender, whose headquarters is Ascendington rather than Divinington.","r":["112:7.12"]},{"x":"The number of a fused Adjuster is stricken from the superuniverse records, and its destiny becomes the same as that of the ascending mortal: the Corps of the Finality.","r":["112:7.11","112:7.13"]},{"x":"Through fusion the Universal Father fulfills his promise to give himself to his material creatures.","r":["112:7.14"]},{"x":"Adjuster-fused mortals are the only human order that passes through the Havona circuits and finds God on Paradise.","r":["40:7.5"]}]}],"see":["Ajustador del Pensamiento","Alma","Cuerpo de la Finalidad","Mundos de estancia","Supervivencia","Luz y vida"]},{"n":83,"t":"Gobierno y sociedad","en":"Government and Society","sum":"Government was not designed by anyone; it is an institution that evolved through trial and error in efforts to adjust human antagonisms and keep the peace. The Urantia Book traces its development from the council of elders to modern representative government and names the separation of executive, legislative, and judicial functions as the only sacred feature of government. It teaches that a state can never rise above the moral values of its citizens, and that true world peace will come when a government of all mankind is established.","sections":[{"h":"The Evolutionary Origin of Government","items":[{"x":"Once man had partly solved the problem of making a living, he faced the task of regulating human relations, and private property made government necessary.","r":["70:0.1"]},{"q":"El gobierno es un desarrollo inconsciente; evoluciona mediante pruebas y errores.","r":"70:0.3"},{"q":"La guerra es el estado y patrimonio naturales del hombre evolutivo; la paz es el metro social que mide el progreso de la civilización.","r":"70:1.1"},{"x":"Peace groups widened from the family to the clan, the tribe, and the nation, and then to the territorial state, now embracing many nations beyond ties of blood.","r":["70:4.1"]},{"x":"The first organ of government was the council of elders, which already contained the seeds of executive, legislative, and judicial functions.","r":["70:5.2","70:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Rights, Justice, and the Gifts of Society","items":[{"x":"Nature confers no rights on man, and the supreme gift of society to man is security.","r":["70:9.1"]},{"x":"Natural justice is a man-made theory; the only justice nature gives is the unfailing conformity of results to causes.","r":["70:10.1","70:10.2"]},{"x":"Liberty is a gift of civilization made possible by the enforcement of law; for one person to be absolutely free, another must be a slave.","r":["134:6.1"]},{"x":"The chief task of government is to define what is right, regulate class differences fairly, and enforce equality of opportunity under the rule of law.","r":["81:5.6"]}]},{"h":"Representative Government and the Separation of Powers","items":[{"x":"Universe administrators have learned by experience that evolutionary peoples are best governed by representative government with three balanced branches.","r":["70:12.1","70:12.2"]},{"q":"El único rasgo sagrado de todo gobierno humano es la división del estado en tres dominios de funciones ejecutivas, legislativas y judiciales.","r":"71:8.1"},{"x":"Mortals must create their own government and constitution and choose the ablest and most worthy as their leaders and judges.","r":["70:12.5"]},{"q":"A pesar de ser la democracia un ideal, es fruto de la civilización, no de la evolución.","r":"71:2.1"},{"x":"Democracy carries dangers such as the glorification of mediocrity, the choice of ignorant rulers, and enslavement to public opinion.","r":["71:2.2","71:2.6"]},{"x":"Educating public opinion is the only safe way to accelerate civilization, and voting is the right method even when doing the wrong thing.","r":["71:2.7","71:2.8"]}]},{"h":"The Ideal State","items":[{"x":"What the state does matters more than its form of government, and no state can rise above the moral values of its citizens.","r":["71:3.1"]},{"x":"The ideal state is moved by three impulses: the love loyalty born of realizing brotherhood, wise patriotism, and cosmic insight.","r":["71:3.3","71:3.6"]},{"q":"El mejor estado es aquél que coordina más y gobierna menos.","r":"71:3.9"},{"x":"In advanced states political service is honored as the highest devotion of the citizen, and public office is regarded as an honor, not a burden.","r":["71:3.10","71:3.12"]},{"x":"An enduring state is founded on culture, ruled by ideals, and motivated by service, and its education aims at wisdom and spiritual values.","r":["71:7.1","71:7.2"]},{"x":"An economy of profit motivation alone is doomed unless supplemented by service motives, yet it must not be abolished suddenly before higher motives are established.","r":["71:6.1","71:6.3"]},{"x":"A continental nation on a neighboring planet, with a federation of one hundred states and a three-branch representative government, has a society more advanced than Urantia's.","r":["72:2.1","72:2.3"]}]},{"h":"Sovereignty and World Peace","items":[{"x":"Relative sovereignty exists on only two levels, the spiritual free will of the individual and the collective sovereignty of mankind as a whole; all groups between are temporary.","r":["134:5.2"]},{"q":"La soberanía mundial es la única solución para prevenir las guerras mundiales —no hay otra salida.","r":"134:6.4"},{"x":"Even if all weapons were abolished, nations clinging to the illusion of national sovereignty would fight with fists and stones.","r":["134:6.6"]},{"x":"The Most Highs rule in the kingdoms of men to bring about the greatest good for all men, not for any chosen people.","r":["134:5.3","134:5.4"]}]},{"h":"The Believer and the State","items":[{"x":"Sonship in the kingdom should make believers better citizens of earthly nations, and believers bear a twofold duty to God and to man.","r":["178:1.4","178:1.5"]},{"x":"Believers must not worship temporal rulers nor try to extend the spiritual kingdom by temporal power.","r":["178:1.6"]},{"x":"The persistent spread of the gospel will in time separate politics from religion and bring intellectual and religious liberty to all peoples.","r":["178:1.9"]}]}],"see":["Civilización","Matrimonio y familia","Hermandad de los hombres","Justicia","Servicio","Reino del cielo"]},{"n":13,"t":"Gran universo y universo maestro","en":"Grand and Master Universe","sum":"El universo maestro es la totalidad de la creación, formada por seis niveles espaciales elípticos y concéntricos centrados en el Paraíso: Havona, los siete superuniversos y los cuatro niveles del espacio exterior. La parte actualmente organizada y habitada, Havona y los siete superuniversos, se llama gran universo. En el espacio exterior están tomando forma desde ahora vastas creaciones futuras, y los ascendentes del gran universo perfeccionado parecen destinados a servir allí en los tiempos venideros.","sections":[{"h":"Gran universo y universo maestro","items":[{"x":"El universo central y divino, junto con los siete superuniversos que lo rodean, se llama gran universo: la creación actualmente organizada y habitada.","r":["0:0.6"]},{"x":"El universo maestro incluye, además del gran universo, los universos del espacio exterior, todavía deshabitados y en proceso de organización.","r":["0:0.6"]},{"x":"Urantia pertenece al universo local de Nebadon, Nebadon al séptimo superuniverso, Orvonton, y los siete superuniversos giran alrededor del universo central de Havona.","r":["0:0.5","12:1.12"]},{"x":"El gran universo tiene un potencial evolutivo de unos siete billones de planetas habitados, pero sus bordes irregulares todavía están sin terminar.","r":["12:1.13"]},{"q":"To created beings the master universe might appear to be almost infinite, but it is far from finished","r":"12:0.3"}]},{"h":"Seis niveles espaciales","items":[{"x":"El universo maestro no es un plano infinito ni un círculo sin fin; funciona como una sola unidad espacial coordinada, con dimensiones y límites definidos.","r":["12:1.1"]},{"x":"Hacia fuera del Paraíso se sitúan Havona, los siete superuniversos y cuatro niveles del espacio exterior, dispuestos como elipses concéntricas.","r":["12:1.3","12:1.9"]},{"q":"The Paradise-Havona System, the eternal universe encircling the eternal Isle, constitutes the perfect and eternal nucleus of the master universe","r":"12:1.11"},{"x":"Entre los niveles espaciales hay zonas de relativa quietud, y los niveles sucesivos giran alternativamente en direcciones opuestas, lo que equilibra las tensiones de la gravedad.","r":["11:7.7","12:4.15"]},{"q":"The central universe is the creation of eternity; the seven superuniverses are the creations of time","r":"12:1.16"},{"x":"Los cuatro niveles del espacio exterior están destinados a eventuar-evolucionar la ultimidad de la creación.","r":["12:1.16"]}]},{"h":"Las creaciones futuras del espacio exterior","items":[{"x":"El primer nivel del espacio exterior es una vasta zona de actividad energética que comienza a unos quinientos mil años luz más allá de la periferia del gran universo y se extiende a lo largo de más de veinticinco millones de años luz.","r":["12:1.14"]},{"x":"El espacio situado más allá de los siete superuniversos se considera en gran parte dominio del Absoluto No Cualificado, y sus energías son transmutadas por los organizadores de fuerza del Paraíso.","r":["12:2.1","12:2.4"]},{"x":"La energía y la materia del espacio exterior equivalen ya a muchas veces la masa total de los siete superuniversos, pero allí no viven seres materiales ni ángeles conocidos.","r":["12:2.4","12:2.5"]},{"x":"Alrededor del noventa y cinco por ciento de la gravedad absoluta del Paraíso se emplea ahora en sostener sistemas materiales más allá de los límites de los universos actualmente organizados.","r":["12:3.8"]},{"x":"La gravedad espiritual funciona casi enteramente en el gran universo, por lo que los universos exteriores parecen todavía no espirituales, mientras que alrededor del quince por ciento de la gravedad de la mente actúa fuera del gran universo.","r":["12:3.9","12:3.10"]},{"q":"Una mayor creación del futuro está en proceso de formación.","r":"12:2.5"}]},{"h":"Espacio y tiempo en expansión","items":[{"x":"La creación física de todo el espacio penetrado se está expandiendo ahora uniformemente hacia fuera, según el ciclo de respiración del espacio de unos dos mil millones de años.","r":["12:4.12"]},{"x":"Las aparentes velocidades de alejamiento de los universos lejanos no son reales, sino que se deben a varios factores de error, como los ángulos de observación y las distorsiones del tiempo-espacio.","r":["12:4.14"]},{"x":"El espacio se origina en el Paraíso, pero no es infinito, y el tiempo y el espacio son inseparables solo en las creaciones espaciotemporales de los siete superuniversos.","r":["12:5.2","12:5.3"]},{"q":"Absolutamente nada es estacionario en todo el universo maestro, excepto el centro mismo de Havona, la Isla eterna del Paraíso, el centro de la gravedad.","r":"12:4.1"}]},{"h":"El cuidado que abarca el todo","items":[{"x":"Las necesidades de todo el universo maestro dependen de los Absolutos para el potencial, del Último para la dirección, del Supremo para la coordinación evolutiva y de los Arquitectos del Universo Maestro para la administración inicial.","r":["12:6.8","12:6.12"]},{"x":"Los Arquitectos absonitos trazan los planes, los Creadores Supremos les dan existencia y el Ser Supremo completa su plenitud.","r":["106:3.1"]},{"x":"La misericordia es la actitud de Dios hacia el individuo y la equidad su actitud hacia el todo, y la voluntad de Dios prevalece finalmente en todo el universo de los universos.","r":["12:7.1"]},{"x":"El tiempo y el espacio son un mecanismo cósmico que permite a las criaturas finitas existir en el cosmos junto con el Infinito.","r":["118:9.1"]},{"x":"Se cree que las nuevas creaciones del espacio exterior serán el futuro campo de actividad de los Cuerpos de la Finalidad que se están reuniendo.","r":["12:2.6"]},{"x":"En las eras futuras, los siete superuniversos parecen destinados a convertirse en las escuelas intermedias de los seres del espacio exterior, y Havona en su escuela de perfeccionamiento.","r":["14:6.41"]},{"q":"En tal momento futuro de la eternidad, el universo maestro aun parecerá juvenil; en efecto, será siempre joven frente a las posibilidades ilimitadas de la eternidad sin fin.","r":"106:7.8"}]}],"see":["Havona","Los siete superuniversos","Paraíso","Dios el Último","Cuerpo de la Finalidad","Tiempo y espacio"]},{"n":18,"t":"Gravedad","en":"Gravity","sum":"La gravedad es la atracción todopoderosa con la que la presencia física del Paraíso sujeta los mundos de todo el espacio. En el universo hay cuatro circuitos absolutos: la gravedad de la personalidad del Padre, la gravedad espiritual del Hijo, la gravedad de la mente del Actor Conjunto y la gravedad cósmica de la Isla del Paraíso, y actúan independientemente del tiempo y del espacio. La materia está sujeta por la gravedad del Paraíso y por la gravedad lineal, pero cuanto más espiritual se vuelve una mente humana, menos responde a la gravedad material y más es atraída por la gravedad espiritual hacia el Paraíso.","sections":[{"h":"El dominio todopoderoso del Paraíso","items":[{"q":"La gravedad es la atracción todopoderosa de la presencia física del Paraíso.","r":"11:8.1"},{"x":"El centro de la gravedad material absoluta es la Isla del Paraíso, complementada y equilibrada por los cuerpos oscuros de gravedad que rodean Havona y por los depósitos de espacio situados arriba y abajo.","r":["11:8.2"]},{"x":"El Controlador Universal está potencialmente presente en los circuitos de gravedad de la Isla del Paraíso, y esa presencia alcanza a todas las partes del universo en el mismo grado, según la masa.","r":["3:1.7"]},{"x":"Puesto que las líneas de la gravedad procedentes de los confines de la creación convergen en la morada del Padre, si él se desplazara de ese lugar se produciría al instante el caos universal.","r":["11:1.4"]},{"x":"Cada nuevo universo requiere un nuevo ajuste de la gravedad, pero el poder de control del Paraíso es suficiente incluso para un universo infinito.","r":["3:4.2"]}]},{"h":"Los cuatro circuitos absolutos","items":[{"x":"En el universo hay cuatro circuitos absolutos: la gravedad de la personalidad del Padre, la gravedad espiritual del Hijo, la gravedad de la mente del Actor Conjunto y la gravedad cósmica de la Isla del Paraíso, y el Padre actúa a través de todos ellos.","r":["12:3.1","12:3.5"]},{"q":"Son circuitos absolutos de presencia y, como Dios, son independientes del tiempo y el espacio.","r":"12:3.6"},{"x":"Toda gravedad está en circuito en la Isla del Paraíso, toda mente en el Actor Conjunto, todo espíritu en el Hijo Eterno y toda personalidad en la presencia personal del Padre.","r":["5:6.11"]},{"x":"Así como el Padre atrae a toda personalidad y el Hijo a toda realidad espiritual, el Actor Conjunto ejerce un poder de atracción sobre toda mente.","r":["9:6.2"]},{"x":"La acción de la gravedad de la personalidad es siempre un acto volitivo del Padre Universal, y la realidad que responde a su circuito no puede medirse.","r":["9:6.4","12:3.12"]}]},{"h":"Etapas de la gravedad física","items":[{"x":"La gravedad absoluta es la gravedad del Paraíso, mientras que la gravedad local o lineal pertenece a la etapa eléctrica de la energía y la materia.","r":["11:8.3"]},{"x":"La energía responde a la gravedad del Paraíso en tres etapas: pregravedad (fuerza), gravedad (energía) y posgravedad (poder universal).","r":["11:8.4","11:8.5","11:8.7"]},{"x":"La gravedad lineal se vuelve plenamente operativa cuando aparece la organización atómica de la materia, mientras que los ultimatones no combinados solo responden a la gravedad circular del Paraíso.","r":["42:6.2","42:6.3"]},{"q":"La gravedad es el único control de la materia-energía.","r":"0:6.11"},{"x":"La gravedad lineal es la fuerza de cohesión de corto alcance del gran universo, y la expresión «en razón inversa del cuadrado de la distancia» es solo una aproximación burda debido a la influencia del espacio.","r":["42:11.5"]},{"x":"El cero absoluto teórico nunca se alcanza realmente debido a la presencia y la acción de la gravedad.","r":["42:4.6"]}]},{"h":"Equilibrio y antigravedad","items":[{"q":"El espacio no responde a la gravedad, pero actúa como un equilibrador de la gravedad.","r":"11:8.3"},{"x":"El Espíritu Infinito posee el poder de la antigravedad, que no se observa ni en el Padre ni en el Hijo, y puede transmitirlo a personalidades superiores.","r":["9:3.2"]},{"x":"La disposición de los niveles espaciales, que giran alternativamente en direcciones opuestas, impide que las presiones de la gravedad lleguen a puntos destructivos.","r":["11:7.9"]},{"x":"Los cuerpos oscuros de gravedad de Havona, con sus cinturones interior y exterior que giran en direcciones opuestas, estabilizan perfectamente el universo central.","r":["14:1.15"]},{"x":"Los universos actualmente organizados utilizan solo alrededor del cinco por ciento de la gravedad absoluta del Paraíso; el resto se emplea en sostener los sistemas materiales del espacio exterior.","r":["12:3.8"]}]},{"h":"La gravedad espiritual y la ascensión","items":[{"x":"La gravedad espiritual está libre de demora temporal, no la disminuye el espacio y no la retarda la masa material.","r":["7:1.2"]},{"x":"Las realidades espirituales responden a la gravedad espiritual según su valor cualitativo, así como la materia responde a la gravedad física según su cantidad.","r":["7:1.3"]},{"q":"A medida que la mente de cualquier personalidad del universo se hace más espiritual —más semejante a Dios— responde menos a la gravedad material.","r":"12:8.5"},{"x":"La acción de la gravedad física es la medida cuantitativa de la energía no espiritual, y la acción de la gravedad espiritual es la medida cualitativa de la energía viviente de la divinidad.","r":["12:8.5"]},{"x":"La espiritualidad en el tiempo y el espacio se mide en proporción inversa a la respuesta a la gravedad lineal.","r":["42:11.4"]},{"q":"El circuito de la gravedad espiritual literalmente arrastra el alma del hombre hacia el Paraíso.","r":"7:3.2"}]}],"see":["Paraíso","Energía y materia","Hijo Eterno","Espíritu Infinito","Los tres Absolutos","Padre Universal"]},{"n":12,"t":"Havona","en":"Havona","sum":"Havona es el universo central eterno de mil millones de mundos perfectos que rodea la Isla del Paraíso. No es producto de la evolución, sino un universo creado perfecto desde el principio; es el modelo de todos los universos, y los mundos de sus siete circuitos son el último campo de formación por el que pasan los peregrinos ascendentes de los universos del tiempo antes de entrar en el Paraíso. En su perfección, sin gobierno y sin pecado, Havona da satisfacción al Padre y a los creadores y un asombro sin fin a los ascendentes.","sections":[{"h":"El universo central, eterno y perfecto","items":[{"x":"Havona es el universo perfecto y divino situado en el centro de toda la creación, alrededor del cual giran las vastas creaciones del tiempo y del espacio.","r":["14:0.1"]},{"q":"Éste es un universo completamente creado y perfecto; no es un desarrollo evolutivo.","r":"14:0.2"},{"x":"Los Hijos Creadores aspiran a duplicar en el tiempo y a reproducir en el espacio la perfección divina de este universo modelo.","r":["14:0.2"]},{"x":"Havona no es exactamente finito ni absoluto; sirve de amortiguador entre el Paraíso absoluto y las creaciones finitas.","r":["105:7.2"]},{"x":"Havona es eterno, pero no estático en el sentido de carecer de crecimiento; en esta era experimenta ciertos cambios progresivos en coordinación con los superuniversos en evolución.","r":["105:7.2","106:0.18"]}]},{"h":"Circuitos y estructura","items":[{"x":"Los mil millones de mundos de Havona están dispuestos en siete circuitos concéntricos que rodean los tres circuitos de los satélites del Paraíso.","r":["14:1.9"]},{"x":"Cada circuito está impregnado por un Espíritu de Circuito, una expresión especializada del Espíritu Infinito, que coordina los asuntos celestiales de ese circuito.","r":["14:1.9"]},{"x":"Fuera se encuentran los enormes cuerpos oscuros de gravedad, que ni reflejan ni absorben la luz y giran en direcciones opuestas, ocultando y estabilizando Havona.","r":["14:1.14","14:1.15"]},{"x":"Un día del Paraíso-Havona equivale casi a mil años de Urantia y sirve de tiempo patrón para los siete superuniversos.","r":["14:1.12","14:1.13"]},{"x":"La materia de Havona está organizada en un sistema triple de energía, fundamentalmente distinto del sistema dual de energía de los superuniversos.","r":["14:2.2","14:2.6"]},{"q":"If a Urantia mortal could be transported to Havona, he would there be deaf, blind, and utterly lacking in all other sense reactions","r":"14:2.4"}]},{"h":"Mundos perfectos sin gobierno","items":[{"q":"Concerning the government of the central universe, there is none.","r":"14:3.1"},{"x":"Cada esfera de Havona está dirigida por un Eterno de los Días de origen trinitario y se desarrolla según los planes propios de este, con tal originalidad que no hay dos iguales.","r":["14:3.3","14:5.6"]},{"x":"En Havona ninguna criatura, nativa o peregrina, ha pecado jamás, y ningún alma ascendente ha entrado nunca antes de tiempo.","r":["14:2.9"]},{"x":"La decadencia y la muerte no forman parte del ciclo de vida de Havona; los seres vivos inferiores cambian de forma, pero nunca se desintegran.","r":["14:4.9"]},{"x":"Los nativos de Havona son descendientes de la Trinidad del Paraíso sin padres criaturas, y por su misma naturaleza viven la voluntad de Dios.","r":["14:4.10","14:4.13"]}]},{"h":"El último campo de formación de los ascendentes","items":[{"x":"Los peregrinos del tiempo llegan a los mundos de recepción del séptimo circuito y avanzan hacia dentro, planeta por planeta y circuito por circuito, hasta que por fin llegan al Paraíso.","r":["14:3.4"]},{"x":"El peregrino llega a Havona poseyendo una sola perfección: la perfección de propósito, probada y comprobada.","r":["26:4.12","26:4.13"]},{"q":"La habilidad para comprender es el pasaporte mortal al Paraíso. El deseo de creer es la llave de Havona.","r":"26:4.15"},{"x":"Al avanzar hacia dentro a través de los circuitos, el peregrino alcanza sucesivamente la identidad de un Espíritu Rector, del Ser Supremo, del Espíritu Infinito, del Hijo Eterno y del Padre Universal.","r":["14:5.4"]},{"x":"La expresión «círculos de progreso» aplicada a la mente humana deriva de esta disposición en circuitos del universo central.","r":["14:5.4"]}]},{"h":"Asombro sin fin","items":[{"x":"La vida en el universo central es tan rica y plena que trasciende los conceptos humanos de lo que los seres creados pueden experimentar.","r":["14:5.2"]},{"q":"La monotonía no es parte de la carrera en Havona.","r":"14:5.9"},{"x":"Cada uno de los mil millones de mundos es una verdadera universidad de sorpresas, y con cada circuito que atraviesa el peregrino encuentra cambios insospechados.","r":["14:5.9"]},{"x":"La aventura y la curiosidad, a menudo reprimidas en la tierra, son dones divinos otorgados para ser plenamente satisfechos en las largas eras venideras.","r":["14:5.10","14:5.11"]}]},{"h":"El propósito del universo central","items":[{"x":"El Padre obtiene una suprema satisfacción paternal de la perfección de Havona y se deleita en la adoración de criaturas perfectas.","r":["14:6.6"]},{"x":"Havona es el campo de formación donde los Hijos Creadores se preparan para crear universos, y todo Hijo Creador procura llevar su propio universo a este nivel de perfección.","r":["14:6.27"]},{"x":"Havona es una revelación de la naturaleza espiritual perfecta del Ser Supremo y un anuncio de su unificación futura.","r":["14:6.23","14:6.24"]},{"q":"Paradise is the home, and Havona the workshop and playground, of the finaliters.","r":"14:6.39"},{"x":"También en las eras futuras Havona parece tener un potencial ilimitado como universo de formación para seres absonitos.","r":["14:6.41"]}]}],"see":["Paraíso","Los siete superuniversos","Ser Supremo","Ascensión mortal","Cuerpo de la Finalidad","Gran universo y universo maestro"]},{"n":48,"t":"Hermandad de los hombres","en":"Brotherhood of Man","sum":"The brotherhood of man is the universal relationship that follows from the fact that every personality is a child of the same heavenly Father. Because God loves each individual and that love reaches all, people are bound together as brothers. Jesus taught the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man as the center of the gospel, and its realization depends not on law or force but on mutual understanding and love, and on the spiritual transformation of mankind.","sections":[{"h":"Brotherhood Flowing from Fatherhood","items":[{"x":"God loves each person as an individual child, yet because that love reaches all, a universal brotherhood arises.","r":["12:7.8","12:7.10"]},{"x":"Brotherhood is a relationship of the whole, not of the parts: the good of each helps all, and the evil of each adds to the suffering of all.","r":["12:7.11"]},{"q":"La hermandad del hombre está, después de todo, basada en el reconocimiento de la paternidad de Dios.","r":"52:6.7"},{"x":"When the belief that we are sons of God becomes effective, the feeling of brotherhood, an altruistic conviction, also becomes real.","r":["103:5.9"]}]},{"h":"The Brotherhood Jesus Taught","items":[{"x":"Jesus taught a new and greater brotherhood beyond the family of blood, the brotherhood of the sons of God.","r":["140:8.14"]},{"x":"Jesus named two laws of the heavenly family, loving the Father and loving one's brother as oneself, and said that brotherly love shows itself in unselfish service.","r":["142:7.4"]},{"q":"Que os améis los unos a los otros así como yo os he amado.","r":"180:1.1"},{"x":"Jesus also used such expressions as the family of God, the fellowship of believers, and the brotherhood of man to refer to the kingdom.","r":["170:2.24"]},{"x":"The religion Jesus founded consists in the personal experience of doing the will of God and serving the human brotherhood.","r":["196:2.6"]}]},{"h":"Spiritual Brotherhood and Social Brotherhood","items":[{"q":"El reino de los cielos no es un orden social ni económico; es una fraternidad exclusivamente espiritual de los individuos que conocen a Dios.","r":"99:3.2"},{"x":"Since the kingdom of heaven is a spiritual brotherhood of spirit-born sons, it can be proclaimed only by the power of the spirit, not by physical force.","r":["178:1.2"]},{"x":"Jesus showed the way to the immediate attainment of spiritual brotherhood, but social brotherhood depends on many personal and planetary changes.","r":["52:6.2"]},{"x":"Religious brotherhood cannot be realized unless all religions give up their claims of ecclesiastical authority and spiritual sovereignty.","r":["134:4.4"]},{"q":"La revelación religiosa es esencial para la realización de la hermandad en Urantia.","r":"52:6.2"}]},{"h":"The Way to Brotherhood","items":[{"x":"Social contact through travel, commerce, and exchange, and intellectual cross-fertilization through acquaintance with one another's thought, hasten brotherhood.","r":["52:6.3","52:6.4"]},{"x":"Ignorance breeds suspicion, and suspicion cannot coexist with sympathy and love.","r":["52:6.4"]},{"x":"Ethical awakening, political wisdom, and above all spiritual insight are needed for the realization of brotherhood.","r":["52:6.5","52:6.6","52:6.7"]},{"x":"The quickest way to brotherhood is spiritual pressure from above, enlarging the soul's capacity to understand and love one another.","r":["52:6.7"]},{"x":"On an isolated world like Urantia, religious revelation is essential for realizing brotherhood.","r":["52:6.2"]},{"q":"La ignorancia produce la sospecha, y la sospecha es incompatible con la actitud esencial de compasión y amor.","r":"52:6.4"}]},{"h":"The Contagion of Love and Future Civilization","items":[{"x":"No one can love his fellows by willpower alone; love is born of a thoroughgoing understanding of a neighbor's motives and sentiments.","r":["100:4.6"]},{"q":"No es tan importante amar a todos los hombres hoy como lo es que cada día aprendes a amar aún a uno más entre los seres humanos.","r":"100:4.6"},{"x":"If every person became a focus of love, that love would encompass all civilization, and the brotherhood of man would be realized.","r":["100:4.6"]},{"x":"The secret of a better civilization lies in Jesus' teachings about brotherhood, the good will of love and mutual trust.","r":["194:3.12"]},{"x":"The progress of civilization leads to the social achievement of the brotherhood of man and the personal status of God-consciousness.","r":["71:4.15"]},{"x":"The hope of modern Christianity lies in learning anew the living gospel of the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man.","r":["195:10.21"]}]}],"see":["Filiación con Dios","Padre Universal","Reino del cielo","Amor","Servicio","Civilización"]},{"n":22,"t":"Hijo Creador Micael","en":"Creator Son Michael","sum":"Un Hijo Creador es un Hijo primario del Paraíso, nacido del Padre Universal y del Hijo Eterno juntos, que diseña, crea y gobierna un universo local. El creador de nuestro universo de Nebadon es Micael, que se ganó su soberanía de manera experiencial autootorgándose siete veces a semejanza de sus criaturas; su autootorgamiento final fue la vida que vivió en Urantia como Jesús de Nazaret. Para nosotros, él es Dios a todos los efectos prácticos, y el camino por el que el Padre se revela.","sections":[{"h":"Origen y naturaleza","items":[{"x":"Un Hijo Creador es un ser de doble origen, que nace en un instante cuando el concepto absoluto de personalidad del Padre y la idea espiritual absoluta del Hijo Eterno se unen perfectamente.","r":["21:0.1","21:1.1"]},{"q":"But each Creator Son is different from every other","r":"21:0.1"},{"x":"Micael de Nebadon es la personalización número 611.121 de un concepto original de identidad infinita, y muestra características más semejantes a las del Hijo Eterno.","r":["33:1.1","33:2.1"]},{"x":"Micael no es miembro de la Trinidad del Paraíso, pero en su universo posee todos los atributos y poderes divinos que tendría el Hijo Eterno si estuviera presente.","r":["33:1.2","33:1.3"]},{"q":"Para nuestro universo y todos sus mundos habitados, para todos los fines y propósitos prácticos, el Hijo Soberano es Dios.","r":"33:1.4"}]},{"h":"Creador de un universo local","items":[{"x":"Antes de elegir su emplazamiento en el espacio, un Hijo Creador pasa largos períodos observando y aprendiendo de las creaciones de sus hermanos mayores en el mismo superuniverso.","r":["21:2.1"]},{"x":"Cuando sale del Paraíso le acompaña una Hija Creativa del Espíritu Infinito, que más tarde se personaliza como el Espíritu Materno del universo local.","r":["21:2.2","21:2.9"]},{"x":"Las nuevas modificaciones de la energía-materia requieren el consentimiento del Espíritu Infinito, y los nuevos diseños de criaturas el del Hijo Eterno, mientras que la personalidad la otorga solo el Padre.","r":["21:2.4","21:2.5","21:2.6"]},{"x":"Como los creadores son diferentes, las formas de vida de los universos locales que diseñan son originales en cada caso.","r":["21:2.10"]},{"x":"Cuando Micael está ausente, Gabriel, la Brillante Estrella Matutina, dirige el universo, y el Espíritu Materno supervisa en lugar de su presencia espiritual.","r":["21:2.11","33:2.5"]}]},{"h":"Siete autootorgamientos y la soberanía","items":[{"x":"Un Hijo Creador podría reclamar la soberanía desde el principio, pero se compromete ante la Trinidad a no asumir la soberanía suprema hasta haber completado siete autootorgamientos.","r":["21:3.2","21:3.12"]},{"q":"but they all could, they are truly freewill Sons.","r":"21:3.3"},{"x":"En sus siete autootorgamientos penetra en siete niveles de vida de las criaturas y revela una por una la voluntad séptuple de la Deidad, tal como está personalizada en los Siete Espíritus Rectores.","r":["21:3.17","21:3.18","119:8.4"]},{"q":"These divine Sons are innately just, but they become understandingly merciful as a result of these successive bestowal experiences","r":"119:0.4"},{"x":"Una vez completados sus autootorgamientos, un Hijo Creador se convierte en un Hijo Mayor, y la incorporación de la experiencia de criatura a su naturaleza produce un cambio permanente.","r":["21:4.6"]},{"q":"Micael nació creador, fue instruido como administrador, capacitado como ejecutivo, pero se le exigió que ganara su soberanía por la experiencia.","r":"119:8.2"}]},{"h":"El autootorgamiento en Urantia","items":[{"x":"Después de seis autootorgamientos, Micael descendió a Urantia a semejanza de la carne mortal, la más baja de las criaturas volitivas.","r":["120:0.2"]},{"x":"El autootorgamiento final fue más allá de ganar la soberanía; fue un plan para la revelación suprema de la sumisión a la voluntad del Padre Universal.","r":["120:0.7","120:0.8"]},{"q":"Jesús fue Dios y hombre —por siempre y para siempre.","r":"120:4.3"},{"q":"No olvidéis jamás el hecho de que el fin espiritual supremo de la encarnación de Micael era el aumentar de la revelación de Dios.","r":"120:4.4"},{"x":"Como su muerte en Urantia completó su carrera de autootorgamiento, pudo decir con verdad: «Consumado es».","r":["21:4.5"]},{"x":"Y así, este pequeño planeta, el hogar mortal del soberano Cristo Micael, se ha convertido en el santuario sentimental de todo Nebadon.","r":["119:8.8"]}]},{"h":"El gobierno y el destino del Hijo Mayor","items":[{"x":"Después del autootorgamiento en Urantia, Micael fue reconocido por los Ancianos de los Días y por el Padre Universal como soberano establecido de Nebadon.","r":["119:8.1"]},{"x":"Cuando el Espíritu Materno se subordinó a él, Micael se convirtió en el depositario personal de la divinidad, con todo poder en el cielo y en la tierra.","r":["33:2.3","33:2.4"]},{"x":"El Hijo Mayor derrama el Espíritu de la Verdad «sobre toda carne» y se comunica así sin cesar con los mundos en los que ha residido.","r":["21:5.10"]},{"x":"La suma de los siete autootorgamientos es una nueva revelación del Ser Supremo para Nebadon, y también ha aumentado la soberanía del Dios el Supremo en evolución.","r":["119:8.3","119:8.5"]},{"x":"Se cree que los Micaeles están destinados a llegar a ser, en la eternidad, literalmente «el camino, la verdad y la vida».","r":["21:6.4"]}]}],"see":["Espíritu Materno del Universo Local","Universo local de Nebadon","Espíritu de la Verdad","Hijos Avonales","Ser Supremo","Ancianos de los Días"]},{"n":4,"t":"Hijo Eterno","en":"Eternal Son","sum":"El Hijo Eterno es la Segunda Fuente y Centro, la expresión perfecta del primer concepto personal y absoluto del Padre Universal. Es la Palabra divina viviente, la revelación final del espíritu y de la personalidad del Padre, y el administrador espiritual que sostiene toda la realidad espiritual en el circuito de gravedad del espíritu. Al extender el amor del Padre como misericordia, se acerca a las criaturas mediante los autootorgamientos de los Hijos Paradisiacos.","sections":[{"h":"Identidad y naturaleza","items":[{"x":"El Hijo Eterno es la expresión completa del primer concepto personal y absoluto del Padre; siempre que el Padre se expresa personalmente, lo hace por medio del Hijo.","r":["6:0.1"]},{"x":"La expresión «primer pensamiento» es solo una concesión a las mentes ligadas al tiempo; el Hijo no tiene comienzo y es coeterno con el Padre.","r":["6:0.2","6:0.4"]},{"q":"La Primera Fuente y Centro es el Absoluto Volitivo; la Segunda Fuente y Centro es el Absoluto de Personalidad.","r":"6:1.2"},{"x":"El Padre nunca actúa personalmente como creador sino en conjunción con el Hijo o con la acción coordinada del Hijo.","r":["6:1.3"]},{"x":"En Urantia se ha confundido al Hijo Original con el Hijo autootorgador, Micael de Nebadon, pero el título de «Hijo Eterno» pertenece únicamente al Hijo Original.","r":["6:1.5","6:1.6"]}]},{"h":"Ministro de la misericordia","items":[{"x":"El Hijo es tan inmutable e infinitamente digno de confianza como el Padre, y a nosotros nos parece más personal, por estar un paso más cerca de nuestro alcance.","r":["6:2.1"]},{"q":"Tal como Dios es amor, así el Hijo es misericordia.","r":"6:3.1"},{"x":"El Hijo no es un intercesor que suplica misericordia al Padre; toda misericordia que muestra el Hijo es una revelación directa del amor del Padre.","r":["6:3.4"]},{"x":"La misericordia es amor aplicado; por analogía, el amor de Dios se asemeja más al amor de un padre, mientras que el amor del Hijo Eterno se asemeja más al afecto de una madre.","r":["6:3.5"]},{"x":"El Padre ama a sus hijos del universo como un padre, mientras que el Hijo Eterno contempla a cada criatura a la vez como padre y como hermano.","r":["6:2.8"]}]},{"h":"El circuito de gravedad del espíritu","items":[{"x":"El Hijo es omnipotente solo en el ámbito espiritual; no actúa personalmente en los dominios físicos ni en el ministerio de la mente, salvo a través del Actor Conjunto.","r":["6:4.2","6:5.1"]},{"x":"La gravedad espiritual está libre de demora temporal, no la disminuye el espacio y no decrece con el cuadrado de la distancia.","r":["7:1.2"]},{"x":"Las realidades espirituales responden a la gravedad espiritual según su valor cualitativo, y esa respuesta es tan segura y previsible como la respuesta de la materia a la gravedad.","r":["7:1.3","7:1.8"]},{"q":"El pecado y la rebelión pueden interferir con el funcionamiento de los circuitos de los universos locales, pero nada puede suspender la gravedad espiritual del Hijo Eterno.","r":"7:1.7"},{"q":"El circuito de la gravedad espiritual literalmente arrastra el alma del hombre hacia el Paraíso.","r":"7:3.2"}]},{"h":"La oración y la relación con el individuo","items":[{"x":"El espíritu del Hijo Eterno nos rodea, pero no mora en nosotros ni llega a formar parte de nosotros como lo hace el Monitor Misterioso.","r":["6:4.6"]},{"x":"El contenido espiritual de la oración sincera se transmite instantáneamente por el circuito de gravedad del espíritu a toda personalidad divina interesada.","r":["7:3.3"]},{"x":"Las peticiones puramente materiales y egocéntricas no pueden entrar en el circuito espiritual y caen muertas.","r":["7:3.6"]},{"q":"Es el pensamiento motivante, el contenido espiritual, el que valida la súplica del mortal. Las palabras carecen de valor.","r":"7:3.7"}]},{"h":"El autootorgamiento y el plan de perfección","items":[{"x":"El Hijo aceptó sin reservas el plan del Padre de logro progresivo, y él mismo propuso el plan de autootorgamiento, que consiste en enviar a los Hijos de Dios a los mundos evolutivos.","r":["7:4.4","7:4.5"]},{"x":"El Hijo Eterno es el fideicomisario personal y el guardián divino del plan de ascensión de las criaturas que el Padre le confió.","r":["7:4.7"]},{"x":"Puesto que la personalidad del Hijo no puede fragmentarse, él participa en la experiencia de las criaturas mediante las encarnaciones de los Hijos Paradisiacos.","r":["7:5.3","7:5.4"]},{"x":"El Hijo Eterno se autootorgó siete veces en los siete circuitos de Havona, un hecho que es un estímulo eterno para todo peregrino que atraviesa Havona.","r":["7:5.5","7:5.9"]},{"q":"Es literalmente cierto que quien haya visto a un Hijo Paradisiaco, ha visto al Hijo Eterno de Dios.","r":"7:5.11"}]},{"h":"Revelación suprema del Padre","items":[{"x":"El Hijo Eterno es la revelación completa y final del espíritu y de la personalidad del Padre, y todo conocimiento del Padre procede del Hijo y de sus Hijos.","r":["7:7.1"]},{"x":"El Padre se acerca a nosotros como personalidad solo por medio de los Hijos divinos del Hijo Eterno, y por ese camino vivo también nosotros ascendemos hacia el Padre.","r":["7:7.4"]},{"x":"Los peregrinos que atraviesan los circuitos de Havona pueden llegar al Hijo mucho antes de estar preparados para discernir al Padre.","r":["7:7.5"]},{"x":"La personalidad del Hijo no brilla con fuerza para la mente material o morontial; solo cuando comienza la ascensión espiritual se vuelve cada vez más real.","r":["6:8.5","6:8.6"]},{"q":"In the same sense that God is the Universal Father, the Son is the Universal Mother.","r":"6:8.1"}]}],"see":["Padre Universal","Espíritu Infinito","Trinidad del Paraíso","Hijo Creador Micael","Oración","Misericordia"]},{"n":25,"t":"Hijos Avonales","en":"Avonal Sons","sum":"Los Hijos Avonales, o Hijos Magisteriales, son la segunda orden de Hijos Paradisiacos, procedentes del Hijo Eterno y del Espíritu Infinito. En los mundos evolutivos sirven como jueces de las dispensaciones, como magistrados que elevan una era planetaria un peldaño más y como Hijos autootorgadores nacidos de mujer que viven como mortales. Gracias a estos «Cristos menores», respaldados plenamente por el poder del Hijo Creador, casi todos los mundos habitados reciben el Espíritu de la Verdad y los Ajustadores del Pensamiento; sin embargo, Urantia nunca ha recibido una misión magisterial.","sections":[{"h":"La segunda orden de Hijos Paradisiacos","items":[{"x":"Cada vez que un concepto absoluto del Hijo Eterno se une con un nuevo ideal de servicio amoroso del Espíritu Infinito, aparece un nuevo Hijo Magisterial del Paraíso.","r":["20:2.1","20:1.11"]},{"x":"Se calcula que los Hijos Magisteriales del gran universo son alrededor de mil millones; los dirige el consejo supremo del Paraíso y, una vez asignados a un universo local, sirven bajo el Hijo Creador.","r":["20:2.2"]},{"q":"since each Avonal Son has an exclusive personality, since no two are alike","r":"20:2.3"},{"q":"Y estos «Cristos menores» son tan eficientes y tan todopoderosos en sus respectivos autootorgamientos planetarios como lo fue el Hijo Creador y Soberano en Urantia.","r":"35:0.1"},{"x":"Mientras que los Hijos Creadores revelan el carácter del Padre, los Avonales, Hijos del autootorgamiento misericordioso, revelan la naturaleza del Hijo Eterno con su compasión infinita.","r":["20:10.3","20:10.4"]}]},{"h":"Jueces de las dispensaciones","items":[{"x":"Los Avonales son los magistrados de los reinos que despiertan a los supervivientes dormidos, ponen fin a una dispensación y reasignan a los ministros planetarios a las tareas de la nueva era.","r":["20:3.1"]},{"q":"though they may render judgments extinguishing the identity of personal creatures, they do not execute such sentences.","r":"20:3.2"},{"x":"En las visitas «técnicas», realizadas únicamente para el juicio dispensacional, no se encarnan, sino que vienen como seres espirituales invisibles para las criaturas materiales.","r":["20:3.3","52:4.3"]},{"x":"La lista de llamada que cierra una dispensación la proclama el arcángel que acompaña al Avonal, y los guardianes seráficos de los durmientes responden a esa «voz del arcángel».","r":["37:3.6"]},{"x":"Incluso en los mundos establecidos en luz y vida continúan sus actos judiciales, pero entonces se vuelven formales y no alteran el curso de los acontecimientos planetarios.","r":["55:0.2"]}]},{"h":"Misiones magisteriales","items":[{"x":"La paz mundial, sin conflictos raciales ni hostilidades nacionales, es la señal de que un planeta está lo bastante maduro para recibir a un Hijo Magisterial.","r":["52:3.12"]},{"x":"En la primera misión magisterial, el Avonal se encarna sin nacer, como adulto plenamente desarrollado de la raza, y aparece como alguien a quien los hombres pueden ver y tocar.","r":["20:4.1","20:2.6"]},{"q":"Each new dispensation extends the horizon of revealed religion","r":"52:4.4"},{"x":"Poco después de la primera visita de un Hijo Magisterial, la humanidad logra la liberación económica, y el trabajo diario necesario para el propio sustento se reduce a unas dos horas y media.","r":["52:4.5"]},{"x":"Si una misión magisterial no prepara al mundo para un Hijo autootorgador, viene un segundo Hijo Magisterial, o más, y hace avanzar a la humanidad una era cada vez.","r":["52:4.9"]}]},{"h":"Misiones de autootorgamiento","items":[{"x":"Todo Avonal se autootorga al menos una vez en alguna raza mortal, y en cada planeta aparece un solo Hijo autootorgador, nacido de mujer.","r":["20:2.7","20:5.4"]},{"q":"Pero un Avonal autootorgador sí declara: «El que me haya visto a mí, ha visto al Hijo Eterno de Dios».","r":"20:6.5"},{"x":"Un Hijo Magisterial se autootorga siempre sujeto no a la voluntad del Padre, sino a la voluntad del Hijo Eterno del Paraíso.","r":["20:6.5"]},{"x":"Los Hijos autootorgadores deben morir, pero el plan divino no exige una muerte violenta, y la mayoría de los mundos los tratan con más consideración.","r":["20:6.6","20:6.7"]},{"q":"Nunca dejan de alcanzar el objetivo de la misión de autootorgamiento.","r":"20:5.7"},{"x":"Cuando un Avonal que ha completado su autootorgamiento y el Hijo Creador envían juntos el Espíritu de la Verdad, las criaturas volitivas normales de ese mundo reciben Ajustadores del Pensamiento.","r":["52:5.6","20:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Colaboradores, y Urantia","items":[{"x":"En las misiones planetarias los Avonales son ayudados por Melquisedek y arcángeles, y en las misiones de autootorgamiento les acompañan Brillantes Estrellas Vespertinas y un séquito de autootorgamiento de 144.","r":["20:2.9","39:1.4"]},{"x":"Por lo general, después de siete misiones un Avonal cede la oportunidad a otros Hijos y se une a la administración del universo en los altos consejos del Hijo Creador.","r":["20:2.8"]},{"q":"Urantia nunca ha recibido a un Hijo Avonal en misión magisterial.","r":"20:4.4"},{"x":"El Hijo autootorgador de Urantia no fue un Avonal, sino Micael mismo, aunque cualquier Hijo autootorgador habría sido igualmente adecuado para la rehabilitación espiritual.","r":["49:5.26","20:5.6"]},{"x":"Puesto que el mundo del autootorgamiento de Micael es pupilo del Hijo Mayor, solo el tiempo revelará cuándo vendrá un Hijo Magisterial a Urantia.","r":["20:4.5"]}]}],"see":["Hijo Creador Micael","Hijos Instructores Trinitarios","Los Melquisedek","Hijo Eterno","Espíritu de la Verdad","Luz y vida"]},{"n":31,"t":"Hijos e Hijas Materiales","en":"Material Sons and Daughters","sum":"The Material Sons and Daughters are an order of sex-endowed Sons produced by the Creator Son for each local system; sent to the evolutionary worlds as Adam and Eve, they are charged with the biologic uplift of the races. Being material, they are visible to mortals and form the last link between the invisible Planetary Prince and human beings. The Adam and Eve of Urantia defaulted in their mission, yet their contribution greatly improved mankind.","sections":[{"h":"Origin and Nature","items":[{"x":"The Material Sons and Daughters are the offspring of the Creator Son; the Universe Mother Spirit takes no part in their production.","r":["51:1.1"]},{"x":"For each system the Creator Son makes only the original pair, fashioned to the life pattern of that system, and all the rest are their descendants.","r":["51:1.2"]},{"x":"They stand eight to ten feet tall and shine with a violet radiance; Adam and Eve are equal yet complementary and usually work as a pair.","r":["51:1.3"]},{"x":"With a dual constitution that takes in both material food and cosmic energy, they are cut off from their life source if they rebel and in the end meet material death.","r":["51:1.4"]},{"q":"Estos Hijos Materiales constituyen el último vínculo físico en la cadena de personalidades que se extiende hacia abajo desde la divinidad y la perfección arriba hasta la humanidad y la existencia material.","r":"45:5.3"}]},{"h":"Life on Jerusem, the System Capital","items":[{"x":"Each family of Material Sons and Daughters lives in the Adamic domain of one thousand centers on Jerusem, and their numbers increase by natural reproduction.","r":["45:5.2","45:5.4"]},{"x":"The Adamites of Jerusem experiment with self-government through elections and representative government, and they handle most of the routine affairs of the capital sphere.","r":["45:5.5","45:5.6"]},{"x":"The Melchizedeks maintain a faculty at each system headquarters for the education and spiritual training of young Material Sons and Daughters.","r":["45:5.7"]},{"x":"While living on the system capital, Material Sons have no Thought Adjusters, but through service they gain capacity for Adjuster indwelling and the ascending career.","r":["51:1.6"]}]},{"h":"The Mission of a Planetary Adam","items":[{"x":"When an evolutionary world reaches the peak of its physical evolution, a volunteer pair is chosen, dematerialized, and carried to that world by seraphim.","r":["51:2.1","51:2.2"]},{"x":"On arrival they are rematerialized under the direction of the Life Carriers, and they remain in the unconsciousness of seraphic sleep throughout the process.","r":["51:2.4"]},{"q":"La actividad principal de dicha pareja importada consiste en multiplicar y elevar a los hijos del tiempo.","r":"51:3.3"},{"x":"Adam and Eve do not mate directly with the evolutionary races; their children voluntarily unite with superior men and women brought to the garden.","r":["51:5.3"]},{"x":"With the added strain of the violet race, more progress is made in one hundred thousand years than in the previous million.","r":["51:5.6"]},{"x":"The garden schools teach practical arts, economics, and civil government, and with the schools of the Planetary Prince they set the pace of civilization.","r":["51:6.2","51:6.4"]}]},{"h":"The Link Between God and Man","items":[{"x":"Unlike the other planetary Sons, Material Sons are visible to mortals, understandable to them, and can actually associate with them.","r":["51:1.7"]},{"q":"En estos Hijos e Hijas Materiales inmortales hallamos el último e indispensable eslabón que conecta a Dios con el hombre, sorteando el abismo casi infinito entre el Creador eterno y las más bajas personalidades finitas del tiempo.","r":"51:6.5"},{"x":"They can see the invisible Planetary Prince and his staff, and so they can interpret him to mortals.","r":["51:6.5"]},{"x":"On the ascending path mortals come to recognize seven fathers, the second of whom is the Planetary Adam, the father of the realm.","r":["51:6.6","51:6.8"]}]},{"h":"The Adam and Eve of Urantia","items":[{"x":"The Adam and Eve who came to Urantia were number 14,311 of the senior corps on Jerusem and had been heads of the laboratory dealing with the modification of life forms.","r":["74:1.1","74:1.2"]},{"x":"They were overcome by the subtle counterplans of Caligastia and violated their covenant, but they did not join the Lucifer rebellion.","r":["51:3.4"]},{"q":"No ha habido ninguna «caída del hombre».","r":"75:8.2"},{"x":"Though the divine plan miscarried, the Adamic bestowal left the peoples of Urantia biologically far better than before.","r":["75:8.1","75:8.3"]},{"x":"Adam and Eve awoke again on the mansion worlds in a special resurrection and returned to Jerusem as ascending citizens.","r":["76:6.2","76:6.3"]},{"q":"El pueblo hace la civilización; la civilización no hace al pueblo.","r":"76:6.4"}]},{"h":"Ascending Material Sons","items":[{"q":"Y en efecto, los Adanes Planetarios —los Hijos e Hijas Materiales de los mundos evolucionarios— son Hijos descendentes, que bajan a los mundos habitados desde sus esferas de origen, las capitales de los sistemas locales.","r":"40:2.1"},{"x":"An Adam and Eve who succeed in their mission may, once the world is settled in light and life, retire from administration and register as perfected Material Sons.","r":["40:2.2"]},{"x":"Material Sons whose planetary assignment is long delayed may also be released from citizenship status and advance toward Paradise with the ascending pilgrims.","r":["31:5.1"]},{"x":"Material Sons are rare in the finaliter companies but are always chosen as leaders, and an Edenic pair sometimes works together as one personality.","r":["31:5.3"]}]}],"see":["Adán y Eva","Razas","Cuerpo de la Finalidad","Portadores de Vida","Seres intermedios","Luz y vida"]},{"n":26,"t":"Hijos Instructores Trinitarios","en":"Trinity Teacher Sons","sum":"Los Hijos Instructores Trinitarios, o Dainales, son Hijos que proceden directamente de la Trinidad del Paraíso y que, junto con los Hijos Creadores y los Hijos Magisteriales, forman la tercera orden de Hijos Paradisiacos. No gobiernan ni juzgan; son los educadores de los universos, dedicados a la iluminación moral y al despertar espiritual tanto de los mortales como de los seres espirituales. En los mundos evolutivos llevan a cabo la última misión divina, que abre una era espiritual que conduce al planeta a la era de luz y vida.","sections":[{"h":"Hijos de origen trinitario","items":[{"x":"Estos Hijos fueron traídos a la existencia por la Trinidad del Paraíso; se les llama Dainales en Havona, Hijos Instructores Trinitarios en Orvonton e Hijos Espirituales Paradisiacos en Salvington.","r":["20:7.1"]},{"q":"Estos seres constituyen el único grupo de Hijos de Dios que os ha sido revelado cuyo origen está en la Trinidad del Paraíso.","r":"19:1.3"},{"x":"De origen trinitario, pero al servicio del ministerio de la filiación divina, tienen una doble condición como seres de enlace entre las personalidades de origen trinitario y las de origen dual.","r":["19:1.1"]},{"x":"A diferencia de los Hijos estacionarios de la Trinidad, cuyo número es fijo, los Hijos Instructores no dejan de aumentar; el número indicado es de algo más de veintiún mil millones, además de grandes reservas en el Paraíso.","r":["19:1.2","20:7.2"]},{"x":"Comparten las naturalezas combinadas de las tres Deidades, pero en Havona parecen reflejar más al Padre, en los superuniversos al Hijo Eterno y en las creaciones locales al Espíritu Infinito.","r":["20:7.4"]},{"q":"En todos los universos, ellos son la manifestación del servicio y la discreción de la sabiduría.","r":"20:7.4"}]},{"h":"Hijos que enseñan en lugar de gobernar","items":[{"x":"No son creadores ni rescatadores, ni jueces ni gobernantes, y por eso no forman parte orgánica de los gobiernos locales ni superuniversales.","r":["20:7.3"]},{"q":"Son los educadores universales, dedicados al despertar espiritual y a la guía moral de todos los reinos.","r":"20:7.3"},{"x":"Son enviados directamente a las sedes centrales de los superuniversos sin formación previa en el universo central, y como no tienen poder propio de atracción espiritual, utilizan la influencia espiritual de los Hijos Creadores y de los Hijos Magisteriales.","r":["20:7.5"]},{"x":"Comienzan su ministerio en los sistemas locales, avanzan a través de las constelaciones hasta la labor más elevada de la creación local y se ocupan por igual de educar a los mortales y a los seres nativos del universo local, como los serafines.","r":["20:8.1","20:8.2"]},{"x":"Son el profesorado encargado de las pruebas y los exámenes de calificación para las etapas inferiores del servicio del universo, y dirigen cursos de formación desde las escuelas planetarias hasta los altos colegios de sabiduría de Salvington.","r":["20:8.3"]},{"x":"El sistema educativo de Nebadon es administrado conjuntamente por los Hijos Instructores y el cuerpo docente de los Melquisedek, y todo el universo se describe como una vasta escuela.","r":["37:6.1","37:6.2"]},{"x":"Adoptan como aprendices a hijos trinidizados por criaturas, los forman y pueden proponerlos para el abrazo de la Trinidad.","r":["22:8.3","22:8.4"]}]},{"h":"La apertura de una era espiritual en un planeta","items":[{"x":"No tienen nada que ver con el fin de las dispensaciones ni con el juicio de los muertos; se dedican por completo a traer a un planeta evolutivo el amanecer de la era de las realidades espirituales.","r":["20:9.2"]},{"q":"Hacen realidad las contrapartes espirituales del conocimiento material y de la sabiduría del tiempo.","r":"20:9.2"},{"x":"Un Hijo Instructor planetario es ayudado por setenta Hijos primarios, doce secundarios y tres de la orden suprema, y el cuerpo permanece no menos de mil años de tiempo planetario.","r":["52:7.2","20:9.3"]},{"q":"Esta misión es una contribución Trinitaria a los esfuerzos antecedentes de todas las personalidades divinas que han ministrado a un mundo habitado.","r":"52:7.2"},{"x":"Como no se materializan para hacerse visibles a los mortales, las Brillantes Estrellas Vespertinas sirven de enlace entre el cuerpo invisible de Hijos Instructores y los mortales del mundo.","r":["20:9.3","37:2.9"]},{"x":"En esta era muchos mortales son trasladados de entre los vivos, y a medida que aumenta la fusión con el Ajustador, la muerte natural se vuelve cada vez menos frecuente.","r":["52:7.4"]}]},{"h":"Urantia y el futuro de luz y vida","items":[{"x":"Como nunca ha pasado por una era espiritual, Urantia no está familiarizada con estos Hijos, pero ya ahora hay Hijos Instructores que visitan el mundo para planificar su futura estancia.","r":["20:9.1"]},{"x":"Aparecerán después de que los habitantes de este mundo se hayan liberado relativamente de las cadenas del animalismo y de los grilletes del materialismo.","r":["20:9.1"]},{"x":"Nadie sabe si la segunda venida prometida por Jesús ocurrirá antes o después de la aparición de un Hijo Magisterial o de los Hijos Instructores.","r":["52:7.1"]},{"x":"Al final de una de sus misiones repetidas, el Príncipe Planetario es elevado a la condición de Soberano Planetario, y el Soberano del Sistema proclama la apertura de la era de luz y vida.","r":["52:7.10"]},{"q":"sooner or later the grace of God and the ministry of angels will usher in the day of the advent of the Trinity Teacher Sons;","r":"52:7.14"},{"x":"En Uversa se cree que los Hijos Instructores, asociados durante mucho tiempo a la vida de los mortales evolutivos, se unirán eternamente al Cuerpo de la Finalidad cuando el superuniverso esté establecido en luz y vida.","r":["20:9.5"]}]},{"h":"La cooperación de los tres Hijos Paradisiacos","items":[{"x":"Los Hijos Creadores revelan el carácter del Padre, los Avonales la misericordia del Hijo Eterno y los Dainales la personalidad docente del Espíritu Infinito; juntos realizan la soberanía de Dios el Supremo.","r":["20:10.4"]},{"q":"En los Hijos Instructores Trinitarios el amor, misericordia y ministerio de las tres Deidades del Paraíso están coordinados en los más elevados niveles de valor espacio-temporal y son presentados a los universos como verdad viviente, bondad divina, y verdadera belleza espiritual.","r":"20:10.3"},{"x":"Los Hijos Instructores son las personalidades coordinadoras supremas de origen trinitario; en el vasto universo existe siempre un gran peligro de puntos de vista estrechos y de conceptos fragmentados de la realidad.","r":["19:1.4"]},{"q":"Ellos son los maestros excelsos de todas las personalidades espirituales, aun los maestros comprobados y auténticos de los Hijos de Dios mismos.","r":"20:8.4"}]}],"see":["Trinidad del Paraíso","Hijos Avonales","Hijo Creador Micael","Luz y vida","Los Melquisedek","Cuerpo de la Finalidad"]},{"n":96,"t":"Huestes angélicas","en":"Angelic Hosts","sum":"The angelic hosts are ministering spirits deriving from the Infinite Spirit: the supernaphim of the central universe, the seconaphim of the superuniverses, and the seraphim, cherubim, and sanobim of the local universes. They have no material bodies, yet they possess distinct individual personalities, and as associates of evolving will creatures they minister to man in daily life and through death and resurrection. Without ever invading the human will, the angels help mortals on their ascending journey with love and sympathy.","sections":[{"h":"Ministering Spirits of Time","items":[{"x":"The personalities of the Infinite Spirit comprise three orders: the angels, ministering spirits of time; the messenger hosts of space; and the higher spirits.","r":["38:0.1"]},{"x":"Supernaphim form the angelic corps of the central universe, seconaphim of the superuniverses, and seraphim, cherubim, and sanobim of the local universes.","r":["38:0.2","28:0.1"]},{"x":"Angels are associates of evolving and ascending will creatures and co-workers with divine personalities, and all are highly individualized, unique personalities.","r":["26:1.1"]},{"x":"In this revelation the word \"angels\" refers chiefly to the seraphic offspring of the Universe Mother Spirit who are concerned with the mortal survival plan.","r":["38:3.1"]}]},{"h":"Origin and Nature of the Seraphim","items":[{"x":"Seraphim are created by the Universe Mother Spirit in projections of 41,472 at a time, and they are still being created, since Nebadon is still in the making.","r":["38:1.1","38:1.3"]},{"q":"Los ángeles no tienen cuerpos materiales, pero son seres definidos y discretos; son de naturaleza y origen espirituales.","r":"38:2.1"},{"x":"Angels are invisible to man, yet they perceive us as we are in the flesh and understand human emotions.","r":["38:2.1"]},{"x":"Seraphim are affectionate and sympathetic but not sex-emotional creatures, and they are much like what we will be on the mansion worlds.","r":["38:2.2"]},{"x":"The Infinite Spirit seeks to create uniformly perfect seraphim, but for unknown reasons the offspring are highly diverse.","r":["39:0.1"]},{"q":"Seraphim are still being periodically created","r":"38:1.3"}]},{"h":"The Angelic Orders","items":[{"x":"Local universe seraphim are divided into seven orders: supreme, superior, supervisor, and administrator seraphim, planetary helpers, transition ministers, and seraphim of the future.","r":["39:0.2","39:0.8"]},{"x":"It is hard to say that any seraphim are inferior to other groups, and the higher orders are the more eager to be assigned to lowly service.","r":["39:0.9","39:0.11"]},{"x":"Cherubim and sanobim, of the same origin as seraphim, are the lowest angelic order; affectionate and almost human, they faithfully assist the seraphim.","r":["38:7.1","38:7.3"]},{"x":"Cherubim are positive senior personalities and sanobim negative complemental ones, and the two are functionally united as one.","r":["38:7.2"]},{"x":"Seraphim may reach Paradise by several paths, such as elevation to Evening Stars or completion of specialized service.","r":["39:8.1","39:8.3"]}]},{"h":"Angels Beside Man","items":[{"q":"The teaching about guardian angels is not a myth","r":"113:1.1"},{"x":"Since Michael's bestowal, seraphim are assigned not by race but according to human intellect, spirituality, and destiny.","r":["113:1.2"]},{"q":"Los ángeles no invaden la santidad de la mente humana; no manipulan la voluntad de los mortales; tampoco se ponen en contacto directo con los Ajustadores residentes.","r":"113:5.1"},{"x":"Angels are very near us and truly care for us; though they have no physical tears, they have spiritual emotions.","r":["113:5.2"]},{"x":"Seraphim work on our behalf under the orders of their superiors, regardless of our requests or whims.","r":["113:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Guides Through Death and Resurrection","items":[{"x":"Jesus said there is joy in the presence of the angels of heaven over one sinner who repents.","r":["167:7.5"]},{"q":"Los ángeles son los guías certeros y celestiales del alma del hombre durante ese período desconocido y de tiempo indefinido que ocurre entre la muerte de la carne y la nueva vida en las moradas espirituales».","r":"167:7.6"},{"x":"On first awakening on the mansion worlds we actually see for the first time the angelic companions who were always with us on earth.","r":["113:7.1"]},{"x":"On the morontia spheres the two attending seraphim, now open companions, aid our progress while they themselves learn and grow.","r":["113:7.2"]}]},{"h":"Seraphim in Planetary Government","items":[{"q":"LOS Altísimos gobiernan en los reinos de los hombres a través de muchas fuerzas y agencias celestiales pero principalmente a través del ministerio de los serafines.","r":"114:0.1"},{"x":"At one noon roll call the planetary angels and guardians of Urantia numbered more than five hundred million pairs of seraphim.","r":["114:0.2"]},{"x":"When the Spirit of Truth was poured out, twelve corps of the master seraphim of planetary supervision came to Urantia with the first resident governor general.","r":["114:6.1","114:6.2"]},{"x":"It is through the ministry of angels that one world can keep in touch with other worlds.","r":["167:7.4"]}]}],"see":["Serafines","Serafines guardianes","Espíritu Infinito","Espíritu Materno del Universo Local","Mundos de estancia","Seres intermedios"]},{"n":62,"t":"Justicia","en":"Justice","sum":"Justice is the application of law; it is not the personal attitude of any one Deity but a collective function of the Paradise Trinity. The Ancients of Days and the Trinity-origin Sons render its verdicts, the personalities of the Infinite Spirit supply the evidence, and justice is always tempered by mercy. Man's idea of justice evolved from blood vengeance to the courts of the state, and Jesus taught that justice should be left to the group while the individual shows mercy.","sections":[{"h":"A Collective Function of the Trinity","items":[{"x":"Law issues from the Father, its administration belongs to the Son, its revelation and interpretation to the Spirit, and justice, the application of law, to the Trinity.","r":["10:6.1"]},{"q":"La justicia no es nunca una actitud personal; es siempre una función plural.","r":"10:6.2"},{"x":"Evidence for fairness is presented by personalities of the Infinite Spirit, and verdicts are rendered by the stationary Sons of the Trinity.","r":["10:6.3","10:6.4"]},{"x":"The Ancients of Days render the decisions of supreme equity in the seven superuniverses, but in perfect Havona this function exists only in theory.","r":["10:6.17"]},{"x":"The Supreme Trinity Personalities represent justice throughout the grand universe and function as the executive judgment of the Trinity.","r":["18:0.10"]}]},{"h":"The Justice and Fairness of God","items":[{"q":"The justice of the Universal Father cannot be influenced by the acts and performances of his creatures","r":"2:3.1"},{"x":"It is futile to plead with God to escape the just results of natural law and spiritual mandates, for one reaps what one sows.","r":["2:3.2"]},{"x":"Mercy guides God's attitude toward the individual, while fairness guides his attitude toward the whole.","r":["12:7.1"]},{"q":"La justicia es el pensamiento colectivo de la rectitud; la misericordia es su expresión personal.","r":"10:6.18"},{"x":"When fully understood, the righteous justice of the Trinity and the merciful love of the Father coincide as one.","r":["10:6.18","2:4.4"]}]},{"h":"The Execution of Justice and Its Delay","items":[{"x":"The final result for a being wholly identified with sin is annihilation, but its execution is delayed until the appointed processes of justice are fulfilled.","r":["2:3.2","2:3.3"]},{"x":"Between identification with sin and the execution of the sentence there must be time enough to satisfy all concerned, even the sinner himself.","r":["54:3.2","54:3.3"]},{"q":"Existe una ley básica de justicia en el universo que la misericordia encuentra impotente de eludir.","r":"146:2.5"},{"x":"The seraphic advocate of the courts is the mortal's defender, representing the element of mercy inherent in justice, the fairness that knows motives and tendencies.","r":["39:1.8"]},{"x":"At the adjudication of survival the Memory of Mercy is read, and justice prevails only when mercy has been exhausted.","r":["28:6.6","28:6.7"]}]},{"h":"Justice as It Evolved in Human Society","items":[{"q":"La justicia natural es una teoría elaborada por el hombre; no es una realidad.","r":"70:10.1"},{"x":"Man's idea of justice is getting his rights; though latent in the spirit-endowed mind, it grew by evolution.","r":["70:10.2"]},{"x":"Primitive society substituted trial by ordeal and blood vengeance for justice, ignoring motive and judging only by the injury inflicted.","r":["70:10.3","70:10.5","70:10.9"]},{"x":"The true administration of justice begins when vengeance is taken from the individual and the kin and given to the state.","r":["70:10.13"]},{"x":"It gradually became clear that the certainty and swiftness of punishment deter crime more than its severity.","r":["70:10.15"]}]},{"h":"Justice as Jesus Taught It","items":[{"q":"El gobierno civil se basa en la justicia, así como la verdadera religión se basa en la misericordia».","r":"132:4.8"},{"x":"A magistrate's duty is not only to punish the guilty but to acquit the innocent, so that injustice befalls not even the humblest citizen.","r":["132:4.8"]},{"x":"The individual should show mercy, but fixing punishment should be left to groups and their representatives who know all the circumstances.","r":["133:1.2","159:1.6"]},{"x":"Jesus possessed a firm sense of justice, but it was always tempered by mercy, and he recognized society's right to punish criminals.","r":["140:8.12","140:8.4"]},{"q":"Tened fe —confianza en el triunfo final de la justicia divina y de la bondad eterna.","r":"140:8.8"}]}],"see":["Misericordia","Trinidad del Paraíso","Ancianos de los Días","Gobierno y sociedad","Pecado","Bondad"]},{"n":41,"t":"Libre albedrío","en":"Free Will","sum":"Free will is the power of choice that the Universal Father gives together with personality. God himself is the original personality with absolute free will, and man shares that will on a relative and finite level. Especially in matters of eternal survival the mortal's choice holds a sovereignty that no being can invade, so free will becomes the key by which man builds his own destiny.","sections":[{"h":"The Free Will of God","items":[{"x":"God is not an automatic force bound by law but the original personality possessed of free will.","r":["12:7.6"]},{"x":"God's free will is conditioned only by his own divine nature and perfect attributes.","r":["4:4.3"]},{"x":"He shares personality and goodness with his creatures, but infinity of will belongs to God alone.","r":["4:4.4"]},{"x":"Even though God foreknows the acts of his children, that foreknowledge does not abrogate their freedom.","r":["3:3.4","118:7.1"]}]},{"h":"The Gift of Choice Given to Personality","items":[{"x":"The two marks that distinguish creature personality are self-consciousness and the associated relative free will.","r":["16:8.5","16:8.6"]},{"x":"Man's relative free will relates to such higher functions as moral decision, spiritual choice, unselfish love, and worship.","r":["16:8.7","16:8.13","16:8.14"]},{"x":"The bestowal of personality adds to a living organism the prerogatives of self-determination and self-evolution.","r":["118:7.6"]},{"q":"El hombre mortal está dotado de libre albedrío, el poder de elección, y aunque dicha elección no sea absoluta es sin embargo relativamente final en un nivel finito y en cuanto respecta al destino de la personalidad que selecciona.","r":"118:6.4"},{"q":"El hombre es en verdad el arquitecto de su propio destino eterno.","r":"103:5.10"}]},{"h":"A Will That No One Invades","items":[{"x":"God has decreed that in matters of eternal survival no being or force can interfere with the free will of a mortal.","r":["5:6.8"]},{"q":"No personal creature can be coerced into the eternal adventure;","r":"5:6.12"},{"x":"The Adjuster brings a plan for the ideal life but never arbitrarily moves man's choices; it always respects his will.","r":["110:2.1"]},{"q":"No human being will ever be spiritualized by a divine Monitor against his will;","r":"110:2.2"},{"x":"Angels, too, do not invade the sanctity of the human mind or manipulate the will, and they have no authority to curtail the prerogatives of choice.","r":["113:5.1"]},{"x":"Even a rebel like Caligastia could not force a normal person to do anything against that person's will.","r":["66:8.6"]}]},{"h":"True Liberty and False Liberty","items":[{"x":"True liberty is the reward of evolutionary progress; false liberty is a subtle deception born of the errors of time.","r":["54:1.2"]},{"q":"La verdadera libertad es el fruto del autocontrol; la falsa libertad, la suposición de la autoafirmación.","r":"54:1.6"},{"x":"Liberty without self-mastery is an illusion, and license masquerading as liberty is the forerunner of bondage.","r":["54:1.5"]},{"x":"The Lucifer rebellion paraded as liberty, but in reality it threatened to rob creatures of their freewill participation.","r":["54:2.3"]},{"x":"Sin arises from an immaturity that, dazzled by freedom of the will, fails to grasp the obligations of universe citizenship.","r":["118:7.4"]}]},{"h":"The Responsibility of Choice and Destiny","items":[{"x":"Energy systems have no choice, but man, by the choices of his free will, has everything to do with determining his own destiny.","r":["112:5.3"]},{"x":"The power of choice is both the greatest opportunity and the supreme responsibility, and the Adjuster, the Father, and the Supreme Being depend on its faithfulness.","r":["112:5.5"]},{"x":"On the lower levels the range of choice is narrow, but as one ascends the universe, choice becomes ever freer.","r":["118:7.8"]},{"x":"Choosing the will of God is not the surrender of will but its consecration, enlargement, and perfection.","r":["111:5.5"]},{"q":"the portal of eternity opens only in response to the freewill choice of the freewill sons of the God of free will.","r":"5:6.12"}]}],"see":["Personalidad","Voluntad de Dios","Supervivencia","Ajustador del Pensamiento","Pecado","Rebelión de Lucifer"]},{"n":93,"t":"Luz y vida","en":"Light and Life","sum":"Light and life is the final evolutionary attainment of the worlds of time and space, the age in which a planet at last becomes settled after the successive ministries of the divine Sons. In this age the planet flourishes under one language, religion, and philosophy, war and poverty disappear, and many mortals fuse with their Adjusters without passing through death and are translated to the morontia career. This settledness begins with the planet and widens through seven stages to the system, constellation, local universe, and superuniverse.","sections":[{"h":"The Final Goal of Evolutionary Worlds","items":[{"q":"LA EDAD de luz y vida es el logro evolucionario final de un mundo del tiempo y del espacio.","r":"55:0.1"},{"x":"An inhabited world passes through the ages of the Planetary Prince, Adam, the Magisterial Son, and the bestowal Son, and is prepared for this age by the ministry of the Trinity Teacher Sons.","r":["55:0.1","52:7.2"]},{"x":"This age begins when the Teacher Sons complete their final mission and continues on that world without end.","r":["55:0.2","55:0.3"]},{"x":"Light and life unfolds in seven stages: planet, system, constellation, local universe, minor sector, major sector, and superuniverse.","r":["55:0.4","55:0.11"]}]},{"h":"The Morontia Temple and the New Rule","items":[{"x":"The appearance of the morontia temple at the planetary capital is the certificate that the world has entered light and life.","r":["55:1.1"]},{"x":"At the center of the temple is the shrine of the bestowal Son, flanked by the seats of the Planetary Sovereign and the chief of finaliters.","r":["55:1.2"]},{"x":"The temple is said to \"come down from heaven,\" but in fact it is built on the spot by the morontia power supervisors from designs made at the system capital.","r":["55:1.3"]},{"x":"In this age the Planetary Prince is elevated to Planetary Sovereign, and finaliters who have reached Paradise return to take part in planetary affairs.","r":["55:7.1","55:4.1"]},{"x":"The visible actual rulers are the Material Son and Daughter, and this arrangement has given renown throughout the universe to the idea of king and queen.","r":["55:7.2"]}]},{"h":"Translation Without Death","items":[{"q":"La muerte física natural no es una inevitabilidad mortal.","r":"55:2.1"},{"x":"Most citizens living in the final era of light and life do not die but are translated directly from the life in the flesh to the morontia existence.","r":["55:2.1","55:2.2"]},{"x":"When fusion is near, the candidate withdraws from duties and, in the morontia temple with family and friends gathered, is translated in a \"flash of life.\"","r":["55:2.3","55:2.4"]},{"x":"Those who come from such worlds are far better prepared to continue the ascent than those from disordered worlds like Urantia.","r":["55:2.10"]}]},{"h":"Life on a Settled World","items":[{"x":"The world attains one language, one religion, and normally one race, yet it is not perfect, for it still has hospitals, accidents, and senility.","r":["55:3.1"]},{"x":"One first-stage world collected a tenth of its income and spent it on truth, beauty, goodness, and disaster relief.","r":["55:3.2","55:3.6"]},{"x":"Most public offices, education, and judicial work were shared by men and women, and the highest honor was the order of \"supreme service.\"","r":["55:3.8","55:3.9"]},{"q":"La guerra ya es cosa de la historia, y ya no existen ejércitos ni fuerzas de policía.","r":"55:5.4"},{"x":"As self-control replaces law, government gradually shrinks, and its extent is in inverse proportion to the morality and spirituality of the citizens.","r":["55:5.4"]},{"x":"Poverty and social inequality all but vanish, and economic life becomes ethical.","r":["55:5.2","55:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Still Mortal","items":[{"q":"Esta gran evolución no es el cielo, pero es un sublime presagio de los mundos divinos de la ascensión al Paraíso.","r":"55:6.2"},{"x":"Society grows more peaceful, and people become more altruistic and fraternal without losing independence or family love.","r":["55:6.1"]},{"x":"Even on such worlds there is still abundant potential evil to stimulate choice between truth and error, good and evil.","r":["55:3.10"]},{"x":"Communion with the Adjusters deepens from age to age, and the ministry of the Holy Spirit and the angels becomes ever more effective.","r":["55:6.4"]},{"q":"Aunque no existiese un futuro de progresión eterna para la criatura, aun entonces los soberbios logros evolucionarios de las razas mortales en dichos mundos establecidos de logro perfeccionado justificarían ampliamente la creación del hombre en los mundos del tiempo y del espacio.","r":"55:6.9"}]},{"h":"Urantia and Light and Life","items":[{"x":"Urantia's greatest handicaps are disease, degeneracy, war, multicolored races, and multilingualism.","r":["55:3.21"]},{"q":"Ningún mundo evolucionario puede esperar progresar más allá de la primera etapa de establecimiento de la luz hasta que no haya alcanzado el estado de un solo idioma, una sola religión y una sola filosofía.","r":"55:3.22"},{"x":"When Urantia reaches that age, Machiventa Melchizedek will assume the place of Planetary Sovereign.","r":["55:7.3"]},{"x":"Even on an isolated world personal attainment is not thwarted; Jesus of Nazareth personally achieved the status of light and life on Urantia.","r":["55:11.7"]}]}],"see":["Urantia","Fusión con el Ajustador","Cuerpo de la Finalidad","Hijos e Hijas Materiales","Evolución","Ser Supremo"]},{"n":67,"t":"Mal","en":"Evil","sum":"Evil is not created by God; it is the shadow cast when immature creatures in an imperfect finite world reject the light or choose wrongly. Evil is the unintended transgression of the Father's will and so differs from sin; when deliberately embraced, it becomes sin. Potential evil is necessary for free will and moral choice, but actual evil need not be experienced, and God brings ultimate good even out of the evil of time.","sections":[{"h":"The Nature of Evil","items":[{"x":"God is so positively good that there is no room for negative evil in him, and he does not create evil.","r":["130:1.5","54:0.2"]},{"q":"El mal es la oscuridad inevitable que pisa los talones del necio rechazo de la luz.","r":"130:1.5"},{"q":"«El mal es la transgresión inconsciente o sin intención de la ley divina, la voluntad del Padre.","r":"148:4.3"},{"x":"Evil is a partial realization of, or maladjustment to, universe reality and indicates a deficiency of wisdom.","r":["67:1.4","67:1.5"]},{"x":"Evil is the misapplication of plans and the maladjustment of techniques, producing universe disharmony and planetary confusion.","r":["75:4.3"]}]},{"h":"A Relative Shadow","items":[{"q":"El mal es un concepto de la relatividad. Surge de la observación de las imperfecciones que aparecen en la sombra proyectada por un universo finito de cosas y seres a medida que tal cosmos oscurece la luz viviente de la expresión universal de las realidades eternas del Único Infinito.","r":"130:4.13"},{"x":"Evil arises from observing the imperfections in the shadow cast when a finite universe obscures the living light of the Infinite.","r":["130:4.13"]},{"x":"Error is the inevitable shadow of incompleteness cast upon the ascending path toward Paradise perfection, not an actual universe quality.","r":["130:4.11"]},{"x":"For relative good to appear, contrast with comparative evil, an imperfection that is not sin, is always necessary.","r":["4:3.6"]},{"x":"Ascending the universe scale, goodness increases and evil decreases, but the possibility of experiencing evil remains until final spirit levels are attained.","r":["132:2.6"]}]},{"h":"Free Will and Potential Evil","items":[{"x":"For evolving man to be free he must be able to err; the only world without the possibility of error is one without free intelligence.","r":["3:5.15"]},{"x":"By giving the power to choose between truth and error, the Father created potential negation, but evil actually exists only when creatures choose it.","r":["130:1.6"]},{"q":"La posibilidad del mal es necesaria para la elección moral, pero la actualidad del mal no es necesaria.","r":"132:2.10"},{"x":"The finite mind's imperfect comprehension of the infinite is itself potential evil; when it is not corrected and error grows, it becomes actual evil.","r":["130:4.14"]},{"x":"Evil deliberately chosen becomes sin, and the persistent pursuit of sin and error becomes iniquity.","r":["54:0.2","130:1.6"]}]},{"h":"How Evil Appears","items":[{"q":"evil always results when purely personal evaluations are elevated to the levels of absolutes.","r":"100:1.1"},{"q":"El mal es una parcialidad de la creatividad que tiende hacia la desintegración y destrucción final.","r":"111:4.11"},{"x":"All inner conflict is evil because it inhibits the creative function; it is a kind of civil war within the personality.","r":["111:4.11"]},{"x":"Suffering is latent in evil, but much suffering has come from sin and iniquity, and the Father does not send suffering as punishment.","r":["148:5.3"]},{"x":"Man should not blame God for the results of his own choices but should overcome earthly suffering through intelligent effort.","r":["148:5.3"]}]},{"h":"The Wisdom That Permits Evil","items":[{"x":"For creatures to be truly free, the possibility of evil and sin is unavoidable, and the rulers do not deprive any being of freedom.","r":["54:3.1"]},{"x":"The Father allows good and evil to grow together, like wheat and tares, until the end of life.","r":["130:1.6"]},{"x":"The Melchizedeks teach that the good resulting from the Satania rebellion is more than a thousandfold the sum of all the evil.","r":["54:6.6"]},{"x":"As wisdom grows through ascension, one better understands how ultimate good arises out of time-limited evil.","r":["54:6.10"]},{"x":"Even man's experience of evil is part of God's unending self-realization in the children of time.","r":["2:2.7"]}]}],"see":["Pecado","Libre albedrío","Bondad","Rebelión de Lucifer","Adversidad y pruebas","Sabiduría"]},{"n":79,"t":"Maquiventa Melquisedek","en":"Machiventa Melchizedek","sum":"Machiventa Melchizedek was a Melchizedek who incarnated as an emergency Son at Salem in Palestine 1,973 years before the birth of Jesus, at a time when the truth of the one God was dying out after Adam's failure. For ninety-four years he taught the covenant that God's favor is received by faith alone in El Elyon, the Most High, and through Abraham he ensured that this truth would be carried on. He prepared the way for Michael's bestowal and is now called the vicegerent Planetary Prince of Urantia.","sections":[{"h":"Incarnation of an Emergency Son","items":[{"x":"For thousands of years after the failure of Adam's mission, revealed truth was in danger of extinction, and by about 3000 B.C. the concept of God had grown very dim.","r":["93:1.1"]},{"x":"Machiventa volunteered from among the twelve planetary receivers and made an emergency Son incarnation, one of only six in the history of Nebadon.","r":["93:1.3"]},{"q":"1.973 años antes del nacimiento de Jesús, Maquiventa se otorgó a las razas humanas de Urantia.","r":"93:2.1"},{"x":"He appeared in the tent of the herder Amdon, ate material food for the first time, and that night began to reveal the truth of God's reality.","r":["93:2.1","93:2.2","93:2.3"]},{"x":"He received a Thought Adjuster but never married and could leave no offspring; his body was of the type of the one hundred staff members.","r":["93:2.6","93:2.7"]}]},{"h":"The Salem Teachings","items":[{"x":"He founded a school at Salem modeled on the training system of the Sethite priests and was known as \"priest of El Elyon\" and \"the sage of Salem.\"","r":["93:2.4","93:3.1"]},{"q":"Creo en El Elyón, el Dios Altísimo, el único Padre Universal y Creador de todas las cosas.","r":"93:4.2"},{"x":"The Salem creed was to believe in the Most High, accept the covenant that he grants favor for faith rather than sacrifice, and keep the seven commandments.","r":["93:4.3","93:4.4","93:4.5"]},{"q":"No dudarás de que la fe es el único requisito para la salvación eterna.","r":"93:4.8"},{"x":"He permitted no sacrifices at Salem and offered the sacrament of bread and wine in place of blood offerings.","r":["93:4.14"]},{"x":"The three concentric circles symbolized the Paradise Trinity, but most understood them as the three kingdoms of men, angels, and God.","r":["93:3.3"]}]},{"h":"The Covenant with Abraham","items":[{"x":"The Melchizedek receivers had long observed Abraham's ancestors, and the family of Terah met their expectations.","r":["93:5.3","93:5.4"]},{"x":"Abraham, who harbored ambitions to become king, won the battle of Siddim despite Melchizedek's dissuasion and then paid him tithes.","r":["93:5.9","93:5.13"]},{"q":"God agrees to do everything; man only agrees to believe God's promises and follow his instructions.","r":"93:6.4"},{"x":"Melchizedek again brought the news that salvation comes by faith, but the Semitic tribes went back to the system of blood sacrifice.","r":["93:6.4"]},{"x":"The covenant was completed after Abraham publicly renounced his personal ambitions, and more than one hundred thousand people were enrolled in the Salem brotherhood.","r":["93:6.7","93:6.8"]}]},{"h":"The Purpose and Spread of the Mission","items":[{"q":"Vino para llevar a cabo dos tareas: Mantener viva en la tierra la verdad del Dios único y preparar el camino para el autootorgamiento en forma mortal subsiguiente de un Hijo Paradisiaco de ese Padre Universal.","r":"93:4.15"},{"x":"He taught that another Son of God would come, born of a woman.","r":["93:3.7"]},{"x":"Salem missionaries went beyond Egypt, Mesopotamia, and Asia Minor, reaching Europe and the British Isles.","r":["93:7.1","93:7.2"]},{"x":"Michael appeared on earth and confirmed everything that Melchizedek had taught about the Paradise Father.","r":["93:3.8"]},{"x":"Because Melchizedek's teachings had been lost, few recognized Michael when he came in the flesh.","r":["93:9.10"]}]},{"h":"Departure and Later Career","items":[{"x":"When people began to regard him superstitiously as a demigod, he left suddenly, soon after the destruction of Sodom and Gomorrah.","r":["93:8.1"]},{"x":"His disappearance left Abraham with a grief he never overcame for the rest of his life.","r":["93:9.1","93:9.2"]},{"x":"What the Old Testament describes as conversations between Abraham and God were actually conferences between Abraham and Melchizedek.","r":["93:9.7"]},{"x":"For nineteen centuries he worked with the prophets to preserve the truth of Salem, and he is now called the vicegerent Planetary Prince of Urantia.","r":["93:10.4","93:10.7"]},{"q":"This is the story of Machiventa Melchizedek, one of the most unique of all characters ever to become connected with the history of Urantia","r":"93:10.11"}]}],"see":["Los Melquisedek","Revelación","Fe","Urantia","Autootorgamiento de Jesús","Adán y Eva"]},{"n":81,"t":"Matrimonio y familia","en":"Marriage and Family","sum":"Marriage is human society's institutional response to the biologic fact of bisexuality, and the home is the crowning fruit of that long evolutionary struggle. The Urantia Book says that marriage is not a sacrament but an essentially human institution, yet it teaches that pair marriage and the good home are the roots of civilization's stability and of morality, and the place where the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man are first learned.","sections":[{"h":"The Origin and Social Meaning of Marriage","items":[{"x":"Marriage is not the mating instinct itself but the institutional reaction society developed to regulate that instinct.","r":["82:1.1","82:3.1"]},{"q":"El matrimonio ha otorgado a la humanidad el hogar, y el hogar es la gloria coronadora de toda la larga y ardua lucha evolucionaria.","r":"82:0.1"},{"x":"Marriage always has an outer domain regulated by mores and law and a private, personal domain between man and woman.","r":["82:3.2"]},{"x":"Marriage has always been bound up with property and religion: property stabilized marriage, and religion moralized it.","r":["82:4.1"]},{"x":"Material necessity founded marriage, sex appetite embellished it, religion sanctioned it, and love later came to justify it.","r":["84:0.1"]},{"x":"Intelligently adjusting the strong sex urge to social regulation is the supreme test of the reality of civilization, and it always demands self-control.","r":["82:1.10"]}]},{"h":"Monogamy and Pair Marriage","items":[{"x":"Monogamy is not natural to evolving man at first, but it has great cultural value and is unquestionably best for the children.","r":["83:6.1","83:6.2"]},{"q":"La monogamia ha sido siempre, es ahora y será perennemente el objetivo ideal de la evolución sexual humana.","r":"83:6.6"},{"x":"The ideal of pair marriage entails self-denial, so it often fails when the partners lack rugged self-control.","r":["83:6.6"]},{"x":"Monogamy fosters delicate sentiments, refinement of moral character, and spiritual growth, and is best for the happiness of parents and the welfare of children.","r":["83:6.7","83:6.8"]},{"x":"Society should not ignore the plight of those who fail to obtain mates but should always treat them with kindness and consideration.","r":["83:6.4","83:6.5"]}]},{"h":"A Human Institution, Not a Sacrament","items":[{"q":"Marriage which culminates in the home is indeed man's most exalted institution, but it is essentially human","r":"83:8.1"},{"x":"Comparing the union of husband and wife to the relation of the Adjuster and man, or to a divine union, is an unfortunate analogy that has caused great confusion.","r":["83:8.2","83:8.3"]},{"x":"The very fact that marriage can be dissolved shows that God is not a party to the union.","r":["83:8.4"]},{"x":"Yet there is an ideal of marriage on the high spheres, embodied supremely by the Material Sons and Daughters; ideal mortal marriage is humanly sacred.","r":["83:8.5"]},{"x":"The marriage ideals of youth should not be crushed, but they should be balanced by learning the realities of home life beforehand, with a degree of disillusionment.","r":["83:8.6","83:8.7"]}]},{"h":"The Home, Chief Civilizing Agency","items":[{"x":"Religious, social, and educational institutions are needed, but since children learn most essentials of life from home and neighborhood, the home is the chief civilizing agency.","r":["82:0.2","82:0.3"]},{"q":"El matrimonio es la madre de todas las instituciones humanas, puesto que conduce directamente al establecimiento y mantenimiento del hogar, que es la estructura básica de la sociedad.","r":"84:6.8"},{"q":"Si las familias son buenas, la sociedad será igualmente buena.","r":"84:7.1"},{"x":"Man and woman can never fully understand each other, but they complement each other effectively, and their differences continue into the morontia and spirit careers.","r":["84:6.3","84:6.6","84:6.7"]},{"x":"Marriage is now passing beyond the stage that regarded the wife as property into a new era that respects personality.","r":["84:7.3","84:5.10"]}]},{"h":"Parents, Children, and the Spiritual Meaning of the Home","items":[{"x":"Bearing children is not a parental right but the supreme responsibility of human existence; civilization places duties on parents and rights on children.","r":["84:7.25","84:7.26"]},{"x":"The home is the basic unit of brotherhood, where parents and children together learn the patience, altruism, tolerance, and forbearance that brotherhood requires.","r":["84:7.28"]},{"x":"Society would be greatly improved by returning to the practice of the family council, as among the Andites, where family affairs were discussed freely and fraternally.","r":["84:7.29"]},{"q":"La vida familiar es el progenitor de la verdadera moralidad, el antepasado de la conciencia de la lealtad al deber.","r":"84:7.30"},{"x":"Jesus said the gospel of the kingdom would be better received when understood in family terms, as the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man.","r":["142:7.4"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that the true family rests on seven facts: existence, safety and pleasure, education, discipline, companionship, love and mercy, and provision for the future.","r":["142:7.5","142:7.11"]},{"x":"After Joseph's death the young Jesus made the support of the family his first duty and acted as a father to his brothers and sisters.","r":["126:3.2","126:3.5"]}]},{"h":"Threats to the Home","items":[{"x":"The greatest threat to family life is the modern pleasure mania that pursues self-gratification.","r":["84:8.1"]},{"q":"El hambre del alma no puede ser satisfecha por los placeres físicos; el amor del hogar y de los hijos no se aumenta con la búsqueda tonta del placer.","r":"84:8.4"},{"x":"Wholesome play and recreation have value, but pleasure that brings the breakup of marriage and the home is self-destructive.","r":["84:8.5","84:8.6"]},{"x":"Attempts to shift parental responsibility to the state or the church would be suicidal to the welfare and progress of civilization.","r":["84:7.27"]}]}],"see":["Civilización","Moralidad","Hermandad de los hombres","Amor","Hijos e Hijas Materiales","Gobierno y sociedad"]},{"n":24,"t":"Los Melquisedek","en":"Melchizedeks","sum":"Los Hijos Melquisedek son la orden primogénita del universo local, traída a la existencia conjuntamente por el Hijo Creador, el Espíritu Materno y el Padre Melquisedek. Situados a medio camino entre la Divinidad más elevada y la vida de criatura más baja, pueden servir a las razas evolutivas sin encarnarse, y trabajan como maestros del universo, como modelo de autogobierno y como Hijos de emergencia, los primeros en actuar ante cualquier crisis. Los mortales ascendentes reciben su enseñanza durante todo el camino, desde los mundos de estancia hasta la Universidad de Melquisedek en Salvington.","sections":[{"h":"Los Hijos primogénitos del universo local","items":[{"x":"De una nueva unión creadora del Hijo Creador y el Espíritu Creativo surgió primero el Padre Melquisedek, y en cooperación con los dos creadores trajo a la existencia a toda esta orden.","r":["35:1.1","20:1.10"]},{"x":"Los Melquisedek de Nebadon fueron creados todos en el plazo de mil años del tiempo patrón; constituyen una orden que no se reproduce y cuenta con más de diez millones de miembros.","r":["35:1.3","35:2.9"]},{"q":"These Sons are naturally at the mid-point of the great personality descent","r":"35:2.1"},{"x":"Por eso se convierten en los intermediarios naturales entre la existencia divina superior y la vida material, los amigos, maestros y consejeros de todos los seres inteligentes.","r":["35:2.1"]},{"x":"El Padre Melquisedek, primer asociado ejecutivo de Gabriel, preside las comisiones de emergencia y actúa como jefe ejecutivo de Nebadon en ausencia de Gabriel.","r":["35:1.2"]}]},{"h":"Una orden de autogobierno y de confianza","items":[{"x":"Los Melquisedek son una orden autónoma que elige a sus propios jefes administrativos, el primer intento de autodeterminación por parte de los seres del universo local.","r":["35:1.3","35:2.2"]},{"q":"not once throughout all the superuniverse of Orvonton have these Melchizedek Sons ever betrayed their trust.","r":"35:2.2"},{"x":"Patrullan el universo por su cuenta e informan al Hijo Creador independientemente de los organismos regulares, y también actúan como tribunales consultivos de revisión que se desplazan de mundo en mundo.","r":["35:2.3","35:2.4"]},{"q":"Los Melquisedek son casi perfectos en sabiduría, pero no son infalibles en su juicio.","r":"35:2.8"},{"x":"En la rebelión de Lucifer todos los Melquisedek permanecieron leales a Micael, y en Panoptia toda la población, bajo su dirección, se mantuvo al lado de Micael.","r":["53:7.4","53:7.1"]}]},{"h":"Maestros del universo","items":[{"x":"La esfera Melquisedek, el mundo piloto del circuito de Salvington, y los mundos asociados a ella se llaman la Universidad de Melquisedek, y todo mortal ascendente pasa por su formación.","r":["35:3.1"]},{"q":"Para un ascendiente este mundo es, probablemente, el lugar más interesante de todo Nebadon.","r":"35:3.11"},{"x":"La educación progresiva de los mortales ascendentes en la carrera morontial se lleva a cabo bajo la supervisión general de los Melquisedek, en asociación con los Hijos Instructores Trinitarios.","r":["35:4.1"]},{"x":"Los Melquisedek dirigen el gran cuerpo docente de los mundos de estancia y ayudan a las almas a proseguir allí los logros que no alcanzaron en la vida en la carne.","r":["45:7.1"]},{"x":"En Jerusem dirigen más de treinta centros educativos, donde forman a los mortales ascendentes en escuelas de administración para que asuman el gobierno representativo.","r":["45:7.3","45:7.4"]},{"q":"El gobierno representativo es el ideal divino del autogobierno entre los seres no perfectos.","r":"45:7.3"}]},{"h":"Hijos de emergencia","items":[{"q":"Dondequiera y cuandoquiera se requiere ayuda especial, allí encontraréis a uno o más de los Hijos Melquisedek.","r":"35:4.2"},{"x":"Son los primeros en actuar ante cualquier emergencia, y a veces sirven como custodios temporales de planetas descarriados o como síndicos de gobiernos planetarios que han fracasado.","r":["35:4.4"]},{"x":"Siete veces en Nebadon un Melquisedek ha servido a un mundo evolutivo a semejanza de la carne mortal, y Melquisedek de Salem, en los días de Abraham, fue uno de ellos.","r":["35:4.4","35:4.5"]},{"x":"Cuando un Hijo Avonal emprende un autootorgamiento, doce Melquisedek lo acompañan como patrocinadores, y también ayudan a los Avonales en las misiones magisteriales.","r":["35:2.6"]},{"x":"Los Melquisedek cooperan con los Portadores de Vida en la revisión de los planes de vida de los nuevos mundos, y el jefe de los Melquisedek representa a menudo al Hijo Creador.","r":["36:2.12"]}]},{"h":"Urantia y los Melquisedek","items":[{"x":"Después de la rebelión del Príncipe Planetario, Urantia fue administrada durante mucho tiempo por un consejo de doce síndicos Melquisedek.","r":["67:6.5","67:6.6"]},{"x":"Los síndicos Melquisedek advirtieron a Adán y Eva de los peligros del príncipe rebelde, y unos siete años después de la llegada de Adán le entregaron la administración del mundo.","r":["51:3.4","74:5.1"]},{"x":"En su primer autootorgamiento Micael apareció como un Hijo Melquisedek desconocido y participó en el servicio de emergencia de esta orden.","r":["119:1.3","119:1.6"]},{"q":"By universal consent he has become chief of Melchizedeks","r":"119:1.5"},{"x":"Se cree que los Melquisedek están destinados a permanecer en su universo de origen y a desempeñar un papel cada vez más importante en el gobierno y la administración del universo local.","r":["55:10.11"]}]}],"see":["Maquiventa Melquisedek","Hijo Creador Micael","Espíritu Materno del Universo Local","Hijos Avonales","Mundos de estancia","Universo local de Nebadon"]},{"n":37,"t":"Mente","en":"Mind","sum":"Mind is the gift of intelligence that originates in the Third Source and Center, the Infinite Spirit, and is bestowed upon creatures through the Seven Master Spirits and the local universe Mother Spirit. Mind deals with meanings between energy and spirit; it dominates matter while responding to the leading of spirit. In man, mind is the arena in which he makes his own decisions and chooses God or forsakes him, so the way the mind is used determines eternal survival.","sections":[{"h":"The Source of Mind: The Third Source and Center","items":[{"x":"Creature mind has its origin only in the Third Source and Center, who is the bestower of mind.","r":["9:5.2"]},{"x":"The Conjoint Actor exerts a gravity pull upon all mind, and every true intellectual value and divine thought is drawn into the absolute mind circuit.","r":["9:6.1","9:6.2"]},{"x":"The mind of man is an individualized circuit, an impersonal part, of the cosmic mind bestowed on the local universe by the Creative Daughter of the Infinite Spirit.","r":["9:5.4"]},{"q":"El Creador Conjunto es el origen de la mente, pero la mente no es el Creador Conjunto.","r":"9:5.5"},{"x":"Mind is absolute on Paradise, subabsolute in Havona, and finite in Orvonton, yet all levels are overspread by the mind-gravity of the Conjoint Actor.","r":["42:10.7"]}]},{"h":"Levels of Mind and the Cosmic Mind","items":[{"x":"Preadjutant-spirit mind is mechanical, nonexperiencing mind, ministered by the Master Physical Controllers.","r":["42:10.3"]},{"x":"Adjutant-spirit mind is the teachable level ministered by the Mother Spirit through the seven adjutant mind-spirits, and here mind first becomes experiencing.","r":["42:10.4"]},{"x":"Morontia mind is the expanding consciousness of personalities in the ascending career, functioning differentially according to the 570 levels of morontia life.","r":["42:10.5"]},{"x":"The Seven Master Spirits are the sevenfold source of cosmic mind, each distributing mind to one superuniverse, and Nebadon is pervaded by its Orvonton-type modification.","r":["9:4.3","16:6.1"]},{"x":"The cosmic mind responds unerringly to three levels of reality, causation (science), duty (morality), and worship (religion), and this underlies reflective thinking.","r":["16:6.6","16:6.7","16:6.8"]},{"x":"Energy is thing, mind is meaning, and spirit is value; mind establishes relationships between energy and spirit in time and space.","r":["9:4.5"]}]},{"h":"Mind at Work Between Matter and Spirit","items":[{"q":"La mente trasmuta los valores del espíritu en significados del intelecto; la volición tiene el poder de fructificar los significados de la mente a los dominios material y espiritual.","r":"9:4.6"},{"q":"El espíritu es el arquitecto, la mente es el constructor, el cuerpo es el edificio material.","r":"42:12.12"},{"x":"Mind is ever creative; the liaison of the cosmic mind and the adjutant mind-spirits fashions a body suited to evolving man.","r":["42:12.9","42:12.11"]},{"x":"The universe is planned, made, and managed by mind, but lower minds cannot discern the creative spirit-mind hidden within the universe mechanism.","r":["42:11.2","42:11.8"]},{"q":"La mente domina universalmente a la materia, así como a su vez responde al supercontrol último del espíritu.","r":"42:12.15"}]},{"h":"The Human Mind: Animal Roots and Moral Insight","items":[{"x":"Human intellect is rooted in the material origin of the animal races, so not all phenomena of mind should be regarded as divine.","r":["9:5.5"]},{"q":"La mente es verdaderamente de origen divino, y tiene un destino divino, pero vuestras mentes mortales no han alcanzado aún la dignidad divina.","r":"9:5.6"},{"x":"Man defiles his mind with insincerity and unrighteousness, animal fear and needless anxiety, and so he should be humble before his immature intellect.","r":["9:5.7"]},{"x":"Only personality knows what it is doing before it does it, and man can exercise scientific, moral, and spiritual insight in advance of experiment.","r":["16:7.2","16:7.3"]},{"x":"To sharpen this inherent cosmic insight is the purpose of education, to ennoble it is the purpose of religion, and to unify it is the purpose of personality.","r":["16:6.11"]}]},{"h":"Mind as the Arena of Choice","items":[{"q":"La mente material es la arena en la cual viven las personalidades humanas, tienen autoconciencia, toman decisiones, eligen a Dios o lo abandonan, se eternizan o se destruyen a sí mismos.","r":"111:1.3"},{"x":"Mind is a temporary intellectual system lent for the material lifetime, and the way it is used accepts or rejects the potential of eternal existence.","r":["111:1.5"]},{"x":"Not what the mind comprehends but what it desires to comprehend, and what it seeks to be like, brings about survival and identification with spirit.","r":["111:1.5"]},{"x":"Mind is a cosmic instrument that, according to the will, can sound the discords of destruction or the exquisite melodies of identification with God.","r":["111:1.6"]},{"q":"La mente es tu buque, el Ajustador es tu piloto, la voluntad humana es el capitán.","r":"111:1.9"},{"x":"Even a personal mind has no survival qualities unless it is identified with spirit; when it lacks the capacity to worship and to crave survival, it is not immortal.","r":["36:5.17"]}]}],"see":["Mente cósmica","Espíritus ayudantes de la mente","Espíritu Infinito","Personalidad","Libre albedrío","Alma"]},{"n":19,"t":"Mente cósmica","en":"Cosmic Mind","sum":"La mente cósmica es la mente séptuplemente diversificada del tiempo y del espacio, que cada uno de los Siete Espíritus Rectores ministra a uno de los siete superuniversos. Es la manifestación, en los niveles finitos, de la mente absoluta del Espíritu Infinito; llega a los mortales del universo local por medio del Espíritu Materno y de los espíritus ayudantes de la mente, y dota a toda criatura volitiva de tres respuestas a la realidad: la causalidad, el deber y la adoración. Aquí se halla el fundamento de la ciencia, la filosofía y la religión, y de un carácter fuerte.","sections":[{"h":"Mente séptuplemente diversificada","items":[{"x":"La mente cósmica es la mente séptuplemente diversificada del tiempo y del espacio; cada uno de los Siete Espíritus Rectores ministra una fase de ella a un superuniverso.","r":["42:10.6"]},{"x":"Los Espíritus Rectores son la fuente séptuple de la mente cósmica y el potencial intelectual del gran universo, y la mente cósmica es una manifestación subabsoluta de la mente de la Tercera Fuente y Centro.","r":["16:6.1"]},{"x":"El otorgamiento de mente a los siete superuniversos procede de los Siete Espíritus Rectores, y Nebadon está impregnado por la modificación de Nebadon del tipo de mente cósmica de Orvonton.","r":["9:4.3"]},{"q":"La mente infinita ignora el tiempo, la mente última trasciende el tiempo, la mente cósmica está condicionada por el tiempo.","r":"9:4.4"},{"x":"La mente cósmica funciona de manera distinta en cada uno de los siete superuniversos, pero está coordinada en el Ser Supremo por una técnica de asociación desconocida.","r":["116:1.4"]},{"x":"En el Paraíso la mente es absoluta, en Havona absonita y en Orvonton finita.","r":["42:10.7"]}]},{"h":"A través del Espíritu Infinito y del universo local","items":[{"x":"La presencia mental de Dios se discierne mejor en la creación finita en el funcionamiento universal de la mente cósmica de los Espíritus Rectores del Paraíso.","r":["3:1.8"]},{"x":"Sin embargo, la mente del orden humano es un otorgamiento de las hijas del Actor Conjunto, las Ministras Divinas de los universos locales.","r":["3:1.8"]},{"x":"Los urantianos viven bajo la influencia del Espíritu Creativo de Nebadon más que bajo la influencia directa de un Espíritu Rector, pero los Espíritus Rectores dominan las reacciones básicas de toda mente de criatura.","r":["16:6.2","16:5.3"]},{"x":"La mente humana es un circuito individualizado y una parte impersonal de la mente cósmica otorgada por la Hija Creativa al universo local.","r":["9:5.4"]},{"x":"La mente cósmica se extiende desde el ministerio primitivo de los espíritus ayudantes hasta la mente de los más altos ejecutivos del universo, unificada bajo la supervisión de los Siete Espíritus Rectores.","r":["56:2.3"]}]},{"h":"Tres respuestas a la realidad","items":[{"x":"En toda asociación de la mente cósmica con la personalidad existe una «respuesta a la realidad» que impide que las criaturas volitivas se conviertan en víctimas indefensas de los supuestos a priori de la ciencia, la filosofía y la religión.","r":["16:6.4"]},{"x":"La mente cósmica responde infaliblemente en tres niveles de la realidad: la causalidad (discriminación matemática), el deber (discriminación judicial) y la adoración (discriminación espiritual).","r":["16:6.5","16:6.6","16:6.7"]},{"q":"Éste es el discernimiento más elevado de la mente cósmica, la forma reverencial y adoradora de la discriminación cósmica.","r":"16:6.8"},{"x":"Cuando estas tres intuiciones se unifican en la personalidad, producen un carácter fuerte, que combina la ciencia basada en los hechos, la filosofía moral y la auténtica experiencia religiosa.","r":["16:6.10"]},{"q":"Es propósito de la enseñanza desarrollar y agudizar estas dotaciones innatas de la mente humana; de la civilización, expresarlas; de la experiencia de vida, comprenderlas; de la religión, ennoblecerlas; y de la personalidad, unificarlas.","r":"16:6.11"},{"x":"Sin embargo, son demasiado pocos en Urantia los que se complacen en cultivar ese pensamiento cósmico valiente e independiente.","r":["16:6.9"]}]},{"h":"Mentes afines y personalidad moral","items":[{"q":"No sólo hay atracción entre los espíritus semejantes, sino que las mentes semejantes también son muy fraternales y se inclinan a la cooperación las unas con las otras.","r":"16:6.3"},{"x":"Así como las nebulosas se originan en las energías cósmicas del espacio, los yoes intelectuales se originan en la mente cósmica.","r":["111:1.2"]},{"x":"Solo una personalidad sabe lo que está haciendo antes de hacerlo, pues posee la percepción anterior a la experiencia.","r":["16:7.3"]},{"x":"La virtud es la rectitud en conformidad con el cosmos, y la virtud no se conoce nombrándola, sino viviéndola.","r":["16:7.6"]},{"x":"La moralidad no puede promoverse mediante la ley ni la fuerza; debe propagarse por el contagio del contacto con quienes tienen fragancia moral.","r":["16:7.9"]},{"q":"La virtud suprema, por lo tanto, es elegir de todo corazón hacer la voluntad del Padre en los cielos.","r":"16:7.10"}]},{"h":"La mente cósmica en la ascensión","items":[{"x":"La conquista del primer círculo cósmico pone fin a la influencia exclusiva de los espíritus ayudantes de la mente, y la mente se acerca cada vez más a la mente cósmica y a las dotes supraayudantes del Espíritu Creativo.","r":["110:6.21"]},{"x":"En la etapa morontial el mortal ascendente recibe la modificación de Nebadon de la mente cósmica otorgada por el Espíritu Rector de Orvonton.","r":["112:6.4"]},{"x":"Al dejar el universo local y alcanzar los niveles espirituales, el ascendente queda sintonizado con el ministerio directo de la mente cósmica de Orvonton.","r":["112:6.10"]},{"x":"Cada vez que una mente en evolución se sintoniza con los circuitos de la mente cósmica, la actualidad del Supremo se vuelve un paso más real en el universo.","r":["117:0.3"]},{"q":"¿Es acaso extraño que la mente cósmica esté autoconscientemente consciente de su propia fuente, la mente infinita del Espíritu Infinito, y, al mismo tiempo, esté consciente de la realidad física de los vastos universos, de la realidad espiritual del Hijo Eterno, y de la realidad de la personalidad del Padre Universal?","r":"16:9.15"}]}],"see":["Siete Espíritus Rectores","Espíritu Infinito","Mente","Espíritus ayudantes de la mente","Espíritu Materno del Universo Local","Ser Supremo"]},{"n":69,"t":"Miedo y preocupación","en":"Fear and Worry","sum":"Fear was a powerful emotion that bound primitive man into society and prepared the first soil of religion, but unreasoned fear and worry now become poisons that hinder the progress of the soul. Revealed religion and the Thought Adjuster seek to change the fear of God into love and trust, and Jesus taught that foresight and prudence are permitted but that worry and anxiety should be abandoned for trust in the Father. His peace is a peace that keeps the heart from being troubled or afraid.","sections":[{"h":"Fear in Evolution","items":[{"x":"Early man lived in constant fear of bad luck, and that fear had a paralyzing power.","r":["86:1.3","86:1.4"]},{"x":"If hunger and love drew men together, vanity and ghost fear held primitive society together.","r":["68:3.4","68:3.1"]},{"x":"It was not the sanctity of life but the fear aroused by the shock of death that fostered primitive religion.","r":["86:3.1","87:1.1"]},{"x":"The false fears of primitive religion prepared the soil of the mind, and the Adjusters have ever since been transforming fear into the love of God.","r":["86:7.6"]},{"x":"Evolutionary religion drives men by fear, but revealed religion leads them to seek a God of love through the longing to be like him.","r":["5:4.1","101:0.1"]}]},{"h":"A Poison to the Soul","items":[{"q":"El temor sin raciocinio es un poderoso fraude intelectual practicado sobre el alma mortal en evolución.","r":"48:7.4"},{"x":"Mental poisons such as fear, anger, envy, and suspicion, like physical poisons, greatly hinder the spiritual progress of the soul.","r":["110:1.5"]},{"x":"The emotion in man that angels find hardest to understand is the inheritance of animal fear that throws even faith into panic.","r":["113:2.5"]},{"q":"Fear is man's chief enslaver and pride his great weakness","r":"142:0.2"},{"q":"«El odio es la sombra del temor; la venganza, la máscara de la cobardía».","r":"145:3.4"},{"q":"El desaliento, la preocupación y la indolencia son prueba positiva de la inmadurez moral.","r":"160:1.6"}]},{"h":"The Worry-Free Life Jesus Taught","items":[{"x":"Jesus did not forbid prudent foresight for the future, but he opposed worry and anxiety.","r":["140:8.3"]},{"x":"Anxiety cannot add a cubit to one's stature or a day to one's life, so trust the Father who feeds even the ravens.","r":["165:5.2"]},{"x":"He counseled not to be overanxious about needs but to spread them before the Father with prayer and thanksgiving.","r":["146:2.16"]},{"x":"To Martha, troubled about many things, he said that the small things of life must give way to the greater things of the kingdom.","r":["162:8.3"]},{"x":"People spend much time crying in fear like lost children, though in fact they are not far from safety.","r":["132:6.1"]},{"x":"Returning from rest in the hills, the apostles realized that many pressing problems were the products of exaggerated fear and anxiety.","r":["143:3.6"]}]},{"h":"The Way to Overcome Fear","items":[{"x":"Jesus told a fear-ridden young man to make his mind not a slave of fear but a courageous ally in solving problems.","r":["130:6.3"]},{"x":"When the indwelling spirit is freed from the fetters of fear, the consciousness of being a child of God overcomes the fear of men.","r":["130:6.3","130:6.4"]},{"q":"Los Ajustadores del Pensamiento querrían reemplazar vuestros sentimientos de temor por convicciones de amor y confianza; pero no pueden hacer estas cosas mecánica y arbitrariamente; ésa es tarea vuestra.","r":"108:5.8"},{"x":"The anxiety arising from the fear of being alone in the universe should be dissolved by the contemplation of faith in the Father and the rest of worship.","r":["143:7.3"]},{"x":"Happy and effective people are motivated not by fear of wrongdoing but by love of right doing.","r":["140:4.6","140:5.6"]},{"x":"Mere belief may not overcome doubt and fear, but living faith always triumphs over doubting.","r":["102:6.7"]}]},{"h":"Peace Without Fear","items":[{"x":"Jesus knew no fear; he faced the realities of life without fear and was always cheerful and glad.","r":["100:7.4","100:7.12"]},{"x":"The peace of Jesus is not passive calm but a peace that keeps the heart from being troubled or afraid amid trials and persecutions.","r":["140:5.18"]},{"q":"Que no se atribule vuestro corazón, y no os dejéis dominar por el temor. Yo he superado el mundo, y en mí triunfaréis todos por la fe.","r":"181:1.5"},{"x":"On the morontia worlds ascenders learn to accept challenges without complaint and to face difficulties and uncertainties without fear.","r":["48:6.35"]},{"x":"Teachers are exhorted to proclaim the love of God that casts out all fear.","r":["48:6.8"]}]}],"see":["Fe","Alegría y felicidad","Adversidad y pruebas","Ajustador del Pensamiento","Amor","Religión institucional"]},{"n":88,"t":"Milagros","en":"Miracles","sum":"In the wilderness Jesus decided not to win people's attention and allegiance by miracles and wonders, and he kept that decision to the end. Yet because one with unlimited creator prerogatives was on earth, filled with divine mercy and human sympathy, extraordinary events such as healings sometimes followed apart from his will. The Urantia Book shows that many events that seemed miraculous were in fact natural occurrences, and it explains that even genuine miracles did not break natural law but involved the elimination of the time factor.","sections":[{"h":"The Decision Not to Work Miracles","items":[{"x":"During the forty days in the wilderness Jesus resolved not to use universe power to satisfy the Jewish craving for signs.","r":["136:8.1"]},{"q":"Se negó a ser simplemente un hacedor de milagros.","r":"136:8.2"},{"x":"Wonder-working only stirs the material mind to outward allegiance; it neither reveals God nor saves men.","r":["136:8.2"]},{"q":"Jesus chose to establish the kingdom of heaven in the hearts of mankind by natural, ordinary, difficult, and trying methods","r":"136:8.6"},{"x":"He did not break this decision even when the Pharisees demanded proof or when he was taunted at Calvary to come down from the cross.","r":["136:7.4"]}]},{"h":"The Wine at Cana","items":[{"x":"At the wedding feast at Cana others expected a miracle, but the most surprised of all was Jesus himself, who had resolved not to work one.","r":["137:4.12"]},{"q":"Pero éste no fue en ningún sentido un milagro. No se había modificado, abrogado, ni trascendido ninguna ley de la naturaleza.","r":"137:4.13"},{"x":"The agents of the Creator made wine by the ordinary natural processes, only independently of time.","r":["137:4.13"]},{"x":"It would not have happened had it been contrary to the Father's will, since Jesus had already committed all things to the Father's will.","r":["137:4.14"]}]},{"h":"Events That Were Not Miracles","items":[{"x":"The great catch of fish was no miracle; Jesus, a skilled fisherman who knew the habits of fish, simply told them where the school was.","r":["145:1.3"]},{"x":"The healing of Peter's mother-in-law's fever was not a miracle either, but a miracle-seeking generation counted all such coincidences as miracles.","r":["145:2.16","145:2.17"]},{"x":"Jesus encouraged the apostles not to attribute ordinary physical events to spiritual causes but to seek the true causes of all phenomena.","r":["164:3.6"]},{"x":"The rabbis regarded blindness from birth as the result of sin, but Jesus rejected such superstitious explanations.","r":["164:3.2","164:3.3"]}]},{"h":"The Sundown Healing and Genuine Miracles","items":[{"x":"At Capernaum, when Jesus said he wished his children to be made whole if it was not contrary to the Father's will, 683 persons were healed in a moment.","r":["145:3.9","145:3.10"]},{"x":"Jesus himself was the most surprised by this healing, having momentarily forgotten the warning that he could not limit the time element of creator prerogatives.","r":["145:3.11"]},{"q":"Los portentos curativos que de cuando en cuando se hicieron presentes durante la misión de Jesús sobre la tierra, no formaban parte de su plan de proclamación del reino.","r":"145:3.15"},{"x":"The cleansing of the leper was the first so-called miracle Jesus performed intentionally.","r":["146:4.5"]},{"q":"Éste fue el primero y único milagro de la naturaleza que realizó Jesús por premeditación consciente.","r":"152:2.10"},{"x":"When Jesus thanked the Father at the raising of Lazarus, the celestial hosts acted, and Lazarus came to life in twelve seconds of earth time.","r":["168:2.2","168:2.3"]}]},{"h":"What the Miracles Left Behind","items":[{"x":"Of the five thousand fed by the miracle, only about five hundred continued to follow Jesus.","r":["152:5.2"]},{"x":"Jesus said he would not turn from his mission of revealing the Father to satisfy the curiosity of wonder-seekers.","r":["145:5.6"]},{"x":"The fame of his healings brought prejudice-raising publicity and unsought notoriety, causing Jesus much trouble.","r":["145:3.12","145:3.15"]},{"x":"The resurrection of Lazarus strengthened the faith of believers, but the religious leaders hastened their decision to destroy Jesus.","r":["168:3.1","168:3.4"]}]},{"h":"The Greatest Miracle","items":[{"x":"To local universe citizens there are few miracles, and the most intriguing of them are the incarnational bestowals of the Paradise Sons.","r":["120:4.5"]},{"q":"Jesús de Nazaret fue una persona milagrosa.","r":"120:4.5"},{"x":"Even in all these extraordinary experiences the Father chose to reveal himself in normal, natural, and dependable ways.","r":["120:4.6"]}]}],"see":["Autootorgamiento de Jesús","Carácter de Jesús","Fe","Misericordia","Enseñanzas de Jesús","Ajustador del Pensamiento"]},{"n":61,"t":"Misericordia","en":"Mercy","sum":"Mercy is justice tempered by wisdom that fully knows the weaknesses and handicaps of creatures. God is merciful by nature and needs no one to persuade him; the Eternal Son is mercy itself, and the Infinite Spirit ministers that mercy throughout the universe. Mercy does not violate justice but applies it with understanding, and man learns true mercy by passing through justice, fairness, patience, and kindness.","sections":[{"h":"Justice Tempered by Wisdom","items":[{"q":"La misericordia es simplemente justicia atemperada por esa sabiduría que proviene de la perfección del conocimiento y del pleno reconocimiento de la debilidad natural y las limitaciones ambientales de las criaturas finitas.","r":"2:4.1"},{"x":"Even divine justice, which lets wrongdoing reap its results, is always tempered by mercy, in proportions determined by infinite wisdom.","r":["2:3.2"]},{"x":"Mercy is not a contravention of justice but an understanding interpretation of supreme justice as fittingly applied to evolving finite creatures.","r":["2:4.5"]},{"x":"When eternal justice and divine mercy work together, what man calls fairness emerges in human experience.","r":["2:4.4","10:6.3"]},{"x":"God is not torn between justice and mercy; in his omniscience he fully satisfies both demands at once.","r":["2:4.3","2:6.6"]}]},{"h":"Mercy Flowing from the Father's Nature","items":[{"q":"La necesidad de la criatura es en sí suficiente para asegurar el pleno caudal de su tierna misericordia y de su gracia salvadora.","r":"2:4.2"},{"x":"Mercy is the natural offspring of goodness and love; a loving father cannot withhold mercy from his children.","r":["2:4.4"]},{"x":"It is an error to think that the Eternal Son pleads with the Father for mercy; all the Son's mercy is a direct revelation of the Father's love.","r":["6:3.4"]},{"x":"God harbors no feelings of wrath or vengeance; such attitudes are inconsistent with the Father's merciful character.","r":["4:3.2","2:6.7"]},{"x":"Even a rebel who turns to righteousness is received in mercy, and God remembers his transgressions no more.","r":["2:5.4"]}]},{"h":"The Son Is Mercy, the Spirit Ministers","items":[{"q":"Dios es amor, el Hijo es misericordia. La misericordia es amor aplicado, es el amor del Padre en acción en la persona de su Hijo Eterno.","r":"6:3.5"},{"x":"The Infinite Spirit inclines toward the Son's attribute of mercy and becomes the mercy minister of the Paradise Deities throughout the grand universe.","r":["8:2.6","8:4.7"]},{"q":"El universo de vuestro origen está siendo forjado entre el yunque de la justicia y el martillo del sufrimiento; pero los que esgrimen el martillo son los hijos de la misericordia, la progenie espiritual del Espíritu Infinito.","r":"9:1.8"},{"x":"Justice is the collective attitude of the Trinity, and mercy is the personal expression of that righteousness.","r":["10:6.2","10:6.18"]},{"x":"Creator Sons are inherently merciful, yet through their bestowal experiences they acquire understanding mercy in a new way.","r":["119:0.4"]},{"x":"Our superuniverse of Orvonton is a demonstration of love and mercy, noted for justice tempered by mercy and power conditioned by patience.","r":["15:14.2"]}]},{"h":"The Record and Limits of Mercy","items":[{"x":"The Memory of Mercy is a living record of the mercy ministry extended to an individual, read as testimony at the adjudication of survival.","r":["28:6.5","28:6.6"]},{"q":"Puesto que la misericordia no ha de ser volcada sobre aquellos que la desprecian, la misericordia no es un don que pueda ser pisoteado por los rebeldes persistentes del tiempo.","r":"28:6.7"},{"x":"Yet for one sincere of purpose and honest of heart, the credit of mercy is always far greater than he could ever exhaust.","r":["28:6.7"]},{"x":"When endless mercy and patience are exhausted, justice prevails, and what mercy cannot rehabilitate justice will eventually annihilate.","r":["21:5.7","2:3.5"]}]},{"h":"Mercy as Man Learns It","items":[{"x":"Mercy is a quality of growth: one can be truly merciful only after first becoming just, fair, patient, and kind.","r":["28:6.8"]},{"q":"Podrá haber patronaje, condescendencia, o caridad —aún lástima— pero no misericordia.","r":"28:6.8"},{"q":"El ministerio de la misericordia es siempre la obra del individuo, pero el castigo de la justicia es la función de los grupos sociales, gubernamentales, o administrativos del universo.","r":"133:1.2"},{"x":"The mercy Jesus spoke of is not passive pity but active and dynamic, the supreme fatherly loving-kindness.","r":["140:5.17"]},{"x":"Disciples are saviors, not judges of men, so they must first show their brothers the mercy they themselves would desire.","r":["140:3.17","140:3.16"]},{"x":"The rule of the kingdom is that mercy determines judgment and love determines conduct, not the reckoning of giving and receiving.","r":["140:6.9"]}]}],"see":["Justicia","Amor","Perdón","Hijo Eterno","Espíritu Infinito","Bondad"]},{"n":65,"t":"Moralidad","en":"Morality","sum":"Morality is the capacity unique to human personality to discern right from wrong and to judge the worth not only of means but of ends, and it distinguishes man from the animal. It evolved from self-conscious reason and grows not by law or force but by personal choice and influence. Morality is a prerequisite of religion but not the whole of religious experience, and the highest moral choice is the choice to do the will of God.","sections":[{"h":"The Moral Nature of Personality","items":[{"q":"La inteligencia por sí sola no puede explicar la naturaleza moral. La moralidad, la virtud, son indígenas a la personalidad humana.","r":"16:7.1"},{"x":"Man can exercise moral insight before exploration or experiment, and only personality knows what it is doing before it does it.","r":["16:7.2","16:7.3"]},{"x":"Intellect only selects means, but a moral being discerns the value of the ends themselves.","r":["16:7.4"]},{"x":"One who cannot discern the goal of his strivings lives on the animal level and has failed to use the advantages of personality.","r":["16:7.5"]},{"x":"A child's first moral choice appears with the seventh adjutant mind-spirit, and only after it is registered is an Adjuster assigned.","r":["108:2.1"]}]},{"h":"Virtue and Moral Choice","items":[{"q":"La virtud es rectitud —conformidad con el cosmos. Nombrar las virtudes no quiere decir definirlas, pero vivirlas es conocerlas.","r":"16:7.6"},{"x":"Choosing between good and evil is influenced not only by moral keenness but also by ignorance, immaturity, and delusion, so a sense of proportion and the art of measurement are needed.","r":["16:7.7","16:7.8"]},{"x":"Moral conduct is the highest performance of intellect: choosing higher ends and choosing moral means suited to those ends.","r":["16:7.10"]},{"q":"La elección moral más elevada es la elección del valor más alto posible, y siempre —en cualquier esfera, en todas ellas— eso consiste en elegir hacer la voluntad de Dios.","r":"39:4.14"}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Morality","items":[{"x":"Morality arose from self-conscious reason; it transcends the animal but is wholly evolutionary.","r":["5:5.1"]},{"x":"Through the long and wasteful struggle to placate ghosts, man became conscious of relative right and wrong, and thus ethics was born.","r":["86:6.7","68:4.3"]},{"x":"Early feelings of duty grew out of emotional fear, but the urge to unselfish service comes from the indwelling divine spirit.","r":["103:5.1"]},{"q":"La conciencia no es una voz divina que habla al alma humana.","r":"92:2.6"},{"x":"Static ethics and traditional morality are only slightly above the animal level; ethics becomes truly human when it is dynamic and progressive.","r":["12:5.10"]}]},{"h":"Morality and Religion","items":[{"q":"La conducta moral es siempre un antecedente de la religión evolucionada y aun forma parte de la religión revelada, pero no es nunca la totalidad de la experiencia religiosa.","r":"5:5.4"},{"x":"The morality of evolutionary religion drives men by fear, but revealed religion draws them by a loving desire to be like God.","r":["5:4.1"]},{"x":"As religion evolves, ethics becomes the philosophy of morals, and morality becomes the discipline of self by the standards of supreme spiritual ideals.","r":["92:7.5"]},{"x":"A religion that stresses an isolated morality apart from truth and beauty fails to win the loyalty of modern people.","r":["2:7.9"]},{"x":"Jesus did not put ethics in the place of religion; he taught religion as the cause and ethics as the result.","r":["170:3.8"]}]},{"h":"How Morality Grows and Spreads","items":[{"q":"La moralidad nunca se puede promover ni por ley ni fuerza.","r":"16:7.9"},{"x":"Morality is a matter of the personality's free will and must spread by the contagion of contact with morally fragrant persons.","r":["16:7.9"]},{"x":"Jesus interpreted the golden rule on the levels of the flesh, feelings, mind, brotherly love, morality, and spirit, teaching at the highest to treat people as God would treat them.","r":["147:4.3","147:4.8","147:4.9"]},{"x":"Primitive man's neighbor was only those near him, but Jesus extended the neighbor to all mankind and even to enemies, and the human heart knows this is right.","r":["103:5.2"]},{"x":"In the ages of philosophy and brotherhood people become truly moral beings and learn to live by the golden rule.","r":["50:5.8"]}]}],"see":["Bondad","Libre albedrío","Voluntad de Dios","Experiencia religiosa","Sabiduría","Pecado"]},{"n":45,"t":"Morontia","en":"Morontia","sum":"Morontia is the vast intermediate level lying between the material and the spiritual. Since God does not change a mortal of animal origin into a perfect spirit in a single step, the surviving human passes through the many morontia worlds of the local universe and, by hundreds of gradual transformations, reaches the threshold of spirit. The morontia life actually begins on earth when the soul is conceived, and its philosophic insight is called mota.","sections":[{"h":"A Level Between Matter and Spirit","items":[{"q":"El telar de morontia es espiritual, su tejido es físico.","r":"0:5.12"},{"x":"Morontia is a broad level of reality that may be personal or impersonal, and may consist of living or nonliving energies.","r":["0:5.12"]},{"x":"The morontia worlds are architectural spheres furnished with one hundred physical elements plus one hundred organizations of energy known as morontia materials.","r":["48:1.3"]},{"x":"Like the \"better and more enduring substance\" of which Paul spoke, morontia material is real and literal.","r":["48:1.7"]},{"x":"Morontia mind is a dual mind in which material and spiritual minds co-operate, governed by a single will.","r":["110:2.6"]}]},{"h":"Why a Morontia Stage Is Needed","items":[{"x":"The Gods do not transform creatures of animal origin into perfect spirits at once by some mysterious magic.","r":["48:0.1"]},{"x":"The belief that the single step of death instantly transforms the mortal mind into a perfected spirit is ignorant superstition.","r":["48:0.2"]},{"x":"A morontia transition always intervenes between mortal state and spirit status, and its purpose is similar in all local creations.","r":["48:0.3"]},{"x":"The morontia career is the transition life between evolutionary material existence and the higher spirit attainment.","r":["47:10.7"]},{"q":"Estas creencias no son sino supersticiones ignorantes y fábulas placenteras.","r":"48:0.2"}]},{"h":"Morontia Bodies and Gradual Transformation","items":[{"x":"The morontia power supervisors provide 570 successive morontia bodies during the morontia career in Nebadon.","r":["48:1.5"]},{"x":"In mortal life the spirit indwells almost as something separate, but in the morontia life the spirit becomes an actual part of the personality.","r":["48:1.6"]},{"x":"Early morontia life resembles the material worlds, but on the constellation and Salvington it reaches increasingly spiritual levels.","r":["48:1.4"]},{"x":"The body that the risen Jesus bore was also a morontia body: no blood circulated in it and it did not take material food, yet it was real.","r":["190:0.3"]}]},{"h":"Those Who Help the Morontia Life","items":[{"x":"Morontia companions are offspring of the local universe Mother Spirit, friendly associates, guides, and interpreters for the ascenders.","r":["48:3.1","48:3.5","48:3.12"]},{"x":"The mansion world teachers are cherubim and sanobim left behind by their seraphim, and they conduct the schools of thinking, feeling, and doing.","r":["48:5.1","48:5.6"]},{"q":"No existen caminos reales, atajos ni senderos fáciles al Paraíso.","r":"48:5.7"},{"x":"The morontia career seeks to eradicate forever such animal vestiges as procrastination, insincerity, and the avoidance of problems.","r":["48:5.8"]},{"x":"Transition seraphim help with the choice of a course, yet they respect the ascender's freewill choices as long as no harm results.","r":["48:6.5","48:6.6"]},{"q":"No act of good is ever wholly lost","r":"48:6.7"}]},{"h":"Mota and the Morontia Progressors","items":[{"x":"Mota is an insight superior to philosophy; as two eyes are to one, it gives stereoscopic depth to meanings and values.","r":["48:6.28"]},{"x":"On the first mansion world mota concepts are taught side by side with the corresponding statements of human philosophy.","r":["48:7.1"]},{"q":"El alma en evolución no se vuelve divina por lo que haga, sino por lo que trata de hacer.","r":"48:7.24"},{"x":"The morontia life actually begins on earth at the moment the Adjuster comes to indwell and the soul is conceived.","r":["48:6.2"]},{"x":"After graduating from the mansion worlds and until attaining spirit status, the ascender is called a morontia progressor.","r":["48:8.1"]},{"x":"The purpose of this long training is not merely eternal ease but preparation for the transcendent service of future ages.","r":["48:8.3"]},{"q":"Mota is more than a superior philosophy","r":"48:6.28"}]}],"see":["Mundos de estancia","Alma","Ascensión mortal","Muerte","Resurrección de Jesús","Filosofía"]},{"n":43,"t":"Muerte","en":"Death","sum":"In The Urantia Book death is not an end but a doorway from the material life to the morontia life. For primitive man death was the supreme shock and the greatest fear, and it gave rise to the development of religion; revelation, however, shows that there are three kinds of death, spiritual, intellectual, and physical, and that the surviving soul sleeps and then awakens again on the mansion worlds. On advanced worlds even natural death becomes increasingly rare.","sections":[{"h":"Primitive Man and the Fear of Death","items":[{"q":"La muerte era para el hombre evolutivo el supremo arcano, la combinación más aterradora de azar y misterio.","r":"86:3.1"},{"x":"Not the sanctity of life but the fear inspired by the shock of death fostered early religion.","r":["86:3.1"]},{"x":"Fearing the ghosts released by death, primitive peoples destroyed the dead person's house and took a different road home from the funeral.","r":["87:1.1","87:1.3","87:1.5"]},{"x":"The concept of a future life, derived from dreams, began to soften the fear of death bound up with the instinct of self-preservation.","r":["86:4.2"]},{"x":"The basic belief of primitive religion was survival after death.","r":["92:6.1"]}]},{"h":"The Three Kinds of Death","items":[{"x":"In relation to personality survival there are three kinds of death: spiritual (soul) death, intellectual (mind) death, and physical (body and mind) death.","r":["112:3.1"]},{"x":"One who has finally rejected survival is, from the universe point of view, already dead, even while the body lives.","r":["112:3.2"]},{"x":"When the mind circuits that make volitional action possible are irretrievably destroyed, the Adjuster departs, and this too is death.","r":["112:3.3"]},{"x":"In physical death the Adjuster remains until the mind ceases to function, then departs for Divinington when the life pulsations of the brain stop.","r":["112:3.4"]}]},{"h":"What Happens After Death","items":[{"x":"The body returns to the elements, but two nonmaterial factors continue: the Adjuster and the morontia soul.","r":["112:3.5"]},{"q":"Upon death the Thought Adjuster temporarily loses personality, but not identity; the human subject temporarily loses identity, but not personality;","r":"112:3.7"},{"x":"From death until repersonalization the surviving soul is wholly unconscious, in the keeping of the guardian of destiny.","r":["112:5.13"]},{"x":"Those who go to the mansion worlds cannot send messages back to their loved ones on earth; such communication is forbidden.","r":["112:3.7"]},{"x":"In the resurrection halls the morontia form, the returning Adjuster, and the conserved soul are united, and identity is reassembled.","r":["112:5.16","112:5.18","112:5.19"]},{"q":"on the mansion worlds both reunite in eternal manifestation.","r":"112:3.7"}]},{"h":"The Eye of Faith on Death","items":[{"x":"The spirit of adventure and the dread of monotony were placed in man to suggest that death is only the beginning of an endless career of adventure.","r":["14:5.10"]},{"x":"Life after death is not essentially different from mortal existence, and every good thing done now enhances the future life.","r":["103:5.7"]},{"x":"True religion does not foster spiritual sloth through the vain hope of gaining noble virtues merely by passing through the portals of death.","r":["103:5.7"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that believers should live as if pursuing their careers with natural death always in prospect.","r":["176:3.3"]},{"q":"and which even now makes certain their resurrection from the bonds of natural death.","r":"190:0.2"},{"q":"La muerte nada agregó a la posesión intelectual ni a la dote espiritual, pero agregó al estado experiencial la conciencia de la supervivencia.","r":"48:7.25"}]},{"h":"Worlds Where Death Fades Away","items":[{"q":"La muerte física natural no es una inevitabilidad mortal.","r":"55:2.1"},{"x":"On worlds settled in light and life, many fuse with their Adjusters and are translated alive into the morontia state.","r":["55:2.1","55:2.2"]},{"x":"On such worlds a \"funeral\" becomes an occasion not of weeping but of joy, deep satisfaction, and inexpressible hope.","r":["55:2.5"]},{"x":"Less advanced mortals would be helped if they too learned to view natural death with such cheerfulness and lightness of heart.","r":["55:2.6"]},{"x":"Yet even on long-settled worlds there is no system in which natural death as a way of leaving the flesh has wholly disappeared.","r":["55:2.8"]}]}],"see":["Supervivencia","Mundos de estancia","Morontia","Alma","Miedo y preocupación","Luz y vida"]},{"n":90,"t":"Muerte en la cruz","en":"Death on the Cross","sum":"Jesus died on the cross at Golgotha on a Friday in A.D. 30. The Urantia Book makes clear that this death was not an atoning sacrifice to appease the wrath of God or pay mankind's debt; it was not required by the Father but planned and carried out by man. The true meaning of the cross lies not in the fact of his death but in the manner and spirit in which he met it, the supreme expression of a love that forgave even enemies, and so the cross became the eternal symbol of unselfish service.","sections":[{"h":"From the Arrest to Golgotha","items":[{"x":"When he was arrested, Jesus knew his work in the flesh was finished and took little interest in the details of the so-called trials.","r":["186:2.1"]},{"x":"He did not answer false testimony, but he always answered the question whether he was the Son of God.","r":["186:2.2"]},{"x":"Convinced that it was the Father's will for him to follow the natural course of events like an ordinary man, he did not try to change the outcome by his eloquence.","r":["186:2.3"]},{"x":"He was crucified at about half past nine on Friday morning, and the unseen hosts of the universe watched in silence as the Creator underwent a creature's death.","r":["187:3.1"]}]},{"h":"Hours on the Cross","items":[{"q":"Las únicas palabras de Jesús, al clavarlo ellos al travensaño, fueron «Padre, perdónalos porque no saben qué están haciendo».","r":"187:2.4"},{"x":"Though thirsty, Jesus refused the drugged wine offered to deaden his suffering.","r":["187:2.3"]},{"x":"Unlike the brigand who mocked him, the other brigand turned wholeheartedly in his last hours and found salvation.","r":["187:4.1","187:4.2"]},{"x":"As a sandstorm darkened the sky, Jesus cried, \"It is finished,\" commended his spirit to the Father, and breathed his last.","r":["187:5.1","187:5.5"]},{"x":"A Roman centurion who saw him die confessed that he truly was a Son of God.","r":["187:5.5"]},{"q":"Jesús murió majestuosamente —tal como había vivido.","r":"187:5.6"}]},{"h":"Not an Atoning Sacrifice","items":[{"x":"Jesus did not die to atone for the racial guilt of mankind or to provide a way of approach to an offended God.","r":["188:4.1"]},{"x":"His death was neither a ransom to buy man back from fallen rulers nor a sacrifice to pay mankind's debt to God.","r":["188:4.3"]},{"x":"The whole idea of ransom and atonement is incompatible with the concept of God as a loving Father, which Jesus taught and showed.","r":["188:4.8"]},{"x":"Sin is not passed from parents to children; it is conscious rebellion committed by individual will creatures.","r":["188:4.5"]},{"x":"Even a sovereign of justice would not be satisfied with the childish scheme of substituting an innocent person for the guilty.","r":["188:4.11"]}]},{"h":"Who Killed Him","items":[{"q":"Fue el hombre y no Dios quien planeó y ejecutó la muerte de Jesús en la cruz.","r":"186:5.2"},{"x":"There is no direct connection between his death and the Jewish Passover sacrificial system.","r":["186:5.1"]},{"x":"The experience required by the bestowal was already complete at his baptism; the manner of his later life and death was his personal ministry for his creatures.","r":["186:5.3"]},{"x":"The gospel of realizing sonship with God by faith does not depend on his death and was illuminated even more by his life than by his death.","r":["186:5.4"]},{"x":"The Father loved mankind just as much before Jesus lived and died as after.","r":["186:5.6"]}]},{"h":"The True Meaning of the Cross","items":[{"q":"Lo extraordinario de la muerte de Jesús, tal como se relaciona con el enriquecimiento de la experiencia humana y la expansión del camino de la salvación, no es el hecho de su muerte sino más bien la manera superior y el espíritu incomparable con que se enfrentó a su muerte.","r":"188:4.12"},{"q":"Coloca para siempre todas las relaciones entre Dios y el hombre sobre la base de familia.","r":"188:5.1"},{"x":"Divine love does not merely forgive wrongs; it absorbs and actually destroys them, so the forgiveness of love transcends the forgiveness of mercy.","r":["188:5.2"]},{"x":"Jesus bore the cross of mortal existence for more than twenty-five years, and Golgotha was the final expression of that love.","r":["188:5.4"]},{"q":"Aunque no sea adecuado hablar de Jesús como de uno que se sacrifica, un rescatador, o un redentor, es totalmente correcto referirse a él como un salvador.","r":"188:4.7"},{"x":"He lived and died not for this world alone but for the whole universe, and his death illuminated the certainty of survival after the death of the flesh.","r":["188:4.6"]}]},{"h":"The Symbol of Service","items":[{"x":"His love that laid down his life for his enemies was greater than any love then known on earth.","r":["188:5.7"]},{"x":"The cross is not a symbol of substitution appeasing wrath but of unselfish service, in which the good bestow themselves on the evil to save them by love.","r":["188:5.9"]},{"x":"Creatures on many worlds, looking upon Jesus on the cross, have not given up the struggle of faith but have pressed on once more.","r":["188:5.5"]},{"x":"On the cross there was nothing the Father required, only what Jesus willingly gave and refused to avoid.","r":["188:5.11"]},{"x":"His death was not meant to reconcile man to God but to awaken man to the Father's eternal love and the Son's mercy.","r":["188:5.13"]}]}],"see":["Autootorgamiento de Jesús","Resurrección de Jesús","Amor","Perdón","Muerte","Servicio"]},{"n":44,"t":"Mundos de estancia","en":"Mansion Worlds","sum":"The mansion worlds are the seven transition worlds surrounding Jerusem, the capital of the local system, and they correspond to the \"many mansions in my Father's house\" of which Jesus spoke. After death the surviving mortal awakens in the resurrection halls of the first mansion world, makes up the deficiencies left unfinished on earth, and, passing through the seven worlds in turn, becomes less and less mortal and more and more morontial. This is the first school of the ascension, linking the material life with the spirit life.","sections":[{"h":"What the Seven Mansion Worlds Are","items":[{"x":"The \"many mansions\" of which Jesus spoke refer especially to the seven satellites of the first transition world surrounding Jerusem.","r":["47:0.1"]},{"x":"The mansion worlds are in the charge of the morontia supervisors and the Melchizedeks, and each world has an acting governor and headquarters for many groups of ministers.","r":["47:0.4"]},{"x":"When a system is settled in light and life, the mansion worlds one by one cease to serve as training spheres and are taken over by the finaliters.","r":["47:0.3"]},{"x":"The seven worlds are in fact demortalizing spheres: on the first one is still largely human, but by graduation one has become nearly morontial.","r":["47:9.5"]}]},{"h":"Awakening on the First Mansion World","items":[{"x":"At the center of the first mansion world stand the resurrection halls, the temple of personality assembly, where guardian seraphim, Adjusters, and archangels work together.","r":["47:3.2"]},{"x":"The sleeping survivor is resurrected when the morontia soul kept by the seraphim and the spirit-mind held by the Adjuster are reunited.","r":["47:3.3"]},{"q":"You begin over there right where you leave off down here.","r":"47:3.7"},{"x":"The resurrected one is granted ten days of liberty to explore the new home and look up loved ones who have gone before.","r":["47:3.6"]},{"x":"Morontia companions are assigned to the ascenders as their friendly associates and guides.","r":["47:3.11","47:3.12"]},{"q":"En los mundos de estancia los sobrevivientes mortales resurgidos reanudan su vida exactamente desde donde la interrumpieron cuando los sobrecogió la muerte.","r":"47:3.1"}]},{"h":"Worlds That Correct Deficiencies","items":[{"x":"The experience of the first mansion world is almost wholly devoted to correcting the defects of character and deficiencies of experience left from the life in the flesh.","r":["47:3.8"]},{"x":"No ascender can escape the experience of rearing children, and fathers must pass through it as surely as mothers.","r":["47:1.6"]},{"q":"Los niños necesitan a sus padres tanto como a sus madres, y los padres necesitan de esta experiencia paternal tanto como las madres.","r":"47:1.6"},{"x":"The second mansion world is devoted to removing intellectual conflicts and healing every kind of mental disharmony.","r":["47:4.8"]},{"x":"Whereas the first two worlds give negative training to make up deficiencies, truly progressive morontia culture begins on the third world.","r":["47:5.3"]}]},{"h":"From World to World","items":[{"x":"With each move to a new world one goes to sleep and awakens in a new morontia body, but at these times the Adjuster does not leave.","r":["47:4.4"]},{"x":"Memories of survival value are kept throughout the ascending career because the Adjuster has made counterparts of them.","r":["47:4.5"]},{"x":"In the morontia body one still eats, drinks, and rests, but the food is completely utilized and leaves no residue.","r":["47:4.6"]},{"x":"On the fourth world ascenders first learn true social life, based not on selfish conquest but on mutual appreciation and unselfish service.","r":["47:6.3"]},{"q":"A real birth of cosmic consciousness takes place on mansonia number five.","r":"47:7.5"},{"x":"Fusion with the Adjuster is often actually effected on the fifth or sixth world, followed by the declaration, \"This is a beloved son in whom I am well pleased.\"","r":["47:8.3","47:8.4"]},{"q":"Se adquiere un cuerpo morontial recién desarrollado y adaptablemente ajustado cuando avanzas de un mundo de estancia a otro.","r":"47:4.4"}]},{"h":"Citizens of Jerusem","items":[{"x":"On the seventh mansion world the remnants of unfortunate heredity and unwholesome environment are cleansed away, and differences of world origin disappear.","r":["47:9.1"]},{"x":"On the seventh world ascenders visit the Father's world and begin a more spiritual worship of the invisible Father.","r":["47:9.2"]},{"x":"The graduates are sent off in classes from the sea of glass and welcomed as citizens of Jerusem.","r":["47:9.4","47:10.1"]},{"x":"Those who pass through all the mansion worlds experience the adjustment sleep and the resurrection awakening seven times, after which consciousness is never again broken.","r":["47:10.5"]},{"q":"Mortal death is a technique of escape from the material life in the flesh","r":"47:10.7"}]}],"see":["Morontia","Muerte","Supervivencia","Ascensión mortal","Fusión con el Ajustador","Constelaciones y sistemas locales"]},{"n":52,"t":"Oración","en":"Prayer","sum":"Prayer is a personal and spontaneous expression of the attitude of the soul toward the spirit, the breath of the soul in the communion of sonship with God. Beginning as primitive petitions for material things, prayer gradually evolved into ethical and spiritual communion. Prayer does not change God but changes the one who prays, and it is truest when it seeks values, not things, and growth, not gratification. Jesus lived a life dedicated in prayer to the Father's will.","sections":[{"h":"What Prayer Is","items":[{"q":"Prayer is entirely a personal and spontaneous expression of the attitude of the soul toward the spirit","r":"144:2.2"},{"x":"Prayer is the communion of sonship and the expression of fellowship; the ideal prayer is spiritual communion leading to intelligent worship.","r":["144:2.2"]},{"x":"Prayer is the breath of the soul, leading one to strive persistently to ascertain the Father's will.","r":["144:2.3"]},{"x":"Prayer is the process of exchanging the human will for the divine will, part of the divine plan for making over what is into what ought to be.","r":["144:4.9"]},{"x":"True prayer is the sincere and trusting communication of the creature's spiritual nature with the omnipresent spirit of the Creator.","r":["91:8.4"]},{"q":"«La oración es el aliento del alma y debe conduciros a persistir en vuestro intento de conocer la voluntad del Padre.","r":"144:2.3"}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Prayer","items":[{"x":"Primitive man prayed for material blessings such as food and rain; this was a perversion of prayer, yet it also stimulated social and ethical effort.","r":["91:1.3"]},{"x":"Prayer is a monologue only in the most primitive minds; it soon becomes a dialogue and broadens into group worship.","r":["91:1.4"]},{"x":"Magic was an attempt to adjust Deity to conditions; prayer is an effort to adjust the personality to the will of Deity.","r":["91:8.2"]},{"x":"The idea of sacrifice, offering material things in place of the will, diminishes the efficacy of true prayer.","r":["91:2.4"]}]},{"h":"Principles of True Prayer","items":[{"x":"Selfish and materialistic prayer is incompatible with ethical religion founded on unselfish love.","r":["91:4.1"]},{"q":"La oración no debe prostituirse nunca tanto hasta el punto de volverse un sustituto de la acción.","r":"91:4.2"},{"x":"Do not be so lazy as to ask God to solve problems for you; ask for wisdom and strength while you face them.","r":["91:6.5"]},{"q":"Ora tan sólo por valores, no por cosas; por crecimiento, no por gratificación.","r":"91:8.13"},{"x":"God answers the attitude of the soul, not words, and he answers prayer with an enlarged revelation of truth, beauty, and goodness.","r":["91:8.11","91:8.12"]},{"x":"Effective prayer requires courageously facing reality, sincere effort, choosing and carrying out the divine will, and living faith.","r":["91:9.2","91:9.5","91:9.8"]}]},{"h":"What Prayer Changes","items":[{"x":"Prayer does not change God, but great and lasting changes take place in the one who prays in faith.","r":["91:4.5"]},{"q":"La oración no cambia la actitud divina hacia el hombre, pero sí cambia la actitud del hombre hacia el Padre inmutable.","r":"146:2.8"},{"x":"As a bird must spread its wings to ride rising air currents, prayer lifts one up on the spiritual currents of the universe.","r":["91:8.9"]},{"x":"The quickest way to overcome the habit of criticizing a friend is to pray for him every day.","r":["91:5.3"]},{"x":"Prayer offered sincerely in faith, even a foolish petition, never fails to enlarge the soul's capacity for spiritual receptivity.","r":["144:4.2"]},{"q":"Recordad, aunque la oración no cambia a Dios, muy frecuentemente efectúa cambios grandes y duraderos en el que ora con fe y confianza.","r":"91:4.5"}]},{"h":"Prayer as Jesus Taught It","items":[{"x":"When one is wholly dedicated to doing the Father's will, every petition is answered, because the prayer is in accord with that will.","r":["146:2.7"]},{"x":"Jesus prayed more for the spiritual progress of his brothers than for himself, and he urged prayer especially for enemies and persecutors.","r":["146:2.10","146:2.11"]},{"x":"One should be able to talk with the Father as a son not only in times of distress but also when the soul is at peace.","r":["146:2.12"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that after praying one should wait in silence for a time, giving the indwelling spirit opportunity to speak to the soul.","r":["146:2.17"]},{"x":"Jesus usually prayed in the plural rather than the singular, and he prayed for himself only in the great crises of his earth life.","r":["144:4.6"]},{"x":"For Jesus prayer was not a religious duty but a sincere expression of spiritual attitude and constant communion with God.","r":["196:0.10"]}]}],"see":["Adoración","Voluntad de Dios","Fe","Filiación con Dios","Experiencia religiosa","Religión personal"]},{"n":1,"t":"Padre Universal","en":"Universal Father","sum":"El Padre Universal es Dios, la Primera Fuente y Centro de todas las cosas y de todos los seres. Es el Creador, el Controlador y el Sostenedor infinito; aunque es un espíritu invisible, es una verdadera personalidad que ama a todas sus criaturas como un padre. Puesto que su fragmento, el Ajustador del Pensamiento, mora en el hombre, cualquiera puede emprender la aventura eterna de encontrar al Padre y llegar a ser semejante a él.","sections":[{"h":"Primera Fuente y Centro","items":[{"x":"El Padre es el Dios de toda la creación, la Primera Fuente y Centro de todas las cosas y de todos los seres, al que hay que concebir primero como Creador, luego como Controlador y por último como Sostenedor infinito.","r":["1:0.1"]},{"x":"El Padre creó personalmente el Paraíso y el universo central, mientras que los universos del tiempo y del espacio son obra de los Hijos Creadores; Nebadon es la creación de su Hijo Micael.","r":["1:2.9"]},{"x":"El Padre actúa físicamente mediante la gravedad de la Isla del Paraíso, mentalmente en el Espíritu Infinito y espiritualmente en el Hijo Eterno, y sin embargo mantiene un contacto directo con sus criaturas.","r":["1:2.10"]},{"q":"Dios no es ni semejante al hombre ni a la máquina.","r":"1:2.1"},{"x":"Para Dios no existen por separado el pasado, el presente y el futuro; todo el tiempo es presente, y ningún acontecimiento del universo lo toma jamás por sorpresa.","r":["2:1.5"]}]},{"h":"Nombre y realidad","items":[{"x":"La Primera Fuente y Centro nunca ha revelado un nombre para sí; el nombre de «Padre» surgió de la relación personal que sus criaturas tienen con él.","r":["1:1.1"]},{"x":"Importa poco el nombre con que se le llame; lo que importa es el deseo de conocerlo y de ser semejante a él.","r":["1:1.6"]},{"x":"Dios es una realidad trascendente, infinitamente mayor que cualquier realidad idealizada, que cualquier ley de la naturaleza personificada o que el «producto más elevado del hombre».","r":["1:2.2"]},{"x":"La existencia de Dios no puede probarse mediante experimentos científicos ni mediante la lógica pura; solo se comprende en el ámbito de la experiencia humana.","r":["1:2.7"]},{"q":"Those who know God have experienced the fact of his presence","r":"1:2.8"}]},{"h":"Espíritu invisible, verdadera personalidad","items":[{"q":"«Dios es espíritu». Es una presencia espiritual universal.","r":"1:3.1"},{"x":"El Padre es invisible no porque se oculte, sino porque los seres materiales no podrían conservar su existencia ante su resplandor espiritual; pero se le puede discernir con el ojo de la fe.","r":["1:3.3"]},{"x":"Su infinitud no debe oscurecer su personalidad; el Padre es la cumbre de la personalidad divina, el origen y el destino de toda personalidad.","r":["1:5.1"]},{"x":"En el universo local el Padre se revela en las personalidades de los Hijos Creadores, de modo que quien ha visto al Hijo ha visto al Padre.","r":["1:5.5","3:0.2"]}]},{"h":"El Padre amoroso","items":[{"q":"Dios no ama como si fuera un padre, sino como un padre.","r":"2:6.4"},{"x":"El amor del Padre no se ganó mediante el sacrificio ni la intercesión de sus Hijos; él ama personalmente a sus hijos desde el principio.","r":["2:5.2"]},{"x":"Los profetas hebreos proclamaron a Dios como el Padre de Israel, pero Jesús lo reveló como el Padre de cada ser humano.","r":["2:6.4"]},{"x":"El Padre participa personalmente en la lucha de toda alma que se esfuerza por alcanzar la perfección: sufre en nuestras aflicciones y triunfa en nuestras victorias.","r":["1:5.15","1:5.16"]},{"x":"Dios Padre ama a la humanidad, Dios Hijo sirve a la humanidad, y Dios Espíritu inspira a sus hijos a ascender en busca del Padre.","r":["3:6.8"]}]},{"h":"El camino hacia el Padre","items":[{"x":"El Padre no requiere culto formal ni servicio servil; la consagración sincera a hacer la voluntad del Padre es el único don verdaderamente personal que el hombre puede ofrecer.","r":["1:1.2"]},{"q":"\"Be you perfect, even as I am perfect.\"","r":"1:0.3"},{"x":"El hombre no puede acercarse directamente al Padre, no porque él esté lejos, sino por la finitud de la criatura; y el camino está abierto para todos.","r":["5:1.1","5:1.8"]},{"q":"¡Qué error soñar en un Dios remoto en los cielos cuando el espíritu del Padre Universal vive dentro de vuestra mente!","r":"5:2.3"},{"x":"Por diferente que sea su condición intelectual y social, todos los hombres han recibido la misma presencia divina, de modo que la posibilidad de progreso espiritual es igual para todos.","r":["5:1.4","5:1.5"]},{"x":"Por mucho tiempo que lleve, el ascendente fusionado con el Ajustador se hallará un día ante el centro divino y verá al Padre cara a cara.","r":["5:1.9"]}]}],"see":["Atributos de Dios","Personalidad de Dios","Trinidad del Paraíso","Ajustador del Pensamiento","Filiación con Dios","Adoración"]},{"n":87,"t":"Parábolas","en":"Parables","sum":"The parable is the storytelling method of teaching that Jesus first used with the multitude by the Sea of Galilee and that thereafter became almost his only method of public instruction. He taught that parables should not be interpreted as allegories with a hidden meaning in every detail but received as true-to-life stories that reveal one central truth. A parable appeals at once to minds of different levels, plants new truth while avoiding prejudice and controversy, and leaves each person to find its meaning in his own soul.","sections":[{"h":"The Beginning of Teaching by Parables","items":[{"x":"Jesus first used this method when, from a boat by the sea, he told the parable of the sower to a crowd of nearly a thousand.","r":["151:1.1","151:1.2"]},{"x":"It was intended that those sincerely wishing to enter the kingdom would grasp the meaning, while those seeking to entrap him would see and not understand.","r":["151:1.4"]},{"x":"From then on Jesus taught the public almost entirely in parables and explained their meaning more fully to the apostles in the evening.","r":["151:4.7"]},{"x":"Parables appealing to nature were the best reply to the charge that his work was done by the power of the devil, and they gave his enemies less to seize upon.","r":["151:3.14"]}]},{"h":"Parables, Not Allegories","items":[{"x":"Peter and Nathaniel disagreed while interpreting the parable of the sower as an allegory with a hidden meaning in every detail.","r":["151:2.1","151:2.4"]},{"x":"Thomas recalled the Master's teaching that illustrations should use true-to-life stories that reveal one central truth.","r":["151:2.5"]},{"q":"Well done, Thomas; you have discerned the true meaning of parables","r":"151:2.7"},{"x":"Jesus said that private flights of imagination may be profitable, but offering them as public teaching is a mistake.","r":["151:2.7"]},{"x":"Jesus advised avoiding fables and allegories and using parables freely, especially those drawn from nature.","r":["151:3.3"]}]},{"h":"The Value of Parables","items":[{"q":"La parábola posibilita la llamada simultánea a niveles vastamente diferentes de mente y espíritu.","r":"151:3.6"},{"q":"La parábola va de las cosas conocidas al discernimiento de lo desconocido.","r":"151:3.7"},{"x":"The parable plants new truth in the mind while bypassing prejudice and arousing a minimum of antagonism.","r":["151:3.8"]},{"x":"Parables avoid direct conflict with tradition and authority and recall the teaching whenever the familiar scene is seen again.","r":["151:3.10","151:3.11"]},{"x":"Hearing the same story, each person can interpret a parable according to his own intellectual and spiritual level.","r":["151:3.1"]}]},{"h":"Parables of the Growing Seed","items":[{"x":"The parable of the sower reviewed the ministry up to then and foreshadowed the varied success later messengers would meet.","r":["151:3.13"]},{"x":"Appealing only to emotion or intellect bears no fruit; true change of character comes from appealing to the spirit that lives within man.","r":["152:6.3"]},{"x":"The parable of the seed that grows by itself into the full ear shows that the kingdom grows quietly beyond human understanding.","r":["151:3.15"]},{"x":"The parables of the mustard seed and the leaven tell how the kingdom, small in its beginnings, grows great and spreads like leaven through the whole lump.","r":["151:4.2","151:4.3"]}]},{"h":"Parables Portraying the Father's Love","items":[{"q":"Pero yo he venido para mostraros que, mientras vosotros buscáis a Dios, Dios del mismo modo os busca a vosotros.","r":"169:1.2"},{"q":"the Father accepts you even before you have repented","r":"169:1.3"},{"x":"The father of the prodigal saw his son returning afar off, ran to meet him, and ordered a feast before the son had finished his confession.","r":["169:1.9","169:1.10"]},{"x":"The three stories of the lost sheep, the lost coin, and the lost son show respectively the Father seeking the lost, the thoroughness of the search, and complete restoration.","r":["169:1.15"]},{"x":"The parable of the prodigal son and the story of the good Samaritan were Jesus' favorite ways of teaching the Father's love and human neighborliness.","r":["169:1.16"]}]},{"h":"Neighborliness, Humility, and Faithfulness","items":[{"x":"To the trick question \"Who is my neighbor?\" Jesus answered with the story of the good Samaritan, letting the lawyer answer for himself.","r":["164:1.2","164:1.3","164:1.4"]},{"x":"The parable of the Pharisee and the publican teaches that salvation cannot be bought by works but is a free gift to all who have faith.","r":["167:5.1"]},{"x":"The parables of the talents and the pounds show that ability is the measure of opportunity and that equal faithfulness receives equal reward.","r":["171:8.10","171:8.13"]},{"q":"Let every man find out the meaning for himself and in his own soul.","r":"167:2.4"}]}],"see":["Enseñanzas de Jesús","Reino del cielo","Amor","Perdón","Misericordia","Los doce apóstoles"]},{"n":11,"t":"Paraíso","en":"Paradise","sum":"El Paraíso es el centro eterno del universo de los universos y la Isla eterna donde moran el Padre, el Hijo y el Espíritu. Es a la vez una morada espiritual y una esfera material compuesta de absolutum; es la fuente de toda energía física y de toda gravedad, y el absoluto de todos los modelos. Existe sin tiempo y no tiene ubicación en el espacio, y es el destino que todo mortal que conoce a Dios está llamado a alcanzar al final de la larga ascensión.","sections":[{"h":"La morada de la Deidad","items":[{"x":"El Paraíso es el centro eterno del universo de los universos, donde moran el Padre, el Hijo y el Espíritu con sus coordinados, y es el cuerpo organizado más gigantesco del universo maestro.","r":["11:0.1"]},{"x":"El Paraíso es a la vez una morada espiritual y una esfera material; ha existido desde la eternidad, y no hay registros ni tradiciones sobre su origen.","r":["11:0.1","11:0.2"]},{"x":"La presencia personal del Padre se halla en el centro del Paraíso superior, rodeada de la presencia del Hijo Eterno y envuelta en la gloria del Espíritu Infinito.","r":["11:1.1"]},{"x":"Ya se sigan las líneas de la gravedad, las de la gravedad espiritual, los circuitos de la mente o el circuito de personalidad, se llega finalmente a la residencia central del Padre.","r":["11:1.4"]},{"q":"Que tan pocas de las criaturas del universo hayan encontrado a Dios en el Paraíso en modo alguno refuta tampoco la realidad de su existencia ni de su persona espiritual en el centro de todas las cosas.","r":"11:1.3"}]},{"h":"Naturaleza de la Isla eterna","items":[{"x":"El Paraíso no es esférico, sino un elipsoide achatado cuyo diámetro norte-sur es un sexto más largo que su diámetro este-oeste, y proporciona el patrón de dirección absoluta en el universo maestro.","r":["11:2.2","11:2.3"]},{"x":"La Isla se divide en Paraíso superior, periférico y bajo; la Trinidad parece presidir el plano superior, que es personal, y el Absoluto No Cualificado el plano inferior, que es impersonal.","r":["11:2.4","11:2.8"]},{"x":"El Paraíso se compone de una organización homogénea de potencia del espacio que no se encuentra en ninguna otra parte del universo, y que los Melquisedek llaman absolutum.","r":["11:2.9"]},{"q":"El Paraíso existe sin tiempo y no tiene ubicación en el espacio.","r":"11:2.10"},{"x":"A grandes rasgos, el espacio parece originarse justo debajo del Paraíso bajo, y el tiempo justo encima del Paraíso superior.","r":["11:2.11"]}]},{"h":"El Paraíso superior y periférico","items":[{"x":"El Paraíso superior contiene el área de la presencia de la Deidad, la Esfera Santísima, destinada a la adoración y a la trinidización, y el Área Santa, destinada a residencia.","r":["11:3.1"]},{"x":"Las siete zonas concéntricas del Área Santa se llaman «las mansiones del Padre en el Paraíso», y la segunda zona está reservada a los ascendentes de los siete superuniversos.","r":["11:3.3"]},{"x":"La provisión residencial para los ascendentes ocupa menos del uno por ciento de la tierra santa asignada, lo que deja amplio espacio para los seres que aún han de venir.","r":["11:3.4"]},{"x":"El Paraíso periférico es el lugar de aterrizaje de los que atraviesan el espacio y alberga vastas áreas de exposición histórica y profética de los universos locales.","r":["11:4.1","11:4.3"]},{"q":"You must wait, and ascend while you wait","r":"11:4.5"}]},{"h":"El Paraíso bajo y el espacio","items":[{"x":"Toda la energía física y todos los circuitos de fuerza cósmica se originan en el Paraíso bajo, donde no mora ninguna personalidad.","r":["11:5.1"]},{"x":"La zona interior del centro de fuerza del Paraíso bajo pulsa como un corazón gigantesco y envía corrientes hasta los confines más exteriores del espacio físico.","r":["11:5.5"]},{"x":"Se cree que la zona exterior es el foco central de la presencia espacial del Absoluto No Cualificado, cuyas emanaciones salen y entran alternativamente en ciclos de algo más de mil millones de años.","r":["11:5.7","11:5.8"]},{"x":"Todo el espacio se expande y se contrae alternativamente, y un ciclo de expansión y contracción dura algo más de dos mil millones de años del tiempo de Urantia.","r":["11:6.1","11:6.5"]},{"x":"El espacio no toca el Paraíso; el Paraíso es el núcleo inmóvil de las zonas de quietud situadas entre el espacio penetrado y el no penetrado.","r":["11:7.1","11:7.2"]}]},{"h":"El absoluto de la gravedad y de los modelos","items":[{"q":"La gravedad es la atracción todopoderosa de la presencia física del Paraíso.","r":"11:8.1"},{"x":"La gravedad absoluta es la gravedad del Paraíso, mientras que la gravedad local o lineal pertenece a la etapa eléctrica de la energía materializada.","r":["11:8.3"]},{"x":"El Paraíso es la fuente absoluta y el punto focal eterno de toda la energía-materia del universo de los universos.","r":["11:8.9"]},{"x":"El sistema Paraíso-Havona es el núcleo eterno del universo maestro, alrededor del cual giran en órbitas establecidas los siete superuniversos y el espacio exterior.","r":["12:1.11"]},{"x":"El Paraíso no es creador ni Deidad; es el absoluto de los modelos, y Havona es el despliegue real de sus potenciales.","r":["11:9.4","11:9.5","0:4.13"]},{"x":"Cuando el Padre expresó su yo espiritual en el Hijo Eterno, reveló simultáneamente el potencial infinito de su yo no personal como Paraíso.","r":["11:9.3"]}]},{"h":"El destino final","items":[{"x":"Para todas las personalidades espirituales, el Paraíso es el reino del origen primordial y la meta del destino final.","r":["11:9.1"]},{"x":"El Paraíso es el centro geográfico de la infinitud, pero no forma parte de ninguna creación universal, ni siquiera de Havona, sino que es una existencia eterna y exclusiva.","r":["11:9.2"]},{"q":"El Paraíso es el Centro de toda la creación, la fuente de todas las energías, y el lugar de origen primordial de todas las personalidades.","r":"11:9.7"},{"x":"El peregrino que cae en el último sueño del tiempo en el primer circuito de Havona despierta en el Paraíso, y solo entonces llega a ser un verdadero hijo del Paraíso.","r":["26:11.6"]},{"x":"En el Paraíso reinan un orden y una armonía perceptibles, y los directores de conducta instruyen a los recién llegados para que puedan vivir allí sin confusión.","r":["27:4.2","27:4.3"]},{"x":"La morada de Dios es el modelo de todos los mundos sede central del universo, y el universo central de su morada es el modelo de los ideales y del destino de todos los universos.","r":["11:9.6"]},{"q":"Cada mortal que conoce a Dios y que ha abrazado la carrera de hacer la voluntad del Padre, ya se ha embarcado en la larga, la larguísima senda hacia el Paraíso en la búsqueda de la divinidad y logro de la perfección.","r":"11:9.8"}]}],"see":["Havona","Gravedad","Los tres Absolutos","Padre Universal","Gran universo y universo maestro","Ascensión mortal"]},{"n":66,"t":"Pecado","en":"Sin","sum":"Sin is not mere imperfection or mistake but the attitude of a personality that knowingly and deliberately resists the Father's will and divine reality: deliberate disloyalty to God. The moral responsibility for sin is wholly personal and is not inherited, and no one loses survival because of another's sin. All sin can be forgiven, but a personality that has become wholly identified with sin becomes unreal and eventually reaches extinction.","sections":[{"h":"What Sin Is","items":[{"q":"«El pecado es la transgresión consciente, conocedora y deliberada de la ley divina, la voluntad del Padre.","r":"148:4.4"},{"x":"Error is the misunderstanding of reality, evil a partial maladjustment to reality, and sin a purposeful resistance to divine reality.","r":["67:1.4"]},{"x":"Error reveals a lack of intellectual keenness, evil a deficiency of wisdom, sin spiritual poverty, and iniquity failing personality control.","r":["67:1.5"]},{"x":"Good is the carrying out of the divine plan; sin is a deliberate rebellion against the divine will.","r":["75:4.3"]},{"q":"El pecado ha de redefinirse como deslealtad deliberada a la Deidad.","r":"89:10.2"}]},{"h":"Imperfection Is Not Sin","items":[{"x":"The natural evil tendencies and imperfections of a person before rebirth are neither sin nor iniquity but only the starting point of the ascending journey.","r":["148:4.6"]},{"x":"Finiteness in itself is neither evil nor sinful; evil and sin arise when the finite is misused and distorted.","r":["111:6.3"]},{"x":"A sense of guilt is only the awareness of having violated a moral code and does not necessarily mean sin; there is true sin only in conscious disloyalty to God.","r":["89:10.3"]},{"x":"The capacity to feel guilt is not a badge of human degradation but a mark of a being with potential greatness.","r":["89:10.4"]},{"x":"Sin reveals the immaturity of one dazzled by the liberty of the will who fails to realize the obligations of universe citizenship.","r":["118:7.4"]}]},{"h":"Consequences of and Responsibility for Sin","items":[{"x":"The effects of sin are never local, but sin is fatal to survival only when it becomes the whole attitude of mind and soul.","r":["67:7.4"]},{"q":"Sin is wholly personal as to moral guilt or spiritual consequences","r":"67:7.7"},{"x":"No being's sin can prevent another's survival; eternal survival is jeopardized only by one's own choosing.","r":["67:7.5"]},{"q":"La naturaleza animal —la tendencia al mal— puede ser hereditaria, pero el pecado no se transmite de padre a hijo.","r":"188:4.5"},{"x":"Repeated sin becomes habit, and the habitual sinner can easily slip into iniquity and become a wholehearted rebel against the universe.","r":["67:1.6"]}]},{"h":"God and Sin","items":[{"x":"God loves the sinner as an eternal personality reality, but sin is neither a person nor a spiritual reality, so only justice takes cognizance of it.","r":["2:6.8"]},{"q":"El amor de Dios salva al pecador; la ley de Dios destruye el pecado.","r":"2:6.8"},{"x":"A being wholly identified with sin becomes unreal and self-destroying, and once the sentence of extinction is executed, it becomes as if it had never been.","r":["2:3.2","2:3.4"]},{"q":"El pecado es una experiencia de la conciencia de la criatura; no es parte de la conciencia de Dios.","r":"174:1.4"}]},{"h":"The Evolution and Correction of the Idea of Sin","items":[{"x":"For primitive man sin was the violation of a ghost-sanctioned taboo, and death was regarded as its penalty.","r":["89:2.2","70:11.4"]},{"x":"Primitive sin was an act, not a thought, and ceremonial; it gave rise to the belief in a fall from a perfect beginning.","r":["89:2.3"]},{"x":"Sacrifice for personal sin gradually developed into the doctrine of atoning sacrifice for the sins of the race.","r":["89:4.5"]},{"x":"Jesus did not die to atone for the racial guilt of mankind or to appease the wrath of God.","r":["188:4.1"]},{"x":"Confession of sin does not remove its temporal consequences, but it is essential to religious growth and spiritual progress.","r":["89:10.5","156:2.7"]}]}],"see":["Mal","Perdón","Libre albedrío","Justicia","Rebelión de Lucifer","Moralidad"]},{"n":92,"t":"Pentecostés","en":"Pentecost","sum":"Pentecost is the day, after Jesus' departure, when the Spirit of Truth was poured out upon the one hundred and twenty believers in the upper chamber in Jerusalem and upon all the sincere throughout the world. The apostles, who had been hiding in fear, came out endowed with new power and boldly preached the gospel, and that day more than two thousand were baptized. The Urantia Book explains that Pentecost was not an outburst of emotion but a spiritual event that freed the religion of Jesus from the fetters of nation, race, and sex, and from dependence on physical force.","sections":[{"h":"What Happened That Day","items":[{"x":"The one hundred and twenty believers at prayer sensed a strange presence in the room and became conscious of a new and profound feeling of spiritual joy, security, and confidence.","r":["194:0.1"]},{"x":"Peter declared this to be the coming of the Spirit of Truth the Master had promised and proposed that they go to the temple to proclaim the good news.","r":["194:0.2"]},{"x":"The apostles, who had hidden for forty days, appeared boldly in the temple crowded for the feast of Pentecost.","r":["194:1.1"]},{"x":"Peter's fervent appeal, made where the Master had last taught, won more than two thousand souls.","r":["194:1.2"]},{"x":"That evening the new believers were baptized in the Master's name at the pool of Siloam, and for a time the believers remained a sect within Judaism.","r":["194:1.4","194:1.5"]}]},{"h":"The Spirit Poured Out on All","items":[{"q":"Do not overlook the fact that the Spirit of Truth was bestowed upon all sincere believers","r":"194:3.6"},{"x":"The gift of the spirit came not only to the apostles but to all the men and women in the upper chamber and to the honest of heart throughout the world.","r":["194:3.6"]},{"x":"At the same hour the spirit came wherever there were true believers, in Philadelphia, Alexandria, and elsewhere.","r":["194:3.17"]},{"x":"Jesus' mother and brother were present but received no greater gift than the others; Pentecost ended belief in holy families and special priesthoods.","r":["194:3.15"]},{"x":"The spirit came upon those quietly sitting in prayer, apart from any form, ceremony, or sacred place.","r":["194:3.10"]}]},{"h":"A Spiritual Event, Not an Emotional One","items":[{"x":"Later Pentecost was confused with uncontrolled emotionalism, but the chief mission of the outpoured spirit was to teach the truths of the Father's love and the Son's mercy.","r":["194:3.1"]},{"q":"Prayer did not bring the spirit on the day of Pentecost","r":"194:3.20"},{"x":"Prayer does not move God to give more liberally, but it had much to do with determining each believer's capacity of receptivity.","r":["194:3.20"]},{"x":"\"Baptism of the spirit\" meant only the conscious reception of the gift of the Spirit of Truth and the acknowledgment of its new power.","r":["194:2.10"]},{"x":"The apostles lost themselves and found the spirit; it was not an emotional experience but a response to their dedication of themselves to God.","r":["194:3.16"]}]},{"h":"Religion Freed from Fetters","items":[{"q":"El día de Pentecostés la religión de Jesús rompió todas las restricciones nacionales y las cadenas raciales.","r":"194:3.5"},{"x":"That many peoples received the apostles' preaching showed that the gospel must not be identified with any race, culture, or language.","r":["194:3.9"]},{"x":"After Pentecost, in the brotherhood of the kingdom, woman stood before God equal with man.","r":["194:3.14"]},{"x":"Pentecost freed the Master's religion from all dependence on physical force, equipping it with the spiritual weapons of forgiveness, good will, and love.","r":["194:3.11"]},{"q":"La humanidad tan sólo puede unificarse mediante el enfoque espiritual, y el Espíritu de la Verdad es una influencia mundial que influye uniformemente.","r":"194:3.18"}]},{"h":"God Seeking Man","items":[{"q":"Up to Pentecost, religion had revealed only man seeking for God","r":"194:3.13"},{"x":"Since Pentecost there shines out the spectacle of God also seeking man and, when he has found him, sending his spirit to dwell within him.","r":["194:3.13"]},{"x":"The bestowal of the Spirit of Truth prepared the minds of all normal people for the subsequent universal bestowal of the Adjusters.","r":["194:2.3"]},{"x":"Thereafter man has threefold guidance: the Adjuster, spirit of the Father; the Spirit of Truth, spirit of the Son; and the Holy Spirit, spirit of the Spirit.","r":["194:2.11"]},{"x":"Within less than a month after the spirit came, the apostles made more spiritual progress than in their four years with Jesus.","r":["194:2.9"]}]},{"h":"The New Message and the Beginning of the Church","items":[{"x":"Their message shifted from the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man to the proclamation of the risen Christ.","r":["194:0.3","194:4.4"]},{"q":"El evangelio del reino, el mensaje de Cristo, súbitamente se ha transformado en el evangelio del Señor Jesucristo.","r":"194:4.5"},{"x":"Calling one another brothers and sisters, the believers formed a fellowship of worship and life, breaking bread, praying, and caring for the poor.","r":["194:4.3","194:4.7"]},{"x":"Stephen's martyrdom led to the formal organization of the early church, and the persecution that followed scattered teachers to the ends of the empire.","r":["194:4.12","194:4.13"]},{"x":"Jesus' earth life becomes the anchor of time, and the Spirit of Truth the source that makes the religion he lived grow forever.","r":["194:3.8"]}]}],"see":["Espíritu de la Verdad","Resurrección de Jesús","Los doce apóstoles","Religión institucional","Ajustador del Pensamiento","Espíritu Santo"]},{"n":68,"t":"Perdón","en":"Forgiveness","sum":"God's forgiveness flows naturally from his infinite understanding; it is given before man asks and requires no intermediary or sacrifice. Yet this forgiveness becomes real in personal religious experience only when one forgives one's fellows. Jesus taught to forgive even seventy times seven, and he said that inability to forgive others is a mark of immaturity that has not attained understanding and love.","sections":[{"h":"Forgiveness in the Father's Nature","items":[{"q":"Puesto que Dios conoce todo acerca de sus hijos, es fácil para él perdonar.","r":"2:4.2"},{"x":"At the bottom of God's goodness lies the universal tendency to love, show mercy, manifest patience, and minister forgiveness.","r":["2:6.9"]},{"x":"The Father is not a personality divided between justice and mercy, and he requires no mediator in order to forgive.","r":["2:6.6"]},{"x":"Divine forgiveness is an inevitable consequence inherent in God's infinite understanding, his full knowledge of his children's errors and choices.","r":["174:1.3"]},{"x":"The understanding love of wise parents usually prevents the very estrangement that would call for repentance and forgiveness.","r":["174:1.2"]}]},{"h":"The Way to Receive Forgiveness","items":[{"x":"Divine forgiveness is the renewal of severed relations of loyalty; it need not be sought, only recognized and accepted.","r":["89:10.6"]},{"q":"The Father in heaven has forgiven you even before you have thought to ask him","r":"146:2.4"},{"x":"God's forgiveness is in fact unconditioned, but in experience it becomes real only when one forgives one's fellows.","r":["146:2.4","170:3.4"]},{"x":"In forgiving his brother, a person creates in his soul the capacity to receive God's forgiveness of his own misdeeds.","r":["170:2.23"]},{"x":"Faith is the price of entrance into God's family, and forgiveness is the act of God in accepting that faith.","r":["170:3.3"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that forgiveness of sin is received by faith in God, without penance or sacrifice.","r":["138:8.2","150:5.2"]}]},{"h":"Forgive One Another","items":[{"q":"the Father in heaven forgives you your sins; therefore should you learn to forgive one another.","r":"159:1.3"},{"x":"When Peter asked whether seven times was enough, Jesus answered to forgive even seventy times seven.","r":["159:1.4"]},{"x":"With the parable of the steward forgiven a great debt by the king who would not forgive his fellow's small debt, he taught the duty of the forgiven.","r":["159:1.4","159:1.5"]},{"x":"The better one understands a neighbor, the easier it is to forgive; when one loves a brother, one has already forgiven him.","r":["2:4.2","174:1.4"]},{"q":"El hombre no perdona de verdad a sus semejantes, a menos que los ame como a sí mismo.","r":"170:3.5"}]},{"h":"The Immaturity That Cannot Forgive","items":[{"q":"«Vuestra incapacidad o falta de deseo de perdonar a vuestros semejantes es la medida de vuestra inmadurez, de vuestra incapacidad para alcanzar una compasión adulta, comprensión y amor.","r":"174:1.5"},{"x":"People hold grudges and nurse vengefulness in proportion to their ignorance of others' inner nature and longings.","r":["174:1.5"]},{"x":"All sin can be forgiven, but it is doubtful that a confirmed iniquitous person would ever truly sorrow or accept forgiveness.","r":["67:1.6"]},{"x":"Those who knowingly and maliciously attribute the works of God to the forces of evil can hardly obtain forgiveness.","r":["153:4.3","165:3.6"]},{"x":"The Father is not an indulgent parent who overlooks everything; he does not condone his children's self-destructive conduct.","r":["147:5.9"]}]},{"h":"Forgiveness in History and the Example of Jesus","items":[{"x":"In primitive religion confession and forgiveness were a meaningless ritual that forgave in advance even the sins of the following week.","r":["89:2.5"]},{"x":"Hosea preached forgiveness through repentance, not sacrifice, and revived the gospel of love and divine mercy.","r":["97:4.5"]},{"x":"Before Jesus, a God who forgives repentant sinners was known, but a God who goes out first to seek the lost sheep was new.","r":["159:5.16"]},{"q":"Las únicas palabras de Jesús, al clavarlo ellos al travensaño, fueron «Padre, perdónalos porque no saben qué están haciendo».","r":"187:2.4"},{"x":"Peter, who had denied the Master, fully believed he was forgiven only after the risen Jesus received him again.","r":["184:2.13","139:2.10"]}]}],"see":["Misericordia","Pecado","Amor","Hermandad de los hombres","Enseñanzas de Jesús","Filiación con Dios"]},{"n":36,"t":"Personalidad","en":"Personality","sum":"Personality is the unique gift that the Universal Father exclusively bestows upon living energy systems of matter, mind, and spirit. It is neither body, mind, spirit, nor soul; it is the one changeless reality amid ever-changing experience, and it unifies all other factors. Personality shows itself in self-consciousness and relative free will; every personality is linked to the Father by his personality circuit and survives death with the survival of the soul.","sections":[{"h":"The Father's Gift","items":[{"x":"God the Father is the bestower and conservator of every personality, and the destiny of all finite personalities who choose the divine will.","r":["5:6.1"]},{"q":"No hay personalidad aparte de Dios el Padre, y no existe personalidad ninguna sino por Dios el Padre.","r":"5:6.4"},{"x":"Personality does not arise of itself; the impersonal never becomes personal without a direct act of the Father.","r":["0:5.4","5:6.3"]},{"x":"Personality is not attained by degrees; it is either present or absent.","r":["5:6.3"]},{"x":"Personality is bestowed directly by the Universal Father, or by the Conjoint Actor acting for him, and may be given to living energy systems endowed with mind or spirit.","r":["112:0.3","112:0.4"]}]},{"h":"What Personality Is","items":[{"q":"Personality is the one changeless reality in an otherwise ever-changing creature experience;","r":"0:5.11"},{"x":"Human personality is neither body, mind, spirit, nor soul, and it unifies all the other factors of individuality.","r":["0:5.11"]},{"x":"Personality is one of the unsolved mysteries of the universe; its components are known, but its real nature is not fully understood.","r":["5:6.2"]},{"x":"Personality has no identity of its own, yet it can unify the identity of a living energy system.","r":["112:0.7"]},{"x":"In the human system personality unifies all activities and imparts the qualities of identity and creativity.","r":["112:1.19"]}]},{"h":"Unique and Changeless","items":[{"x":"Personalities may be similar but never the same; even those of the same series and type are not identical.","r":["16:8.4"]},{"x":"Because of personality we can recognize a being as the very one we knew before, however much its form or spiritual status has changed.","r":["16:8.4"]},{"q":"they are associable but nontotalable.","r":"112:0.12"},{"x":"Adjusters are alike in nature when they come from the Father, but personality is diverse, original, and exclusive.","r":["16:8.3"]},{"x":"Through all the stages of evolution there is in each person a changeless part, the personality that endures amid change.","r":["112:0.1"]}]},{"h":"Self-Consciousness and Free Will","items":[{"x":"Creature personality is distinguished by two phenomena: self-consciousness and the associated relative free will.","r":["16:8.5"]},{"x":"Self-consciousness is awareness of one's own personality reality, and it includes the ability to recognize the reality of other personalities.","r":["16:8.6"]},{"x":"Human free will relates to seven domains, among them moral decisions, spiritual choices, unselfish love, and worship.","r":["16:8.7","16:8.8","16:8.14"]},{"q":"Puede dar un don a Dios: dedicación del libre albedrío a hacer la voluntad de Dios.","r":"112:0.10"},{"x":"Having provided for the growth of the soul, the Father steps aside; in the matter of eternal survival he has decreed the absolute sovereignty of the mortal will.","r":["5:6.8"]}]},{"h":"The Personality Circuit and Relationships","items":[{"x":"All personalities are circuited in the personal presence of the Universal Father, and the Father is personally conscious of every personality.","r":["5:6.10","5:6.11"]},{"x":"This personality circuit exists apart from the mission of the Thought Adjusters, and personalities not indwelt by Adjusters are also embraced in it.","r":["5:6.10","5:6.12"]},{"x":"Personality responds directly to the presence of other personality and is characterized by a morality that recognizes the relativity of its relations with others.","r":["112:0.11","112:0.13"]},{"q":"Personality cannot very well perform in isolation.","r":"112:1.16"},{"x":"Because we are conscious of God as Creator Father, we become conscious of men as creature brothers.","r":["16:9.14"]}]},{"h":"Survival and Destiny of Personality","items":[{"x":"The material self has a temporal identity and the Adjuster an eternal identity, and together they produce the surviving identity of the immortal soul.","r":["5:6.7"]},{"q":"La identidad de la personalidad sobrevive mediante la sobrevivencia del alma y en ella.","r":"16:9.3"},{"x":"Human personality is eternal yet conditional as to identity; it must choose for itself whether to stand where destiny is fulfilled.","r":["112:5.2"]},{"x":"Relationships between personalities are not scaffolding; mortal memories of personal relations have cosmic value and persist on the mansion worlds.","r":["112:5.22"]},{"x":"The fact that God became man has forever changed all the meanings and values of human personality.","r":["112:2.7"]}]}],"see":["Padre Universal","Alma","Mente","Libre albedrío","Supervivencia","Personalidad de Dios"]},{"n":3,"t":"Personalidad de Dios","en":"Personality of God","sum":"El Padre Universal es infinito y, sin embargo, una verdadera personalidad. La personalidad no es un atributo entre muchos, sino la manera en que se revela la totalidad de su naturaleza infinita y de su voluntad unificada. La personalidad de toda criatura es otorgada por el Padre y sostenida en su circuito de personalidad, y como Dios es personal, el hombre puede comulgar con él, amarlo y llegar a ser su amigo.","sections":[{"h":"Dios infinito y personal","items":[{"q":"Dios es infinito y personal; es una personalidad infinita.","r":"1:5.1"},{"x":"Dios trasciende con mucho todo concepto de personalidad que el hombre pueda captar, pero no puede ser nada menos que una personalidad eterna, verdadera, buena y bella.","r":["1:5.2"]},{"x":"Sin Dios y su personalidad central no habría personalidad en ninguna parte del vasto universo.","r":["1:5.7"]},{"x":"La personalidad no es un atributo de Dios, sino la totalidad de su naturaleza infinita coordinada y de su voluntad divina unificada: la revelación de Dios al universo de los universos.","r":["1:5.13"]},{"x":"Dios es más que poder, energía, modelo o presencia; es una personalidad que ejerce una voluntad soberana, experimenta la autoconciencia de la divinidad y revela un amor de padre a sus hijos.","r":["3:6.7"]}]},{"h":"Ideas erróneas sobre la personalidad","items":[{"q":"Human personality is the time-space image-shadow cast by the divine Creator personality.","r":"1:6.1"},{"x":"La personalidad no requiere un cuerpo material; a causa de este error, el materialismo niega la personalidad de los muertos y el panteísmo la personalidad de un Dios sin cuerpo.","r":["1:5.12"]},{"x":"Negar la personalidad de la Primera Fuente y Centro deja solo los dos dilemas filosóficos del materialismo y el panteísmo.","r":["1:5.11"]},{"x":"La razón, la sabiduría y la experiencia religiosa implican la personalidad de Dios, pero no la prueban; este concepto llegó a la humanidad principalmente por medio de la revelación.","r":["1:5.10"]},{"q":"Dios es para la ciencia una causa; para la filosofía, una idea; para la religión, una persona, incluso el amante Padre celestial.","r":"1:6.2"},{"x":"El hombre contempla lo infinito desde lo finito, y Dios contempla lo finito desde lo infinito; por eso el concepto de la personalidad divina mejora a medida que mejora la comprensión humana de la personalidad humana.","r":["1:6.3"]}]},{"h":"El otorgador de la personalidad","items":[{"x":"El Padre es el otorgador y conservador de toda personalidad, desde el mortal más humilde hasta el creador más elevado, y el destino de toda personalidad finita que elige su voluntad.","r":["5:6.1"]},{"x":"La mente, el espíritu o la energía física por sí solos no son personalidad; la personalidad es la dotación que el Padre otorga exclusivamente a los sistemas vivientes de materia, mente y espíritu.","r":["5:6.3","5:6.4"]},{"q":"La personalidad no es tampoco un logro progresivo.","r":"5:6.3"},{"x":"Así como toda la gravedad está vinculada a la Isla del Paraíso, la mente al Actor Conjunto y el espíritu al Hijo Eterno, así toda personalidad está vinculada al circuito de personalidad del Padre.","r":["5:6.11"]},{"x":"Aparte de la misión de los Ajustadores, el Padre tiene conciencia personal de las personalidades de todos los niveles de existencia autoconsciente y está en contacto con ellas.","r":["5:6.10"]}]},{"h":"Respeto por el libre albedrío","items":[{"x":"Al otorgar la personalidad a una criatura, el Padre le otorga también una libertad relativa respecto de la respuesta servil a la causalidad antecedente.","r":["5:6.9"]},{"x":"Una vez que ha provisto para el crecimiento del alma, el Padre se retira, y ha decretado como ley absoluta la soberanía de la voluntad mortal en lo referente a la supervivencia eterna.","r":["5:6.8"]},{"q":"No personal creature can be coerced into the eternal adventure","r":"5:6.12"}]},{"h":"Comunión con un Dios personal","items":[{"x":"Entre cosas impersonales solo hay interacción; una comunión como la de un padre y un hijo solo puede disfrutarse cuando ambos son personalidades.","r":["1:7.1"]},{"q":"El hombre no logra la unión con Dios como una gota de agua podría encontrar unidad con el océano.","r":"1:7.2"},{"x":"La verdad y la belleza pueden concebirse aparte de la personalidad, pero la bondad divina solo se comprende en relación con la personalidad, y solo una personalidad puede amar y ser amada.","r":["1:7.3"]},{"x":"Puesto que Dios puede conocer y ser conocido, amar y ser amado, también el hombre puede ser conocido como amigo de Dios.","r":["1:5.8"]},{"x":"Jesús realizó plenamente el potencial de la personalidad espiritual en la experiencia humana, por lo que su vida es la revelación más práctica de la personalidad de Dios.","r":["1:6.8"]},{"x":"Si el hombre no llega a ver el amor de un Dios personal, el reino de Dios se convierte en un mero reino del bien.","r":["2:5.12"]}]}],"see":["Padre Universal","Personalidad","Libre albedrío","Atributos de Dios","Amor","Autootorgamiento de Jesús"]},{"n":30,"t":"Portadores de Vida","en":"Life Carriers","sum":"Los Portadores de Vida son Hijos del universo local creados conjuntamente por el Hijo Creador, el Espíritu Materno del Universo y uno de los Ancianos de los Días; diseñan la vida de las criaturas, la implantan en los planetas y fomentan su evolución. La chispa de vida se da por medio de ellos, pero su factor esencial procede del Espíritu Materno del Universo, y sus manipulaciones terminan en cuanto aparecen seres con voluntad. Urantia es un mundo de modificación de la vida, y su vida se formuló de nuevo aquí mismo, en el planeta.","sections":[{"h":"Origen y organización","items":[{"x":"Los Portadores de Vida son vástagos del Hijo Creador, del Espíritu Materno del Universo y de un Anciano de los Días designado; son el único grupo de vida inteligente del universo local en cuya creación participan los gobernantes del superuniverso.","r":["36:1.1"]},{"q":"A ellos se les ha confiado diseñar y llevar la vida que va a tomar la forma de las criaturas, a las esferas planetarias.","r":"36:0.1"},{"x":"Después de crear tres órdenes de hijos, entre ellos los Melquisedek, el Hijo y el Espíritu del universo local cooperan con el nivel siguiente de Dios el Séptuple para producir a los Portadores de Vida.","r":["35:0.7"]},{"x":"En Nebadon se han creado cien millones, dirigidos por el trío determinante de la vida formado por Gabriel, el Padre Melquisedek y Nambia, el Portador de Vida primogénito.","r":["36:1.2"]},{"x":"Se dividen en tres grupos: Portadores de Vida decanos, ayudantes y custodios; el cuerpo enviado a un planeta consta por lo general de cien decanos, cien ayudantes y mil custodios.","r":["36:1.3","36:3.2"]},{"x":"Pueden funcionar en tres niveles: el nivel físico de la electroquímica, el nivel intermedio de la existencia cuasimorontial y el nivel semiespiritual.","r":["65:1.2","65:1.3","65:1.5"]}]},{"h":"El diseño y la implantación de la vida","items":[{"q":"La vida no aparece espontáneamente en los universos; los Portadores de Vida deben iniciarla en los planetas estériles.","r":"36:3.1"},{"x":"En los siete mundos de los Portadores de Vida del circuito de Salvington estudian la planificación de la vida, su conservación, la evolución, la vida asociada a la mente y más; los diseños originales de la vida los proporciona el Hijo Creador.","r":["36:2.1","36:2.12"]},{"q":"La chispa vital —el misterio de la vida— se otorga a través de los Portadores de Vida, no por ellos mismos.","r":"36:3.4"},{"x":"Ellos formulan el plasma vital, pero la chispa de energía que vivifica el cuerpo y presagia la mente procede del Espíritu Materno del Universo.","r":["36:3.4"]},{"x":"Al impartir la vida no transmiten nada de su naturaleza personal; como presencias catalíticas vivientes, se limitan a iniciar las revoluciones esenciales de la materia.","r":["36:3.5"]},{"q":"Los Hijos de Dios pueden construir las formas de la vida, pero es el Espíritu de Dios el que realmente contribuye con la chispa vital.","r":"36:6.4"}]},{"h":"El fomento de la evolución y sus límites","items":[{"x":"Para establecer la vida en un mundo nuevo se concede alrededor de medio millón de años de tiempo planetario; cuando ese período termina, ya no se puede añadir nada nuevo.","r":["36:3.6"]},{"x":"Hasta que aparecen seres morales pueden manipular el entorno para favorecer la evolución, pero no se les permite intervenir mecánica ni arbitrariamente en el proceso evolutivo.","r":["36:3.7","65:3.2"]},{"q":"Y por tanto, la evolución —en Urantia y en otras partes— siempre entraña un propósito y no es nunca fortuito.","r":"65:0.7"},{"x":"Cuando aparecen seres con voluntad, su labor termina, y deben abandonar el planeta o prestar juramentos de renuncia para no influir más en la evolución.","r":["36:3.8","65:1.8"]},{"x":"Dos Portadores de Vida decanos y doce custodios permanecen todavía hoy en Urantia como consejeros, bajo juramento de renuncia.","r":["36:3.9"]},{"x":"Como no se puede hacer que la vida se despliegue más deprisa que el desarrollo físico del planeta, los Portadores de Vida deben esperar a la evolución geológica.","r":["58:1.2","65:8.2"]}]},{"h":"El experimento de la vida en Urantia","items":[{"x":"Urantia es un planeta decimal, un mundo de modificación de la vida, donde los Portadores de Vida intentaron modificar y mejorar los diseños de vida estándar.","r":["58:0.1","65:4.1"]},{"q":"La vida en Urantia es única, original con el planeta.","r":"58:4.1"},{"x":"Como el protoplasma de Urantia fue planeado para funcionar solo en una solución salina, la implantación esperó a que las aguas del mar fueran lo bastante saladas.","r":["58:1.3"]},{"x":"Hace quinientos cincuenta millones de años, el cuerpo de Portadores de Vida regresó e hizo tres implantaciones de vida marina en las ensenadas tropicales resguardadas del mar central, entre los continentes que se separaban.","r":["58:4.2","58:4.4"]},{"x":"La fórmula química de la cicatrización de las heridas se eligió tras más de medio millón de experimentos, lo que muestra que la vida humana fue planeada inteligentemente.","r":["65:4.3","65:4.4"]},{"x":"Urantia es el único planeta de Satania en el que la voluntad de tipo humano apareció en una raza anterior a las razas de color.","r":["65:4.11"]}]},{"h":"Vida, mente y espíritu","items":[{"x":"Los siete espíritus ayudantes de la mente acompañan siempre a los Portadores de Vida a un nuevo planeta, y su foco central se encuentra en el mundo sede central de los Portadores de Vida.","r":["36:5.4","36:2.10"]},{"q":"life springs only from life.","r":"36:6.2"},{"x":"Las formas experimentales de vida que organizan en los mundos de Salvington carecen siempre de capacidad reproductora.","r":["36:6.3"]},{"x":"Saben que la vida fluye del Padre, por medio del Hijo y por el Espíritu, pero ni siquiera ellos comprenden plenamente la naturaleza y la fuente de la chispa que activa la vida.","r":["36:6.7"]},{"x":"Cuando el universo esté establecido en luz y vida, esperan alcanzar una cuarta etapa de existencia, enteramente espiritual.","r":["65:1.9"]}]}],"see":["Evolución","Espíritu Materno del Universo Local","Espíritus ayudantes de la mente","Urantia","Los Melquisedek","Hijo Creador Micael"]},{"n":80,"t":"Razas","en":"Races","sum":"Mankind on Urantia began nearly a million years ago with Andon and Fonta, and about five hundred thousand years ago the six colored races, red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and indigo, appeared all at once in one Sangik family. The violet race of Adam and Eve was later added, forming the Andites, and no pure races remain today. The races differ in mental outlook and capacity, yet all races have the same standing before heaven and are indwelt by the same spirit.","sections":[{"h":"Andon and Fonta","items":[{"x":"Urantia was registered as an inhabited world when the twins, the first two human beings, were eleven years old.","r":["63:0.1"]},{"q":"«Ha aparecido la mente humana en el 606 de Satania, y estos padres de una raza nueva se llamarán Andón y Fonta.","r":"63:0.2"},{"x":"Mankind has a history of nearly a million years; the Andonites avoided the forests and made progress in open lands and higher latitudes.","r":["64:0.2","64:1.3"]},{"x":"Again and again in Urantia's history superior stocks have mixed with inferior stocks and deteriorated.","r":["64:1.7","64:1.8"]}]},{"h":"The Emergence of the Six Sangik Races","items":[{"x":"About five hundred thousand years ago, in the highlands of northwestern India, a Sangik family produced unusually intelligent children.","r":["64:5.1","64:5.2"]},{"q":"Entre estos diecinueve hijos figuraron cinco rojos, dos anaranjados, cuatro amarillos, dos verdes, cuatro azules y dos índigos.","r":"64:5.3"},{"x":"On an average planet the races appear one after another beginning with the red, but on Urantia the six races came from one family at the same time.","r":["64:6.1"]},{"x":"The red, yellow, and blue are primary races and the orange, green, and indigo secondary, and their intellectual and spiritual gifts overlap.","r":["51:4.3","82:6.2"]},{"x":"Differentiation into the various colored races gives mankind desirable variation that could not be obtained otherwise.","r":["51:4.4"]}]},{"h":"Histories of the Races","items":[{"x":"Driven out of Asia by the yellow man, the red man crossed to North America about eighty-five thousand years ago, where Onamonalonton for a time restored peace.","r":["64:6.4","64:6.5","64:6.7"]},{"x":"The yellow race first achieved settled agriculture and social cooperation and, under Singlangton's leadership, worshiped \"One Truth.\"","r":["64:6.14","64:6.15"]},{"x":"The orange and green races, after endless strife, were absorbed into other races and disappeared.","r":["64:6.13","64:6.20"]},{"x":"The blue man invented the spear and laid the foundations of the modern arts; the so-called white race is mainly descended from him.","r":["64:6.21","64:6.24"]},{"x":"The violet race of Adam and Eve spread out from the second garden and blended with the Nodites and Sangik races to become the Andites.","r":["78:0.1","78:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Racial Diversity and Blending","items":[{"x":"Diversity stimulates natural selection and healthy competition, and differences among races foster tolerance and altruism.","r":["64:6.31","64:6.33","64:6.34"]},{"q":"La homogeneidad de la raza humana no es deseable hasta que los pueblos de un mundo evolutivo logren niveles comparativamente altos de desarrollo espiritual.","r":"64:6.35"},{"q":"Hoy en día no hay razas puras en el mundo.","r":"82:6.1"},{"x":"The blending of superior and dissimilar stocks produces new and vigorous strains, and the dangers of race mixture have been much exaggerated.","r":["82:6.5","82:6.8"]},{"x":"Most objection to race mixture rests on social and cultural prejudice rather than on biology.","r":["82:6.7","82:6.8"]}]},{"h":"Equal Standing Before Heaven","items":[{"q":"A pesar de su atraso, estos pueblos índigos ocupan ante los poderes celestiales el mismo nivel de importancia que cualquier otra raza terrestre.","r":"64:6.27"},{"q":"Las mentes raciales pueden diferir, pero la humanidad toda está habitada por el mismo espíritu divino y eterno.","r":"155:6.8"},{"x":"Human unity and brotherhood can be achieved only through the religion of the spirit, which is personal experience, not through religions of authority.","r":["155:6.8"]},{"x":"The risen Jesus commanded that the gospel of the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man be wisely carried to all nations and races.","r":["191:4.4"]},{"x":"Pentecost wiped out all religious discrimination based on race, culture, caste, or sex.","r":["194:3.14"]}]}],"see":["Evolución","Adán y Eva","Urantia","Civilización","Hermandad de los hombres","Caligastia"]},{"n":98,"t":"Realidad","en":"Reality","sum":"In The Urantia Book reality is the totality of all existence, originating in the infinite volition of the Universal Father and differentiated and actualized on various universe levels. Reality is divided into actual and potential, absolute and subabsolute, existential and experiential, personal and impersonal, and its totality is infinity, which no finite mind can fully grasp. Man recognizes fact, meaning, and value through science, philosophy, and religion, and spirit is the basic reality of all personality experience.","sections":[{"h":"The Source of Reality","items":[{"x":"Reality originates in and by the infinite volition of the Universal Father and is differentiated and actualized on various universe levels.","r":["0:4.1"]},{"x":"Universe philosophers attribute absolute primal causation in infinity to the Universal Father functioning as the I AM.","r":["105:1.1"]},{"q":"El YO SOY es el Infinito; el YO SOY es también la infinidad.","r":"105:1.3"},{"x":"All absolute reality, the three Deities, the Isle of Paradise, and the three Absolutes, is from eternity and without beginning.","r":["105:2.1"]},{"x":"The primal differentiation of reality is into the deified and the undeified, the Deity Absolute and the Unqualified Absolute, whose tension is resolved by the Universal Absolute.","r":["0:4.5"]}]},{"h":"The Differentiation of Reality","items":[{"x":"Reality appears as undeified reality, deified reality, and the interassociated reality between the two.","r":["0:4.2","0:4.3","0:4.4"]},{"x":"From the viewpoint of time and space, reality is divided into actual and potential, absolute and subabsolute, existential and experiential, personal and impersonal.","r":["0:4.7","0:4.8","0:4.10"]},{"x":"Paradise Deity is existential, but the emerging Supreme and Ultimate are experiential.","r":["0:4.9"]},{"x":"The grand universe and the emerging master universe consist of many levels of reality beginning with the incomplete finite, and Urantia mortals are on its first level.","r":["106:0.2","106:0.3"]},{"x":"On absolute and eternal levels potential reality is as meaningful as actual reality; only to time-bound creatures do the two seem so different.","r":["118:1.10"]}]},{"h":"The Limits of the Finite Mind","items":[{"x":"Even to high intelligences infinity is only partially comprehensible, and the finality of reality only relatively so.","r":["105:0.1"]},{"q":"reality totality is infinity and therefore can never be fully comprehended by any mind that is subinfinite in concept capacity.","r":"105:0.2"},{"x":"Concepts of reality inevitably suffer serious distortion when translated to the level of mortal comprehension.","r":["105:0.3"]},{"x":"The mortal mind can hardly comprehend seven levels of relative cosmic reality, but it can grasp much of the three functioning levels of finite reality.","r":["12:8.9"]}]},{"h":"Fact, Meaning, and Value","items":[{"q":"Tan sólo hay tres elementos en la realidad universal: hecho, idea y relación.","r":"196:3.2"},{"x":"We call these three realities thing, meaning, and value, and science, philosophy, and religion respectively recognize them.","r":["196:3.2"]},{"x":"The three insights inherent in cosmic mind, causation, duty, and worship, make possible the recognition of scientific, moral, and spiritual reality.","r":["16:6.6","16:6.7","16:6.8"]},{"x":"Physical certainty lies in the logic of science, moral certainty in the wisdom of philosophy, and spiritual certainty in the truth of genuine religious experience.","r":["196:3.5"]},{"x":"In the final analysis matter vanishes from the senses and mind too disappears, but spirit insight still recognizes spiritual reality and supreme value.","r":["112:2.11"]}]},{"h":"Spirit, the Basic Reality","items":[{"q":"El espíritu es la realidad personal básica de los universos, y la personalidad es básica para toda experiencia progresiva con la realidad espiritual.","r":"12:9.1"},{"x":"Because God is spirit, changeless spirit is the basic reality of all personality experience, beyond the experiential variables of mind and matter.","r":["12:8.14"]},{"x":"It is an error to regard matter as basic reality and mind and spirit as rooted in matter.","r":["8:2.3"]},{"q":"The spirit is the creative reality","r":"42:12.14"},{"x":"The physical is the time-space reflection of spirit reality; matter is the skeleton of morontia, and both are shadows of spirit reality.","r":["42:12.14","189:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Reality and God","items":[{"x":"The soul is a new morontia reality born in experience, with the indwelling spirit as father and the material mind as mother.","r":["0:5.10"]},{"q":"La comprensión progresiva de la realidad es el equivalente de acercarse a Dios.","r":"196:3.3"},{"x":"To experience total reality is the full realization of God, the finality of the God-knowing experience.","r":["196:3.3"]},{"x":"Ascending man advances at once inward toward the experience of God and outward toward the understanding of energy.","r":["103:7.3"]}]}],"see":["Los tres Absolutos","Padre Universal","Ser Supremo","Experiencia","Ciencia y religión","Filosofía"]},{"n":76,"t":"Rebelión de Lucifer","en":"Lucifer Rebellion","sum":"The Lucifer rebellion was the revolt launched some two hundred thousand years ago by Lucifer, sovereign of the system of Satania, together with his first assistant, Satan. It began with a \"Declaration of Liberty\" that denied the reality of the Father, the sovereignty of Michael, and the ascension plan. Thirty-seven Planetary Princes joined it, and Urantia was among their worlds. The rebellion sprang from self-contemplation and pride; the universe rulers waited long so that every being could make a full choice, and Michael's bestowal virtually ended the rebellion.","sections":[{"h":"Lucifer and the Origin of the Rebellion","items":[{"x":"Lucifer was not an ascendant being but a brilliant Son created in the local universe, and he ruled Satania with its 607 inhabited worlds.","r":["53:1.1","53:1.2"]},{"q":"La autocontemplación es sumamente desastrosa, aun para las personalidades excelsas del mundo celestial.","r":"53:1.3"},{"x":"No special conditions in Satania favored rebellion; the idea of revolt originated in Lucifer's own mind.","r":["53:2.2","53:2.3"]},{"x":"In a pride that led to self-deception, he at some point became disloyal, and evil turned into deliberate sin.","r":["53:2.5"]},{"x":"On Urantia Lucifer entrusted his cause to his first assistant, Satan, and Caligastia took his side here.","r":["53:1.4","53:7.2"]}]},{"h":"The Lucifer Manifesto","items":[{"x":"Lucifer claimed that the Universal Father did not really exist and was a myth invented by the Sons to maintain their rule.","r":["53:3.2"]},{"x":"He demanded self-government for the local systems and attacked the sovereignty of Michael and the interference of the Ancients of Days as tyranny.","r":["53:3.3","53:3.4"]},{"x":"He denounced the plan of long training for ascending mortals as a waste of time and energy.","r":["53:3.6"]},{"q":"La autoaserción fue el grito de batalla de la rebelión de Lucifer.","r":"53:4.2"},{"x":"Lucifer pointed to the merciful delays of justice as proof that the government of the Sons was incompetent.","r":["53:4.5"]}]},{"h":"War in Heaven and Its Losses","items":[{"x":"Michael, not yet having completed his bestowals, chose noninterference, and Gabriel led the loyal hosts.","r":["53:5.1","53:5.4"]},{"x":"The war in heaven was not a physical conflict, but it was far more deadly because eternal life was at stake.","r":["53:5.6","53:5.7"]},{"x":"Thirty-seven Planetary Princes joined the rebellion; only on Panoptia did the people refuse to follow their prince and stand with Michael.","r":["53:7.1"]},{"x":"The angelic orders suffered the greatest losses, yet no being of Paradise origin and none of the Trinitized Sons went astray.","r":["53:7.5","53:7.6","53:7.8"]},{"q":"it is recorded to the glory of the wisdom of the ascension scheme that not a single member of the Satania ascendant citizenship resident on Jerusem participated in the Lucifer rebellion.","r":"53:7.10"}]},{"h":"True and False Liberty","items":[{"x":"The greatest confusion left by the Lucifer rebellion came from the failure to distinguish true liberty from false liberty.","r":["54:1.1"]},{"q":"La verdadera libertad es el fruto del autocontrol; la falsa libertad, la suposición de la autoafirmación.","r":"54:1.6"},{"x":"Liberty becomes self-destroying when it is divorced from justice, fairness, forbearance, moral obligation, and spiritual values.","r":["54:1.3","54:1.4"]},{"x":"Lucifer's folly lay in attempting to short-circuit time in an experiential universe.","r":["54:2.3"]}]},{"h":"The Wisdom of Delay and the End of the Rebellion","items":[{"q":"El amor de un Padre domina la justicia suprema; por lo tanto la justicia nunca destruirá lo que la misericordia pueda salvar.","r":"54:5.3"},{"x":"It was advised that an arbitrary suppression would have led at least three times as many beings astray.","r":["54:5.12"]},{"x":"Michael offered the rebels forgiveness and restoration to service if they repented, but none of the leaders accepted.","r":["53:9.1"]},{"x":"Michael's bestowal ended the rebellion throughout Satania, and Lucifer was afterward detained by the Ancients of Days.","r":["53:8.3","53:9.2"]},{"q":"faith is an effective armor against sin and iniquity.","r":"53:8.8"},{"x":"The Melchizedeks teach that the good resulting from the Satania rebellion is more than a thousand times the sum of all the evil.","r":["54:6.6"]}]}],"see":["Caligastia","Libre albedrío","Pecado","Mal","Hijo Creador Micael","Constelaciones y sistemas locales"]},{"n":49,"t":"Reino del cielo","en":"Kingdom of Heaven","sum":"The kingdom of God, or kingdom of heaven, is the central concept of the gospel Jesus proclaimed; above all it is the personal spiritual experience of the heavenly Father's will ruling in the believer's heart. It is founded on the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man, is entered now by faith, and bears fruit in loving service. In later times the kingdom concept was replaced by the institutional church, but the spiritual kingdom Jesus taught will yet be proclaimed again.","sections":[{"h":"\"The Kingdom Is Within You\"","items":[{"x":"Jesus used the kingdom of heaven and the kingdom of God with the same meaning, and made it the name for his bestowal mission.","r":["170:0.1"]},{"x":"To his apostles Jesus taught the kingdom as a personal experience lived in relation to one's fellows and to the heavenly Father.","r":["170:1.13"]},{"q":"En relación con el reino, sus últimas palabras siempre fueron: «el reino está dentro de vosotros».","r":"170:1.13"},{"x":"Jesus tried to persuade his followers to use \"the will of God\" in place of \"the kingdom,\" and to replace the idea of king and subjects with that of a heavenly family and liberated sons.","r":["170:2.11","170:2.12"]}]},{"h":"Foundations and Gifts of the Kingdom","items":[{"x":"The kingdom of heaven begins with and is centered in the truth of the fatherhood of God and the fact of the brotherhood of man.","r":["170:2.1"]},{"x":"This teaching frees man from age-old animal fears and gives him new courage and spiritual power.","r":["170:2.1","170:2.2"]},{"x":"The gospel of the kingdom gives assurance and comfort even to the poor, and teaches the superiority of the spiritual over the material.","r":["170:2.3","170:2.5"]},{"x":"When the Father's will is your law, you are barely in the kingdom; when the Father's will becomes your will, you are truly in the kingdom.","r":["141:2.2"]}]},{"h":"How One Enters","items":[{"q":"Jesús enseñó que, por la fe, el creyente entra ahora al reino.","r":"170:2.20"},{"x":"The two conditions for entering the kingdom are childlike faith and sincerity, and a hunger for righteousness.","r":["170:2.21","170:2.22"]},{"x":"Simple, childlike belief is the key that opens the door, but once inside there are steps of righteousness to climb.","r":["170:3.2"]},{"q":"Faith is the price you pay for entrance into the family of God","r":"170:3.3"},{"x":"God's forgiveness is actually experienced in so far as one forgives one's fellows, and love of neighbor is the highest ethic.","r":["170:3.4","170:3.6"]},{"q":"El perdón de Dios se hace realmente disponible y el hombre lo experimenta personalmente sólo en la medida en que él mismo perdona a sus semejantes.","r":"170:3.4"}]},{"h":"Fruits and Stages of the Kingdom","items":[{"x":"The inner religion of the kingdom increasingly shows itself in practical social service; Jesus taught religion as the cause and ethics as the result.","r":["170:3.8"]},{"q":"La religión del reino es personal e individual; los frutos, los resultados, son familiares y sociales.","r":"170:3.10"},{"x":"Jesus taught two phases of the kingdom: the kingdom in this world and the kingdom in heaven.","r":["170:2.18","170:2.19"]},{"x":"The kingdom has five phases: the inner experience of the individual, the brotherhood of believers, the superhuman brotherhood, a new social order, and the age of light and life.","r":["170:4.2","170:4.4","170:4.6"]},{"x":"The kingdom is not a social or economic order but a spiritual brotherhood of God-knowing individuals.","r":["99:3.2"]}]},{"h":"The Kingdom and the Church","items":[{"x":"For Jesus the kingdom was the sum of individuals who had confessed faith in the fatherhood of God and dedicated themselves to doing his will.","r":["170:5.11"]},{"x":"The rise of the church was itself natural, but the tragedy was that it almost wholly displaced Jesus' concept of the kingdom.","r":["170:5.7","170:5.10"]},{"x":"Church membership does not mean fellowship in the kingdom; the one is spiritual, the other chiefly social.","r":["170:5.18"]},{"x":"Some day a greater John the Baptist will appear, proclaiming a return to Jesus' concept of the kingdom as the Father's will ruling in the believer's heart.","r":["170:5.19"]},{"x":"The outward church is only the larval stage of the thwarted spiritual kingdom, and the teachings of Jesus will never remain fruitless.","r":["170:5.21"]},{"q":"Pero no dudéis, este mismo reino del cielo que el Maestro enseñó existe en el corazón del creyente, y resta ser proclamado a esta iglesia cristiana, y aun a todas las demás religiones, razas y naciones de la tierra —aun a cada ser.","r":"170:5.8"}]}],"see":["Voluntad de Dios","Filiación con Dios","Hermandad de los hombres","Fe","Enseñanzas de Jesús","Religión institucional"]},{"n":56,"t":"Religión institucional","en":"Institutional Religion","sum":"Institutional religion is the church and religious organization formed as individual religious experiences gather socially. It is natural for religious groups to arise when people share their faith, and such groups have practical value in fostering worship, education, and fellowship. But the more religion is institutionalized, the weaker its power for good and the greater the dangers of dogmatism, sectarianism, and alliance with secular power. The Urantia Book regards the church's displacement of Jesus' spiritual kingdom as a tragedy.","sections":[{"h":"Why Religion Becomes Social","items":[{"x":"Religion is the personal experience of knowing God as Father, but it leads to recognizing men as brothers, and so it has a social side.","r":["99:5.1"]},{"x":"When people share their religious beliefs, some form of religious group with common goals inevitably arises.","r":["99:5.7"]},{"x":"The purpose of the religious group is to dramatize loyalty, enlarge the attractions of truth, beauty, and goodness, and foster fellowship, the home, religious education, and group worship.","r":["99:6.2"]},{"x":"Prayer sooner or later becomes a technique for institutionalizing every religion, giving rise to secondary agencies such as priests, scriptures, and rituals.","r":["91:5.6"]},{"q":"Los objetivos, más bien que los credos, deberían unificar a los religiosos.","r":"99:5.7"}]},{"h":"Dangers of Institutionalization","items":[{"q":"El sectarismo es una enfermedad de la religión institucional, el dogmatismo es el avasallamiento de la naturaleza espiritual.","r":"99:6.1"},{"q":"Es mucho mejor tener una religión sin iglesia que una iglesia sin religión.","r":"99:6.1"},{"q":"Pero cuando la religión se vuelve institucionalizada, se limita su poder para el bien, mientras que las posibilidades del mal se multiplican grandemente.","r":"99:6.3"},{"x":"The dangers of formalized religion include fixation of beliefs, fossilization of truth, diversion from the service of God to the service of the church, and oppressive authority.","r":["99:6.3"]},{"q":"La religión formal frena a los hombres en sus actividades espirituales personales en vez de liberarlos para un servicio enaltecido de constructores del reino.","r":"99:6.4"}]},{"h":"Institutional Religion and Society","items":[{"x":"Institutionalized religion has become part of the social order that must be reconstructed, and so it cannot lead the coming social reconstruction.","r":["99:2.1","99:2.2"]},{"x":"Religionists should take part in social and political life as individuals, not as groups; a religious group acting politically becomes a party or an economic organization.","r":["99:2.3","99:3.15"]},{"x":"Early Christianity was free from all civil and economic entanglements, but later institutional Christianity became part of the structure of Western civilization.","r":["99:3.1"]},{"x":"To be free from secular alliances, religion needs a critical philosophy, political and economic independence, loving fellowship, and a scientific attitude.","r":["99:3.9","99:3.10","99:3.11","99:3.14"]},{"x":"Religious peace will not come until all religions renounce ecclesiastical authority and claims of spiritual sovereignty; God alone is spiritual sovereign.","r":["134:4.4"]},{"q":"Religionists, as a group, must never concern themselves with anything but religion","r":"99:3.15"}]},{"h":"The Religion of Authority","items":[{"x":"The religion of traditional authority offers an easy refuge to fearful souls, but at the price of spiritual and religious liberty.","r":["155:5.9","155:6.5"]},{"x":"The religions of authority divide people by demanding uniformity of belief, while the religion of the spirit requires only unity of experience.","r":["155:6.9"]},{"x":"True religion is not slavish belief in threats of punishment or in promises of mystical rewards.","r":["99:5.2"]},{"x":"Jesus did not ask people to recite formulated creeds; he asked them to gather and share a supper in remembrance of his life.","r":["99:5.10"]}]},{"h":"The Church and the Kingdom of Heaven","items":[{"x":"The rise of the church was itself natural and desirable; the trouble was that it almost wholly displaced Jesus' concept of the kingdom.","r":["170:5.7"]},{"x":"A formal, institutionalized church came to take the place of the kingdom brotherhood of spirit-led individuals.","r":["170:5.9"]},{"x":"Church membership does not mean kingdom fellowship; the one is spiritual, the other mainly social.","r":["170:5.18"]},{"x":"The present church is the larval stage of the thwarted spiritual kingdom, a cocoon carrying the kingdom through the material age.","r":["170:5.21"]},{"x":"A church that worships the living God, affirms the brotherhood of man, and removes the pressure of creeds holds great hope.","r":["103:5.12"]}]}],"see":["Religión personal","Reino del cielo","Experiencia religiosa","Hermandad de los hombres","Gobierno y sociedad","Enseñanzas de Jesús"]},{"n":55,"t":"Religión personal","en":"Personal Religion","sum":"Personal religion is the \"religion of the spirit,\" in which each person discovers and experiences God within his own soul, unlike the \"religion of the mind,\" which leans on tradition and ecclesiastical authority. It cannot be received, borrowed, or learned from others; it grows with loyalty to supreme values. Jesus proclaimed this religion of living personal experience beyond the religion of authority, and its fruits appear in love and service.","sections":[{"h":"Religion of the Mind and Religion of the Spirit","items":[{"x":"There is the primitive religion of fear, the religion of civilization based on traditional authority, and the religion of revelation validated in human experience.","r":["155:5.3","155:5.4","155:5.5"]},{"q":"Jesús aclaró que la gran diferencia entre la religión de la mente y la religión del espíritu es que, mientras la primera es sostenida por la autoridad eclesiástica, la última está completamente basada en la experiencia humana.","r":"155:5.6"},{"x":"The religion of authority offers an easy refuge to fearful and uncertain souls, but it demands only passive, intellectual assent.","r":["155:5.9"]},{"q":"La religión del espíritu significa esfuerzo, lucha, conflicto, fe, determinación, amor, lealtad, y progreso.","r":"155:5.11"},{"x":"The religion of the mind ties one to the past, but the religion of the spirit, through progressive revelation, ever beckons to higher attainment.","r":["155:6.4"]}]},{"h":"Discovering God for Oneself","items":[{"x":"The greatest discovery a human soul can make is to find God for itself within itself and to live that as personal experience.","r":["155:6.3"]},{"x":"It is good to revere the God-knowing leaders of the past, but not at the cost of sacrificing one's own experience of knowing God.","r":["155:6.7"]},{"x":"Do not seek the word of God only in ancient records; the one born of the spirit discerns the word of God wherever it comes from.","r":["155:6.12"]},{"x":"Once one begins to find God in one's soul, one soon finds him in the souls of others and in all creation.","r":["155:6.13"]},{"x":"The religion of the apostles was to be not a theological refuge from fear but a real experience testifying that God had found and exalted them.","r":["155:6.18"]}]},{"h":"A Religion That Cannot Be Given","items":[{"q":"La religión no se puede regalar, recibir, prestar, aprender ni perder.","r":"100:1.7"},{"x":"Every child should be given the opportunity to grow his own religious experience; an adult's finished experience should not be forced upon him.","r":["100:1.3"]},{"x":"Children are permanently impressed only by the loyalties of the adults with whom they live.","r":["100:1.4"]},{"q":"La forma más rápida para que un renacuajo se torne rana, consiste en vivir lealmente cada momento como renacuajo.","r":"100:1.4"},{"x":"Some people are too busy to grow; the chief obstacles to growth are prejudice and ignorance.","r":["100:1.2"]}]},{"h":"Growth of Personal Religion","items":[{"x":"Spiritual development depends on maintaining a living connection with true spiritual forces and bearing fruit by passing on to fellows what has been received.","r":["100:2.1"]},{"x":"Spirituality measures both nearness to God and usefulness to fellows, and it grows as the selfish qualities of love are eliminated.","r":["100:2.4"]},{"x":"Habits such as sensitivity to divine values, reflective meditation, and worshipful problem solving favor religious growth.","r":["100:1.8"]},{"x":"Even when floods of adversity and hatred sweep over, the God-knowing person has a citadel of the spirit that is never assailed.","r":["100:2.7"]},{"q":"La espiritualidad se vuelve de inmediato el indicador de la propia cercanía a Dios y la medida de nuestra propia utilidad para con los semejantes.","r":"100:2.4"}]},{"h":"Social Fruits of Personal Religion","items":[{"x":"The religions of authority divide people, but the religion of the spirit binds them together in unity of experience and destiny while allowing diversity of belief.","r":["155:6.9"]},{"x":"The unity and brotherhood of mankind can be achieved only through the religion of personal spiritual experience.","r":["155:6.8"]},{"x":"The evidence of knowing God is the fruit of the spirit borne in daily life and a life plan that stakes everything on the adventure of survival.","r":["155:6.14","155:6.15","155:6.16"]},{"x":"The religion of the kingdom is personal, but its fruits are familial and social; no one can keep it within himself alone.","r":["170:3.9","170:3.10"]},{"x":"The Father responds to the faintest flicker of faith, but those who are called must believe with body, mind, and spirit.","r":["155:6.17"]},{"q":"The religions of authority can only divide men and set them in conscientious array against each other","r":"155:6.9"}]}],"see":["Experiencia religiosa","Religión institucional","Fe","Reino del cielo","Ajustador del Pensamiento","Crecimiento"]},{"n":91,"t":"Resurrección de Jesús","en":"Resurrection of Jesus","sum":"Before dawn on Sunday, April 9, A.D. 30, Jesus came forth from the tomb, not in the flesh but as a morontia personality, just as ascenders awaken in the resurrection halls of the mansion worlds. His physical body remained in the tomb and was later dissolved at the request of the archangels. During forty days the risen Jesus appeared nineteen times to believers while experiencing the morontia career of ascending mortals, and his resurrection revealed the gift of life that assures every believer of rising after death.","sections":[{"h":"The Resurrection Morning","items":[{"q":"at two minutes past three o’clock, this Sunday morning, April 9, A.D. 30, the resurrected morontia form and personality of Jesus of Nazareth came forth from the tomb.","r":"189:1.1"},{"x":"Even after he came forth, his body of flesh lay wrapped in linen, and the stones of the tomb and Pilate's seals remained undisturbed.","r":["189:1.2"]},{"x":"Seven Paradise personalities surrounded the tomb, but no creature of this local universe took part in his awakening.","r":["189:1.4","189:1.5"]},{"x":"The risen Jesus told the morontia groups that he would tarry for a time to know more fully the career of ascending creatures and to further reveal the Father's will.","r":["189:1.10"]},{"x":"That same morning the morontia Michael directed Gabriel to begin the planetary roll call of the resurrection.","r":["189:3.1"]},{"x":"The sleeping survivors of Urantia since the days of Adam awoke in the resurrection halls of Mansonia; this was the third dispensational resurrection.","r":["189:3.2","189:3.3"]}]},{"h":"In What Body He Arose","items":[{"q":"Su cuerpo material o físico no fue parte de la personalidad resurgida.","r":"189:1.7"},{"x":"He came forth from the tomb neither as a spirit nor in the form of Michael the Creator as he was before incarnation.","r":["189:1.8"]},{"x":"He came forth as a morontia personality, like the ascenders who awaken in the resurrection halls of the first mansion world.","r":["189:1.9"]},{"x":"So that the human form of the Creator would not be seen slowly decaying, the archangels took charge of his body and dissolved it by a process of accelerated time.","r":["189:2.1","189:2.3"]},{"x":"Secondary midwayers rolled away the stones of the tomb, and the guards who saw it fled in terror.","r":["189:2.4"]}]},{"h":"The Morontia Appearances","items":[{"x":"Jesus appeared to believers nineteen times before his ascension.","r":["190:2.1"]},{"q":"No apareció ante sus enemigos ni tampoco ante los que no podían hacer uso espiritual de su manifestación en forma visible.","r":"190:2.1"},{"x":"At the empty tomb Mary Magdalene took Jesus for the gardener and asked where he had taken the Master.","r":["189:4.10"]},{"q":"«No me toques, María, porque no soy como me conociste en la carne.","r":"189:4.12"},{"x":"Human eyes could see his morontia form because of the special ministry of the transformers and the midwayers.","r":["189:4.11"]},{"x":"Jesus appeared alone to Peter, who was weighed down by the guilt of denying the Master, and enabled his faith to overcome his doubts.","r":["191:1.1","191:1.2"]},{"q":"Benditos son los en las edades por venir que creerán aunque no me hayan visto con los ojos de la carne, ni me hayan oído con el oído mortal».","r":"191:5.5"}]},{"h":"Apostles Slow to Believe","items":[{"x":"The apostles had taken lightly Jesus' words about his death and resurrection and believed only when faced with undeniable experience.","r":["190:1.1"]},{"x":"When the women reported, only John among the apostles was inclined vaguely to believe in the resurrection; the others thought the Jews had moved the body.","r":["190:1.2","190:1.3"]},{"x":"Jesus told the apostles that as the Father had sent him so he sent them, to reveal divine love in their daily lives.","r":["191:5.3"]}]},{"h":"The Meaning of the Resurrection","items":[{"q":"All this power which is inherent in Jesus—the endowment of life—and which enabled him to rise from the dead, is the very gift of eternal life which he bestows upon kingdom believers","r":"190:0.2"},{"x":"Mortals too will rise on the resurrection morning in morontia bodies like the one Jesus wore, bodies without circulating blood yet real.","r":["190:0.3"]},{"x":"Man is slow to realize that matter is the skeleton of morontia and that both are the reflected shadow of enduring spirit reality.","r":["189:1.3"]},{"x":"The greatest news the disciples proclaimed at Pentecost was the risen Lord, and this led Christianity to grow up around fellowship with the risen Christ.","r":["194:0.3","194:0.4"]}]},{"h":"The Ascension","items":[{"x":"The so-called ascension, when Jesus vanished on Olivet, was no different from his other disappearances from view during the forty days.","r":["193:5.3"]},{"x":"Passing through Jerusem and Edentia, he was released from the morontia state and returned to Paradise sonship and supreme sovereignty on Salvington.","r":["193:5.4"]},{"x":"It was about a quarter to eight that morning when Jesus vanished from the sight of the eleven and began his ascent to the Father to receive confirmation of his completed sovereignty over Nebadon.","r":["193:5.5"]}]}],"see":["Muerte en la cruz","Morontia","Pentecostés","Supervivencia","Mundos de estancia","Los doce apóstoles"]},{"n":75,"t":"Revelación","en":"Revelation","sum":"Revelation is the direct presentation by the real spiritual world of the truth that evolutionary religion seeks by circuitous ways, and it sorts and elevates evolutionary religion. Truth is autorevelation when it comes through the Adjuster and epochal revelation when it comes through celestial beings. Urantia has had five epochal revelations; revelation keeps in touch with evolution so as not to be too far removed from the thought of its age, and it coordinates science, religion, and philosophy as one truth.","sections":[{"h":"Evolutionary and Revealed Religion","items":[{"q":"La revelación es evolucionaria pero siempre progresista.","r":"92:4.1"},{"q":"La religión evolucionaria ilustra los intentos tortuosos de la humanidad en búsqueda de la verdad; la religión revelatoria es esa verdad misma.","r":"92:4.3"},{"x":"Revealed religion is always characterized by belief in a Deity of final values and a concept of the survival of personality after death.","r":["92:4.2"]},{"x":"To elevate evolutionary religion, revelation must present teachings not too far removed from the thought of its age.","r":["92:4.1"]},{"x":"The morality of evolutionary religion drives by fear, but revealed religion leads people to seek a God of love through the longing to be like him.","r":["5:4.1"]}]},{"h":"The Five Epochal Revelations","items":[{"x":"There have been only five revelations of epochal significance; the first was the Dalamatia teachings of the one hundred of Caligastia's staff.","r":["92:4.4","92:4.5"]},{"x":"The second was the Edenic teachings of Adam and Eve; though interrupted by the default of the Garden, the Sethite priests carried on part of them.","r":["92:4.6"]},{"x":"The third was the revelation of Machiventa Melchizedek of Salem, who taught trust and faith.","r":["92:4.7"]},{"x":"The fourth was Jesus of Nazareth, who revealed God as the Universal Father and taught love and service.","r":["92:4.8"]},{"x":"The fifth is the Urantia Papers, presented jointly by many beings.","r":["92:4.9"]},{"q":"Pero ninguna revelación es completa hasta la que se obtiene cuando se llegue al Padre Universal.","r":"92:4.9"}]},{"h":"Truth Is Always a Revelation","items":[{"q":"La verdad es siempre una revelación: autorrevelación cuando surge como resultado del trabajo del Ajustador residente; revelación de época cuando se presenta mediante la función de alguna otra agencia, grupo o personalidad celestial.","r":"101:4.3"},{"q":"El perseguimiento del conocimiento constituye la ciencia; la búsqueda de la sabiduría es la filosofía; el amor de Dios es la religión; el hambre de la verdad es una revelación.","r":"102:3.12"},{"x":"That the First Cause of science is a Father full of mercy can be known only through revelation.","r":["4:4.7","101:2.3"]},{"x":"Revelation does not originate science or religion; its function is to coordinate both with the truth of reality.","r":["103:7.8"]},{"x":"Revelation is validated only by human experience, and it confirms the harmony of the approaches of science, religion, and philosophy.","r":["101:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Methods and Limits of Revelation","items":[{"x":"The revelators give preference to the highest existing human concepts and resort to pure revelation only when there is no adequate expression.","r":["0:12.11"]},{"x":"These papers are based on more than a thousand human concepts gathered from God-knowing mortals.","r":["0:12.12"]},{"x":"The laws of revelation forbid imparting unearned or premature knowledge, so the cosmology contained in revelation soon becomes outdated.","r":["101:4.1","101:4.2"]},{"x":"Revelation is a spiritual phenomenon, but its statements on cosmology are not inspired; their value lies in reducing error and restoring lost knowledge.","r":["101:4.5","101:4.6","101:4.8"]},{"x":"Because of the isolation of rebellion, the revelation of truth was mixed with transient cosmologies, but eternal truth should not be slighted for that reason.","r":["102:1.3"]}]},{"h":"What Revelation Does","items":[{"x":"Revelation compensates for the absence of the morontia viewpoint, providing a technique of unity for understanding the relationships of matter and spirit.","r":["101:2.2"]},{"q":"La verdadera revelación no vuelve jamás artificial a la ciencia, irrazonable a la religión ni ilógica a la filosofía.","r":"101:2.2"},{"x":"Revelation compensates for the weaknesses of evolving philosophy and accomplishes what metaphysics could not.","r":["103:8.6","101:2.7"]},{"x":"Revelation liberates man for the eternal adventure and gives assurance of the survival of personality.","r":["102:3.6","102:3.9"]},{"x":"Revelation glorifies man and discloses his capacity to be a partner with God.","r":["102:3.7"]}]}],"see":["Verdad","Ciencia y religión","Filosofía","Maquiventa Melquisedek","Adán y Eva","Autootorgamiento de Jesús"]},{"n":64,"t":"Sabiduría","en":"Wisdom","sum":"Wisdom goes beyond knowledge to embrace facts and ideals, the relationships and meanings of things. God's wisdom exists perfectly in his infinite insight, but human wisdom evolves through experience, through trial and error, and especially through adjustment to failure. The adjutant spirit of wisdom lays its foundation, the Adjuster and the Spirit of Truth lead it toward truth, and in time thinking leads to wisdom and wisdom to worship.","sections":[{"h":"Divine Wisdom and Experiential Wisdom","items":[{"q":"Man's wisdom grows out of the trials and errors of human experience; God's wisdom consists in the unqualified perfection of his infinite universe insight","r":"4:3.4"},{"x":"Because of the discrimination of infinite wisdom, God can be both just and merciful at the same time in any situation.","r":["2:4.3","2:3.2"]},{"x":"Wisdom has a dual origin: the divine insight of perfect beings and the personal experience of evolutionary creatures.","r":["19:2.4"]},{"x":"Superuniverse administration always associates the Perfectors of Wisdom, with their divine insight, and ascendant personalities seasoned by experience.","r":["19:2.4"]},{"x":"Infinite wisdom ordains that anything be done in the best way, the right way, in the circumstances.","r":["12:7.2"]}]},{"h":"The Foundation of Wisdom in Mind","items":[{"x":"The spirit of wisdom is the highest of the adjutant mind-spirits, coordinating the work of all the others.","r":["36:5.12"]},{"q":"La sabiduría es la cima de la realización intelectual. La sabiduría es el objetivo de la existencia puramente mental y moral.","r":"36:5.12"},{"x":"Animals may possess knowledge, but only man has the potential of wisdom that weaves ideas from memory.","r":["101:6.4"]},{"x":"Wisdom is consciousness in which knowledge is elevated to new levels of meaning and activated by the adjutant of wisdom.","r":["180:5.3"]},{"q":"Aunque el discernimiento divino o espiritual sea un don, la sabiduría humana debe evolucionar.","r":"101:4.2"}]},{"h":"Wisdom Distinct from Knowledge and Truth","items":[{"q":"El conocimiento tiene que ver con los hechos; la sabiduría, con las relaciones; la verdad, con los valores de la realidad.","r":"132:3.2"},{"x":"Science leads to fact-consciousness, religion to value-consciousness, and philosophy, or wisdom, to the co-ordinating consciousness that embraces both.","r":["102:3.5"]},{"x":"Science classifies men and religion loves men, but wisdom does justice to differing men.","r":["102:3.7"]},{"x":"When the viewpoints of material fact and spiritual value are harmonized, wisdom interprets universe phenomena through progressive personality experience.","r":["130:4.10"]},{"x":"Knowledge is gained by education, but the wisdom true culture requires comes only through experience; intelligence controls civilization, and wisdom directs it.","r":["81:6.13","81:6.27"]}]},{"h":"The Way to Wisdom","items":[{"q":"El éxito puede generar valor y promover confianza, pero la sabiduría sólo proviene de las experiencias del ajuste al resultado de los propios fracasos.","r":"160:4.14"},{"x":"Neither the idealist who ignores facts nor the materialist without spiritual outlook is wise, but only the one who adjusts facts to ideals.","r":["160:4.14"]},{"x":"Knowledge, culture, and wisdom are different, and wisdom always dominates knowledge and glorifies culture.","r":["160:4.16"]},{"x":"Wisdom is superknowledge; when people pool their minds, they can share each other's insight and avoid prejudice and narrowness.","r":["160:2.7"]},{"x":"Jesus told James that true wisdom embraces discretion as well as courage.","r":["181:2.15"]}]},{"h":"From Wisdom to Faith and Worship","items":[{"x":"Reason, wisdom, and faith are man's three highest attainments, and in the higher philosophy wisdom becomes allied to faith.","r":["103:9.6","103:9.10"]},{"x":"True wisdom counsels allowing faith to accomplish what knowledge and reason cannot.","r":["102:1.2"]},{"x":"The superphilosophic wisdom of the enlightened recognizes that to doubt God is to be untrue to the indwelling Adjuster.","r":["101:1.7"]},{"q":"Con el tiempo, el pensamiento lleva a la sabiduría y la sabiduría conduce a la adoración; en la eternidad, la adoración conduce a la sabiduría, y la sabiduría resulta en la finalidad del pensamiento.","r":"112:2.13"}]}],"see":["Filosofía","Verdad","Espíritus ayudantes de la mente","Mente","Ciencia y religión","Experiencia"]},{"n":8,"t":"Ser Supremo","en":"Supreme Being","sum":"El Ser Supremo es la Deidad experiencial que evoluciona en el tiempo y el espacio. Deriva su personalidad espiritual de la Trinidad del Paraíso y su poder todopoderoso de los tres primeros niveles de Dios el Séptuple, y ambos se están unificando en la Mente Suprema. Como superalma del gran universo y suma de la realidad finita, registra la experiencia de toda criatura y de todo creador, y se actualiza un paso más cada vez que el hombre hace la voluntad de Dios.","sections":[{"h":"Deidad experiencial en evolución","items":[{"x":"El Padre, el Hijo y el Espíritu son Deidades existenciales, mientras que Dios el Supremo, Dios el Último y Dios el Absoluto son Deidades experienciales que se están actualizando en la evolución posterior a Havona de los universos.","r":["0:7.1","0:7.5"]},{"q":"WITH God the Father, sonship is the great relationship. With God the Supreme, achievement is the prerequisite to status","r":"115:0.1"},{"x":"Havona no crece, simplemente es, mientras que el crecimiento es la característica del gran universo y la señal de la Deidad experiencial.","r":["116:0.3"]},{"x":"El Ser Supremo funciona como personalidad espiritual en el universo central y como Dios el Todopoderoso, una personalidad de poder, en el gran universo.","r":["116:0.5"]},{"x":"El destino del Supremo es la perfección, pero su experiencia actual contiene elementos de crecimiento y de imperfección.","r":["116:0.4"]}]},{"h":"Orígenes: la Trinidad y Dios el Séptuple","items":[{"x":"La personalidad espiritual del Supremo procede de la Trinidad del Paraíso, y su crecimiento deriva de las dos triunidades de la actualidad y de la potencialidad.","r":["115:4.2","115:4.7"]},{"x":"El poder del Todopoderoso descansa en los éxitos de divinidad de Dios el Séptuple, y el Actor Conjunto otorga la mente de la Supremacía, que une el poder y la personalidad espiritual.","r":["115:4.7"]},{"x":"El Ser Supremo depende absolutamente de la Trinidad del Paraíso para la realidad de su naturaleza personal y espiritual.","r":["115:5.1"]},{"x":"Dios el Supremo no solo es evolucionado por los creadores y derivado de la Trinidad; es también un ser volitivo que participa él mismo en su propia actualización.","r":["117:3.7"]},{"q":"Lo que la Trinidad es para Dios el Supremo, el Ajustador es para el hombre en evolución.","r":"117:3.10"}]},{"h":"Superalma del gran universo","items":[{"q":"El Supremo es la belleza de la armonía física, la verdad del significado intelectual y la bondad del valor espiritual.","r":"117:1.1"},{"x":"En el Ser Supremo, el Creador y la criatura se unifican en una sola Deidad, cuya voluntad es algo más grande que la voluntad del creador o la de la criatura.","r":["117:1.5"]},{"x":"Él es la síntesis finita de la experiencia de los creadores que descienden para revelar a Dios y de las criaturas que ascienden en busca de Dios.","r":["117:1.2"]},{"x":"La personalidad de quien no sobrevive es absorbida en la superalma de la creación y vuelve al Supremo como una gota de agua vuelve al mar.","r":["117:4.2","117:4.4"]},{"x":"El hombre no pierde su identidad personal en la unificación con el Supremo, y los ecos de todas sus experiencias pasan a formar parte de la experiencia del Supremo.","r":["117:5.5"]},{"x":"El gran universo es un organismo viviente magníficamente sensible, impregnado de circuitos de inteligencia y canales de energía.","r":["116:7.1"]}]},{"h":"La interdependencia del hombre y el Supremo","items":[{"x":"En la medida en que hacemos la voluntad de Dios en cualquier lugar, el potencial todopoderoso del Supremo se vuelve un paso más real.","r":["117:0.1"]},{"x":"La criatura no puede evolucionar sin el Supremo, ni puede completarse la evolución del Supremo sin la evolución plena de todas las criaturas.","r":["117:4.9"]},{"x":"Esta relación entre el hombre y el Supremo es el fundamento de la moralidad cósmica, que reconoce la obligación experiencial hacia la Deidad experiencial.","r":["117:4.8"]},{"q":"Dios tanto confía, tanto ama, que otorga una porción de su naturaleza divina a las manos aun de los seres humanos para su salvaguardia y autorrealización.","r":"117:4.3"},{"x":"Mientras nosotros buscamos al Padre, el Supremo también busca, en nosotros y con nosotros, al Creador Paradisiaco de todas las cosas.","r":["117:4.6"]}]},{"h":"El camino para encontrar al Supremo","items":[{"x":"Así como Dios es el Padre divino, el Supremo es la Madre divina, en quien somos nutridos a lo largo de nuestras carreras en el universo.","r":["117:6.2"]},{"q":"Man can discover the Father in his heart, but he will have to search for the Supreme in the hearts of all other men","r":"117:6.23"},{"x":"Cada individuo puede encontrar al Padre, pero al Supremo no se le encontrará individualmente hasta un futuro lejano, cuando todas las criaturas juntas alcancen la madurez cósmica y lo encuentren.","r":["117:6.16","117:6.21"]},{"x":"El amor del Padre solo se vuelve real cuando se otorga a los semejantes, y el afecto fraternal que fluye de este modo es la esencia del amor del Supremo.","r":["117:6.10"]},{"x":"El hombre no descubre al Supremo de repente, como golpea un terremoto, sino lenta y pacientemente, como un río desgasta la tierra.","r":["117:6.25"]},{"q":"¡Comprender más que el Supremo sería ser más que finito!","r":"117:6.19"},{"x":"El mortal que conoce a Dios nunca está solo; el Padre lo acompaña durante todo el camino, y el sendero mismo que recorre es la presencia del Supremo.","r":["117:6.27"]}]},{"h":"El futuro del Supremo","items":[{"x":"Cuando el gran universo esté establecido en luz y vida, la personalidad espiritual y el poder todopoderoso se unificarán en la Mente Suprema, y el Ser Supremo se factualizará como actualidad completa.","r":["117:0.2","117:7.14"]},{"x":"Se cree que el Supremo llegará entonces a ser el soberano real del gran universo y que las distinciones entre los siete superuniversos desaparecerán gradualmente.","r":["117:7.15"]},{"x":"Los ciudadanos del universo perfeccionado afrontarán entonces un nuevo desafío: la búsqueda de Dios el Último.","r":["117:7.17"]}]}],"see":["Dios el Séptuple","Trinidad del Paraíso","Dios el Último","Voluntad de Dios","Luz y vida","Evolución"]},{"n":27,"t":"Serafines","en":"Seraphim","sum":"Los serafines son ángeles creados por el Espíritu Materno del universo local, y junto con los querubines y los sanobines forman el cuerpo de espíritus ministrantes del universo local. Aunque carecen de cuerpo material, son seres espirituales con personalidad individual que comprenden y aman a los seres humanos. Divididos en siete órdenes, desde los serafines supremos hasta los serafines del futuro, ayudan en casi todas las tareas del universo local: la administración, la educación, el transporte, los registros y la supervisión planetaria. Ellos mismos son seres ascendentes, destinados a llegar al Paraíso pasando por Serafington.","sections":[{"h":"Origen y naturaleza","items":[{"x":"Los serafines son creados por proyección del Espíritu Materno del Universo, 41.472 cada vez, y como Nebadon todavía está en formación, se siguen creando periódicamente.","r":["38:1.1","38:1.3"]},{"x":"Así como los supernafines sirven al universo central y los seconafines a los superuniversos, en el universo local los serafines, junto con los querubines y los sanobines, forman las huestes angélicas.","r":["38:0.2"]},{"q":"Los ángeles no tienen cuerpos materiales, pero son seres definidos y discretos; son de naturaleza y origen espirituales.","r":"38:2.1"},{"x":"Son plenamente conscientes de las luchas morales y de las dificultades espirituales de los humanos, disfrutan de la música, del arte y del verdadero humor, y aman a los seres humanos.","r":["38:2.1"]},{"x":"Aunque no son criaturas sexuadas, son profundamente afectuosos; viven en parejas de seres negativos y positivos y llevan a cabo la mayoría de sus misiones de dos en dos.","r":["38:2.2","38:4.3"]},{"q":"Si los ángeles no emiten un juicio sobre la humanidad, tampoco deberían los mortales prejuzgar a sus congéneres.","r":"38:2.4"},{"x":"Está bien amar a los ángeles, pero no se les debe adorar; son consiervos del hombre en la adoración de Dios.","r":["38:2.5"]}]},{"h":"Formación y organización","items":[{"x":"Pasan su primer milenio como observadores en las escuelas de Salvington y el segundo en los mundos seráficos; luego pasan por la constelación y el sistema antes de ser comisionados como espíritus ministrantes del tiempo.","r":["38:5.1","38:5.3"]},{"q":"Their work in the universe is without bounds and limitations","r":"38:5.4"},{"x":"A partir de grupos de doce parejas se organizan en compañías, batallones, unidades, legiones, huestes y ejércitos angélicos, cada uno doce veces mayor, y los ejércitos están al mando de Brillantes Estrellas Vespertinas y otros.","r":["38:6.1","38:6.2"]},{"x":"Las «más de doce legiones de ángeles» de las que habló Jesús en Getsemaní se refieren precisamente a estas legiones de serafines.","r":["38:6.1"]},{"x":"Desde el autootorgamiento de Micael en Urantia, los serafines y todas las órdenes del universo local han quedado bajo la soberanía del Hijo Mayor.","r":["38:6.3"]},{"x":"Los querubines y los sanobines, del mismo origen que los serafines, son la orden más baja de ángeles; trabajan en parejas y son los fieles ayudantes de los serafines.","r":["38:7.1","38:7.3"]}]},{"h":"Las siete órdenes y su labor","items":[{"x":"Los serafines revelados se dividen en siete órdenes: supremos, superiores, supervisores, administradores, ayudantes planetarios, ministros de transición y serafines del futuro.","r":["39:0.1","39:0.2","39:0.8"]},{"q":"La misericordia es la clave del servicio seráfico y del ministerio angélico.","r":"39:2.5"},{"x":"Los serafines de transporte enserafinan a los ascendentes y los llevan de un mundo a otro; el ser así envuelto duerme durante un tiempo determinado y despierta en su destino.","r":["39:2.10","39:2.12"]},{"x":"Los arquitectos sociales, entre los serafines supervisores, fomentan los contactos sociales auténticos y ayudan a formar grupos de trabajo eficientes y armoniosos.","r":["39:3.4","39:3.5"]},{"x":"Los consejeros morales, entre los serafines administradores, enseñan la interacción entre la libertad y la lealtad y presentan la vida mortal como el primer eslabón de una larga cadena ininterrumpida.","r":["39:4.10","39:4.13"]},{"q":"The keys of the kingdom of heaven are: sincerity, more sincerity, and more sincerity.","r":"39:4.14"},{"x":"Los ministros de transición fomentan el progreso morontial de los supervivientes en los mundos de estancia y se cuentan entre los serafines que más se acercan a los seres humanos.","r":["48:6.1","48:6.34"]}]},{"h":"El ministerio angélico en el planeta","items":[{"x":"Incluso después del fracaso del régimen adánico, los espíritus de la fraternidad, las almas de paz y los espíritus de la confianza, entre los ayudantes planetarios, continúan su labor en Urantia.","r":["39:5.4","39:5.5","39:5.8"]},{"x":"La idea de que los ángeles tienen alas procede en gran parte de tradiciones basadas en antiguas observaciones de serafines que se preparaban para el transporte.","r":["39:5.12"]},{"x":"Con el derramamiento del Espíritu de la Verdad llegaron las doce legiones de decanos serafines de supervisión planetaria, que se ocupan de las épocas, el progreso, la religión, las naciones, las razas, la educación, la salud, el hogar, la industria, el esparcimiento y más.","r":["114:6.1","114:6.4"]},{"x":"Mientras que los ángeles del progreso promueven nuevos avances, los guardianes religiosos transmiten a la generación siguiente los valores inmortales contenidos en formas más antiguas, y así se equilibran mutuamente.","r":["114:6.6","114:6.7"]},{"q":"Ninguno de estos grupos angélicos ejerce un control directo o arbitrario sobre los dominios de sus asignaciones.","r":"114:6.18"}]},{"h":"El destino de los serafines","items":[{"x":"Los serafines pueden llegar al Paraíso por varios caminos, entre ellos el logro perfecto de un servicio especializado, la convocatoria a Serafington y la guarda de mortales evolutivos.","r":["39:8.2","39:8.3","39:8.4"]},{"x":"Los ángeles no están seguros de su futuro eterno hasta que llegan a Serafington, y no se sabe de ningún ángel que, habiendo alcanzado Serafington, se haya extraviado jamás.","r":["39:8.9"]},{"x":"También los querubines y los sanobines pueden renacer como serafines plenos después de un largo servicio y de repetidos abrazos del Espíritu Materno del Universo.","r":["38:8.6"]},{"x":"Muchos caminos se abren ante los serafines de consumación, pero lo que más desean es servir como acompañantes de autootorgamiento de los Hijos del Paraíso encarnados.","r":["39:9.3"]},{"q":"A lo largo de la entera ascensión morontial y espiritual subsiguiente, vuestra fraternidad con los serafines será ideal; vuestro compañerismo será soberbio.","r":"38:2.6"}]}],"see":["Huestes angélicas","Serafines guardianes","Espíritu Materno del Universo Local","Seres intermedios","Mundos de estancia","Morontia"]},{"n":28,"t":"Serafines guardianes","en":"Guardian Seraphim","sum":"Los serafines guardianes son los serafines que velan por los mortales individuales. Cuando una persona alcanza el tercer círculo, toma la decisión suprema de llegar a ser semejante a Dios o entra en el cuerpo de reserva del destino, se le asigna un guardián personal, un guardián del destino. Actúan a través de las circunstancias exteriores sin invadir la voluntad humana; después de la muerte custodian los valores de supervivencia del alma, ayudan en la repersonalización en los mundos de estancia y acompañan al ascendente en la carrera ascendente. Para los serafines, esta asignación es el camino más seguro hacia el Paraíso.","sections":[{"h":"Cómo se asignan los ángeles guardianes","items":[{"q":"The teaching about guardian angels is not a myth","r":"113:1.1"},{"x":"Desde el autootorgamiento de Micael, los serafines se asignan no según la raza, sino según el intelecto, la espiritualidad y el destino de los seres humanos.","r":["113:1.2"]},{"x":"Las personas corrientes están al cuidado de serafines guardianes según el círculo alcanzado: en grupos de mil en el séptimo círculo, de quinientas en el sexto, de cien en el quinto y de diez en el cuarto.","r":["113:1.6","113:1.7"]},{"x":"Al alcanzar el tercer círculo, un ángel personal (en realidad, dos) se dedica por completo a ese mortal.","r":["113:1.8"]},{"x":"Cuando una persona es inscrita en el cuerpo de reserva del destino o toma la decisión suprema, un verdadero compromiso con el Ajustador, se le asigna de inmediato un guardián personal, cualquiera que sea su círculo.","r":["113:1.5"]},{"x":"Para los reservistas elegidos como guardianes del destino planetario, el jefe de los serafines planetarios designa guardianes personales del destino.","r":["114:7.2"]}]},{"h":"Los guardianes del destino","items":[{"x":"A los serafines no se les llama guardianes del destino hasta que el ser humano ha tomado la decisión suprema, ha entrado en el tercer círculo o ha sido incorporado al cuerpo de reserva del destino.","r":["113:2.1"]},{"x":"El primer mortal de Urantia que recibió un guardián personal fue Rantowoc, un sabio de la raza roja, hace mucho tiempo.","r":["113:2.2"]},{"x":"Las asignaciones se hacen siempre entre voluntarios de serafines experimentados y probados, y más de cien serafines han solicitado la guarda de una sola persona.","r":["113:2.3","113:2.7"]},{"x":"Uno de la pareja está siempre de servicio, mientras que su complemento actúa como ángel registrador de la persona, y los registros los llevan los querubines y sanobines asociados.","r":["113:2.7","113:2.9"]},{"x":"Los serafines anhelan por igual acompañar a un Hijo encarnado y ser asignados como guardianes del destino, y esto último es el pasaporte más seguro hacia el Paraíso.","r":["39:1.6"]},{"x":"Los ángeles sienten un afecto duradero por sus asociados humanos, pero les cuesta comprender los temores animales que dominan incluso la fe humana.","r":["113:2.5"]}]},{"h":"Ayudar desde fuera, no desde dentro","items":[{"x":"El guardián coordina personalmente las múltiples influencias impersonales del Espíritu Infinito y las correlaciona con la presencia espiritual del Padre y del Hijo.","r":["113:3.1","113:3.2"]},{"q":"Los servidores angélicos tienen el don de combinar el amor del Padre y la misericordia del Hijo en su ministerio a las criaturas mortales.","r":"113:3.3"},{"x":"Mientras que el Ajustador actúa desde dentro, a través del alma, los serafines actúan desde fuera hacia dentro, a través del entorno social, ético y moral de los seres humanos.","r":["113:4.1"]},{"q":"The Adjuster is the essence of man's eternal nature; the seraphim is the teacher of man's evolving nature","r":"113:4.2"},{"x":"Aceptar la guía seráfica no hace fácil la vida; al contrario, uno se encuentra con las escarpadas colinas de la elección moral y del progreso espiritual.","r":["113:4.3"]},{"x":"El impulso de orar de las personas conscientes de Dios surge a menudo de la influencia seráfica, y el guardián es más activo cuando el Ajustador lo es menos.","r":["113:4.4","113:4.5"]}]},{"h":"Un ministerio que respeta la voluntad humana","items":[{"q":"Los ángeles no invaden la santidad de la mente humana; no manipulan la voluntad de los mortales; tampoco se ponen en contacto directo con los Ajustadores residentes.","r":"113:5.1"},{"x":"Los serafines no tienen lágrimas físicas, ni cuerpo, ni alas, pero experimentan emociones espirituales algo semejantes a los sentimientos humanos.","r":["113:5.2"]},{"x":"No responden directamente a las oraciones, sino que actúan por orden de sus superiores, y por eso funcionan independientemente de los caprichos y estados de ánimo humanos.","r":["113:5.3"]},{"q":"No son dueños ni directores; son simplemente guardianes.","r":"113:5.4"},{"x":"Cuando una persona traza su propio rumbo, los ángeles ayudan a sacar de él el mejor provecho posible, e intervienen solo en las emergencias, y entonces por lo general por orden de sus superiores.","r":["113:5.4"]}]},{"h":"Después de la muerte y en la carrera ascendente","items":[{"x":"A la muerte, el guardián conserva los registros de la persona, las especificaciones de su identidad y la realidad morontial del alma, y aguarda el despertar de su pupilo en el primer mundo de estancia.","r":["113:6.1","113:6.2"]},{"q":"El Ajustador te identificará; el serafín guardián te repersonalizará y luego te volverá a presentar al Monitor fiel de tus días terrestres.","r":"113:6.6"},{"x":"Los de los círculos inferiores que no tuvieron guardián personal son reunidos por los guardianes de grupo en las salas de resurrección de las esferas de estancia al final de una dispensación.","r":["113:6.7"]},{"x":"Todo mortal adquiere un guardián permanente antes de dejar los mundos de estancia, y ese guardián permanece hasta que el ascendente es enseconafinado para la partida hacia Havona.","r":["113:7.4"]},{"q":"Para los serafines, la manera más segura de llegar a las Deidades del Paraíso es mediante la guía conseguida de un alma de origen evolucionario hasta las compuertas del Paraíso.","r":"113:7.7"},{"x":"Solo las parejas de guardianes del destino alcanzan la unidad espiritual y entran en el Cuerpo de la Finalidad primario, o mortal, convirtiéndose en compañeros eternos de los seres humanos.","r":["113:7.8"]}]}],"see":["Serafines","Huestes angélicas","Ajustador del Pensamiento","Mundos de estancia","Muerte","Supervivencia"]},{"n":29,"t":"Seres intermedios","en":"Midwayers","sum":"Los seres intermedios, o criaturas intermedias, son seres nativos del planeta que existen en un nivel situado a medio camino entre los mortales y los ángeles. En Urantia, los intermedios primarios procedieron del séquito corpóreo del Príncipe Caligastia, y los intermedios secundarios de los hijos únicos de Adansón y Ratta. Muchos se extraviaron en la rebelión, pero los leales, como Seres Intermedios Unidos, ayudan a los serafines y guardan la memoria del planeta; cuando llegue la era de luz y vida, emprenderán la carrera al Paraíso como hijos ascendentes de Dios.","sections":[{"h":"Seres entre el hombre y el ángel","items":[{"x":"Se les llama criaturas intermedias porque funcionan en un nivel de vida situado entre los mortales y las órdenes angélicas, y aparecen en la mayoría de los planetas habitados y en todos los planetas decimales.","r":["77:0.1","38:9.2"]},{"x":"No son un accidente de la evolución, sino parte esencial de un plan preordenado por los arquitectos del universo y diseñado por los Portadores de Vida.","r":["38:9.5"]},{"x":"Tienen una triple clasificación: por su origen son hijos ascendentes, de hecho son ciudadanos virtualmente permanentes y por su función se cuentan entre los espíritus ministrantes del tiempo.","r":["38:9.1"]},{"q":"Midwayers are not men, neither are they angels, but secondary midwayers are, in nature, nearer man than angel","r":"77:8.4"},{"q":"La laguna entre los mundos material y espiritual está perfectamente salvada por la asociación seriada del hombre mortal, el ser intermedio secundario, el ser intermedio primario, el querubín morontial, el querubín de fase media y el serafín.","r":"38:9.9"}]},{"h":"El origen de los intermedios primarios","items":[{"q":"It was immediately discovered that a creature of this order, midway between the mortal and angelic levels, would be of great service in carrying on the affairs of the Prince's headquarters,","r":"77:1.3"},{"x":"Se concedió permiso a las parejas del séquito corpóreo del Príncipe Caligastia, y nacieron los cincuenta primeros, a los que siguió con el tiempo el cuerpo original de cincuenta mil.","r":["77:1.3","77:1.4"]},{"x":"Como cuerpo de información de la administración del Príncipe, estudiaron las razas del mundo y ayudaron a influir en las sociedades humanas alejadas de la sede central.","r":["77:1.6"]},{"x":"En la rebelión planetaria, 40.119 de los cincuenta mil originales se unieron a la secesión de Caligastia.","r":["77:7.1"]},{"x":"Los intermedios primarios leales entraron al servicio de los síndicos Melquisedek, y su jefe, el primer 1-2-3, se mantuvo firme junto a Van y Amadón el día de la rebelión.","r":["77:1.7","77:9.5"]}]},{"h":"El origen de los intermedios secundarios","items":[{"x":"Los intermedios secundarios procedieron de los hijos de Adansón, hijo mayor de Adán y Eva, y de Ratta, la última descendiente de línea pura del séquito del Príncipe.","r":["77:5.1","77:5.5"]},{"x":"Dieciséis hijos únicos de Adansón, que formaban ocho parejas, produjeron cada una un intermedio secundario cada setenta días, hasta que llegaron a ser 1.984 en total.","r":["77:6.2","77:6.4"]},{"q":"Jamás había sido posible en la tierra este fenómeno antes de esa época, tampoco ha vuelto a producirse nunca.","r":"77:6.2"},{"x":"Tras la muerte de Adansón, los intermedios secundarios quedaron a la deriva sin organización, y 873 de ellos, que no quisieron seguir el gobierno de Micael, fueron internados con la adjudicación de Pentecostés.","r":["77:6.6","77:7.2"]},{"x":"Antes de Pentecostés, los intermedios rebeldes podían influir en la mente de mortales inferiores, pero desde el derramamiento del Espíritu de la Verdad ningún espíritu desleal puede invadir la mente humana.","r":["77:7.5","77:7.8"]}]},{"h":"El servicio de los Seres Intermedios Unidos","items":[{"x":"Actualmente las dos órdenes de Urantia funcionan como un solo grupo de 10.992, gobernado alternativamente por el miembro más antiguo de cada orden.","r":["77:8.1"]},{"x":"Son seres no materiales que no duermen ni se reproducen, pero pueden disfrutar del humor humano y seguir la adoración humana.","r":["77:8.3"]},{"x":"Organizados como mensajeros intermedios, centinelas planetarios, personalidades de enlace y ayudantes del progreso, sirven junto con los serafines planetarios.","r":["77:8.5","77:8.7","77:8.8"]},{"x":"Los intermedios secundarios pueden establecer contacto físico con las cosas materiales, y muchos de los fenómenos literales atribuidos a los ángeles fueron obra suya.","r":["77:8.11","77:8.12"]},{"x":"Hoy su tarea principal es ser los asociados no reconocidos de los hombres y mujeres que forman el cuerpo de reserva del destino.","r":["77:8.13"]},{"q":"El lema de su orden evoca su resolución: «Lo que emprendan los Seres Intermedios Unidos, lo realizan los Seres Intermedios Unidos».","r":"77:9.3"}]},{"h":"Ciudadanos permanentes del planeta y su destino","items":[{"q":"The seraphim come and go, but the midway creatures remain","r":"77:9.2"},{"x":"Se han comprometido a no abandonar el planeta hasta que las autoridades del universo los liberen, y permanecen en él hasta la era de luz y vida.","r":["77:9.4"]},{"q":"Las generaciones de hombres olvidan; el cuerpo de seres intermedios recuerda, y esa memoria es la mina de oro de las tradiciones de vuestro mundo habitado.","r":"77:9.9"},{"x":"La civilización de Urantia es el producto conjunto de los mortales y los intermedios, y la distancia entre los dos niveles culturales no se salvará antes de la era de luz y vida.","r":["77:9.8"]},{"x":"Cuando el planeta alcance la luz y la vida, ambos grupos serán liberados del servicio planetario, inscritos como hijos ascendentes de Dios, y comenzarán la ascensión al Paraíso con sus hermanos terrenales.","r":["40:3.1","38:9.13"]},{"x":"Todos los intermedios secundarios se fusionan finalmente con Ajustadores y son incorporados al Cuerpo de la Finalidad mortal.","r":["31:6.2"]}]}],"see":["Caligastia","Adán y Eva","Rebelión de Lucifer","Serafines","Urantia","Luz y vida"]},{"n":63,"t":"Servicio","en":"Service","sum":"Service is one way in which divinity is revealed on the personal level: the Son serves mankind, and the Infinite Spirit and his children possess by nature the urge to minister. For man, service is the social fruit of true religion, the inner experience of loving God flowing out as loving service to one's fellows. Jesus showed by washing feet that the one who serves is great, and the path of ascension leads on into endless universe service.","sections":[{"h":"The Source of Divine Service","items":[{"x":"On personality levels creatures can comprehend divinity as love, mercy, and ministry.","r":["0:1.17"]},{"q":"Dios el Padre ama a los hombres; Dios el Hijo sirve a los hombres;","r":"3:6.8"},{"x":"Ministry to mind is the essence of the Infinite Spirit, and all his spirit offspring share the divine urge to serve.","r":["8:4.1","8:4.2"]},{"x":"The family of the Infinite Spirit is forever devoted to ministering the love of God and the mercy of the Son, becoming a living ladder by which mortals ascend.","r":["9:8.25"]},{"x":"The attributes of mercy and service displayed by the descending Sons derive from the Eternal Son.","r":["7:6.2"]}]},{"h":"The Fruit of True Religion","items":[{"q":"La religión no es una técnica para llegar a una paz mental estática y dichosa; es un impulso hacia la organización del alma para el servicio dinámico.","r":"100:3.1"},{"x":"One who has found God seeks out and serves less enlightened fellows, not to boast but out of overflowing goodness.","r":["102:3.4"]},{"q":"La marca intelectual de la religión es la certeza; la característica filosófica es la uniformidad; los frutos sociales son el amor y el servicio.","r":"102:7.5"},{"x":"Jesus taught religion as the cause and ethics and service as the effect; inner religion shows itself in practical social service.","r":["170:3.8","170:3.9"]},{"x":"Religion becoming a personal experience is not dangerous so long as it does not lose the motive of unselfish social service.","r":["99:4.7"]},{"x":"Contact with the Adjuster is fostered by meditation, but it occurs more often in loving service to one's fellows.","r":["91:7.1"]}]},{"h":"The Way of Service Jesus Showed","items":[{"x":"At the Last Supper, before apostles quarreling over places, Jesus knelt like a servant and washed the feet of all twelve, even Judas.","r":["179:3.1","179:3.7"]},{"q":"El que quiere ser grande entre vosotros, que sea como el más joven; y el que quiere ser jefe, que sea como el que sirve.","r":"179:3.9"},{"x":"The lesson of the foot washing was that the secret of greatness in the spiritual kingdom differs from the methods of power in the material world.","r":["179:3.8"]},{"q":"Mi reino está fundado en el amor, proclamado en la misericordia y establecido mediante el servicio generoso.","r":"155:1.2"},{"x":"Jesus asked not for sacrifice but for loyalty; service rendered by a friend for a friend cannot be called sacrifice.","r":["180:1.6"]},{"x":"Even a small loving service, like a cup of cold water given to a thirsty soul, is always recorded by the Father's messengers.","r":["159:2.1"]}]},{"h":"Service in Society and Civilization","items":[{"q":"En la economía, la motivación de lucro es para la motivación de servicio lo que el temor es para el amor en la religión.","r":"71:6.2"},{"x":"The profit motive should not be abolished suddenly but gradually transformed into unselfish motives.","r":["71:6.2"]},{"x":"Apart from parental instinct, altruism does not arise spontaneously, so an unselfish social order requires the impulses of reason, morality, and religion.","r":["16:9.7"]},{"x":"True parents engage in continuous service-ministry that their children, as they grow, will come to recognize and appreciate.","r":["84:7.26"]},{"x":"The social service and intellectual fellowship of believers are precious, but as by-products of inner transformation they cannot replace the proclamation of the gospel.","r":["178:1.11"]}]},{"h":"Service That Continues into Eternity","items":[{"x":"On the fourth mansion world ascenders first experience a social order based on the love of mutual service rather than selfish conquest.","r":["47:6.3"]},{"x":"What the Father and the Sons bestow on us we bestow in turn on our fellows and the Supreme; the experience of love, joy, and service is mutual.","r":["56:8.3"]},{"x":"Entry into the Mortal Corps of the Finality is the beginning of eternal service to the Paradise Trinity.","r":["27:7.8","27:7.10"]},{"x":"In the present universe age the finaliters return to the universes of time and serve in one superuniverse after another.","r":["31:0.10"]}]}],"see":["Amor","Hermandad de los hombres","Experiencia religiosa","Cuerpo de la Finalidad","Enseñanzas de Jesús","Espíritu Infinito"]},{"n":20,"t":"Siete Espíritus Rectores","en":"Seven Master Spirits","sum":"Los Siete Espíritus Rectores son las personalidades primarias del Espíritu Infinito, y cada uno expresa una de las siete asociaciones posibles de las tres Deidades: el Padre, el Hijo y el Espíritu. Desde la periferia del Paraíso, cada uno supervisa uno de los siete superuniversos, y son la fuente séptuple de la mente cósmica y los antepasados de los directores del poder. Las criaturas de cada superuniverso llevan para siempre el carácter distintivo de su Espíritu Rector, y el Espíritu Rector Número Siete, que supervisa Orvonton, representa al Ser Supremo.","sections":[{"h":"Siete asociaciones posibles","items":[{"x":"Los Siete Espíritus Rectores son las personalidades primarias del Espíritu Infinito, y como solo hay siete asociaciones posibles inherentes a las tres Deidades, el universo se administra en siete grandes divisiones.","r":["16:0.1"]},{"x":"Cada uno deriva su carácter de una de siete semejanzas: el Padre, el Hijo, el Espíritu, el Padre y el Hijo, el Padre y el Espíritu, el Hijo y el Espíritu, y el Padre, el Hijo y el Espíritu.","r":["16:0.2","16:0.9"]},{"q":"Nos referimos a la personalización triple de la Deidad como la inevitabilidad absoluta, mientras que nos referimos a la aparición de los Siete Espíritus Rectores como una inevitabilidad subabsoluta.","r":"16:1.1"},{"x":"Personalizados por el primer acto creador de Deidad del Espíritu Infinito, son los distribuidores del Espíritu Infinito a los universos.","r":["9:8.2"]},{"x":"En carácter y naturaleza espirituales los Siete Espíritus son como uno solo, pero en todos los demás aspectos de su identidad son claramente distintos.","r":["16:0.11"]},{"q":"Los Espíritus Rectores tienen muchas funciones, pero en este momento su ámbito específico es la supervisión central de los siete superuniversos.","r":"16:0.12"}]},{"h":"La voz del Espíritu Infinito","items":[{"q":"Fuera del Paraíso y de Havona el Espíritu Infinito habla sólo mediante las voces de los Siete Espíritus Rectores.","r":"16:2.2"},{"x":"La presencia superuniversal del Espíritu Infinito en cualquier mundo está condicionada por la naturaleza distintiva del Espíritu Rector que supervisa ese segmento.","r":["16:2.3"]},{"x":"Los atributos de omnipotencia, omnisciencia y omnipresencia solo aparecen cuando actúan juntos; individualmente, cada uno está limitado al superuniverso que supervisa.","r":["16:2.4"]},{"x":"Cuando los Siete Espíritus Rectores se reúnen alrededor del Actor Conjunto, representan colectivamente el poder, la sabiduría y la autoridad funcionales de la Trinidad en los universos evolutivos.","r":["16:1.3"]},{"x":"Son el tercer nivel de Dios el Séptuple; los ascendentes, pasando por los Ancianos de los Días, descubren la personalidad de un Espíritu Rector antes de seguir hacia el Padre.","r":["0:8.4","0:8.9"]}]},{"h":"El carácter distintivo de los Siete","items":[{"x":"El Espíritu Rector Número Uno expresa directamente al Padre, está estrechamente asociado con el jefe de los Ajustadores y en el consejo habla siempre en nombre del Padre.","r":["16:3.2"]},{"x":"El Número Dos representa al Hijo Eterno, el Número Tres al Espíritu Infinito y el Número Cuatro la naturaleza combinada del Padre y del Hijo.","r":["16:3.4","16:3.6","16:3.8"]},{"x":"El Número Cinco representa al Padre y al Espíritu y es el consejero de los directores del poder y de los controladores físicos, mientras que el Número Seis representa al Hijo y al Espíritu.","r":["16:3.10","16:3.12"]},{"x":"El Espíritu Rector Número Siete, que preside Orvonton, representa por igual al Padre, al Hijo y al Espíritu, y tiene una relación personal y orgánica con la persona espiritual del Ser Supremo.","r":["16:3.14","16:3.15"]},{"q":"Durante la actual era universal de imposibilidad de contacto con la persona del Supremo, el Espíritu Rector Número Siete actúa en el lugar del Dios de las criaturas ascendentes en lo que concierne las relaciones personales.","r":"16:3.19"}]},{"h":"La supervisión superuniversal y la mente cósmica","items":[{"x":"Cada Espíritu Rector tiene su sede central en la periferia del Paraíso, frente al superuniverso que supervisa, y allí convergen las líneas radiales de los límites de ese superuniverso.","r":["16:0.12"]},{"x":"Los Espíritus Rectores se comunican con los gobiernos superuniversales por medio de los Siete Ejecutivos Supremos y mantienen una comunicación constante con los Espíritus Reflectivos de cada capital superuniversal.","r":["17:1.2","16:3.20"]},{"q":"Es literalmente verdad que estos Siete Espíritus son el poder físico personalizado, la mente cósmica, y la presencia espiritual de la Deidad triuna, «los Siete Espíritus de Dios enviados a todo el universo».","r":"16:4.1"},{"x":"Son la fuente séptuple de la mente cósmica y los antepasados de los directores del poder del universo, y también ayudan materialmente a los Hijos Creadores que organizan los universos locales.","r":["16:4.2","16:4.3","16:6.1"]},{"x":"La sustancia morontial y la mente morontial, que combinan materia y espíritu, parecen estar relacionadas con actividades no reveladas de los Espíritus Rectores.","r":["16:4.5"]},{"x":"Sin embargo, no tienen nada que ver con el otorgamiento y el ministerio de los Ajustadores ni con la función del Absoluto No Cualificado.","r":["16:4.16"]},{"x":"En la era actual el potencial mental del Supremo está confiado a los Siete Espíritus Rectores, y el Séptimo Espíritu Rector en particular conoce al Supremo y está en contacto personal con él.","r":["116:1.3","116:4.2"]}]},{"h":"Un carácter impreso en las criaturas","items":[{"x":"Cada mundo goza de la sabiduría combinada de los siete Espíritus Rectores, pero recibe su toque y su colorido personales de uno solo.","r":["16:5.1"]},{"x":"Un Espíritu Rector no entra directamente en la mente material de los mortales; su influencia llega por medio del ministerio del Espíritu Creativo del universo local, que se le asemeja mucho.","r":["16:5.3"]},{"q":"A lo largo de toda la eternidad, un mortal ascendente mostrará rasgos que indican el Espíritu que dirige el superuniverso de natalidad.","r":"16:5.5"},{"x":"Por eso, incluso el Cuerpo de la Finalidad, cuando representa una relación completa con la creación evolutiva, reúne un grupo de siete finalistas, uno de cada superuniverso.","r":["16:5.5"]},{"x":"En el séptimo circuito de Havona el ascendente debe captar la identidad del Espíritu Rector de su superuniverso antes de avanzar al sexto circuito.","r":["14:5.4"]},{"x":"Hay siete grandes avenidas hacia el Padre Universal, y cada ascensión se realiza a través de la divinidad de uno de los Siete Espíritus Rectores.","r":["117:6.15"]}]}],"see":["Espíritu Infinito","Mente cósmica","Los siete superuniversos","Dios el Séptuple","Ser Supremo","Ancianos de los Días"]},{"n":14,"t":"Los siete superuniversos","en":"The Seven Superuniverses","sum":"Los siete superuniversos son las creaciones que evolucionan en el tiempo y el espacio, formadas al dividir en siete segmentos el primer nivel espacial más allá de Havona. Cada superuniverso contiene alrededor de un billón de mundos habitables, es gobernado por tres Ancianos de los Días desde un mundo sede central arquitectónico y es supervisado desde el Paraíso por uno de los Siete Espíritus Rectores. Orvonton, el séptimo superuniverso, al que pertenece Urantia, es conocido como una demostración universal de amor y misericordia.","sections":[{"h":"La rueda gigantesca","items":[{"x":"En lo que concierne a la Trinidad del Paraíso, fuera de Havona hay solo siete universos habitados, y estos tienen jurisdicción sobre el primer nivel espacial más allá de Havona.","r":["15:0.1"]},{"q":"the hub being the eternal Isle of Paradise, the seven spokes the radiations of the Seven Master Spirits, the rim the outer regions of the grand universe.","r":"15:0.1"},{"x":"El plan séptuple de organización superuniversal se estableció al principio de la materialización de la creación universal, y el sistema administrativo actual existe casi desde la eternidad.","r":["15:0.2"]},{"x":"Los siete superuniversos giran en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj alrededor del Paraíso y de Havona, siguiendo una enorme trayectoria elíptica.","r":["15:1.2","15:3.14"]},{"x":"Urantia no se precipita a ciegas en un espacio desconocido, sino que sigue la trayectoria ordenada y predeterminada del nivel espacial superuniversal.","r":["15:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Unidades de organización","items":[{"q":"Only the Universal Father knows the location and actual number of inhabited worlds in space","r":"15:2.1"},{"x":"Unos mil mundos habitables forman un sistema, cien sistemas una constelación y cien constelaciones un universo local.","r":["15:2.3","15:2.4","15:2.5"]},{"x":"Cien universos locales forman un sector menor, cien sectores menores un sector mayor y diez sectores mayores un superuniverso, que contiene alrededor de un billón de planetas habitables.","r":["15:2.6","15:2.7","15:2.8"]},{"x":"Para todo el gran universo se prevén unos siete billones de mundos habitables, pero estas cifras son solo aproximaciones.","r":["15:2.9","15:2.25"]},{"x":"Los sectores menores son gobernados por tres Recientes de los Días, los sectores mayores por tres Perfecciones de los Días y los superuniversos por tres Ancianos de los Días.","r":["15:2.6","15:2.7","15:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Orvonton y nuestro lugar","items":[{"x":"Casi todas las estrellas visibles a simple vista desde Urantia pertenecen a Orvonton, el séptimo superuniverso, y la Vía Láctea es el núcleo central de Orvonton.","r":["15:3.1"]},{"x":"El centro de rotación de nuestro sector menor se encuentra en la nube estelar de Sagitario, y todos los sectores de Orvonton giran alrededor de Uversa, su sede central.","r":["15:3.5","15:3.7"]},{"x":"Urantia es el mundo número 606 del sistema de Satania, y pertenece a Orvonton a través de Satania, Norlatiadek, Nebadon, Ensa y Splandon.","r":["15:14.5","15:14.6","15:14.7"]},{"q":"Vuestro planeta forma parte de un cosmos enorme; vosotros pertenecéis a una familia casi infinita de mundos, pero vuestra esfera es administrada con igual precisión y se fomenta con igual amor como si fuera el único mundo habitado en toda la existencia.","r":"15:14.9"}]},{"h":"Formación física y control de la energía","items":[{"x":"Los organizadores de fuerza del Paraíso son originadores de nebulosas: movilizan las fuerzas del espacio para poner en movimiento las vastas ruedas matrices que dan origen a los soles y sistemas.","r":["15:4.4"]},{"x":"La energía se distribuye de manera universal, no por nebulosas, de modo que cada universo local contiene exactamente una cienmilésima parte de la energía total de su superuniverso.","r":["15:4.6"]},{"x":"Todos los cuerpos espaciales, salvo las esferas arquitectónicas, son de origen evolutivo, y nuestro sistema solar consta de planetas nacidos en un proceso de explosión gravitacional.","r":["15:5.5","15:6.7"]},{"x":"La luz es materia real que tiene peso, como lo muestran las colas de los cometas, que apuntan en dirección opuesta al sol.","r":["15:6.13"]},{"q":"Las nebulosas pueden dispersarse, los soles quemarse, los sistemas desaparecer, los planetas perecer, pero los universos no se descargan.","r":"15:8.10"}]},{"h":"El gobierno superuniversal","items":[{"x":"Las sedes centrales de los superuniversos son mundos arquitectónicos construidos especialmente, que dan luz sin calor y se encuentran cerca del centro astronómico de cada superuniverso.","r":["15:7.1"]},{"q":"En realidad, todos los mundos sede central son paradisiacos.","r":"15:7.3"},{"x":"El ejecutivo del gobierno superuniversal está formado por los Ancianos de los Días, los Perfeccionadores de la Sabiduría, los Consejeros Divinos y los Censores Universales, junto con los mortales ascendentes glorificados: los Mensajeros Poderosos, Aquellos Elevados en Autoridad y Aquellos sin Nombre ni Número.","r":["15:10.3","15:10.12"]},{"x":"Cada superuniverso es supervisado por uno de los Espíritus Rectores del Paraíso por medio de los Espíritus Reflectivos destacados en su capital.","r":["9:8.3","116:4.4"]},{"x":"Los Hijos del universo local pueden decretar la supervivencia de los mortales, pero los veredictos ejecutivos sobre la vida y la muerte eternas solo los dictan los Ancianos de los Días.","r":["15:12.2"]},{"x":"La asamblea deliberativa de Uversa está formada por representantes elegidos entre los graduados ascendentes calificados para Havona, y nunca ha estado en desacuerdo con el ejecutivo.","r":["15:11.2","15:11.3"]}]},{"h":"Admisión en la confederación y propósito","items":[{"x":"Un universo local solo puede entrar en la confederación superuniversal después de alcanzar la estabilidad física y la lealtad espiritual a su Hijo Soberano.","r":["15:9.16","15:9.17"]},{"x":"Nebadon todavía no pertenece siquiera al orden físico establecido del superuniverso, pero el gobierno superuniversal anhela su plena admisión y lo está ayudando.","r":["15:9.18"]},{"x":"Los superuniversos están aislados unos de otros y conocen los asuntos de los demás solo a través de la agencia distribuidora del Paraíso, aislamiento que continuará hasta que se factualice la soberanía del Ser Supremo.","r":["15:10.23"]},{"x":"Cada uno de los siete propósitos principales de la evolución superuniversal se expresa con mayor plenitud en un superuniverso.","r":["15:14.1"]},{"q":"Orvonton es la demostración universal del amor y de la misericordia.","r":"15:14.2"},{"x":"En Orvonton se están enlazando los propósitos de los otros seis superuniversos, y se conjetura que Dios el Supremo gobernará algún día desde Uversa los siete superuniversos perfeccionados.","r":["15:14.3","117:7.16"]}]}],"see":["Ancianos de los Días","Siete Espíritus Rectores","Universo local de Nebadon","Gran universo y universo maestro","Havona","Ser Supremo"]},{"n":42,"t":"Supervivencia","en":"Survival","sum":"Survival means that the mortal personality, beyond the death of the flesh, awakens again in the morontia worlds and continues the eternal ascent. The Urantia Book teaches that survival is a gift of God, but a gift that man must desire and choose for himself. What survives is the soul built together with the Adjuster, and the key to it is not knowledge or doctrine but the sincere determination to find God and be like him, and a living faith.","sections":[{"h":"Survival Is a Chosen Gift","items":[{"q":"survival is a gift of the Gods which must be desired by the creatures of time.","r":"110:2.2"},{"x":"Human identity is real only in so far as the personality chooses to become a continuing universe phenomenon, and that path must be pursued by free will.","r":["112:5.3"]},{"x":"Personality is destined for a divine goal, but man must choose for himself whether he will be present where that goal is attained.","r":["112:5.2"]},{"x":"The capacity to reject survival did not arise with the Lucifer rebellion; it is an endowment of choice that mortals have always possessed.","r":["54:6.9"]},{"q":"The energy system must continue, it has no choice; but man has everything to do with determining his own destiny.","r":"112:5.3"}]},{"h":"What Survives","items":[{"x":"The reality that survives the death of the material body and mind is the soul, the morontia self born of man and the Adjuster together.","r":["112:5.12"]},{"x":"After death the Adjuster goes to Divinington bearing the memory transcript of the life, and the soul is held by the guardian of destiny.","r":["112:3.5"]},{"x":"The surviving self evolves only by transferring the seat of identity from the material body to the immortal morontia soul.","r":["112:2.20"]},{"x":"Memories without spiritual meaning perish with the brain, but memories of relationships between personalities have cosmic value and remain.","r":["112:5.22"]},{"x":"Man survives mortal death by the identification of his identity with the indwelling spark of divinity.","r":["132:3.6"]}]},{"h":"Conditions of Survival","items":[{"q":"El secreto de la supervivencia se envuelve en el deseo supremo humano de ser semejante a Dios y en la disposición asociada a hacer y ser una y todas las cosas que son esenciales para el logro final de ese anhelo sobrecogedor.","r":"110:3.2"},{"x":"Success or failure in survival depends less on theories of belief than on decisions, determinations, and steadfast faith.","r":["110:3.2"]},{"q":"Sólo la resistencia consciente a la guía del Ajustador puede prevenir la supervivencia del alma inmortal evolutiva.","r":"110:3.5"},{"x":"Ignorance, confusion, or fearful doubt alone cannot prevent the survival of the God-knowing soul.","r":["110:3.5"]},{"x":"Doing the will of God is the secret of survival and of perfection in survival.","r":["111:5.2"]}]},{"h":"Faith and the Assurance of Survival","items":[{"x":"Religious experience leads at last to a sure consciousness of God and an undoubted assurance of the survival of the believing personality.","r":["101:1.6"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that once one has established himself by faith as a son of God, there is nothing more to worry about regarding the certainty of survival.","r":["176:3.3"]},{"x":"The risen Jesus said that survival depends first on being born of the spirit that seeks truth and God.","r":["193:2.2"]},{"q":"Faith in the survival of supreme values is the core of religion;","r":"111:3.5"},{"x":"The faith-activated soul cannot stop, because it has the task of finding God, and once it reaches the goal it can never end.","r":["132:3.7"]}]},{"h":"Merciful Adjudication and the Orders of Survival","items":[{"x":"Every will creature is sure to experience one genuine opportunity to make an unquestioned final choice.","r":["112:5.9"]},{"x":"Those who, through no fault of their own, have not mastered the circles on earth are given extended probation if they have the will to survive.","r":["112:5.6"]},{"x":"When a verdict is in doubt, the universe government always decides in favor of the individual.","r":["112:5.7"]},{"x":"Survivors reach the mansion worlds in several orders, among them dispensational group roll calls, individual ascensions, and probationary dependents.","r":["49:6.4","49:6.8","49:6.11"]},{"x":"Those who attained the third circle or higher and received personal guardians may be repersonalized on the mansion worlds on the third day after death.","r":["49:6.9","112:4.12"]},{"q":"Deberíamos más bien correr el riesgo de una rebelión en el sistema que cortejar el peligro de privar a un mortal que lucha, de cualquier mundo evolucionario, de la felicidad eterna de perseguir la carrera de ascensión.","r":"112:5.8"}]}],"see":["Muerte","Alma","Ajustador del Pensamiento","Mundos de estancia","Libre albedrío","Fe"]},{"n":97,"t":"Tiempo y espacio","en":"Time and Space","sum":"In The Urantia Book time and space are the conjoined mechanism of the master universe, provided so that finite creatures can coexist with the Infinite. Space is a bestowal of Paradise that alternately expands and contracts as if breathing, and time arises from motion and from mind's awareness of sequence. Paradise has neither time nor space, and the maturing personality, by unifying past and future in the present, gradually transcends the limitations of time and participates in eternal purposes.","sections":[{"h":"A Device for Finite Creatures","items":[{"q":"El tiempo y el espacio constituyen un mecanismo conjunto del universo maestro.","r":"118:9.1"},{"x":"Time and space insulate finite creatures from the absolute levels, and without them no mortal could exist.","r":["118:9.1"]},{"x":"Time and space are inseparably bound together only within the time-space creations of the seven superuniverses.","r":["12:5.3","65:8.1"]},{"q":"The grand universe is mechanism as well as organism, mechanical and living","r":"118:9.4"}]},{"h":"Space","items":[{"x":"Space is a bestowal of Paradise, yet it is neither infinite nor absolute, and we do not know its absolute limits.","r":["12:5.2","11:7.4"]},{"q":"El espacio no existe en ninguna de las superficies del Paraíso.","r":"11:7.1"},{"x":"Between pervaded and unpervaded space lie the relatively quiet midspace zones that separate them.","r":["11:7.2","11:7.3"]},{"x":"All space alternately contracts and expands as if breathing; when universe space expands, reservoir space contracts.","r":["11:6.1","11:6.2"]},{"x":"Space is not empty; it is the nonabsolute reality nearest to the absolute that man knows.","r":["130:7.6","118:3.5"]},{"x":"Space may be thought of as a property of bodies, so that when a body moves it carries its space with it.","r":["118:3.6"]}]},{"h":"Time","items":[{"x":"Time too is an indirect bestowal of Paradise, arising from motion and from mind's awareness of sequence.","r":["12:5.1"]},{"q":"El tiempo es la corriente de los acontecimientos temporales percibidos por la conciencia de la criatura.","r":"130:7.4"},{"x":"Time is perceived on three levels: duration perceived by mind, motion toward God perceived by spirit, and the unique awareness of presence held by personality.","r":["12:5.6","12:5.9"]},{"x":"As man progresses inwardly, the sequence of events is increasingly seen as one related whole.","r":["130:7.5"]},{"x":"For an individual creature the standard of time is the length of its own life, and to those not bound by time evolution is not so long a process.","r":["65:8.3"]}]},{"h":"Time and Maturity","items":[{"x":"In any intelligence there is a direct relation between the degree of maturity and the unit of time consciousness.","r":["118:1.3"]},{"q":"Patience is exercised by those mortals whose time units are short","r":"118:1.6"},{"x":"True maturity transcends patience by a forbearance born of real understanding.","r":["118:1.6"]},{"x":"To mature is to live more intensely in the present while transcending its limits by embracing past experience and future values.","r":["118:1.5","118:1.7"]},{"x":"A spirit-indwelt person has forward-looking insight, and only a progressive, forward-looking attitude is personally real.","r":["12:5.10"]}]},{"h":"Truth and Eternity","items":[{"q":"Things are time conditioned, but truth is timeless.","r":"118:3.2"},{"x":"The more truth we know, the better we can understand the past and comprehend the future.","r":["118:3.2"]},{"x":"In the evolving universes eternity is temporal everlastingness, the everlasting now.","r":["118:1.1"]},{"x":"On infinite and absolute levels the present moment contains all of the past and all of the future.","r":["118:1.9"]},{"x":"Eternity cannot be comprehended by the finite minds of time, but it is better thought of as an endless circle than as a straight line.","r":["32:5.4","32:5.6"]}]},{"h":"Personality Transcending Time","items":[{"x":"Mortal personality can become eternal by choosing to do the Father's will and becoming one with the indwelling spirit.","r":["118:1.2"]},{"x":"To God as an absolute, an ascending mortal who has made the eternal decision is already a Paradise finaliter.","r":["118:1.10"]},{"x":"Paradise pilgrims become unconscious as they pass through the midspace zones in crossing from time to eternity.","r":["12:5.4"]},{"x":"As spiritual values are recognized, personality is gradually freed from the limitations of time and transcends the bounds of space.","r":["65:8.6"]}]}],"see":["Paraíso","Gran universo y universo maestro","Realidad","Ser Supremo","Experiencia","Búsqueda de la perfección"]},{"n":10,"t":"Los tres Absolutos","en":"The Three Absolutes","sum":"Los tres Absolutos son los Absolutos de la potencialidad: el Absoluto de Deidad, el Absoluto No Cualificado y el Absoluto Universal. El Absoluto de Deidad es la totalidad de todo el potencial de Deidad; el Absoluto No Cualificado es la finalidad de la realidad no deificada y de todo potencial impersonal; y el Absoluto Universal unifica y coordina a los dos. Existen eternamente junto con la diferenciación de la realidad hecha por el libre albedrío del Padre, y son el fundamento cósmico que hace posible que los universos y las personalidades finitas coexistan con el Infinito.","sections":[{"h":"La diferenciación de la realidad y los tres Absolutos","items":[{"x":"La realidad infinita total existe en siete Absolutos coordinados, tres de los cuales son el Absoluto de Deidad, el Absoluto Universal y el Absoluto No Cualificado.","r":["0:3.1","104:3.5"]},{"x":"El Absoluto Universal resuelve la tensión primordial que surgió cuando el Padre, por su libre albedrío, dividió la realidad en deificada y no deificada.","r":["0:3.21","0:4.5"]},{"x":"Cuando se creó Havona, el Padre separó su presencia del potencial infinito, y este potencial está oculto en el Absoluto No Cualificado y abarcado por el Absoluto de Deidad.","r":["0:11.1"]},{"q":"En último análisis y en la comprensión final, los tres son un solo Absoluto.","r":"0:11.15"},{"x":"En los niveles subinfinitos los tres Absolutos existen por separado, pero en la infinitud parecen ser uno solo.","r":["56:9.1"]}]},{"h":"El Absoluto de Deidad","items":[{"x":"El Absoluto de Deidad son las posibilidades causales y potencialmente personales de la realidad universal, la totalidad de todo el potencial de Deidad.","r":["105:3.6"]},{"q":"El Absoluto de Deidad es el cualificador de lo absoluto y el absolutizador de lo cualificado —el indicador del destino.","r":"105:3.6"},{"x":"El Absoluto de Deidad nunca parece reaccionar de manera subabsoluta ante ninguna situación, sino que siempre parece reaccionar en función del bienestar de toda la creación y de toda la eternidad futura.","r":["0:11.5"]},{"x":"Los valores espirituales existenciales encuentran su origen y su destino en la triunidad del Padre Universal, el Hijo-Espíritu y el Absoluto de Deidad.","r":["104:4.20","104:4.21"]},{"x":"El Hijo Eterno domina los valores espirituales reales, mientras que el Absoluto de Deidad parece impregnar el vasto dominio de los valores espirituales que todavía son potenciales.","r":["7:1.10"]},{"x":"Dios el Absoluto existe ahora como el Absoluto de Deidad, y se postula que podría personalizarse experiencialmente mediante la función de la Trinidad Absoluta.","r":["0:2.18","106:6.6"]},{"q":"Amo y adoro a Dios el Padre; respeto y honro al Absoluto de Deidad.","r":"10:8.5"}]},{"h":"El Absoluto No Cualificado","items":[{"x":"El Absoluto No Cualificado es no personal y no divino, y ni los hechos, ni la verdad, ni la experiencia, ni la revelación pueden penetrar su naturaleza.","r":["0:11.7"]},{"q":"The Unqualified Absolute is a positive universe overcontrol in infinity","r":"0:11.8"},{"x":"No es una influencia vaga, como un concepto panteísta o la hipótesis del éter de la ciencia antigua, sino una presencia real que impregna el gran universo y el espacio que se extiende más allá.","r":["0:11.8","0:11.9"]},{"x":"El Absoluto No Cualificado es coordinado con el Paraíso, y en todo el espacio solo su presencia está en reposo.","r":["105:3.4","105:3.7"]},{"x":"La potencia del espacio, la energía que todavía no responde a la gravedad del Paraíso, deriva del Absoluto No Cualificado.","r":["0:6.5"]}]},{"h":"El Absoluto Universal","items":[{"x":"El Absoluto Universal unifica lo deificado y lo no deificado y correlaciona lo absoluto y lo relativo.","r":["105:3.8"]},{"q":"The finite can coexist in the cosmos along with the Infinite","r":"0:11.13"},{"x":"Esto es posible porque el Absoluto Universal equilibra las tensiones entre el tiempo y la eternidad, lo finito y lo infinito, el hombre y Dios.","r":["0:11.13"]},{"x":"La diferencia de potencial infinito entre el Absoluto No Cualificado y el Absoluto de Deidad hace posible la existencia de los universos materiales y de las personalidades finitas en el tiempo.","r":["0:11.12"]},{"x":"Se cree que la presencia imprevisible que funciona junto a los circuitos de la mente deriva en parte de la función del Absoluto Universal.","r":["9:6.8"]}]},{"h":"La triunidad de la potencialidad y el destino","items":[{"x":"La asociación de los tres Absolutos no es una trinidad, sino la triunidad de la potencialidad, ya que no los tres son Deidad.","r":["104:5.7","106:5.4"]},{"x":"La triunidad de la potencialidad correlaciona todas las realidades energéticas latentes, espirituales, mentales y cósmicas, y es infinita en potencialidad.","r":["104:5.11"]},{"x":"Los potenciales pueden quedar en parte sin realizarse en el tiempo, pero no fracasan en su totalidad, y la voluntad de Dios termina prevaleciendo.","r":["115:3.13"]},{"x":"Dentro de los tres Absolutos siempre quedan posibilidades desconocidas que ningún desarrollo experiencial podrá agotar jamás.","r":["106:7.1"]},{"q":"¡La búsqueda de Dios no tiene fin!","r":"106:7.5"},{"x":"Los Absolutos no son una deidad impersonal panteísta; en todo lo que concierne a la personalidad del universo, están estrictamente limitados por la Trinidad y dominados por la Deidad.","r":["0:11.16"]}]}],"see":["Trinidad del Paraíso","Padre Universal","Paraíso","Dios el Último","Realidad","Energía y materia"]},{"n":6,"t":"Trinidad del Paraíso","en":"Paradise Trinity","sum":"La Trinidad del Paraíso es la unión indivisible de Deidad de tres personas coordinadas: el Padre, el Hijo y el Espíritu. La Trinidad no es en sí misma una personalidad, pero es una realidad verdadera y absoluta cuyas funciones son más que la suma de los atributos de las tres personas. Administra la justicia y ejerce el supercontrol de la totalidad en los universos, y es el único hecho inevitable del universo, el que libera al Padre del absolutismo de la personalidad para que pueda otorgarse sin reservas.","sections":[{"h":"La única unión inevitable","items":[{"x":"La Trinidad une la expresión de la voluntad personal infinita de Dios con el carácter absoluto de la Deidad, y libera al Padre de las limitaciones del absolutismo de la personalidad.","r":["10:0.1"]},{"q":"we can discover only one inescapable inevitability in universe affairs, and that is the Paradise Trinity.","r":"10:0.3"},{"x":"El Padre ha transmitido a sus Hijos todo el poder y toda la autoridad que pueden delegarse; la personalidad divina no es egocéntrica y se complace en compartir.","r":["10:1.2","10:1.3"]},{"x":"Al otorgar personalidad absoluta al Hijo, el Padre llegó a ser el Padre del Hijo, y el Padre y el Hijo juntos otorgaron personalidad conjunta al Espíritu Infinito.","r":["10:1.4","10:2.2"]}]},{"h":"Tres personas, una Deidad","items":[{"q":"A pesar de que existe una sola Deidad, hay tres personalizaciones positivas y divinas de la Deidad.","r":"10:3.1"},{"x":"Cada uno de los tres es original, ninguno es duplicado de otro, y sin embargo todos están unidos.","r":["10:2.6"]},{"x":"Solo el Hijo Eterno experimenta a la vez la filiación hacia el Padre y la paternidad hacia el Espíritu, y por eso conoce la plenitud de la relación de la personalidad divina.","r":["10:2.7"]},{"q":"God speaks through the Son and, with the Son, acts through the Infinite Spirit","r":"10:3.3"},{"x":"La paternidad no es real sin la filiación, y el Padre nunca ha existido solo, sin el Hijo y el Espíritu.","r":["10:3.5"]},{"x":"Fuera de Havona, el Padre actúa por medio de los Hijos Creadores, la gravedad, el Hijo, el Creador Conjunto, el circuito de personalidad y los Ajustadores, y como Deidad total actúa solo en la Trinidad.","r":["10:3.9","10:3.16"]}]},{"h":"Una realidad verdadera, no una personalidad","items":[{"x":"La Trinidad es una asociación de personas infinitas que actúan en una capacidad impersonal, pero no contraria a la personalidad, comparable a una corporación que actúa según la voluntad personal de sus miembros.","r":["10:4.3"]},{"q":"La Trinidad es una realidad de Deidad supersumativa que se eventúa de la conjunción de las tres Deidades del Paraíso.","r":"104:2.4"},{"x":"Las tres Deidades como individuos pueden cooperar como quieran, pero esa cooperación no es la Trinidad.","r":["10:4.4"]},{"x":"Así como el potencial de un grupo supera la suma de los atributos de sus miembros, las funciones de la Trinidad son más que la simple suma de los atributos de las tres Deidades.","r":["10:5.2"]},{"x":"Hay muchas triunidades existenciales, pero una sola Trinidad existencial; la Trinidad no es una asociación funcional, sino Deidad indivisa.","r":["104:3.15","104:3.16"]}]},{"h":"La justicia y el supercontrol cósmico","items":[{"x":"La ley procede del Padre, la administración de la ley espiritual corresponde al Hijo, la revelación de la ley al Espíritu, y la justicia, que es la aplicación de la ley, pertenece a la Trinidad.","r":["10:6.1"]},{"q":"La justicia no es nunca una actitud personal; es siempre una función plural.","r":"10:6.2"},{"x":"Los Hijos estacionarios de la Trinidad, como los Ancianos de los Días, administran los juicios de los superuniversos a partir de las pruebas presentadas por las personalidades del Espíritu Infinito.","r":["10:6.4","10:6.17"]},{"x":"La justicia es el pensamiento colectivo de la rectitud, y la misericordia es su expresión personal; cuando se comprenden plenamente, la justicia de la Trinidad y el amor del Padre coinciden.","r":["10:6.18"]},{"x":"Respecto de lo finito, la Trinidad actúa como la Trinidad de la Supremacía, y respecto de lo absonito, como la Trinidad de la Ultimidad.","r":["10:5.4","10:5.5"]},{"x":"Incluso las catástrofes y los cambios inexplicables de la vida pueden entretejerse en un diseño significativo gracias a las funciones del Supremo y al supercontrol de la Trinidad.","r":["10:7.5"]}]},{"h":"La comprensión humana de la Trinidad","items":[{"x":"Los conceptos de una deidad trina de la religión evolutiva surgieron de asociaciones naturales, como las falanges de un dedo o un taburete de tres patas, y deben distinguirse del concepto revelado de la Trinidad.","r":["104:0.1","104:0.3"]},{"q":"La verdadera concepción de la trinidad no es simplemente el agrupamiento de tres dioses separados.","r":"104:1.7"},{"x":"En Urantia la Trinidad fue presentada sucesivamente por el séquito de Caligastia, por Adán y Eva y por Maquiventa Melquisedek.","r":["104:1.1","104:1.2","104:1.3"]},{"x":"El concepto cristiano de la Trinidad, aunque erróneo en cuanto a los hechos, era prácticamente verdadero respecto de las relaciones espirituales.","r":["104:1.13"]},{"x":"Una Deidad personal requiere una relación con otras personalidades iguales; un concepto de Deidad sin tal relación se reduce fácilmente a un absoluto panteísta.","r":["104:2.2"]},{"x":"El reconocimiento del concepto de la Trinidad hace posible cierta comprensión de la interrelación entre el amor y la ley en las creaciones del tiempo y del espacio.","r":["104:2.3"]}]}],"see":["Padre Universal","Hijo Eterno","Espíritu Infinito","Los tres Absolutos","Ser Supremo","Justicia"]},{"n":15,"t":"Universo local de Nebadon","en":"Local Universe of Nebadon","sum":"Nebadon es el universo local, organizado y gobernado por el Hijo Creador Micael y el Espíritu Materno del Universo, al que pertenece Urantia. Destinado a constar de cien constelaciones y diez mil sistemas, es una creación relativamente joven de Orvonton; desde su capital, Salvington, Micael gobierna como representante del Padre y del Hijo, mientras que Gabriel actúa como jefe ejecutivo. El universo local es evolutivo, y las criaturas alcanzan la perfección ascendiendo paso a paso desde abajo.","sections":[{"h":"Un universo local en evolución","items":[{"x":"Un universo local es obra de un Hijo Creador de la orden de Micael; consta de cien constelaciones, cada una de las cuales contiene cien sistemas.","r":["32:0.1"]},{"x":"Todos los universos del tiempo y del espacio son evolutivos, y los planes de los Hijos Creadores siguen siempre el camino del desarrollo progresivo de las criaturas.","r":["32:0.2"]},{"x":"Un universo local es concebido por los Arquitectos del Universo Maestro en el Paraíso, y el Hijo Creador comienza su organización solo después de que los directores del poder han movilizado las energías del espacio.","r":["32:0.4","32:1.2"]},{"x":"Nebadon se extiende hasta donde llega la presencia espacial del Espíritu Materno de Salvington; lo que está más allá se encuentra fuera de Nebadon.","r":["41:0.1"]},{"q":"Con excepción del universo central, la perfección es un logro progresivo.","r":"32:3.3"}]},{"h":"Organización y nuestro lugar","items":[{"x":"La primera creación física terminada en Nebadon fue el mundo sede central, Salvington, seguido de cien sedes centrales de constelación y diez mil sedes centrales de sistema.","r":["32:2.3"]},{"x":"Salvington está situado en el centro exacto de energía-masa del universo local.","r":["32:2.4"]},{"x":"En el último registro Nebadon contaba con 3.840.101 planetas habitados, y la organización de moradas planetarias sigue en curso.","r":["32:2.9"]},{"x":"Nebadon se encuentra hacia el borde de Orvonton, y Satania, a su vez, en las afueras de Nebadon.","r":["32:2.11"]},{"x":"Nebadon es el universo número ochenta y cuatro del sector menor de Ensa, y Salvington es su capital.","r":["15:14.6"]}]},{"h":"Micael, el Hijo Soberano","items":[{"x":"Micael de Nebadon es la personalización número 611.121 de un concepto original que surge del Padre y del Hijo Eterno; no es el Hijo Eterno del Paraíso mismo.","r":["33:1.1","33:1.2"]},{"q":"Para nuestro universo y todos sus mundos habitados, para todos los fines y propósitos prácticos, el Hijo Soberano es Dios.","r":"33:1.4"},{"x":"Tras completar sus siete autootorgamientos como criatura, Micael gobierna Nebadon como un soberano de misericordia comprensiva.","r":["119:0.4","119:0.7"]},{"x":"Su poder solo está limitado por los circuitos de gravedad del Paraíso y por los Ancianos de los Días, que se reservan el veredicto final sobre la extinción de la personalidad.","r":["33:2.2"]},{"x":"En la administración del universo local el Padre actúa solo por medio del Hijo Creador, pero está íntimamente presente en los mortales como Ajustador residente.","r":["33:0.1","32:3.4"]}]},{"h":"El gobierno conjunto del Hijo y del Espíritu","items":[{"x":"El Espíritu Materno del Universo crea y gobierna el universo junto con Micael, y el Hijo otorga al Espíritu una posición coordinada y la misma autoridad en todos los asuntos.","r":["33:3.2","33:3.3"]},{"x":"Cuando Micael volvió de su autootorgamiento en Urantia, el Espíritu del Universo reconoció públicamente por primera vez su subordinación al Hijo.","r":["33:3.5"]},{"x":"El Hijo proclamó entonces, en la «Proclamación de Igualdad», que el Espíritu es igual a él en todos los atributos de la personalidad, un ideal elevado para la familia y el matrimonio.","r":["33:3.6"]},{"q":"El Hijo y el Espíritu presiden ahora el universo en forma muy similar a un padre y una madre que vigilan y asisten a su familia de hijos e hijas.","r":"33:3.7"},{"x":"Ante la rebelión solo el Hijo actúa como salvador, pero ningún Hijo podría tener éxito sin la cooperación incesante de la Ministra Divina.","r":["33:3.4"]}]},{"h":"Administración y tribunales","items":[{"x":"Gabriel, la Brillante Estrella Matutina, nacido de la primera creación conjunta del Hijo y del Espíritu, es el jefe ejecutivo de Nebadon.","r":["32:2.6","33:4.5"]},{"x":"Emanuel de Salvington, el embajador de la Trinidad, es la única personalidad de Nebadon que no reconoce su subordinación a Micael, y solo aconseja cuando se le pide.","r":["33:5.1","33:5.2"]},{"x":"Los sistemas se ocupan principalmente de los problemas biológicos, las constelaciones de la unidad y la estabilidad sociales, y los gobernantes del universo del estado espiritual de los reinos.","r":["33:6.3"]},{"x":"Micael se ocupa solo de la creación, el sustento y el ministerio; los creadores nunca se sientan a juzgar a sus propias criaturas.","r":["33:7.1"]},{"q":"Vosotros vivís en un universo bien ordenado, y podéis confiar en que, tarde o temprano, seréis tratados con justicia, aun con misericordia.","r":"33:7.8"}]},{"h":"La ascensión y el propósito de las criaturas","items":[{"q":"Es un hecho: el que ha visto a un Hijo Creador, ha visto al Padre.","r":"32:3.6"},{"x":"Cuanto más abajo está una criatura en la escala de la vida, más difícil le resulta reconocer al Padre en el Hijo Creador, pero aferrarse a la verdad de la presencia del Padre en sus Hijos es la salvaguardia más segura.","r":["32:3.6"]},{"x":"El origen evolutivo animal no es un estigma; quienes suben la escalera de la vida desde abajo obtienen mayor honor y una experiencia más plena.","r":["32:3.10"]},{"x":"El universo local es el punto de partida de la verdadera evolución, donde personalidades imperfectas cocrean su propio futuro y en el que incluso los creadores evolucionan.","r":["116:4.8"]},{"x":"En la mente de Dios hay un plan eterno de oportunidad infinita y vida sin fin que abarca a toda criatura.","r":["32:5.7"]},{"q":"¡El objetivo de la eternidad os aguarda!","r":"32:5.8"}]}],"see":["Hijo Creador Micael","Espíritu Materno del Universo Local","Constelaciones y sistemas locales","Los siete superuniversos","Autootorgamiento de Jesús","Urantia"]},{"n":95,"t":"Urantia","en":"Urantia","sum":"Urantia is the universe name of the earth on which we live, the 606th inhabited world of the system of Satania, in the constellation of Norlatiadek, in the local universe of Nebadon. Urantia is a life-modification world where the Life Carriers formulated an original life, and an isolated world spiritually quarantined through Caligastia's betrayal and Adam's default. Yet it is also known throughout the universe as the \"World of the Cross,\" where Michael, the Creator Son, made his final bestowal.","sections":[{"h":"Its Place in the Universe","items":[{"q":"Vuestro mundo se denomina Urantia, y es el número 606 en el grupo planetario, o sistema, de Satania.","r":"15:14.5"},{"x":"Urantia belongs to Norlatiadek, one of the one hundred constellations of the local universe of Nebadon, which is part of the superuniverse of Orvonton.","r":["43:0.1","0:0.5"]},{"x":"Satania is an unfinished system with only 619 inhabited worlds, and the number 606 means that this was the 606th world in it on which human beings appeared.","r":["49:0.3"]},{"x":"Urantia reached its present size about a billion years ago and was entered under this name in the physical registry of Nebadon.","r":["57:8.1"]}]},{"h":"A Life-Modification World","items":[{"x":"Urantia originated from your sun, which is one of the many offspring of the Andronover nebula.","r":["57:1.1"]},{"x":"There are only sixty-one life-modification planets like Urantia in all Satania, and Urantia was a decimal planet on which the life designs could be modified.","r":["58:0.1","58:1.1"]},{"q":"La vida en Urantia es única, original con el planeta.","r":"58:4.1"},{"x":"The ancient inland seas were the cradle of evolution, recording the history of life on pages of stone.","r":["57:8.26"]},{"x":"Man can live in comfort thanks to more than forty seemingly accidental protective factors, such as the ozone layer.","r":["58:2.4"]},{"x":"Urantia was officially recognized as a planet of human habitation 993,408 years ago, and its first parents were Andon and Fonta.","r":["62:7.7","63:0.2"]}]},{"h":"An Isolated World","items":[{"q":"Gran, muy gran, parte de la dificultad que tienen los mortales de Urantia para comprender a Dios se debe a las vastas consecuencias de la rebelión de Lucifer y a la traición de Caligastia.","r":"4:3.3"},{"x":"Since Caligastia's betrayal, Urantia has been one of the isolated worlds of Norlatiadek, with a Most High observer stationed on it.","r":["43:5.17"]},{"x":"The Life Carriers regret that Caligastia's betrayal and Adam's default greatly hindered their efforts to improve intelligent life.","r":["65:5.1"]},{"x":"The planet's spiritual isolation had no effect on the presence and function of the spirit-gravity circuit of the Eternal Son.","r":["7:1.7"]},{"x":"Urantia is still under partial spiritual quarantine, so the reflective seraphim cannot function freely.","r":["28:7.4"]}]},{"h":"The Opportunity of Isolation","items":[{"q":"Pero el aislamiento de estas esferas ofrece a sus razas una oportunidad única para ejercer la fe y para desarrollar una calidad peculiar de confianza en la confiabilidad cósmica que no depende de la vista ni de otras consideraciones materiales.","r":"50:7.1"},{"x":"Mortals from worlds quarantined because of rebellion may turn out in the end to be extremely fortunate.","r":["50:7.1"]},{"x":"Though Urantia mortals differ in opportunity and endowment, their spiritual endowment is equal, since all enjoy the same indwelling divine spirit.","r":["5:1.5"]}]},{"h":"The World of the Bestowal","items":[{"x":"Your little world has become known throughout Nebadon as the place where Michael completed the experience required for sovereignty.","r":["119:8.2"]},{"q":"Es un hecho que Urantia se conoce entre otros planetas vecinos habitados como «el mundo de la cruz».","r":"188:4.1"},{"x":"On completing his Urantia bestowal Michael received the title Planetary Prince of Urantia and sought to set right the confusion left by Caligastia's betrayal.","r":["120:2.3"]},{"x":"The life lived on Urantia was intended as an inspiration not only to this planet but to beings on all the worlds of Nebadon.","r":["120:2.7"]}]},{"h":"The Future of Urantia","items":[{"x":"Urantia's greatest handicaps on the way to light and life are disease, degeneracy, war, multicolored races, and multilingualism.","r":["55:3.21"]},{"x":"When that time comes, Machiventa Melchizedek, the vicegerent Planetary Prince, will take the place of Planetary Sovereign.","r":["55:7.3"]},{"x":"Even if Urantia is restored to the system circuits, difficulties will remain for a time because all of Satania is isolated.","r":["46:8.2"]},{"q":"Jesús de Nazaret, como hombre entre los hombres, alcanzó personalmente el estado de luz y vida en Urantia más de mil novecientos años atrás.","r":"55:11.7"}]}],"see":["Universo local de Nebadon","Constelaciones y sistemas locales","Evolución","Rebelión de Lucifer","Caligastia","Autootorgamiento de Jesús"]},{"n":57,"t":"Verdad","en":"Truth","sum":"Truth is a spirit-discerned living reality that goes beyond knowledge, which deals with facts, and wisdom, which deals with relationships, to deal with reality values. God is the first truth, and all truth issues from him. Truth cannot be confined in words or creeds but is defined only by living, and static truth is dead truth. The Spirit of Truth enables people to realize this living, growing truth, and truth is unified with beauty and goodness in God.","sections":[{"h":"What Truth Is","items":[{"q":"La verdad no se puede definir en palabras, sino tan sólo viviéndola.","r":"132:3.2"},{"x":"Knowledge originates in science, wisdom in philosophy, and truth in the religious experience of spiritual living; truth deals with reality values.","r":["132:3.2"]},{"x":"Knowledge is demonstrable, but truth is experienced; knowledge is a possession of the mind, truth an experience of the soul.","r":["130:4.10"]},{"x":"God is the first truth and the last fact, so all truth takes origin in him.","r":["102:6.6"]},{"x":"Truth is always a revelation: autorevelation when it comes through the work of the Adjuster, epochal revelation when presented by celestial agencies.","r":["101:4.3"]}]},{"h":"Living Truth","items":[{"x":"Physical facts are uniform, but truth is a living and flexible factor in the philosophy of the universe.","r":["2:7.2"]},{"x":"Truth cannot be imprisoned in formulas, codes, or creeds; when one attempts to formulate it, it speedily dies.","r":["180:5.2"]},{"q":"La verdad estática es verdad muerta, y sólo la verdad muerta puede ser contenida en una teoría.","r":"180:5.2"},{"x":"Truth is unshaken by shocks and free from all temporal fluctuations, yet it is never formalized and is always vital.","r":["118:3.3"]},{"x":"It is folly to regard the past as the only source of truth, for truth lives always in the present and finds new expression in each generation.","r":["79:8.8"]},{"q":"La verdad es relativa y extensible, siempre vive en el presente logrando nuevas expresiones en cada generación de hombres, aun en cada vida humana.","r":"79:8.8"}]},{"h":"The Way to Know Truth","items":[{"x":"Truth cannot become man's possession without faith, for a person's thoughts and ideals can never rise higher than his faith.","r":["132:3.5"]},{"q":"Revealed truth, personally discovered truth, is the supreme delight of the human soul","r":"132:3.4"},{"x":"Fearing the unknown, man tends to fixate science, formalize philosophy, and dogmatize truth.","r":["132:3.3"]},{"x":"There is never conflict between true knowledge and truth; conflict arises between knowledge and human beliefs colored by prejudice and fear.","r":["132:3.4"]},{"x":"The more one knows truth and the more one becomes truth, the more one can understand the past and grasp the future.","r":["118:3.2"]}]},{"h":"The Spirit of Truth","items":[{"x":"The Spirit of Truth is not the letter or law of truth but the conviction of true meanings on real spirit levels, a living and growing teacher.","r":["180:5.1"]},{"x":"The God-knowing person lifts wisdom to the level of living truth, but the spiritually unprogressive soul drags living truth down to dead wisdom.","r":["180:5.4"]},{"x":"Even the golden rule remains a mere ethical rule without the insight of the Spirit of Truth; its meaning is realized only by living it.","r":["180:5.5","180:5.11"]},{"x":"Truth, the understanding of cosmic relationships and spiritual values, is best attained through the ministry of the Spirit of Truth.","r":["103:7.8"]},{"q":"La verdad divina es una realidad viva discernida por el espíritu.","r":"180:5.2"}]},{"h":"Truth, Beauty, and Goodness","items":[{"q":"La verdad es bella porque es pletórica y simétrica.","r":"2:7.4"},{"x":"Because truth can be acted upon and lived, happiness follows the recognition of truth, while disappointment and sorrow follow error.","r":["2:7.6"]},{"x":"All truth, whether material, philosophic, or spiritual, is both beautiful and good.","r":["2:7.11"]},{"x":"Truth is coherent, beauty attractive, and goodness stabilizing; when these are harmonized, they become a high love.","r":["2:7.12"]},{"x":"Truth is the basis of science and philosophy and the intellectual foundation of religion.","r":["56:10.10"]}]}],"see":["Belleza","Bondad","Espíritu de la Verdad","Sabiduría","Fe","Revelación"]},{"n":50,"t":"Voluntad de Dios","en":"Will of God","sum":"The will of God is the eternal purpose of the First Source and Center, and in the life of the individual it is partnership with the way and choice of God. The Urantia Book regards doing the will of God as the secret of survival and of perfection, and says that it is not a surrender of will but its consecration and expansion. Throughout his life Jesus lived \"not my will but yours\" and became the example of that way.","sections":[{"h":"What the Will of God Is","items":[{"x":"The will of God is the purpose of the First Source and Center, personalized in the Eternal Son and shown in universe action in the Infinite Spirit.","r":["117:0.1"]},{"q":"En substancia Jesús dijo: la voluntad de Dios es el camino de Dios, el asociarse con la elección de Dios frente a cualquier alternativa potencial.","r":"130:2.7"},{"x":"Doing the will of God is therefore the experience of becoming more and more like God, the source of all that is good, beautiful, and true.","r":["130:2.7"]},{"x":"Doing the will of God reveals a willingness to share one's inner life with God, and sharing is a divine thing.","r":["111:5.1"]},{"x":"In his mind Jesus unified all the attributes of God in \"the will of the Father in heaven.\"","r":["196:0.2"]}]},{"h":"The Gift of a Dedicated Will","items":[{"x":"The loving dedication of the human will to doing the Father's will is the highest and the only truly valuable gift man can offer God.","r":["1:1.2"]},{"x":"God requires no coerced worship or slavish service; man must of himself love and worship God.","r":["1:1.2"]},{"q":"Such a creature choice is not a surrender of will. It is a consecration of will, an expansion of will, a glorification of will, a perfecting of will","r":"111:5.5"},{"x":"This choice lies less in the negation \"not my will but yours\" than in the positive affirmation \"it is my will that your will be done.\"","r":["111:5.6"]},{"x":"God too first consented to entrust a fragment of himself to the human will and to dwell within it.","r":["111:5.3","111:5.4"]},{"q":"The affectionate dedication of the human will to the doing of the Father's will is man's choicest gift to God","r":"1:1.2"}]},{"h":"The Fruits of a Life That Does His Will","items":[{"x":"The imitation of God is the key to perfection, and doing his will is the secret of survival and perfection.","r":["111:5.2"]},{"x":"Peace in this life, survival after death, perfection in the next life, and service in eternity are already achieved in spirit when one chooses to submit the will to the Father's will.","r":["111:5.4"]},{"x":"By choosing to do the Father's will, the mortal personality may become one with the indwelling spirit and so become eternal.","r":["118:1.2"]},{"x":"A life that lives the Father's will is founded on truth, sensitive to beauty, governed by goodness, and shown outwardly in loving service.","r":["106:9.12"]},{"x":"In many cases the Thought Adjuster is dispatched at the very moment a person quietly resolves to do the Father's will.","r":["108:2.10"]},{"q":"La imitación de Dios es la clave para la perfección; hacer su voluntad es el secreto de la sobrevivencia y de la perfección en la supervivencia.","r":"111:5.2"}]},{"h":"The Adventure of Finding and Doing His Will","items":[{"q":"No olvidéis jamás que hay tan sólo una aventura que es más satisfactoria y emocionante que el intento de descubrir la voluntad del Dios vivo, y ésa es la experiencia suprema de tratar honestamente de hacer la voluntad divina.","r":"155:6.11"},{"x":"The will of God can be done in any occupation, and for those who are spirit led there is no division between holy and secular callings.","r":["155:6.11"]},{"x":"When one is wholly dedicated to the Father's will, prayer comes into harmony with that will, and every petition is answered.","r":["146:2.7"]},{"x":"The idea of sacrifice impairs the efficacy of true prayer by offering material things instead of one's own will.","r":["91:2.4"]},{"x":"The will of God does not prevail from moment to moment, but viewed over a whole lifetime it becomes ever clearer in the fruits of those who are led by the spirit.","r":["12:7.7"]}]},{"h":"Jesus, the Example of a Life Lived in the Father's Will","items":[{"q":"«Sea yo quien fuere y sea cual fuere el poder que yo pueda ejercer o no, he estado siempre y siempre estaré sujeto a la voluntad de mi Padre Paradisiaco».","r":"128:7.2"},{"x":"In every situation of life the mind of Jesus held to \"not my will but yours,\" and this consecration is the true passport to divine attainment.","r":["109:6.5"]},{"x":"The great task of Michael's bestowal was to reveal God to the creatures of flesh by living a life that did the Father's will.","r":["120:2.8"]},{"x":"By dedicating his will to doing the divine will, Jesus made the greatest offering man can make to God.","r":["196:0.10"]},{"x":"Jesus tried to persuade his disciples to use \"the will of God\" in place of the word \"kingdom.\"","r":["170:2.11"]}]}],"see":["Libre albedrío","Reino del cielo","Oración","Adoración","Carácter de Jesús","Ser Supremo"]}];
